PVD("bangladesh_ndp_2016-2020",{"docs":["","BGD NDP 2016 2020"],"s":{"1":[[1,"438","3","Local Governance Capacity and Service Delivery Strengthening","LGD is working to mobilize local resources, establish good governance at the local level, providing civic/utility services to the citizen of Paurashavas and City corporations, rural and urban infrastructures development, supplying of safe drinking water in rural and urban areas, gradually shifting from underground source to surface water sources, solid waste disposal and sanitation all over the country.","LGD"],[1,"438","5","Safe Water Supply and Sanitation Services","Department of Public Health Engineering (DPHE) under LGD is providing safe water supply and sanitation facilities to rural and urban areas.","Department of Public Health Engineering (DPHE) | LGD"],[1,"439","1","Urban Water Supply, Sewerage and Drainage Maintenance","maintenance of water supply, sewerage and drainage facilities in Dhaka, Chittagong, Khulna and Rajshahi Cities.",""],[1,"440","1","Local Service Delivery and Community Infrastructure Package","Ensure provision of health services (c) Arrange for supply of safe drinking water and promote sanitation programme, (d) Construction of inter-ward roads, maintenance of the same, management of small scale irrigation and water resources, (e)Implementation of afforestation programme along the Union Parishad roads and all earthen embankments, (f) Peaceful resolution and amicable settlement of inter ward disputes, (g) Promote social resistance over violence against women, terrorism, all types of crimes and cooperate with administration for maintenance of law and order and(h) Up-to-date registration of birth, death and marriages.",""],[1,"440","2","City Corporation Service Delivery Functions","The main functions of the City corporations includes to manage and maintain (a) public health, (b) water supply and drainage, (c) food and beverage, (d) animals, (e ) town planning, (f) building control, (g) streets, (h) public safety, (i) trees, park, gardens and forest, (j) education and culture, (k) social welfare and (l) development plan.",""],[1,"440","3","City Corporation Service and Urban Management Functions","The main functions of the City corporations includes to manage and maintain (a) public health, (b) water supply and drainage, (c) food and beverage, (d) animals, (e ) town planning, (f) building control, (g) streets, (h) public safety, (i) trees, park, gardens and forest, (j) education and culture, (k) social welfare and (l) development plan.",""],[1,"442","8","Urban Local Services and Infrastructure Improvement","The targets for the sub-sector will be to create better living environment in urban centres, develop Paurashavas capacities to provide better services, including providing safe water, sanitation and drainage for people living in slums and fringes, and in the process generate employment for urban dwellers.",""],[1,"442","8","Urban Infrastructure and Basic Services Upgrading","The other issues include employment, better provision of basic services by overcoming deficient infrastructure and low level of urban services (transport, water supply, sanitation, solid and liquid waste management, drainage, municipal facility etc.); and overcoming growing spatial dimension of Urbanization with faster growth of urban population and rural-urban migration with increase in number of urban slum and squatters, effectively shifting of poverty from rural to urban areas.",""],[1,"446","11","Community-Based Faecal and Solid Waste Management","Community based faecal and solid waste management.",""],[1,"489","9","Total Sanitation Campaign Sustaining and Replication Initiative","Sustaining & replication of Total Sanitation Campaign with a variety of water supply initiatives.",""],[1,"489","11","Routine Tube Well Water Quality Monitoring and Remedial Action","Monitoring water quality of the tube wells in arsenic prone areas on a routine basis & suggesting for remedial actions.",""],[1,"554","17","Safe Water and Sanitation Facilities Expansion","Ensuring safe water and sanitation facilities for all through the development of different water supply & sanitation options",""],[1,"555","1","Safe Water Supply Development in Contaminated Areas","Ensuring safe water through the development of different water supply options in areas affected by the presence of arsenic, salinity and other chemical pollutants in ground water and presence of micro-organisms, industrial wastes, fertilizers, insecticides, herbicides etc. in surface water.",""],[1,"555","2","Safe Sanitation Facilities Development and Upgradation","Ensuring safe sanitation facilities for all through the development and up- gradation of different sanitation options (sanitation ladder) based on hydro-geology/ weather, socio-economic condition of the people/ community, soil condition etc.",""],[1,"555","3","Safe Water and Sanitation Technology Development for Difficult Areas","Ensuring safe water and sanitation facilities in the hydro-geologically difficult and problematic areas through the development of appropriate and affordable technological options.",""],[1,"555","4","WSS Human Resource Development Centre Establishment","Establishment of WSS HRD centre in DPHE to ensure adequate supply of trained and skilled manpower in the WSS sector for its balanced development and effective management.",""],[1,"555","5","Establishment of the National Water Supply and Sanitation Information Centre","Establishment of the NAWASIC (National Water Supply & Sanitation Information Centre) in DPHE to ensure information management of the WSS sector and DPHE as well, necessary for policy making and strategic planning of the sector.","DPHE"],[1,"555","6","National Water Quality Monitoring and Surveillance System","Establishment of water quality examination, monitoring and surveillance systems throughout the country by establishing laboratory network and onsite testing facilities using portable water testing kits.",""],[1,"555","7","Water Supply and Sanitation Resource Mobilization Mechanism","Generation of adequate resource allocation through ensuring GoB fund, resource mobilization from other sources (Development partners/ financial institutions/ Private entrepreneurs/ Private operators etc.) shall be explored for desired development of the WSS sector.",""],[1,"555","11","DPHE Organizational Strengthening for Local Government Support","Update and strengthen \"Organizational Setup\" of DPHE to orient it to support the LGIs, particularly the City Corporations the Paurashavas and Union Parishads in formulating, implementation and operation of the scheme",""],[1,"555","12","Hydrological and Hydro-geological Investigation and Emergency Water Intervention Programme","DPHE will concentrate to continue with hydrological and hydro-geological investigation for ground and surface water and emergency intervention during natural calamities through proper staffing with the development of skill.",""],[1,"555","13","WSS Human Resources Development and Capacity Building","DPHE will carry out the WSS Human Resources Development (HRD) activities for capacity building of personnel (Public/LGIs/ Private/ NGOs/ Unemployed youth etc.) involved in the development and O&M of WSS system.",""],[1,"555","13","Technical Staff Secondment to Local Government Institutions","DPHE will also consider deputing its professional staff to LGIs to transfer the technical knowledge.",""],[1,"556","1","WSS Sector Information Management and R&D Support","DPHE will carry out and look after information management and R&D activities of the WSS sector to support policy making and strategic planning.",""],[1,"556","2","DPHE Facilitation and Capacity-Building Support for LGIs","DPHE will facilitate overall capacity building of the concerned LGI and continue their technical support until LGIs are capable to manage the scheme by themselves.",""],[1,"556","3","National Water Quality Monitoring and Surveillance Programme","To carry out national water quality monitoring and surveillance including groundwater level, water quality and gradually expand the Water Safety Plan through system development and awareness creation;","DPHE | WARPO | WDB | DOE"],[1,"556","3","Surface Water Source Development and Pollution Control Coordination","DPHE will also co-ordinate with WARPO, WDB, DOE and other agencies to develop the surface water source and its pollution control.","DPHE | WARPO | WDB | DOE"],[1,"556","4","Public-Private Partnership for WSS Infrastructure Development and O&M","DPHE will explore the strategies to encourage the Public-Private partnership in the development of infrastructure for adequate WSS service and its subsequent O&M.",""],[1,"556","5","DPHE Multidisciplinary Staffing Expansion","DPHE has begun to be oriented as multi-disciplinary department.",""],[1,"556","6","Dhaka Sustainable Water Supply Strategy","As part of sustainable water supply strategy DWASA wants to ensure water production ratio where 70% will come from surface water and 30% from ground water.",""],[1,"556","6","Dhaka Sanitation Coverage Expansion","To improve on sanitation services it aims at ensuring sanitation facilities for city dwellers by increasing the existing coverage from 40% to 60% during the 7th plan period.",""],[1,"556","6","Dhaka Drainage System Expansion for Waterlogging Reduction","As part of its strategy of removal of Water Logging from Dhaka city so as to provide hygienic living conditions it plans to increase the existing coverage of drainage system from 60% to 80%.",""],[1,"556","6","Khulna and Rajshahi Water Supply, Sanitation, and Waterlogging Strategy","Khulna WASA and Rajshahi WASA also has strategic plans for increasing sustainable quality water supply, improve sanitation services and water logging in the Khulna and Rajshahi city areas.",""]],"2":[[1,"359","7","Integrated Urban Water Treatment and Supply Facilities","The urban areas need integrated water treatment and efficient water supply facilities.",""]],"3":[[1,"48","4","Phased Implementation of the Rational Social Security Strategy","Phased implementation of the recently adopted rational Social Security Strategy of the Government of Bangladesh will provide comprehensive social protection to all poor and vulnerable citizens.",""],[1,"56","4","National Social Security Strategy Implementation","The successful implementation of NSSS will provide a strong basis for Bangladesh to extend proper social protection to its poor and vulnerable population.",""],[1,"56","4","Social Protection Reform Package","The Proposed reforms will be instrumental in eliminating leakages, improving targeting, increasing the average value of the transfers, lower the risks faced by the poor and vulnerable population, reduce poverty, help reduce income inequality and build social capital.",""],[1,"56","4","Increase Public Spending on Social Protection","Additionally, effort will be made to increase public spending on social protection from 2.02% of GDP in FYI5 to 2.3% of GDP by FY20.",""],[1,"72","4","Ongoing Social Protection Programmes","In social protection, the Government has continued to implement ongoing programmes.",""],[1,"72","4","National Social Security Strategy","Additionally, it has prepared and adopted a new National Social Security Strategy (NSSS) with a view to strengthening the poverty impact of the public spending on social protection and to modernize the social security system to address the social security challenges of a middle income economy.",""],[1,"72","5","National Social Security Strategy Modernization","It seeks to modernize the Bangladesh social security by combining tax-funded safety net programmes with contributory social insurance and employment regulations to protect the workers.",""],[1,"72","5","Social Protection Administrative Reform Package","It also seeks to considerably improve the administrative arrangements for social protection programmes by consolidating complementary programmes, by strengthening staffing and institutions, by instituting a modern MIS system, by gradually replacing food-based transfer payments with cash-based payments using the financial sector based G2P (government to people) system, by introducing a grievance redressing mechanism and by installing proper results-based M&E system.",""],[1,"72","6","National Social Security Strategy Reform Implementation","The associated reforms will be instrumental in eliminating leakages, improving targeting, increasing the average value of the transfers, lower the risks faced by the poor and vulnerable population, reduce poverty, improve social inclusion, help reduce income inequality and build social capital.",""],[1,"80","5","National Social Security Strategy Implementation","the need to implement the newly approved National Social Security Strategy.",""],[1,"103","3","Social Protection System Expansion","First, an effective social protection system will be put in place to help those who may be bypassed or even impoverished by the growth process.",""],[1,"104","3","Social Protection Schemes for the Elderly and Disabled","social protection schemes for the elderly and disabled, protecting labour rights to organize and strive for decent wages and safe working conditions.",""],[1,"110","5","National Social Security Strategy Implementation","Accordingly, the Government has adopted a new and strengthened National Social Security Strategy (NSSS) with a view to lower poverty and vulnerability.",""],[1,"143","4","National Social Security Strategy Implementation","Accordingly, the Government has developed a new broad-based strategy for social protection known as the National Social Security Strategy (NSSS).",""],[1,"160","1","Social Protection Expenditure Programmes","the public sector will continue to play the crucial role of making the growth more inclusive through fiscal and other interventions by making the tax system more equitable and undertaking expenditure programmes aimed at strengthening social protection by improving quality of living for the underprivileged segments of the society.",""],[1,"160","2","National Social Security Strategy Implementation","Phased implementation of the recently adopted National Social Security Strategy of the Government of Bangladesh will provide comprehensive social protection to all poor and vulnerable citizens based on a modern Life Cycle based approach.",""],[1,"162","1","National Social Security Strategy","The government has approved a National Social Security Strategy (NSSS), which outlines the new direction that the government needs to move in the coming years based on a Life Cycle Approach to Social Protection/Security.",""],[1,"162","1","Rights-Based Publicly Funded Old Age Pension Plan","The hallmarks of the NSSS will be the introduction of a rights based publicly funded Old Age Pension Plan for the Poor;",""],[1,"162","1","Maternal and Child Care Support for Poor Pregnant Mothers","all poor pregnant mothers receiving Pre- and Post-Natal Child Care for up to 4 years in order to ensure healthy future generation (free from stunting and mal-nutrition);",""],[1,"162","1","Education Stipend for Poor School-Going Children","all poor school going children receiving education stipend for attending primary and high school;",""],[1,"162","1","Training Facility for Poor and Abandoned Women and Widows","training facility for the poor and abandoned women and widows;",""],[1,"162","1","Financial Support for Poor Elderly Citizens","and financial support for the poor elderly citizens.",""],[1,"668","1","Social Protection Income Transfer and Benefit Programmes","The social protection programmes provide income transfers and other benefits to the poor and vulnerable population with a view to helping them climb out of the poverty trap.",""],[1,"670","1","Workfare Scheme Reform","The Sixth Plan continued with the implementation of the existing programmes while seeking to introduce reforms in a number of areas including reform of the workfare schemes, efforts to reduce leakages through better improvements in design and service delivery and selectively introducing monitoring and evaluation of individual schemes.",""],[1,"670","1","Leakage Reduction in Social Protection Delivery","efforts to reduce leakages through better improvements in design and service delivery and selectively introducing monitoring and evaluation of individual schemes.",""],[1,"670","1","Inter-Ministerial Safety Net Coordination Committee","An inter-ministerial coordination committee was established to better monitor and coordinate the implementation of the safety net system.",""],[1,"670","1","Strengthened Social Protection System Preparation","The Government also charged this committee to oversee the preparation of a new and strengthened social protection system in order to ensure that the poor and vulnerable citizens benefit most from the available budget resources.",""],[1,"670","3","National Social Security Strategy Implementation","The NSSS provides a sound strategy that defines the various life-cycle risks faced by poor and vulnerable population and seeks to mitigate those risks by instituting a well-designed income transfer system that reaches the poorest and most vulnerable segment of the population (the young children, school going children, vulnerable women, the elderly and the physically challenged).",""],[1,"670","3","Social Security System Modernization Reform","It seeks to modernize the Bangladesh social security by combining tax-funded safety net programmes with contributory social insurance and employment regulations to protect the workers.",""],[1,"670","3","Social Protection Administration Strengthening Package","It also seeks to considerably improve the administrative arrangements for social protection programmes by consolidating complementary programmes, by strengthening staffing and institutions, by instituting a modern MIS system, by replacing food-based transfer payments with cash-based payments using the financial sector based G2P (government to people) system, by introducing a grievance redressing mechanism and by installing proper results-based M&E system.",""],[1,"670","4","National Social Security Strategy Implementation","The successful implementation of this NSSS will provide a strong basis for Bangladesh to extend proper social protection to its poor and vulnerable population.",""],[1,"670","4","Social Protection Reform Package","The proposed reforms will be instrumental in eliminating leakages, improving targeting, increasing the average value of the transfers, lower the risks faced by the poor and vulnerable population, reduce poverty, help reduce income inequality and build social capital.",""],[1,"671","2","Inclusive Social Security System Development","Build an inclusive Social Security System (SSS) for all deserving Bangladeshis",""],[1,"671","4","National Social Security System Reform","Reform the National Social Security System by ensuring more efficient and effective use of resources, strengthened delivery systems and progress towards a more inclusive form of Social Security that effectively tackles lifecycle risks, prioritizing the poorest and most vulnerable members of society.",""],[1,"671","13","Priority Transfer Delivery System Strengthening","Strengthening the delivery systems for priority transfers by establishing advanced management information systems and trained professional staff.",""],[1,"671","14","Social Security Programme Awareness Expansion","Expanding the awareness of the social security programmes for the beneficiaries and motivating potential contributors.",""],[1,"671","15","Life Cycle Risk Programme Consolidation","The NSSS will strengthen the transformation towards a lifecycle system by consolidating programmes in a small number of priority schemes.",""],[1,"672","10","Strengthened Workfare Programme for the Unemployed Poor","Implementing a strengthened workfare programme for the unemployed poor.",""],[1,"672","10","Conversion of Food-Based Programmes to Cash-Based Support","The Government will in a longer perspective consider converting food-based programmes into cash-based and consolidating fragmented schemes.",""],[1,"672","10","Consolidation of Fragmented Social Protection Schemes","The Government will in a longer perspective consider converting food-based programmes into cash-based and consolidating fragmented schemes.",""],[1,"673","13","Benefit Rate Setting and Monitoring Guidelines for Reach Programme","The Central Monitoring Committee under the Cabinet Division will develop guidelines for determining the benefit rates, considering the need to adjust to inflation index.","Cabinet Division"],[1,"674","1","Small Scheme Consolidation and Review Process","Under the leadership of the General Economics Division (GED) of the Planning Commission, each sponsoring Ministry/Division of these small schemes will be responsible for determining the value of these schemes and will present a business case if they believe that the programme should continue.","General Economics Division (GED) of the Planning Commission | each sponsoring Ministry/Division"],[1,"675","3","Simplified Institutional Arrangement for NSSS Implementation","A vastly simplified institutional arrangement that allows proper planning, implementation and M&E of the National Social Security Strategy (NSSS).",""],[1,"675","4","Social Security Scheme Staff Professionalization","The professionalization of staff so that there is a group of public servants who are experts in the delivery of Social Security schemes at both national and local levels.",""],[1,"675","6","MIS Upgrading for Transfer Delivery and Coordination","Up-grading the MISs so that they are able to underpin the effective and efficient delivery of transfers and promote cross-governmental coordination and monitoring of performance.",""],[1,"675","8","Grievance Redress System","Establishing an effective grievance redress system so that all citizens have recourse to appeal decisions on selection and can notify the competent authorities about instances of misconduct and failures in the delivery of the promised benefit.",""],[1,"675","9","Thematic Cluster Coordination for Administrative Reforms","The Government will introduce five thematic clusters, a) social allowances, b) food security and disaster assistances, c) social insurance, d) labour/livelihood interventions, and e) human development and social empowerment, for coordination and cooperation of ministries engaged in programme implementation.",""],[1,"675","11","NGO Partnership for Social Security Service Delivery","The Government will continue, and where necessary, deepen the partnership with NGOs in the area of delivering Social Security services based on the NSSS.",""],[1,"676","1","Single Registry Management Information System","In effect, a form of national Single Registry can be established, based on a network of independent but interlinked scheme-specific MISs.",""],[1,"676","2","National Single Registry Establishment","The Government will, therefore, establish a national Single Registry that uses the database from the national identity system and is based on building scheme-specific MISs that communicate with each other and deliver comprehensive information across government.","Statistics and Information Division"],[1,"676","3","Government-to-Person Payment System Reform","A further key reform that will be introduced is an initiative to transform the Government to Person (G2P) payment systems so that they promote financial inclusivity and prevent leakages.","Finance Division of the Ministry of Finance"],[1,"676","5","Nationwide Complaints and Grievance Redress Mechanism","The Ministry of Social Welfare in close consultation with SID will develop a nationwide complaints and grievance redress mechanism.","Ministry of Social Welfare"],[1,"676","6","National Social Security Strategy Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","M&E activities will be divided into three components.","Implementing Ministries/Divisions | IMED | GED | Central Monitoring Committee (CMC)"],[1,"677","1","M&E Findings Dissemination Mechanism","specified mechanisms for disseminating the findings of the M&E.",""],[1,"677","2","NSSS Reform Performance Review and Coordination Mechanism","Performance Review and Coordination of reform implementation will be done by the CMC chaired by the Cabinet Secretary and CMC will report on implementation progress to the Cabinet on a regular basis.",""],[1,"685","9","Safety Net Programme Administration and Monitoring","Approval, administration and monitoring of safety net programmes such as Test Relief (TR), Vulnerable Group Feeding (VGF), Vulnerable Group Development (VGD), Food For Works programme.",""]],"4":[[1,"428","2","Digital Bangladesh Transformation Initiative","The Government of Bangladesh is pledged to transform the country into 'Digital Bangladesh', which implies the broad use of computers, and embodies the modern philosophy of effective use of technology in terms of implementing Government's commitment for development in education, health, job placement and poverty reduction.",""],[1,"428","2","Universal Postal and Telecommunications Access Expansion","the government is committed to ensure this.",""],[1,"428","3","Digital Bangladesh Infrastructure and Pro-People Service Delivery","PTD is engaged with its highest effort to ensure the necessary infrastructure and deliver pro-people services.","Posts and Telecommunications Division (PTD)"],[1,"428","3","Affordable Telecommunication and Postal Services Access Initiative","PTD identified the affordable telecommunication and postal services as citizen's right and working towards the establishment of that right.","Posts and Telecommunications Division (PTD)"],[1,"428","6","National Fiber Optic Network Expansion","BTCL is going to install fiber optic network up to the root level of the country i.e. union level to give last mile solution to its subscribers and install Next Generation Network based telephone system through which triple play i.e. Voice, Video and Data connectivity can be provided to the subscribers using a single line.",""],[1,"429","1","Submarine Cable Capacity Expansion and International Connectivity","BSCCL has become a member of the newly formed SMW-5 Consortium to join in the newly planned Submarine Cable which will provide more capacity i.e 1400 Gbps and redundancy for Bangladesh.",""],[1,"429","1","International Internet Gateway Broadband Service Expansion","Recently BSCCL has started operation as IIG (International Internet Gateway) which will help the people to get broadband Internet with cheaper rate and better quality of service.",""],[1,"429","1","National ILDTS and ICT Policy Implementation for Broadband Network Development","BSCCL is a leading company for implementing National ILDTS and ICT policies to develop modern telecommunication network and to provide high speed Broadband Internet in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"429","5","New Telecom Policy Proposal","With the help of the International Telecommunication Union (ITU), stakeholders and Policy think tanks - PTD will propose a new Telecom Policy to the Government during 7th Plan.",""],[1,"429","6","Telecommunication Network Installation and Development","Installation and development of the telecommunication network",""],[1,"431","1","Bangabandhu Satellite Launch Project","Bangladesh looks forward to a successful launch of the country's first satellite which will ensure improved connectivity with the rest of the world.",""],[1,"431","1","Satellite Orbit Claim and Backup Orbit Arrangement","Bangladesh has already filed its claim to ITU for its own orbit.",""],[1,"617","4","Investment Promotion and Financing Facility for PPP Projects","The Investment Promotion and Financing Facility (IPFF) project is aimed at funding PPP Projects, co- sponsored by government of Bangladesh and the Bank.",""],[1,"617","4","Updated ICT Infrastructure Eligibility for IPFF Financing","Recently, the policy of eligible sector list has been updated to include ICT infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"621","14","Info-Sarkar National ICT Infrastructure Network Phase II","The \"National ICT Infra-Network for Bangladesh Government Phase-II\" or the \"Info-Sarkar\" project is being implemented by the BCC to provide optical fibre connectivity across government offices in all 64 districts and 487 upazilas.",""],[1,"621","16","National Data Centre Operations and Service Provision","National Data Centre is in operation at the BCC.",""],[1,"621","16","IV-Tier Data Centre Establishment","The process of setting up an IV-tier data Centre is underway.",""],[1,"628","3","Tele-Centre and Community E-Centre Expansion","The Plan calls for establishment of tele-Centre/community e-centres with internet facilities across all unions and increasing tele density to 70 per cent by 2015.",""],[1,"628","6","Second Phase of SASEC","The second phase of SASEC is underway.",""],[1,"628","6","Wireless Broadband Network for Digital Bangladesh (4G, LTE)","after the project \"Installation of Wireless Broadband network for Digital Bangladesh (4G, LTE)\" ends.",""],[1,"628","6","SEA-ME-WE-5 Submarine Cable Connectivity","Bangladesh officially joined the submarine cable SEA-ME- WE-5 - its second - and hopes to get connected to it by the first quarter of 2016.",""],[1,"630","5","Bandwidth Connectivity Expansion","Wider usage of the bandwidth should receive immediate priority.",""],[1,"630","5","Fixed ICT Infrastructure Investment","A special challenge will be to expand the bandwidth connectivity through investments in fixed infrastructure as well as lower access cost through tax reductions in ICT taxes.",""],[1,"630","5","ICT Tax Reduction for Lower Access Costs","A special challenge will be to expand the bandwidth connectivity through investments in fixed infrastructure as well as lower access cost through tax reductions in ICT taxes.",""],[1,"632","1","ICT Infrastructure Expansion","Policies will need to focus on expanding ICT infrastructure, improving incentives by lowering taxes on ICT products, greatly expanding the ICT skills base and investing in ICT-related research and development.",""],[1,"641","6","Tier IV Certified Data Centre","Besides, ICT Division is implementing a tier IV certified Data Centre.","ICT Division"],[1,"641","7","Civil Service Connectivity Upgrade","Providing reliable and high-speed connectivity across all tiers within the central and field administration, and within a defined timeframe, is a high priority.",""]],"5":[[1,"647","1","Expansion of Science and Technology Education and Centres of Excellence","The Government will support the growth of centres of excellence in science and technology through grants.",""],[1,"647","2","Research and Development Spending Expansion","The Government will also expand the spending on R&D for the economy that will support the growth of scientific education and research.",""],[1,"647","3","IT Student Enrollment Expansion Plan","Encourage IT student enrolment: a long term plan will be undertaken so that current supply of 5,000 yearly IT graduates can be doubled in next 2-3 years.",""],[1,"647","4","Special Education Loan Policy and Scholarship Programmes for IT Education","special education loan policy and scholarship programmes will be designed to encourage students for IT education enrolment.",""],[1,"647","4","Industry-Academia Engagement in Academic Programmes","More industry involvement will be ensured during academic programmes.",""],[1,"647","5","Vocational Stream Rebranding and Expansion","This will require re-branding of the vocational stream in order to ensure that the curriculum is market-ready, linking graduates to the job market more effectively and making appropriate use of ICTs for training purposes.",""],[1,"647","5","ICT Vocational Institutions Establishment","Several number of ICT vocational institutions will be established that will offer ICT based diploma/certificate courses on the basis of industry requirements subject to periodic review.",""],[1,"647","6","IT Graduate Pipeline Expansion","tertiary educational institutions, industry and the government must work together to rapidly increase the number of qualified IT graduates who are industry-ready every year.",""],[1,"647","6","Company In-House IT Training Scheme","In-house training may need to be established in companies (perhaps funded by the government)",""],[1,"647","6","IT Accreditation and Certification Mechanism","accreditation mechanisms must be in place to ensure high quality, as noted earlier with regard to the establishment of a National Certifying Authority.",""],[1,"653","20","ICT Capacity Building in Public Institutions","Provide funding for ICT capacity building in public institutions",""],[1,"654","4","Establish Virtual University and Multimedia University","Establish Virtual University, Multimedia University",""]],"6":[[1,"7","4","Export-Oriented Manufacturing Development","growth will be driven by diversified export oriented manufacturing sector and enhanced labour productivity with special focus on governance issues to grab the opportunity of enhancing total factor productivity.",""],[1,"11","4","Export-Oriented Manufacturing and Productivity Enhancement","growth will be driven by diversified export oriented manufacturing sector and enhanced labour productivity with special focus on governance issues to grab the opportunity of enhancing total factor productivity.",""],[1,"48","1","Export Base Diversification Strategy","The strong performance in the balance of payments will be preserved by promoting a strong and diversified export base.",""],[1,"52","1","Tariff Regime Restructuring for Export Competitiveness","Bangladesh would have to restructure its tariff regime in order to gradually reduce effective protection levels and consequent anti-export bias.",""],[1,"52","2","Service Sector Modernization and Export Promotion","Modernizing the service sector with emphasis on export of non-factor services;",""],[1,"52","2","Private Investment Incentive Reform for Services","Improve the incentive policies for boosting private investment in services;",""],[1,"52","2","Public Investment in Service Sector Infrastructure","Increasing public investment in key service sector infrastructure;",""],[1,"52","3","Non-Factor Service Export Promotion Strategy","The emphasis on non-factor service exports such as ICT, aviation, shipping and tourism is a critical element of the service sector development strategy for the 7th Plan.",""],[1,"82","13","Industrialization and Trade Policy Reform","promoting a favourable industrialization and trade policy regime",""],[1,"98","5","Trade Liberalization and Foreign Trade Regime Reform","Bangladesh made significant progress in reforming the foreign trade regime and reducing protection since the early 1990s.",""],[1,"98","5","Further Trade Reform to Broaden the Export Base","Further trade reforms are essential to eliminate the bias against an export-led growth strategy.",""],[1,"282","18","Inspection and Certification of Locally Made Boilers","Inspection & Certification of Local Made Boilers.",""],[1,"282","21","Export Competitiveness and Diversification Measures","On the supply side, much of the policy attention will have to focus on production incentives, quality and cost competitiveness through improvement of infrastructure and trade logistics, and diversification of our export basket.",""],[1,"283","2","Trade Reform","Trade reform which stagnated over the past few years needs to be put back on track.",""],[1,"283","6","Special Products Branding Initiative","Branding of Special Products.",""],[1,"283","7","Industrial Capacity Utilization Support","Ensuring that there is full utilization of current production capacity in the industrial sector.",""],[1,"283","7","SME Infrastructure and Special Facilities Support","Provide special facilities as well as infrastructural support to Cottage and Small and Medium enterprises (SME) located in- different parts of the country.",""],[1,"283","7","Agro-Processing and Hygienic Marketing Support","Provide financial, technical, technological and infrastructural facilities in order to market agro-based goods hygienically by processing in frozen, pasteurized, canned or dry form so that goods produced in the country are preserved and marketed in compliance with modern standards in order to ensure that they can be made available in the local market or exported throughout the year.",""],[1,"283","8","Infrastructure Development and Private Investment Promotion","Give preference to infrastructural development including ports, power, transport and communications, and human resources development.",""],[1,"283","9","Backward Linkage Industry Support Programme","Assisting backward linkage industries on a priority basis.",""],[1,"283","9","Value-Added Linkage and Subcontracting Industry Support","Provide necessary assistance to value added linkage industries and subcontracting industries so that they are developed.",""],[1,"283","10","Priority Support for Readymade Garment and Textile Industries","Treating the readymade garment and textile industries as priority sectors in view of their special contributions to the country's export trade, and strengthening other industry related policies such as the Textiles policy, Jute policy, and Silk policy as supplementary to the Industrial Policy.",""],[1,"284","1","Coordinated Management Information Service for Bangladesh Missions Abroad","Establish coordinated and extensive Management Information service (MIS) comprising different public and private agencies under the. Ministry of industries (various chambers of commerce and industries) and arrange for information received from MIS to be supplied to administrative divisions and districts levels.","Ministry of industries"],[1,"284","2","Investment Policy Non-Discrimination Reform","Remove policy discrimination, if any, between domestic and foreign investments, and enhance regional and sub-regional cooperation.",""],[1,"284","2","WTO-Aligned Industrial Development Measures","Take necessary steps to bring about the country's industrial development in line with different agreements with the World Trade Organization (WTO).",""],[1,"284","3","Capital Market Strengthening and Industrial Working Capital Support","Provide all-out assistance to create a strong capital market so that investments in the industrial sector are increased.",""],[1,"284","3","Post-Establishment Industrial Working Capital Facility","Ensuring the availability of the working capital from financial institutions after the establishment of an industry so that working capital can be obtained in time.",""],[1,"284","4","Industrial Park and Economic Zone Development","Take initiatives to set up industrial parks with a view to establishing economically viable industries in these industrial sub- sectors.",""],[1,"284","4","Compact Industrial Area Support Facilities","Provide further structural and other facilities to establish and develop compact industrial areas.",""],[1,"284","4","Economic Zone Development in High-Potential Areas","Develop planned industrial areas by establishing Economic Zones in areas with vast economic potentials, and utilizing local resources.",""],[1,"284","7","Foreign Direct Investment Promotion for Technology Transfer","Promoting foreign direct investments in order to bring about technology transfer, efficiency and management development and enhance marketing skills.",""],[1,"284","8","Long-Term Industrial Credit Fund","Creating a long-term credit fund to generate industrial production capacity",""],[1,"284","8","Creative Industries Venture Capital Fund","also a venture capital fund to support in the commercial production and marketing of creative industries",""],[1,"284","8","Capital Market Support for Industrial Entrepreneurs","Also ensuring the availability of assistance of the capital market so that industrial entrepreneurs can overcome the lack of capital and mobilize the necessary capital from the capital market in order to establish or administer industrial enterprises",""],[1,"305","7","Priority Market Marketing Support","Devise and ensure the right level of marketing support in the priority markets;",""]],"7":[[1,"317","7","Climate Change Adaptation Research Promotion","Encourage research on adaptation to climate change, and proper use of genetically modified technology in agriculture.",""],[1,"318","9","Agricultural Technology Development and Adoption","The research programmes of the National Agricultural Research System (NARS) organizations have been striving to develop technologies of crops that are both economically viable as well as ecologically sound.",""],[1,"318","9","Agro-Ecological Technology Choice Development","This calls for developing technology choices according to agro-ecological conditions and market demand, soil health management, enhancement of water conservation to allow ground water recharge, quality and affordability of inputs, credit and insurance.",""],[1,"323","2","Agricultural Research Investment and Scientist Incentive Package","Research Investment needs to increase to a considerable level to facilitate lab, infrastructure, higher studies and training opportunities.",""],[1,"325","3","Climate-Resilient Agricultural Production and Diversification Strategy","The development vision for agriculture under the 7th Five Year Plan is to ensure food and nutritional security, enhancement of sustainable intensification and diversification of climate resilient agricultural production with increased commercialization, and livelihood improvement through technological innovations and use, strengthening of research and extension system, developing supply chain extension, value addition of agricultural products, and linking farming community with markets, both local and global.",""],[1,"325","8","Science-Led Climate-Resilient Agricultural Technology Promotion","Promote science-led agriculture technology systems and encourage research and adoption of modern agricultural practices for development of drought, submergence and saline prone agriculture considering water and time economy, adaptation to climate change, proper use of genetically modified technology in agriculture, and promote adoption of modern agricultural practices in dry land, wetland, hills and coastal areas including use of environment friendly green",""],[1,"326","1","Climate-Smart and Stress-Tolerant Agricultural Technologies","technologies (e.g. IPM, INM, AWD, etc.) and climate-smart/resilient technologies; introduce salinity, submergence and other stress tolerant varieties specially in the Southern regions;",""],[1,"327","4","Science and Technology for Higher Food Production","crop production output will be increased by growing more crops per year through expansion of water management practices, improve pest control and use of short duration variety.",""],[1,"327","4","Genetic Improvement and Crop Protection Research","Greater stability and dependability in food production will be achieved through genetic improvement, crop management, post-harvest handling and through crop protection.",""],[1,"327","4","Development of Crops for Nutrient-Poor Soils","Plants with superior characteristics will be developed so that they will be productive on nutrient poor soil.",""],[1,"327","4","Basic Biological Productivity Research Programme","Research programme on the basic biological processes that control productivity will be given emphasis.",""],[1,"328","2","Demand-Led Agricultural Research and Technology Development","The National Agricultural Research System (NARS) institutes generate the demand-led agricultural technologies (varieties and management practices) and information.",""],[1,"328","2","Climate-Resilient Crop Variety Development","It will also address climate change effects by breeding and introducing saline and drought tolerant, short duration varieties, introduction of high value commodities and low-cost, high-impact post-harvest technologies as well as research on packaging, harvesting, maturity index, food processing and market intelligence.",""],[1,"328","2","Agricultural Research on IPM, Water Management, Biotechnology, and Biosecurity","Research on IPM, on-farm water management, food technology, biotechnology, bio-security and socio economic condition will have special emphasis along with other contemporary issues.",""],[1,"328","2","Crop Yield and Quality Improvement Programme","Research thrust would include, but not limited to, quality seeds, yield and quality improvement programme of rice, wheat, maize, pulses, jute, seaweeds and aquatic plants, oilseeds vegetables, fruits, cotton, sugar cane and stress tolerant and climate change resilient variety development; improved management practices for field crops, vegetables, fruits, flowers with thrust on marginal and unfavourable eco-system; post-harvest management, processing and value addition of agricultural commodities; pest and disease management for crop, natural resource management (NRM): land, water and bio-diversity; energy management in agriculture; equipment development for farm mechanization; socio-economic, policy and extension research, etc.",""],[1,"328","2","Research on Climate-Resilient Sugar Crops","Considering climate change and other issues like salinity, research emphasis will also be on sugar crops including sugarcane, sugar beet, date palm, palmyra, palm, jute, cotton, tea, etc.",""],[1,"328","3","Pilot Farming System Research Programme","Farming system research will be undertaken on a pilot basis to extrapolate advanced technology and identify adoption constraints and their solution and establish strong linkages among research-extension and farmers communities.",""],[1,"328","4","Agricultural Research and Innovation Programme","Research thrust on yield and quality improvement of rice, wheat, maize, pulses, oilseeds, tuber crops, vegetables, fruits, cotton, jute, seaweeds, aquatic plants, spices and stress tolerant, climate change resilient variety development and improved management practices; post-harvest management, processing and value addition of agricultural commodities; pest and disease management for crop; natural resource management (NRM); biotechnology & bio-diversity; farm mechanization etc .;",""],[1,"328","6","Hybrid and Biotech/Transgenic Crop Development and Research Capacity Strengthening","Development of hybrid and biotech/transgenic crop through strengthened capacity on this sectors and initiate basic research to support applied and adaptive research;",""],[1,"329","2","Climate-Smart Agriculture Research and Climate-Resilient Crop Variety Development","Research on climate SMART agriculture, breeding and introduction of climate resilient varieties for saline and drought tolerant, heat & cold tolerant, submergence etc .;",""],[1,"333","3","Expansion of Salinity-Tolerant and Stress-Tolerant Rice Varieties","Different salinity tolerant Boro and other stress tolerant varieties of rice should be extended;",""],[1,"333","6","High-Value Crop Diversification and Cotton Expansion","Diversification to high value crops, i.e. cotton crops in Barind area, Hilly areas, southern coastal region and char land areas with appropriate extension strategy as cotton varieties are highly drought and salt tolerant.",""],[1,"333","11","Environmentally Sound Farming Practices Promotion","Development and promotion of environmentally sound farming practices;",""],[1,"334","3","Advance Planning for Agricultural Expansion in Newly Accreted Coastal Land and Marine Islands","Advance planning should be adopted to utilize the land for agriculture expansion.",""],[1,"334","4","Marine and Coastal Resource Utilization Research","Research work will be initiated to utilize marine and coastal resources.",""],[1,"334","5","Research-Extension Linkage and Salt-Tolerant Crop Development","Strengthening research and establishment of research-extensions linkage for development and disseminating salt tolerant varieties and for introduction of new profitable cropping patterns in the newly accreted coastal land and marine islands.",""],[1,"334","8","Seaweed Cultivation Research and Site Survey Programme","The technology for the cultivation of different commercially important seed stocks and their improvements will have to be developed through research.",""],[1,"334","9","Crop Disease Management and Integrated Disease Control","Diseases control measures will be addressed considering the host- environment-pathogen-triangle.",""],[1,"335","2","Systematic Bio-Control Research and Development for Pest Management","Therefore, research and development activities in these areas have to be planned and implemented systematically for the interest of crop protection, human health and safe environment.",""],[1,"335","4","Climate-Smart Agricultural Weather Forecasting System","Therefore, research work need to be conducted to generate technology based timely, accurate and well-organized weather forecasting system in the context of climate change and crop production.",""],[1,"335","4","Climate-Resilient Crop Variety Research","In addition to that research for producing crop varieties in considering climatic variability, crop-cultural practices to minimize the effects of mid-seasonal hazardous weather phenomena, medium range weather forecasts with a validity period that enables farmers to organize and carry out appropriate operations will be tried out.",""],[1,"335","4","Localized Agricultural Weather Information Services","The rapid advances in Information Technology and its spread to rural areas will be used as a tool for reducing impact of such mid- seasonal weather related hazards.",""],[1,"335","4","Pre-Seasonal Forecasting and Hazard Response Measures","Pre-seasonal forecasts with reasonable validity period and field-measures to counter the effects of forecasted hazardous weather, pests, diseases etc. will be a priority of the Ministry of Agriculture.","Ministry of Agriculture"],[1,"464","9","Climate-Smart Food Systems Development","Develop 'climate-smart food systems', ensuring that climate threats to other elements of food systems beyond agriculture, such as storage, distribution and access are taken into consideration.",""],[1,"475","6","Climate-Resilient Crop Variety Development","Climate smart agricultural practices and technologies focusing on climate resilient crop varieties will also be developed to ensure food security.",""],[1,"475","6","Climate-Resilient Cropping Systems Development","Climate change resilient cropping systems will also be developed to ensure food security.",""],[1,"475","6","Food Storage, Distribution, and Access Improvement","Other aspects of food systems, such as storage, distribution, and access will be ensured.",""],[1,"477","4","Academic Research on Climate-Resilient Crop Varieties","Government will take initiative to promote more academic research into this issue.",""]],"8":[[1,"619","4","ICT Literacy Assessment in Public Service Entrance Exams","ICT literacy evaluation as part of Public Service entrance exams has been introduced, but it needs to be extended in terms of depth of questions regarding the usage of ICTs for good governance in the delivery of public provisions.",""],[1,"620","1","E-Governance and Government Business Process Re-engineering","e-governance will manage the way that citizens deal with the government and with each other, allow citizens to communicate with government, participate in government policy making and planning, and to communicate with each other.",""],[1,"620","4","E-Administration and National Portal Expansion","All public information is being made accessible in Bangla through electronic means and also mobile phones.",""],[1,"620","5","National Portal Content Management and E-Services Information System","This Portal embeds key information pertaining to agriculture, education, health, law and human rights, human resource development, social security, environment and disaster management, tourism and history, natural and archaeological sites, educational institutions, business organizations, public representatives and eminent persons, freedom fighters list, government circular/gazette, procedures for applying and receiving public services, government forms, citizen charter, list of officers and personnel, digital guard files, e- directory, district-level and other e-services, development projects' activities and other information of public interest.","Cabinet Division"],[1,"620","6","District e-Service Centres","The government established District e-Service Centres (DESCs) across all 64 districts in 2011 to start the work on online-data sharing and decision making system.",""],[1,"620","6","National e-Service System Development","The development of National e-Service System (NESS) is also underway (see Box 12.2).",""],[1,"621","1","National E-Governance Service System (NESS) Rollout","Work is in progress across 16,000 government offices to launch the NESS by 2015.",""],[1,"621","3","Multi-Channel Application Submission Service","Provide service for any kind of application submission through mobile, internet, UDC, upazila Centre, etc.",""],[1,"621","4","Application Tracking Inquiry Service","Offer inquiry service to enable tracking progress of applications.",""],[1,"621","7","Provider-Recipient Social Networking for Service Delivery Feedback","Empower citizens to discuss service delivery issues, provide suggestions and recommendations, and share ideas through a provider-recipient social networking.",""],[1,"621","9","e-Filing for File and Record Management","Initiate e-Filing to simplify the process of file processing (i.e. file put up, file sending, file seeing) and it is to be noted that Secretariat Instructions 2008 has been amended to incorporate use of ICTs in file and record management;",""],[1,"621","10","File and Decision Management Tracking System","Enable tracking of any information at any time through file management and decision management;",""],[1,"621","11","Automated Work Progress Register","Maintain auto register so that each day's work/progress is entered automatically;",""],[1,"621","12","Single Government Service Monitoring Dashboard","Enable monitoring of all service providing government organizations from one single dashboard to ensure accountability and transparency;",""],[1,"621","13","Automated Scheduled E-Communication Alerts","Allow automatic scheduled e-communication such as SMS, email or any other kind of alert for meetings, events, etc.",""],[1,"621","15","Government Video Conferencing System Expansion","Video conferencing system has been introduced between PMO, Cabinet Division, Divisional Commissioners' offices and DC offices to speed up field administration activities.","PMO | Cabinet Division"],[1,"621","15","Video Conference System Launch in District Commissioner and Divisional Offices","The Cabinet Division has undertaken a Programme for launching video conference system in 64 DC offices and 7 Divisional Commissioners' offices.","Cabinet Division"],[1,"621","15","Info-Sarkar Video Conferencing Infrastructure Project","The Info-Sarkar project is to set up 800 video conferencing systems at different offices including the ministry, department, and upazila office and training centres.",""],[1,"621","17","Public Sector E-Learning Initiative","The Bangladesh Public Administration and Training Centre (BPATC), Bangladesh Civil Service Administration Academy (BCSAA) and Bangladesh Institute of Management (BIM) are pioneering an initiative to introduce e-learning in public sector training organizations.",""],[1,"623","4","E-Citizen Services Public Service Delivery Mechanism","The public service delivery mechanism of Bangladesh is in the midst of reinventing itself to become more transparent, accountable and responsive to citizens' needs.",""],[1,"623","5","Government Services and Forms Portal Integration","All ministries, divisions, directorates and corporations are being linked with \"Sebakunja\" - about 400 services of 36 Directorates/Offices have been amassed in a \"Single Access Point.\"","Cabinet Division"],[1,"640","3","Maintenance and Mobile Access of RTI-Based Government Portals","The RTI-based portals set up in all 25,000 offices of the government offices will be maintained with up-to-date information and made accessible through mobile phones and service access points.",""],[1,"640","3","Service Process Simplification Initiative","The next logical step for the concerned government agencies is to simplify service delivery using the methodology called Service Process Simplification (SPS), devised by the a2i Programme to reduce transaction costs for citizens.",""],[1,"640","3","Whole-of-Government Electronic Service Delivery Dashboards","A whole-of-government approach will be adopted to set up electronic dashboards with administrative alerts across all ministries, directorates, districts, upazilas and union parishads, in order to monitor the speed and quality of service delivery.",""],[1,"640","4","Strengthening and Expansion of Service Access Points","These service access points must be nurtured and made financially sustainable by strengthening the entrepreneurship-based model.",""],[1,"640","4","Integration of Additional Government and Non-Government Service Access Points","The number of service access points may also be increased by incorporating other government agencies such as the post offices and community clinics, and non-government agency offices.",""],[1,"640","4","Mobile Phone Delivery of Government Services","Within the duration of the Seventh Plan, it is projected that over half of critical government services may be made available over mobile phones.",""],[1,"640","6","E-Filing System in DC Offices","The e-Filing system in operation in the DC offices since 2012 has proven that unprecedented administrative efficiency gain is possible by leveraging ICTs.",""],[1,"641","1","Government e-Filing and ERP Integration","Additional systems such as human resources, payroll, leave, study tour, and training management, budgeting and expense management, inventory management and other ERP and decision support modules should be integrated with e-Filing to broaden and deepen administrative efficiency in government organizations.",""],[1,"641","2","Formalization of Digital Citizen Engagement Platforms","lessons from such a virtual platform needs to be further formalized within the government structure to make it more responsive to social injustices.",""],[1,"641","3","Civil Service ICT Change Management Initiative","The introduction and beneficial use of ICT in reforming civil service and creating better service delivery is essentially a change management process.",""],[1,"641","5","Paperless Civil Service Strategy","It is important to develop a strategy towards a 'less paper' environment for the civil service.",""],[1,"642","1","Mandatory ICT Proficiency for Government Officers","Mandatory ICT proficiency for all government officers will be ensured according to ICT Policy 2009.",""]],"9":[[1,"187","5","GED Institutional Capacity Strengthening and Staff Stability Measures","the Government recognizes that to strengthen GED capacity undertaking the aforementioned responsibilities, specific institutional rearrangements will be needed.",""],[1,"208","2","Institutional Strengthening for Governance and Public Administration","the 7th Pan takes a relatively more focused approach to develop strong institutions in order to substantially improve performance in strategic areas that are central for achievement of overall development goals.",""],[1,"208","2","Public Administration Capacity Improvement","These critical areas for intervention include: (a) public administration capacity;",""],[1,"208","2","Implementation of Remaining Sixth Plan Governance Strategies","the 7th Plan also prioritizes the implementation of strategies and policies that were charted out in the 6th Plan and are still relevant.",""],[1,"211","1","Public Service Act Enactment","A draft of the Public Service Act (which is now called Government Employee Act) has been formulated and awaits enactment into law by Parliament.",""],[1,"211","2","Revision of Conduct Rules","The revision of the conduct rules is under progress.",""],[1,"211","2","Phased Revision of Public Sector Pay Scales","The proposed revision in pay scales is being implemented in phases, starting with the Budget of FY2016.",""],[1,"214","5","Civil Service Reform Programme","Progress is ongoing in reforming civil service in a number of areas.",""],[1,"215","1","Systematic and Periodic Civil Service Training","promotion and to upgrade skills through more systematic and periodic training.",""],[1,"215","1","Specialized Civil Service Attraction and Retention Measures","Special efforts are needed to attract and retain civil servants in a number of specialized areas such as economic management, tax planning, financial management, project management and results-based monitoring and evaluation.",""],[1,"215","3","Annual Performance Agreement System","Under the system an Annual Performance Agreement is signed between the Secretary of the concerned Ministry/Division and the Cabinet Secretary.",""],[1,"215","3","National Committee on Government Performance","A National Committee on Government Performance (NCGP) has been constituted headed by the Cabinet Secretary to provide the overall guidance for the implementation of GPMS.",""],[1,"216","4","Institutional Improvement Measures for Governance Reform","the Seventh Plan harnesses a more focused approach to ensure effective measures are taken to facilitate governance improvements through institutional improvements in some key areas where governance weaknesses were observed.",""],[1,"216","5","Institutional Governance Improvement Measures","the Seventh Plan takes a more focused approach to ensure effective measures are taken to facilitate governance improvements through institutional improvements in some key areas where strong governance weaknesses were observed between 2009 and 2014.",""],[1,"219","6","Government Administrative Capacity Strengthening","Hence, improving Government's administrative capacity is fundamental for enhancing Government's effectiveness, and under the Seventh Plan the following activities will be implemented.",""],[1,"219","7","Government Servants Act Reform","The Government Servants Act is a critical first step for achieving Vision 2021 as outlined in the Perspective Plan, providing the foundation for removing excessive partisan influence in the appointment of civil servants.",""],[1,"219","10","On-the-Job and Classroom Training Linkage for Career Advancement","Develop greater opportunities for on-the-job training and classroom-based training with linkage between training and criteria for career advancement.",""],[1,"219","11","Civil Service Terms of Reference Development","Developing a clear terms of reference for civil servants, thus promoting accountability.",""],[1,"219","12","Civil Service Performance Evaluation Reform","Reforming civil servants' performance evaluation through emphasis on establishing clearer annual work objectives and performance on these objectives and greater differentiation of annual evaluations and having promotion depend more directly on performance evaluations.",""],[1,"219","13","Permanent Salary Commission","Establishing Permanent Salary Commission to recommend annual increment in the salary of the government servant consistent with the increased prices of commodities, specifically inflation rate and conforming the affairs related to the administrative reforms.",""],[1,"220","1","Citizen's Charter Institutionalization","Institutionalizing the citizen's charter to provide regular feedback on public services.",""],[1,"220","2","Increase Female Representation in Senior Public Sector Posts","The Government will increase the share of female officers (Grade-9 and above) in the public sector to 25 percent by 2020.",""],[1,"220","3","Civil Service Promotion and Posting Policy","Promotion and posting of the government servant will be decided by the clear policy to be mad under the act.",""],[1,"220","5","Performance-Based Recruitment and Promotion System","Performance based recruitment and promotion system should be introduced.",""],[1,"220","6","Public Service Commission Reform","Government will establish transparent recruitment process for appointees, have financial autonomy in terms of its budget, and make it more transparent to the public in its activities.",""],[1,"220","7","Citizen Feedback and Public Grievance Redress Mechanisms","The Government will establish mechanisms for citizen feedback regarding Government performance.",""],[1,"220","8","Annual Performance Agreement Institutionalization","Under the 7th Plan's time interval, the Govt. will undertake all necessary actions to make APA an effective institutional arrangement for enhancing the state of accountability across public sector organizations and government employees.",""],[1,"220","9","Strengthening the Central Grievance Redress System","The Government of Bangladesh has already established a separate branch within the Cabinet Division to facilitate a central Grievance Redress System (GRS).","Cabinet Division"],[1,"235","8","Public Administration Capacity-Building Programmes","In recognition of the long-term nature of strengthening public administration, additional development programmes will be adopted to move forward with the public capacity building effort.",""],[1,"649","5","Governance Structure Reform and Public Service Delivery Upgrade","the modern society that the Digital Bangladesh vision aspires also requires fundamental reforms in governance structure which would significantly upgrade public service delivery systems and make it responsive to citizens' needs for information and services.",""],[1,"649","5","Review of Incentive Systems and Regulatory Frameworks","Hence, it is needed to review the incentive systems and regulatory frameworks such as 'Government Servants Act' and promulgate/update related laws etc. to remove risks and uncertainties.",""]],"10":[[1,"568","5","Scale-Up of Technologies and Interventions Across Public Services","The Government plans to scale up technologies and interventions across public services and encourage the same in the private sector.",""],[1,"571","6","Health Workforce Expansion and Vacancy Filling","the government has taken steps to fill up the vacant positions and create new ones",""],[1,"572","2","Health Human Resources Augmentation and Planning","Augmentation of HR in health service delivery is a continuous effort being made by the MOHFW.","MOHFW"],[1,"572","3","Health Workforce Information System Strengthening","They are currently piloting data collection processes through providing training and supplies at community clinic and household levels.","DGHS | DGFP"],[1,"572","3","Health Management Information System Strengthening and Reorganization","Both MISs would need to be strengthened and reorganized personnel structure to support the investment already made.","DGHS | DGFP"],[1,"573","1","National Health Care Technology Management Policy","The Government will address these issues and work to develop a national policy on management of health care technology.",""],[1,"573","12","Health Workforce Education and Training Capacity Enhancement","To enhance national capacity for pre-service education (SBA/nursing, Paramedics, midwifery), provide in-service training and better management of Human Resources.",""],[1,"577","6","National Health Workforce Strategy","Develop a national health workforce strategy",""],[1,"577","6","Health Human Resources Action Plan","Implement an HR action plan to ensure adequate number of personnel with appropriate skill mix, deployment with terms and conditions, retention, career progression, job satisfaction, etc.",""],[1,"577","7","M&E Action Plan Implementation","Implement the M&E Action Plan",""],[1,"577","7","Health Information System Strengthening","Further improve health information systems through strengthened collaboration of DGHS and DGFP by scaling up RHIS initiative",""],[1,"577","7","Timely Reporting from Reporting Units","Ensure timely reporting from all reporting units",""],[1,"577","9","ICT-Enabled Service Delivery and Management Efficiency Initiative","Explore full potential of ICT to facilitate service delivery, education, information gathering and management efficiency",""],[1,"577","9","Health Manager Capacity Building for Data Analysis and Planning","Build capacity of health managers and at district and sub-district levels, particularly on data analysis, heath planning and monitoring.",""]],"11":[[1,"50","7","Energy Mix Diversification for Energy Security","Ensure energy mix for energy security",""],[1,"53","3","Infrastructure Development Priority Initiative","Accelerating GDP growth during the 7th FYP depends on assuaging the infrastructure constraint, especially power and energy, by focusing priority attention to infrastructure development.",""],[1,"53","4","Power Generation Capacity Expansion","The total power generation capacity in 2015 stands around 14000 MW which will be increased to 23000 MW by 2020 at the end of the ill Plan, the increase is estimated to be shared at 60:40 ratio between public and private sector.",""],[1,"53","4","Transmission and Distribution Network Expansion","The target is to provide electricity to almost all the population with special emphasis on reliable power to productive sectors which will require major expansion and up gradation of transmission and distribution networks.",""],[1,"53","4","Coal-Based Power Plant Development","Most of the new generation would come from coal based power plants with state of the art technology that minimizes impact on environment and ensures high efficiency.",""],[1,"53","4","Renewable Energy Expansion","Renewable energy is expected to provide 5-10% of total generation.",""],[1,"53","4","Regional Power Connectivity Expansion","Regional connectivity will be expanded and strengthened.",""],[1,"75","3","Power Sector Fuel Diversification and Least-Cost Expansion Programme","the Seventh Plan will have to put considerable emphasis on coal, possibility of new gas exploration, nuclear power and imports from India, Nepal and Bhutan.",""],[1,"116","1","Power Sector Joint Ventures and Electricity Imports","Joint venture initiatives in the power sector along with import of electricity from India will also help contain public sector domestic investment requirement.",""],[1,"116","2","Transport and Energy Infrastructure Expansion through ADPs","most emphasis will be given to Transport and energy under the 7th Plan through ADPs.",""],[1,"116","2","Power Generation Expansion under the Power Sector Master Plan","The planned massive expansion in electricity generation under the Power Sector Master Plan to meet the rapidly growing power sector needs of a growing economy will require large investments in power generation alone.",""],[1,"116","6","Government Investment in Power Generation Capacity Expansion","direct government investment in the sector will be sizable over the Plan period.",""],[1,"116","6","Private Sector Power Purchase Agreement Investment","private sector will continue to invest in power generation through Power Purchase Agreements with the government or Power Development Board (PDB),",""],[1,"116","6","Large-Scale Coal Power Plant Development","Under the 7th Plan larger projects, including several large coal-based power plants will come into effect with a view to expand generation capacity to 23,000 MW by FY20.",""],[1,"129","9","Power Sector Master Plan Implementation","implementation of the Power Sector Master Plan to ensure sustainable power supply at competitive prices",""],[1,"155","6","Electricity Supply Expansion in Lagging Districts","Supply of electricity would be increased in the lagging districts in priority basis since development of manufacturing sector demands access to electricity supply.",""],[1,"160","2","Power Sector Projects Acceleration","In addition major initiatives will be taken to broaden and accelerate the implementation of other major highways and bridges, power sector projects, and providing access to serviced land to foreign and domestic investors in the context of the Special Economic Zones (SEZ) initiative.",""],[1,"283","3","Power Crisis Response Measures","innovative ways must be found to address the power crisis.",""],[1,"283","3","Electricity Demand Management","Among the solutions include better demand management,",""],[1,"283","3","Cross-Border Energy Trade Expansion","more aggressive efforts for energy trade with neighbours,",""],[1,"283","3","Electricity Production and Distribution Efficiency Improvement","ensuring the efficiency of electricity production and distribution,",""],[1,"283","3","Electricity Industry Financial Viability Reform","and ensuring the financial viability of the electricity industry.",""],[1,"283","4","Long-Term Sound Energy Policy for Industrial Electricity Supply","A sound energy policy for the long-term will have to ensure adequate electricity to industry based on the optimal balance of fuel sourcing - gas, coal, fuel oil, and hydro - including the exploitation of power trade opportunities across borders.",""]],"12":[[1,"143","2","Equitable Access to Basic Education and Health Services","Accordingly, the Seventh Plan will pay special attention to further closing the gap between the rich and the poor in accessing these basic services with special focus on the bottom 20 percent where the gap is the highest.",""],[1,"145","14","Increase Public Spending on Education and Health","The top most policy priority is to raise the share of public spending on education and health to at least 3.0 and 1.2 percent of GDP respectively.",""],[1,"145","14","Education and Health Service Delivery Reform","This will also require major improvements in the delivery of public education and health services through education policies, governance and institutional reforms.",""],[1,"160","2","Health and Education Budget Increase","Budgetary allocations to the priority social sector programmes in the health and education sectors will be increased to create better human capital through universal general education, skill development programmes, and greater access to improved public healthcare systems.",""],[1,"160","2","Universal General Education and Skills Development Programme","Budgetary allocations to the priority social sector programmes in the health and education sectors will be increased to create better human capital through universal general education, skill development programmes, and greater access to improved public healthcare systems.",""],[1,"160","2","Improved Public Healthcare Access Initiative","Budgetary allocations to the priority social sector programmes in the health and education sectors will be increased to create better human capital through universal general education, skill development programmes, and greater access to improved public healthcare systems.",""],[1,"162","3","Increase Education, Health Care, and Social Welfare Spending","Such an increase in the size of the budget would allow for increasing the education budget by 0.8 percentage points to 3.0% of GDP, increase the public spending on health care by at least 0.4 percentage points to 1.2% of GDP, and spending on social welfare by 0.3 percentage points to 2.3% of GDP.",""],[1,"715","4","Quality and Gender-Sensitive Primary and Secondary Education Improvement","Quality and gender sensitivity of primary and secondary education would be ensured for girls and boys through teachers' education and training, curriculum improvement (including subjects to promote equality and equity by gender, ethnicity, class, physical ability etc.), and introduction of extra-curriculum activities to build confidence and to overcome the limitations in learning outcomes.",""],[1,"715","4","Poverty-Focused Stipends and Free Education Support","Transition from primary and completion of secondary education for both boys and girls would be ensured with continued support from poverty focused stipend, free education, books, and so on.",""],[1,"715","4","Girls' Tertiary and Technical Education Expansion","Girls' participation at the tertiary level and technical education would be increased through increased community motivation to change social norms on girls' education, providing scholarships, special quota provisions, infrastructure including accommodation, transport, hygienic sanitation for girls and such support.",""],[1,"715","4","Women Teachers and Safe School Environment Initiative","Other actions would include increasing the percentage of women teachers and teachers' training on inclusive education and making the education environment safe for girls.",""],[1,"716","5","Girls' Participation in Sports and Cultural Activities","Women's participation in sports and cultural activities would be ensured from school to build self-confidence amongst girls.",""],[1,"716","5","Extracurricular Activities Support in Educational Institutions","Extra-curriculum activities would be encouraged and supported in educational institutions and outside.",""]],"13":[[1,"625","5","Community Radio Early Warning and IVR Disaster Alert Services","Today, fourteen community radio stations are proactively providing interactive voice response (IVR) related services and early disaster warnings to more than 4.6 million listeners of 67 upazilas under 13 districts.",""],[1,"625","5","Digital Early Warning Dissemination for Climate-Vulnerable Areas","Using websites and mobile phones, early warnings are being sent out across the country's climate vulnerable areas, prone to cyclones, floods and other natural disasters.",""],[1,"644","5","Geostationary Satellite Weather Monitoring Initiative","initiative to install geostationary satellite would be undertaken to ensure close and constant monitoring of weather patterns to forecast climatic events.",""],[1,"644","5","Satellite Data Analysis Capacity Strengthening","A related priority is to improve internal capacity to analyse satellite data.",""],[1,"644","5","Automated Weather Station Investment","The Government will invest in 'automated weather station', now available at much lower cost than in the past, that measures various weather parameters like river water level, rainfall, precipitation, temperature, humidity, wind speed and direction etc.",""],[1,"644","6","Free Mobile-Based Early Warning Service","Given its nature, the Government will amend related rules so that all cell phone carriers make it a free service for their customers.",""],[1,"644","6","Location-Based Mobile Warning Network Upgrade","The mobile communication network will be upgraded to leverage 'location based service', which will allow a message to reach to all phones of a particular geographic location.",""],[1,"644","7","Satellite-Based Hazard Warning and First Responder Communication System","GPS technology can be incorporated into the radio receiver set, along with the unique code assigned to every receiver, which will allow hazard warnings to be issued in text and audio formats to sets that are within a vulnerable area, and also to radio sets with specific assigned codes.",""],[1,"644","7","Digital Communication Support for First Responders and Disaster Managers","Internet and email, particularly using handheld devices, will be promoted for the first responders, coordinating bodies or disaster managers.",""],[1,"645","2","Community Radio for Disaster Warning and Recovery","The established community radios can play a critical role in broadcasting disaster warning to not only among the community, but their signal can also reach out to the fishermen operating in the open water so that they can get back to safety in time.",""]],"14":[[1,"415","5","Transport Safety Audit Programme","Improving on transport safety standards to reduce incidence of accidents by implementing safety audit periodically.",""],[1,"415","10","Strict Axle Load Control Policy","Strict axle load control policy to reduce road damages caused by overloading.",""],[1,"416","12","Road Transport Quality and Safety Improvement","For the 7th FY plan, in addition to the physical targets for expansion of the road network, a major objective is to have well-maintained, cost effective, durable and safer quality road network by:",""],[1,"416","13","Road Safety Improvement Initiative","Improve road safety situation in the country by achieving 50 per cent reduction in road traffic accident fatalities by 2020 in line with the UN Decade of Action for Road Safety",""],[1,"416","16","Roadside Land Use and Right-of-Way Control Policy","strict roadside land use development and right of way (r.o.w) control policies should be adopted.",""],[1,"417","3","Road Damage Monitoring and Penalty Enforcement System","the implementation of road damage monitoring system will be strengthened with enforcement of penalties for violation.",""]],"15":[[1,"409","4","River Route Dredging and Navigability Improvement Projects","Accordingly, the Bangladesh Inland Water Transport Authority (BIWTA) has been trying to implement more dredging related projects under this plan.","Bangladesh Inland Water Transport Authority (BIWTA)"],[1,"409","7","Waterway Improvement through Dredging","Improvement of waterways through dredging",""],[1,"409","9","River-Based Container Port Establishment","Establishment of river based container port",""],[1,"409","10","Port Infrastructure and Modern Facilities Development","Establishment of port infrastructure and installation of modern facilities",""],[1,"409","11","Pontoons Procurement and Installation","Procurement and installation of pontoons",""],[1,"409","13","Private Sector Partnership for Accelerated Dredging","Given the long lead time for results, the Government will explore the possibility of working with private sector in speeding up dredging.",""],[1,"413","4","Mongla Port Jetty Development through PPP","2 Jetties at Mongla Port through PPP",""],[1,"413","11","Laldia Bulk Terminal Construction","Construction of Laldia Bulk Terminal",""],[1,"413","12","New Inland Container Depot Construction","Construction of a New Inland Container Depot (ICD) near Dhirasram Railway Station",""],[1,"413","15","Inland Container Terminal Construction and Operation","Construction & Operation of Inland Container Terminal (ICT) at Khanpur",""],[1,"414","1","Chittagong Port Capacity Expansion","and to address the anticipated Chittagong port capacity constraints owing to growing income and international trade.",""],[1,"420","14","Safe and Low-Cost Inland Water Transport Development","the Government is committed to supporting the development of a safe and low-cost inland transport alternative based on use of the Bangladesh's vast inland waterways.",""],[1,"421","1","Inland Waterway Navigability Improvement Programme","development of navigability of inland waterways by dredging and resuscitation of dead and dying river routes;",""],[1,"421","2","Navigable Waterway Maintenance Dredging","maintenance of navigable waterways by regular dredging;",""],[1,"421","3","Inland River Port and Navigational Aids Development","facilitating flow of passenger and cargo by development of inland river ports, and by providing navigational aids for smooth and safe movement of cargo and passenger vessels;",""],[1,"421","4","Inland Container River Port Development","develop inland container river port for transportation of containers by waterways to/from two sea- ports;",""],[1,"421","5","River Port Handling and Storage Facilities Upgrade","develop river port handling facilities as well as storage facilities and introduce mechanical equipment for handling cargo in order to save waiting time for berthing of vessels;",""],[1,"421","6","Rural Launch Landing Station Development","develop rural launch landing stations by providing pontoon facilities for smooth embarkation/ disembarkation of passenger and loading/ unloading of cargo;",""],[1,"421","8","River Main Channel Protection and Clearance","protect the main channel of the river by clearing & removing garbage & unauthorized encroachment; and",""],[1,"421","9","Buriganga and Dhaka Waterways Restoration","restoration of the Buriganga and waterways around Dhaka city for making it pollution free navigable and wider.",""],[1,"421","10","BIWTA Comprehensive Development Plan","a comprehensive development plan has been prepared by BIWTA for implementation during the Seventh Plan",""],[1,"421","12","Waterway Development and Navigability Maintenance","Development of new waterways and maintaining navigability of existing channels.",""],[1,"421","13","Hydrographic Survey and Dredging Programme for Inland and Coastal Waterways","Hydrographic Survey in 6000 km of inland waterways & in 1000sq km of coastal waters; -Dredging of 3600 lakh m3 - Procurement of 30 nos. dredger; - Several lots of Navigational Aids; - Procurement of different no. of service vessels.",""],[1,"421","14","Landing Station and River Port Development and Maintenance","Operation, maintenance and establishment of landing stations and river ports for bulk cargo and container.",""],[1,"421","15","River Port Construction and Modernization Programme","Construction of 10 nos. River Port - Modernization of 9 nos. River Port;",""],[1,"421","15","Container Terminal Construction Project","Construction of 2 nos. Container Terminal (ICT)",""],[1,"421","15","Pontoon Procurement Programme","Procurement of different size such as 5 nos. (large), 45 nos. (medium), 50 nos. (small), 35 nos. (special type) of Pontoon",""],[1,"421","15","Civil Structure Works Programme","Several lots of Civil Structure.",""],[1,"425","6","River Navigability Improvement and River Protection Measures","The government's initiatives to improve river navigability through dredging and other investments along with the River Protection Commission Act are very welcome.",""]],"16":[[1,"414","18","Dhaka Subway Feasibility Study","Feasibility study for construction of Sub-way (underground railway) in Dhaka city",""],[1,"417","4","MRT Line-6 Implementation","the Government has taken initiatives to implement the MRT Line-6 project from Uttara to Motijheel under the supervision of Dhaka Transport Coordination Authority (DTCA).",""],[1,"417","4","Dhaka East-West Expressway Feasibility Study","feasibility study of Dhaka East-West expressway will be carried.",""],[1,"417","4","Buriganga Convention Centre and Flyover Construction","The Government plans to construct an international convention centre on the other side of the Buriganga and a fly-over starting from Shantinagar, crossing over the Buriganga to ensure faster communication with the convention centre.",""],[1,"417","4","Dhaka Elevated Expressway Construction","a contract has been signed with the investment partner to construct the 46.73 km. long Dhaka elevated express way from Hazrat Shah Jalal International Airport to Kutubkhali of Dhaka-Chittagong highway.",""],[1,"418","5","Mass Transit-Oriented Land Use and Transport Development","Adhering mass transit oriented land use and transport development policies; main focus needs to be on the development of signal free road network and public transport infrastructures (viz. dedicated bus lanes, passenger transfer facilities, bus bays, turnaround facilities, stopover terminals etc. which are now grossly missing)",""],[1,"418","6","Pedestrian-Friendly Walking and Crossing Infrastructure Development","Besides reclaiming footpath, adequate pedestrian friendly walking and crossing infrastructures should be developed.",""],[1,"418","10","Public Transport-Oriented Infrastructure Development","For core areas, the optimum infrastructural development strategies would involve early implementation of all the STP recommended public transport oriented projects and improvement initiatives like introduction of bus route franchising (BRF) scheme.",""],[1,"420","3","Two-Tier Urban and Suburban Railway Development","In the long run for even distribution of traffic load, urban contribution of railway in terms of carrying commuter traffic (which is now less than 1 percent of the total daily trips of Dhaka city) needs to be increased by adopting two-tier railway system i.e. sub-urban and urban rail.",""],[1,"420","3","Integrated Urban Rail Network Development","Urban rail network need to be developed by including the circular rail and by integrating fully with the long distance sub-urban rail (may start from Tongi & Narayanganj) as well as STP (Strategic Transport Plan 2004-2024) and DHUTS (Dhaka Urban Transport Studies 2010-2050) recommended BRT and MRT based urban mass transit network systems.",""],[1,"425","3","Urban Traffic Management Reform","This will be a combination of land use zoning laws, parking regulations, time of day traffic flow regulations, efficient functioning of traffic signals and solid monitoring and implementation of all traffic laws and regulations.",""],[1,"425","3","Dhaka Light Rail Investment","the proposed light rail for Dhaka",""],[1,"536","2","Dhaka Expressway Construction Project","There is also a PPP contract for building the Dhaka Expressway connecting Uttara and Kamlapur.",""],[1,"536","2","Commuter DEMU Train Service","As part of the multi modal transport system commuter DEMU (Diesel Electric Multiple Unit) train service has been introduced.",""],[1,"536","2","Metro Rail System Development Project","A project to introduce metro rail system has been taken up with support from JICA.",""],[1,"536","4","Revision of the Strategic Transport Plan","Presently, DTCA has taken initiative to revise this plan under the title \"Revision of Strategic Transport Plan\".","Dhaka Transport Coordination Authority (DTCA)"],[1,"536","4","Transport Project Alignment with the Strategic Transport Plan","All the departments working in the transport sector in greater Dhaka city will have to conceive their projects in accordance with the proposals of STP to avoid duplication and ensure planned development.",""],[1,"544","4","Public Transport Expansion and Rapid Bus Transit Development","steps, therefore, should be taken to increase the number of large-size buses including double-decker buses on trunk routes and buses of optimum sizes on other routes.",""],[1,"544","4","Rapid Bus Transit with Dedicated Bus Lanes","Introduction of Rapid Bus Transit through the use of high capacity dedicated bus lanes should be given high priority.",""],[1,"544","4","Rail-Based Mass Transit Development","Rail- based mass transit systems will also be built as parts of a long-term integrated transport strategy for Dhaka Metropolitan Area.",""],[1,"545","2","Metropolitan Commuter Bus and Rail Services","Comfortable bus and rail-based commuter services will be provided to encourage people to stay in surrounding satellite towns and commute to their work places in the city.",""],[1,"552","7","Mass Rapid Transit System Introduction","With a 14% annual increase in motorized vehicles and the 8% population growth with resultant pollution and congestion calls for major rethinking of its transport system, and for which a strategic choice for introducing Mass Rapid Transit System (MRTS).",""]],"17":[[1,"117","1","Regional Railway Connectivity Expansion","linking Bangladesh Railway system with destinations in India and Myanmar and further to the Asian Railway system",""],[1,"117","1","Khulna-Mongla Rail Link Development","directly linking Khulna and Mongla with Dhaka and Chittagong directly by rail using the Padma Bridge",""],[1,"414","10","Railway Reform and Modernisation Investment","Continuation of investment to reform and modernise railways.",""],[1,"414","11","Dhaka Circular Railway Construction","Construction of circular rail road track around Dhaka city.",""],[1,"418","12","Railway Infrastructure Investment and Modernization","To achieve this, substantial investment in infrastructure, equipment and technical modernization will be required, as is adoption of a more commercial approach to management.",""],[1,"418","13","Railway Expansion and Modernization Programme","The Ministry of Railways has adopted railway expansion and modernization Programme during the Seventh Plan that will substantially strengthen the performance of the railway.","Ministry of Railways"],[1,"419","2","Railway System Expansion and Improvement","Expand and improve railway system to provide safer, better,",""],[1,"419","3","Railway Network Expansion","Expansion of railway network to expand rail operations",""],[1,"419","4","New Rail Track Construction","Undertake construction of 856 kilometre of new rail track.",""],[1,"419","5","Environment-Friendly and Cost-Effective Transport Facilities","environment friendly & less expensive transport facilities to the national and international traffic to increase its market share.",""],[1,"419","7","Dual Gauge Double Tracking of Rail Lines","undertake dual gauge double tracking of 1110 kilometre",""],[1,"419","8","Rail Rehabilitation and Upgrading Programme","Rehabilitate/upgrade existing rails for improved speed and safety",""],[1,"419","9","Rail Track Rehabilitation Programme","Undertake rehabilitation of 725 km of existing rail track",""],[1,"419","10","Railway Bridge and Operational Infrastructure Construction","Construction of railway bridges and other infrastructure for operational improvement.",""],[1,"419","11","Rail Bridge and Level Crossing Infrastructure Improvement","Undertake construction of rail bridges, improvement of level crossing gates and improvement of other infrastructure.",""],[1,"419","12","Locomotive Procurement for Rail Service Improvement","Procure new locomotives to improve service quality",""],[1,"419","13","Railway Rolling Stock and Equipment Procurement","Purchase 100 new locomotives, 1 locomotive simulator and 4 relief cranes.",""],[1,"419","14","Passenger Coach Procurement","Procure new coaches for passenger comfort.",""],[1,"419","15","Passenger Coach Procurement and Rehabilitation Programme","Purchase 1120 passenger coaches and rehabilitate 624 coaches.",""],[1,"419","17","Railway Workshop Upgrading","Upgrade railway workshops and",""],[1,"419","18","Modern Maintenance Equipment Procurement","Procure modern maintenance equipment",""],[1,"419","20","Rail Signal Upgrade for Stations","Upgrade rail signal for 81 stations",""],[1,"419","21","Railway Management Strengthening","Strengthen railway management",""],[1,"419","22","Operational Deficit Reduction through Price Increases and Efficiency Gains","Eliminate operational deficit through price increases and operational efficiency gains.",""],[1,"419","25","Dhaka-Laksham Elevated Rail Cord Line Construction","priority will be given to construct Dhaka-Laksham elevated cord line via Fatullah in Narayanganj (new gateway).",""],[1,"419","26","Phased Double Tracking of Major Railway Corridors","Bangladesh Railways needs to undertake double tracking of all major railway corridors by phases.",""],[1,"419","27","Grade-Separated Rail Corridor Development","Developing a full access controlled right of way as well as capital intensive grade separated measure to make level crossing free allowing segregated rail corridor and thereby ensuring operation of commuter trains in urban areas, particularly for Dhaka city.",""],[1,"419","28","South Asia and Trans-Asian Railway Connectivity Strengthening","Strengthening South Asia regional and Trans-Asian railway connectivity.",""],[1,"419","29","Rail Freight Capacity Expansion","Taking into cognizance that the railway freight transportation cost in Bangladesh is one of the highest in the world and presently it takes about 18 days to bring a container to Dhaka from Chittagong Port mainly due to acute shortage of freight trains, and most importantly very low average travelling speed (15-20 km/h), besides augmenting rolling stock, development of dedicated",""],[1,"420","1","High-Speed Freight Corridor Development","high speed freight corridor capable of carrying double layer container is a must.",""],[1,"420","2","Railway Infrastructure for EPZ/SEZ and ICD Connectivity","Priority would be given to connect large EPZ/SEZ mouth ICDs and thereby to develop market oriented container transport friendly new railway infrastructures.",""],[1,"420","5","Single-Line Dual Gauge Railway Construction from Dohazari to Cox's Bazar and Ramu to Gundhum","Construction of Single Line Duel Gauge Railway Track from Dohazari to Cox's Bazar via Ramu and Ramu to Gundhum near Myanmar Border.",""],[1,"420","7","Double Track Standard Gauge Railway Line Construction","Construction of Double Track Standard Gauge Railway Line from Dhaka to Chittagong via Comilla/Laksam (expressway)",""],[1,"420","8","Modern Railway Workshop Construction at Rajbari","Construction Modern Railway Workshop at Rajbari.",""],[1,"420","9","Double-Line Railway Track Construction between Joydebpur and Iswardi","Construction of Double Line (Duel Gauge) Railway Track between Joydebpur-Iswardi sections;",""],[1,"420","10","Bangabandhu Railway Bridge Construction","Construction of Bangabandhu Railway Bridge (2nd) over the River Jamuna;",""],[1,"420","11","Khulna to Mongla Port Railway Line Construction","Construction of Railway line from Khulna to Mongla Port with feasibility Study;",""],[1,"420","12","Dual Gauge Double Rail Line Construction and Rail Conversion Project","Construction of Dual Gauge Double Rail Line and Conversion of Existing Rail Line into Dual Gauge between Akhaura and Laksam.",""],[1,"420","13","Rail Line Construction and Reconstruction Programme","the construction and reconstruction of 441 km rail line is already under way",""],[1,"420","13","Dhaka-Chittagong Railway Corridor Upgrading","the Government has taken initiatives to upgrade Dhaka-Chittagong corridor into double lines",""],[1,"420","13","Second Bhairab and Titas Rail Bridge Construction","the construction of 2nd Bhairab and 2nd Titas Rail Bridge is in progress",""],[1,"420","13","Dhaka-Sylhet Railway Revitalization Plan","The Dhaka-Sylhet railway communication is extremely delicate and the Government has taken up a plan to revamp it",""],[1,"420","13","Dhaka-Mongla and Chittagong-Cox's Bazar Rail Line Construction","The Government also intends to construct in phases the Dhaka-Mongla and Chittagong-Cox's Bazar rail lines",""],[1,"420","13","Rail Capacity Strengthening for Coal Transport","the rail capacities will be strengthened to allow the transfer of coal from the proposed new port at Matarbari to the required coal-fire based power stations",""],[1,"422","1","Intermodal Rail and River Connectivity Expansion","Reducing port induced semi-trailer truck traffic by developing wider intermodal rail and river connectivity.",""],[1,"426","3","Railway Operational Deficit Elimination Action Plan","The Railway Ministry should prepare an action plan to ensure the elimination of the railway operational plan by the end of the second year of the Seventh Plan.","Railway Ministry"],[1,"427","4","Railway Reform Programme","The rail ministry should revisit the reform agenda and prepare an actionable Programme for government approval and implementation during the Seventh Plan.","Ministry of Railways"]],"18":[[1,"283","5","Transport Network Investment and Traffic Management Improvement","Trade logistic cost has to be brought down substantially through new investment in transport network including sea-ports, improvements in performance of existing facilities, and much better traffic management.",""],[1,"293","5","River Dredging and Port Capacity Improvement","Huge investments are needed for river dredging to make them more navigable and conducive to the use of modern river vessels.",""],[1,"299","1","Port, Airport, and Container Terminal Infrastructure Investment","to be cashed in through proper public investments in related infrastructure (sea ports and airports, and container terminals) and facilitating regulatory policies.",""],[1,"299","1","Shipping and Air Industry Capacity and Standards Upgrade","Strong efforts are needed during the Seventh Plan to reduce this deficit by raising the capacities and performance standards of the shipping and air industry.",""],[1,"301","5","Civil Aviation Authority Head Office Construction","Construction of Civil Aviation Authority's Head Office",""],[1,"301","6","Cox's Bazar Airport Development","Development of Cox's Bazar Airport",""],[1,"301","7","Airport Infrastructure Development and New International Airport Construction","Infrastructural development of the existing airports and construction of a new international airport.",""],[1,"305","4","Aviation Infrastructure Expansion and Safety Upgrade","Expansion of fixed infrastructure to facilitate an expanded and safe aviation system in Bangladesh",""],[1,"305","5","Civil Aviation Capacity Upgrade Programme","the Seventh Plan has adopted a significant plan to upgrade both the international and domestic aviation capacities.",""]],"19":[[1,"145","8","Rural Infrastructure Spending Increase","Increase spending on rural infrastructure",""],[1,"146","7","Fiscal Reallocation for Social Programmes and Infrastructure Investment","This combination of expenditure reallocation (1% of GDP) and additional tax effort focused on personal income, VAT and local government revenues (4.8% of GDP) can finance the additional 4% of GDP required to fund critical social programmes, while also leaving a surplus of 1.8% of GDP for additional investment in infrastructure.",""],[1,"155","1","ADP Fund for Infrastructure and Lagging Region Development","A separate fund would have to be kept in the Annual Development Programme (ADP) for infrastructure development, emphasizing technical education and giving greater accessibility to the lagging regions in wider economy which will address regional disparity issues.",""],[1,"155","2","Infrastructure Improvement in Lagging Districts","Improvement of infrastructural facilities is one of the key interventions that can open the door of economic opportunities in the lagging districts.",""],[1,"160","1","Public Infrastructure and Social Development Investment","Through public sector investment in infrastructure and social development and through regulatory reforms conducive for private savings and investment, the Government will try to achieve the economic and social development objectives established under the Plan.",""]],"20":[[1,"438","4","Rural and Urban Infrastructure Development by LGED","Local Government Engineering Department (LGED) under LGD has been contributing enormously towards people's socio-economic uplift by building rural and urban infrastructures like constructions of roads, culverts, bridges, growth centre for expansion of market facilities, development of small scale water resources, construction of Union and Upazila Parishad building, construction of cyclone/flood shelter, construction of bus terminal, landing ghats, construction of rural and municipal markets, slum improvements, etc.","Local Government Engineering Department | Local Government Division | Ministry of Local Government, Rural Development & Cooperatives"],[1,"440","6","Urban Infrastructure Improvement Programme for Paurashavas","The MSP and its successor institution, Bangladesh Municipal Development Fund, presented a model of supporting decentralization especially by opening up access to infrastructure funding based on objective",""],[1,"451","5","Rural Road and Structure Maintenance Policy Implementation","The \"Rural Road & Structure Maintenance Policy-2013\" has made lot of directives to arrange adequate funds for maintenance by Public Private Partnership, involvement of LGIs etc.",""],[1,"452","1","Rural Roads and Structures Maintenance Strategy","adoption of a Rural Roads & Structures Maintenance Strategy, maintenance plan and according higher priority to maintenance over new construction,",""],[1,"452","1","Road Construction Quality Assurance Measures","ensuring quality of construction, more involvement of Local Government Institutions (LGI) and ensuring utilization and maintenance of constructed facilities.",""],[1,"452","2","Upgrading and Maintenance of Busy Upazila and Union Roads","The first priority will be to Double lane/Upgrade and maintain selected busier Upazila Roads, Union Roads that are being used by a large number of commercial vehicles including maintenance/rehabilitation of bridges/culverts in these roads.",""],[1,"452","2","Maintenance of Existing Paved Rural Road Network","Proper maintenance of the existing paved rural network will also be included in first priority.",""],[1,"452","3","Upazila, Union, and Priority Village Roads Improvement Programme","The second priority will be to improve Upazila Roads, Union Roads and prioritized Village Roads including culverts/bridges which have strategic importance to connect road network, railway and waterway.",""],[1,"452","4","Growth Centre and Ghat Facility Improvement","The third priority will be to improve Growth Centres and construction of 'ghat' facilities at Growth Centres located on the bank of inland waterways to ensure better integration of road and water ways and thereby stimulating the rural transport and trading system.",""],[1,"452","5","Rural Roads and Structures Maintenance Strategy","adoption of a Rural Roads & Structures Maintenance Strategy, maintenance plan and according higher priority to maintenance over new construction",""],[1,"452","5","Local Government Institution Engagement in Road Development","more involvement of Local Government Institutions (LGI)",""],[1,"452","5","Maintenance and Utilization of Constructed Facilities","ensuring utilization and maintenance of constructed facilities",""],[1,"452","8","Rural Road Master Plan Update and Infrastructure Development","Rural Road Master Plan of LGED will be updated.",""],[1,"453","1","Rural Infrastructure Maintenance and Local Funding Mechanism","For sustainability of rural infrastructure, adequate maintenance system and a viable funding mechanism based on local resources and emphasizing local participation and ownership will be arranged.",""],[1,"453","2","Local Infrastructure Maintenance Funding and Efficiency Improvement","the Government and the local bodies will make special efforts to fully fund these needs and LGED will make continuous efforts to improve maintenance efficiency and ensure local participation.",""],[1,"453","4","Upazila Road Improvement Programme","Improvement of the Upazila Road (5000 Km).",""],[1,"453","5","Selected Upazila and Union Road Upgrading Programme","Double lane/Widening/ Up gradation/Rehabilitation of selected Upazila /Union Roads that needs up-gradation being used by a large number of commercial vehicles (10000 Km)",""],[1,"453","7","Selected Union Road Improvement Programme","Improvement of the selected Union Road. (8000 Km)",""],[1,"453","8","Prioritized Village Road Improvement Programme","Improvement of prioritized Village Road (12000 Km)",""],[1,"453","9","Bridge and Culvert Reconstruction and Road Widening","Re-construction/Double lane of Bridges and Culverts on Upazila Road, Union Roads (12000 Meter) being used by a large number of commercial vehicles",""],[1,"453","10","Bridges and Culverts Construction on Upazila and Union Roads","Construction of Bridges and Culverts on Upazila Road, Union Roads (140000 Meter)",""],[1,"453","11","Construction of Bridges and Culverts on Prioritized Village Roads","Construction of Bridges and Culverts on prioritized Village Road (50000 M)",""],[1,"453","18","Rural Road Safety Engineering Improvement","Improvement of road safety engineering in rural roads to minimize road accidents.",""],[1,"453","19","Periodic and Routine Rural Road Maintenance","Periodic and Routine maintenance of Paved and Herring Bone Bond (HBB) roads & structures on rural roads",""],[1,"453","21","Rural Transport Reorientation for Integrated Access","The development strategy for the rural transport will be reoriented for efficient external access through optimal integration of road and inland water transport and off-road internal accesses;",""],[1,"454","3","Transport Safety Standards Improvement","Attention will be given to improve transport safety standards including specific attention to women safety in all means of transportation with a view to substantially reducing the incidence of accidents.",""],[1,"454","4","National Road Design and Loading Standards","National standard for road design, geometry and loading capacity will be set, especially for the rural roads connecting the upazilas with zila.",""],[1,"455","10","Boat Landing Ghat Construction","Construction of boat landing ghat",""]],"21":[[1,"406","5","Weigh-Bridge Installation for Overload Control","Attempts have been made to control overload by means of installing weigh-bridges at each important traffic origination point in different National Highways.",""],[1,"406","5","Umbrella Road and Bridge Project Approach","Umbrella projects will be better in regard to approval and implementation instead of single road projects, especially in case of construction and rehabilitation of Zila roads and that of small and medium length bridges.",""],[1,"408","13","Local Government Institution Capacity Building for Road Maintenance and Road Safety","Capacity building of LGIs for road maintenance and road safety.",""],[1,"408","14","Road Upgradation Land Acquisition","Land acquisition for up-gradation of Roads",""],[1,"409","1","Local Government Capacity Building for Roadside Planned Development Framework","Capacity building of LGIs to develop a framework of planned development beside roads to resist drainage congestion.",""],[1,"413","20","Vehicle Axle Load Control Station Operation Policy","To help improve road safety the Government has adopted the \"Vehicle Axle Load Control Station Operation Policy 2012\".",""],[1,"413","23","Transport Infrastructure Strategy Implementation Gap Remediation","An important priority will be to address the implementation gaps of the Sixth Plan.",""]],"22":[[1,"7","4","Transformational Infrastructure and Mega Projects Programme","Infrastructure will be made suitable for a middle income country which will include transformational mega projects for energy and transport sectors.",""],[1,"11","4","Transformational Energy and Transport Infrastructure Projects","Infrastructure will be made suitable for a middle income country which will include transformational mega projects for energy and transport sectors.",""],[1,"42","4","Padma Bridge Construction","continuing with the construction of the Padma Bridge despite myriad challenges",""],[1,"48","2","Major Infrastructure Project Investment","As in the past, much of the public sector investment needs to be directed to major infrastructure projects including the 8 transformational projects identified by the government and in realizing the Power Sector Master Plan.",""],[1,"48","4","Fast-Tracking Nationally Important Development Projects","Thrust on development expenditure to alleviate infrastructure constraints by fast tracking nationally important projects will continue.",""],[1,"48","4","Expansion of Major Highways, Bridges, and Power Projects","In addition initiatives will be taken to broaden and accelerate the implementation of other major highways and bridges, power sector projects, and providing access to serviced land to foreign and domestic investors in the context of the Special Economic Zones (SEZ) initiative.",""],[1,"50","10","Padma Multipurpose Bridge Construction","Construction of 6.15 km. long Padma Multipurpose Bridge at Mawa-Janjira",""],[1,"50","11","Dhaka Elevated Expressway Construction","Construction of about 26 km. long Dhaka Elevated Expressway",""],[1,"50","12","Dhaka-Chittagong Expressway Construction and Highway Upgradation","Construction of Dhaka-Chittagong expressway and upgradation of Dhaka-Chittagong highway to 4-6 lane.",""],[1,"53","6","Completion of Ongoing Roads and Bridges Projects","Timely completion of all ongoing roads and bridges projects especially related to inter-city highways;",""],[1,"53","6","Fast-Tracking Transformational Infrastructure Investments","A top priority is to focus on fast tracking a number transformational infrastructure investment;",""],[1,"53","6","Regional Connectivity and Trans-Asian Highway Support","to promote regional connectivity and support for the Trans-Asian Highway Project;",""],[1,"76","6","Transport Infrastructure Improvement Programme","These issues will be tackled in the 7th Plan.",""],[1,"84","11","Padma Multipurpose Bridge Construction","Construction of 6.15 km. long Padma Multipurpose Bridge at Mawa-Janjira",""],[1,"84","12","Dhaka Elevated Expressway Construction","Construction of about 26 km. long Dhaka Elevated Expressway",""],[1,"84","13","Dhaka-Chittagong Expressway Construction and Highway Upgradation","Construction of Dhaka-Chittagong expressway and upgradation of Dhaka-Chittagong highway to 4-6 lane.",""],[1,"116","1","Fast Track Infrastructure Project Acceleration","The Government has already identified and put on a Fast Track list a number of important projects for speedy implementation.",""],[1,"116","1","Infrastructure Constraint Alleviation through Fast Track Expansion","The list will be expanded, as needed, to make sure that the infrastructure constraints, including in power, will be greatly alleviated under the 7th Plan.",""],[1,"116","1","ADP Expansion for Infrastructure Investment","These efforts notwithstanding the size of the ADP would need to be increased by almost 2 percentage points to 6.9% of GDP by FY20 in order to address the growing infrastructure needs.",""],[1,"117","1","Padma Bridge Construction","Major infrastructure projects like construction of Padma Bridge",""],[1,"117","1","Dhaka-Chittagong Highway Expansion","completion of Dhaka- Chittagong 4-lane highway and broadening it further to at least six lanes",""],[1,"117","1","National Highway Widening Programme","making all national highways to at least 4-lane highways",""],[1,"117","1","Elevated Road Construction in Major Cities","construction of elevated roads in major cities",""],[1,"129","9","Fast Track Priority Projects Acceleration","speedy implementation of other priority projects which are in the list of Fast Track projects of the Government",""],[1,"154","14","Padma Multi-purpose Bridge Construction","Construction of the Padma Multi-purpose Bridge is expected to benefit large number of people living in some of the lagging districts in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"155","3","Inter-District Transport System Improvement","Transport system between the better off districts (i.e. with Dhaka and Chittagong) and lagging districts would be improved in order to increase economic activities in the lagging districts.",""],[1,"155","3","Padma Bridge Construction Project","One of the major transport projects, construction of Padma Bridge is expected to be completed by early 2018",""],[1,"155","4","Inter-District and Intra-District Road Transport Development","Both inter district and intra district road transport system would be developed to increase economic mobility within the lagging districts.",""],[1,"160","2","Fast-Tracking Nationally Important Infrastructure Projects","Thrust on development expenditure will be to alleviate infrastructure constraints by fast tracking nationally important projects.",""],[1,"160","2","Major Highways and Bridges Expansion Programme","In addition major initiatives will be taken to broaden and accelerate the implementation of other major highways and bridges, power sector projects, and providing access to serviced land to foreign and domestic investors in the context of the Special Economic Zones (SEZ) initiative.",""],[1,"405","6","Strategic Road Corridor Development and Management","Develop and manage strategic road corridors",""],[1,"405","9","Padma Multipurpose Bridge Construction","Construction of Padma Multipurpose",""],[1,"405","10","Expressway Public-Private Partnership Investment Mobilization","Leverage private investments through PPPs for Expressways (Bangladesh Bridge Authority)","Bangladesh Bridge Authority"],[1,"405","11","Dhaka Elevated Expressway PPP Construction","Construct Dhaka Elevated Expressway on PPP basis;",""],[1,"406","2","Asian Highway Connectivity Works","The initial work for connectivity to the Asian Highway network has also started.",""],[1,"406","5","Special Road Planning for Mixed Traffic Conditions","This particular aspect needs to have a special attention while planning and designing for construction of a road.",""],[1,"407","1","Padma Bridge Construction Project","Construction of the Padma Bridge at the Mawa-Janjira point has been a major infrastructure project under the Sixth Plan.",""],[1,"413","6","Santinagar to Mawa Road Flyover and New Buriganga River Bridge","Flyover from Santinagar to Mawa Road (New) Bridge over Buriganga River",""],[1,"413","7","Dhaka Bypass Upgrading to Four Lanes","Upgrading of Dhaka Bypass to 4 Lane (Joydevpur- Debogram-Bhulta-Madanpur)",""],[1,"414","1","Regional Connectivity and Trans-Asian Highway Support","Government's commitment to promote regional connectivity and support for the Trans-Asian Highway Project;",""],[1,"414","1","Strategic Transport Infrastructure Project Prioritization","Bangladesh needs to be more strategic about identifying transport infrastructure projects and then allocating resources accordingly.",""],[1,"414","1","Timely Completion of Transformational Infrastructure Investments","The priority should be to focus on timely completion of transformational infrastructure investment.",""],[1,"414","5","Road Repair, Maintenance, Improvement and Expansion Programme","Continue to repair, maintain, improve and expand existing roads on a priority basis",""],[1,"414","6","Padma Multipurpose Bridge Construction","Construction of Padma Multipurpose Bridge to be completed by 2018",""],[1,"414","7","Karnaphuli River Multi-Lane Tunnel Construction","Construction of a multi-lane tunnel underneath the river Karnaphuli in Chittagong",""],[1,"414","8","National Highway Four-Laning Programme","Conversion of nationally important highways into four lanes gradually",""],[1,"414","9","Transport Connectivity to Economic Hubs","Connect important economic activity hubs such as Payra Port and Economic Zones to National Highways.",""],[1,"415","2","Critical Transport Links Completion for Regional Connectivity","Timely completion of critical transport links (roads, bridges, railways and river waterways) related to regional and multi-regional connectivity.",""],[1,"415","3","Backbone Network for Strategically Important National Highways","there needs to be an access controlled 'Backbone Network' considering strategically important national highways.",""],[1,"415","11","High-Speed Transport Corridor Infrastructure Development","Develop middle-income enabled quality infrastructures with high-speed mobility facilities.",""],[1,"416","11","Padma Bridge Completion Project","The Government accords the highest priority to the completion of the Padma Bridge project by 2018.",""],[1,"416","11","Dhaka Ring Road Interface Connectivity Development","As a corridor improvement approach, the construction of Padma Bridge would be integrated with the development of interface connectivity with the capital city of Dhaka using ring road system as has been stipulated in the DHUTS-2010 and thereby to reduce overall journey time.",""],[1,"416","11","Karnaphuli River Tunnel Construction","The Government is also giving priority to the construction of a multi-lane tunnel underneath the Karnaphuli River to lower congestion and improve roads transport movement.",""],[1,"416","11","National Highway Four-Laning Programme","Regarding highways, the topmost priority is to convert important national highways into four lanes.",""],[1,"416","11","Ongoing Highway Project Completion","The initial effort will focus on completing the ongoing highway projects; especially the upgrading of the Dhaka- Chittagong Highway is of utmost importance.",""],[1,"416","11","Dhaka-Chittagong 4-Lane Highway and Rail Double-Tracking","Early completion of the Dhaka-Chittagong 4-lane highway (along with the double tracking of the railway connection) could raise productivity of the Chittagong port, which could provide dividend of generating substantial extra value added along the supply chains.",""],[1,"416","14","Highway Upgrading to Access-Controlled Arterial Roads","Gradually developing the existing interrupted highways to uninterrupted arterial roads by adopting two-tiered access controlled layout configuration for segregating mobility and accessibility functions of highways.",""],[1,"416","15","At-Grade Junction Interchange Construction and Highway Widening","As at-grade junctions' dictates constructing interchange facility that should increase overall capacity of the highways, besides highway widening at the major-major junctions.",""],[1,"417","1","Shift to Concrete Highway Pavement","Moreover, to reduce maintenance frequency of highways, focus could be shifted from bituminous pavement which is inherently water sensitive to maintenance insensitive 'fit and forget' and perpetual in nature type concrete pavement.",""]],"23":[[1,"685","9","Rural Infrastructure Maintenance Programme","Institutional Feeding programme, Rural Infrastructure Maintenance programme, Risk Reduction Programme, Road Maintenance Programme, House Building Grants etc.",""],[1,"685","9","Road Maintenance Programme","Institutional Feeding programme, Rural Infrastructure Maintenance programme, Risk Reduction Programme, Road Maintenance Programme, House Building Grants etc.",""],[1,"689","2","Rural Road Improvement Projects","To facilitate economic enhancement and better communication during disasters, MoDMR is implementing projects to improve the rural earthen roads.","MoDMR"],[1,"689","2","Rural Earth Road Construction under the Seventh Five-Year Plan","Besides, 2,50,000 km rural earth roads is planned to be constructed in 7th FYP period.",""],[1,"689","2","Coastal Pacca Road Construction in Komen-Affected Areas","Further, 33km pacca roads will be constructed in collaboration with LGED with JICA assistance in 19 districts of Komen affected areas in coastal areas, and 3145 km Herring Bone Bond (HBB) roads will be constructed by 2020.","LGED"],[1,"689","2","Bridge and Culvert Construction Project","Further, a project for construction of bridge/culvert has been undertaken to implement for the period 2016-2020.",""],[1,"689","2","Small Bridge, Embankment, and Sluice Gate Construction in Komen-Affected Areas","In addition, 356 meter of small scale bridge, 7 km of embankment and 8 no. of sluice gates will be constructed in collaboration with BWDB with support from the government of Japan in Komen affected areas of Bangladesh.","BWDB"]],"24":[[1,"422","2","Karnaphuli General Cargo Berthing Modernization Project","Enhancing already saturated container storage port yard facilities by developing existing dilapidated 2.3km general cargo berthing (GCB) facilities at Karnaphuli into a modern gateway- terminal of international standard",""],[1,"422","4","Channel Navigability Maintenance and Dredging Programme","Maintaining and improving the navigability of the channel through capital dredging and regular maintenance dredging ;",""],[1,"422","5","Container Handling Capacity Expansion","Increasing container handling capacity through expansion of terminal/yard facilities, acquisition of modern container handling equipment and procurement of harbour crafts and vessels to ensure improved operating system.",""],[1,"422","6","Inland Container Depot and Container Freight Station Development","Setting up ICDs/CFS by the Public/Private sector at all potential cargo distribution centres across the country to decongest the port.",""],[1,"422","9","Mongla Port Utilization Expansion","The Government will take all necessary steps to step up the use of Mongla Port facility.",""],[1,"422","9","Sonadia Deep Seaport Development under G2G Arrangement","steps have been taken to implement the project under Government to Government (G2G) arrangement.",""],[1,"422","9","Coal Import Port Facilities Priority Development","The development of port facilities for coal imports will be given top priority in order to support the power generation plan.",""],[1,"422","9","Matarbari Deep Sea Port and Coal Transshipment Terminal","JICA is also examining the possibility to set up the large coal transhipment terminal at the Matarbari port to cater the demand of nearly 3,500MW of power generation by 2020.",""],[1,"422","9","Land Port Strengthening for Trade Facilitation","the Government is also taking steps to strengthen the land ports to facilitate trade with neighbours.",""]],"25":[[1,"410","11","Airport Runway, Taxiway, and Apron Strengthening","Strengthening of existing runway, taxi-way and apron for safe and secured operation of modern aircraft;",""],[1,"410","12","Construction of New Airports","Construction of new airports for better communication with remote area.",""],[1,"410","13","Airport Parking Area Expansion","Expansion of parking area to accommodate new aircrafts of domestic and international airports of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"410","14","Airport Operational Facilities Enhancement","Enhancement of operational facilities at airports.",""],[1,"410","15","Control Tower Operational Facilities Upgrade at HSIA","Enhance the operational facilities of Control Tower at HSIA",""],[1,"410","16","Modern Navigational Equipment Installation","Installation of modern Navigational equipment.",""],[1,"410","17","Bangladesh Biman Operational Performance Strengthening Initiative","Initiatives to strengthen the operational performance of Bangladesh Biman.",""]],"26":[[1,"305","2","Bangladesh Biman Twinning and Commercial Management Reform","the Government will explore the option of twining arrangement between Bangladesh Biman and a reputed international airline.",""],[1,"305","3","Domestic Aviation Joint Venture Promotion","Regarding domestic aviation, the possibility of joint ventures with international partners will be encouraged.",""],[1,"305","3","International Shipping Joint Venture Exploration","The possibility of joint ventures in international shipping will also be explored.",""],[1,"305","3","Aviation and Shipping Reform Study","For both areas, a special study will be commissioned to highlight the constraints and identify specific reforms.",""]],"27":[[1,"293","5","River Transport Safety Standards Monitoring and Enforcement","a combination of major investments in river dredging and river ports combined with effective monitoring and implementation of safety standards will substantially improve the quality of water transport and spur private investment and value-added.",""],[1,"307","7","Driver Licensing and Driving Record Monitoring","Strict monitoring of licensing and driving records of truck and bus drivers.",""],[1,"307","8","Road Damage Monitoring Based on Vehicle Weight and Loading Norms","Monitoring of road damage based on vehicle weight and loading norms.",""],[1,"307","9","Commercial Vehicle Safety Features Enforcement","Strict implementation of safety features of commercial vehicles",""],[1,"307","10","River Vessel Inspection and Load Monitoring","Strict inspection of all river vessels and monitoring of vessel loads.",""],[1,"307","11","Mandatory Accident Insurance for Transport Enterprises","Require purchase of accident insurance for all enterprises engaged in the transport industry.",""]],"28":[[1,"414","12","Payra Third Sea Port Construction","Construction of the 3rd Sea port at Payra in Patuakhali.",""],[1,"414","13","Moheshkhali Sea Port and LNG Terminal Construction","Construction of a sea port and an LNG terminal at Moheshkhali",""],[1,"414","14","Third Terminal Construction at Hazrat Shah Jalal International Airport","Construction of third terminal at Hazrat Shah Jalal International Airport (HSIA)",""],[1,"414","15","Khan Jahan Ali Airport Construction","Construction of a new airport named Khan Jahan Ali Airport",""],[1,"414","19","Biman Fleet Capacity and Management Improvement","Strengthen Fleet capacity while making Biman a profitable organisation by improving its management and enhancing the capacity of passenger transport.",""],[1,"423","1","Phased Air Service Infrastructure Support Plan","the Government has adopted a phased implementation plan for adding air service infrastructure support.",""],[1,"423","1","Airport Service Upgrade and Multimodal Transfer Facilities","the planned investment is necessary to upgrade airport services and to improve terminal accessibility by establishing multi-modal transfer facilities by integrating HSIA with the nearby Airport railway station, on-going three Bus Rapid Transport (BRT) and Dhaka elevated expressway projects.",""],[1,"423","1","Cox's Bazar Airport International Upgrade","The Government also intends to upgrade the airport at Cox's Bazar to an international level to promote tourism.",""],[1,"423","1","Integrated Sea Beach Front Land Use and Transport Planning","there is a strong need for adopting an integrated sea beach front land use and transport development approach.",""],[1,"423","4","Airport Operational Facilities Enhancement and New Airport Development","To enhance/ strengthen operational facilities of existing airports and development of new airports.",""],[1,"423","5","Hazrat Shahjalal International Airport Facilities Expansion","Expansion of operational and passenger facilities of Hazrat Shahjalal International Airport (HSIA).",""],[1,"423","5","Cox's Bazar Airport International Upgrade","Development of Cox's Bazar Airport into international airport for operation of wide-body airport.",""],[1,"423","7","Wide Area Multilateration, ATC, and Communication System under PPP at HSIA","Wide Area Multilateration-WAM along with ATC and Communication system at Hazrat Shahjalal International Airport (HSIA), Dhaka under PPP",""],[1,"423","8","HSIA Third Terminal and Infrastructure Construction","Construction of 3rd Terminal Building and other infrastructure at HSIA",""],[1,"423","9","Cargo Aircraft Parking Facility Enhancement at Shah Amanat International Airport","Enhancement of Cargo aircraft parking facilities at Shah Amanat International airport (SAIA).",""],[1,"423","10","Runway Extension at HSIA","Extension of Runway at 32 end of HSIA.",""],[1,"423","11","Saidpur Airport Development","Development of Saidpur Airport",""],[1,"423","12","Runway Strengthening at SAIA","Strengthen existing runway at SAIA.",""],[1,"423","13","Cargo Apron Expansion at HSIA","Extension of apron towards North of existing cargo apron at HSIA.",""],[1,"423","14","Construction of Cargo Village Phase II at HSIA","Construction Cargo village (Phase-II) at HSIA.",""],[1,"423","15","Osmani International Airport Runway Strengthening","Strengthen existing runway at Osmani International airport, Sylhet.",""],[1,"423","16","Airport Parking Bay and Hangar Construction","Construction of parking Bay and 2 Nos. Hanger for National Airline and Private Airlines at HSIA.",""],[1,"423","19","Cox's Bazar Airport Phase I Development","Development of Cox's bazar airport(Phase-I)",""],[1,"423","20","Terminal Building and Cargo Construction","Construction of Terminal Building, Cargo",""],[1,"423","23","Cargo Apron Construction","Construction of Cargo Apron in front of Cargo",""],[1,"423","25","Runway Asphalt Concrete Overlay at SAIA, Chittagong","Asphalt concrete overly over the existing runway at SAIA, Chittagong.",""],[1,"423","26","Runway Asphalt Concrete Overlay at SAIA, Sylhet","Asphalt concrete overly over the existing runway at SAIA, Sylhet.",""],[1,"423","27","Khanjahan Ali Airport Construction","Construction of Khanjahan Ali Airport.",""],[1,"423","28","Barisal Airport Development","Development of Barisal Airport.",""],[1,"427","5","Bangladesh Biman Performance Strengthening Reforms","Additional reforms that will be pursued during the Seventh Plan include: development of infrastructure facilities like construction of Second Hangar Complex to enhance aircraft maintenance capability and achieve international standard in aircraft maintenance through achieving EASA certification; enter into full automation with implementation of different software and enrich IT facilities; arrange training at all levels to enhance manpower skills and develop human capital; provide policy support in favour of national airlines to protect from unhealthy competition of aggressive foreign airlines in aviation business; and infusion of sufficient working capital for running as a commercial airline.","Ministry of Civil Aviation and Tourism"]],"29":[[1,"718","2","Women-Friendly Public Transport Improvement Measures","The public transport system would be made more frequent, safe and affordable.",""],[1,"718","2","Traffic Safety Training and Enforcement Measures","Road safety would be ensured through enforcement of traffic rules and laws.",""],[1,"718","2","Workplace Support Facilities and Regulatory Provisions","workplace safety and security concerns, child care, housing and toilet facilities, etc. would be addressed by ensuring regulatory provisions with private sectors and also by encouraging private sectors to develop low cost housing and child care facilities.",""],[1,"722","2","Gender-Responsive Infrastructure for Mobility and Economic Gains","infrastructure that facilitates women's human development, mobility and economic gains;",""]],"30":[[1,"53","2","Comprehensive Long-Term Water Resource Management Plan","A comprehensive long term water resource management plan is in the making under the umbrella of the Bangladesh Delta Plan.",""],[1,"78","6","Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 Formulation and Implementation","The formulation of the Bangladesh Delta Plan-2100 and its timely implementation during the Seventh Plan will be a major long-term policy and institutional initiative for building resilience and reducing the effects of disaster.",""],[1,"80","5","Delta Plan Water Management Strategy","Successful development of the Delta Plan strategy for water management and management of other environmental hazards will be a major challenge for the Seventh Plan.",""],[1,"100","3","Long-Term Bangladesh Delta Plan","A long term vision has been developed and comprehensive measures have to be taken with the development and implementation of a long term Bangladesh Delta Plan to adapt to climate change and manage the water challenges.",""],[1,"174","8","Public Investment Prioritization Framework","Public investment priorities will be determined on the basis of realization of key Seventh Plan targets with respect to real GDP growth, poverty reduction and social protection for the poor and vulnerable, human resource development, enhancing social equity through inclusive growth and ensuring the sustainability of growth through continued macroeconomic stability.",""],[1,"174","8","Annual Allocation for Bangladesh Delta Plan Investment Programmes","In addition, annually around 2% of GDP will be allocated to the investment programmes which will be related to 'Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100'.",""],[1,"175","1","Delta Fund for Delta Plan Financing","Government will form a Delta Fund for mobilising necessary resources to implement Delta Plan.",""],[1,"467","2","Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 Strategy and Investment Plan Implementation","Promote implementation of Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 strategies and investment plans.",""],[1,"467","3","Climate-Proofing of Structures in Climate Risk Areas","Introduce climate proofing of structures for the areas of climate risk.",""],[1,"475","8","Infrastructure Repair, Rehabilitation, and Maintenance Programme","GoB will repair and rehabilitate existing infrastructure, including river embankments and drainage systems, and ensure proper operation and maintenance.",""],[1,"475","8","Urgent New Infrastructure Planning and Construction","Steps will be taken to plan, design, and construct urgently needed new infrastructure.",""],[1,"475","9","Integrated River Management and River Training Works","The introduction of Integrated River Management Plan, River Management Improvement and Land development projects on right Bank of Jamuna at Sirajgonj - Belkuchi will stabilize the river plan form and make room for efficient river channelization.",""],[1,"475","9","River Channelization and Land Reclamation Works","Reclamation of land and enhancing the navigability of the river by reducing the width is possible by river training works to create conditions for sustainable development and poverty alleviation of the northern districts of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"490","15","Implementation of Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 Strategies and Investment Plans","Implementing relevant strategies and investment plans of Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100.",""],[1,"491","8","Rural Land, Water Conservation, and Waterlogging Response Programmes","Against that context, the GoB has considered the following programmes under the 7th FYP to address such concerns.",""],[1,"492","7","BDP 2100 Programme Implementation","Implement programmes of BDP 2100",""],[1,"493","3","Implementation of Relevant BDP 2100 Programmes","Implementation of relevant programmes of BDP 2100.",""],[1,"494","1","River Protection Programmes under BDP 2100","Implementation of relevant programmes for river protection under BDP 2100.",""],[1,"494","5","Coastal Zone Policy and Coastal Zone Strategy Implementation","Coastal zone policy & coastal zone strategy to be put to use.",""],[1,"509","7","Robust Adaptive Integrated Delta Strategy","Ensure long term water and food security, economic growth and environmental sustainability while effectively coping with natural disasters, climate change and other delta issues through robust, adaptive and integrated strategies, and equitable water governance.",""],[1,"510","3","Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 Hotspot Programme Package","Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 Formulation Project (BDP2100) has initially identified several hotspot wise programmes for the 7th Five Year Plan (2016-2020) to meet up the goals and to deal with the challenges of BDP 2100 as a short term measure.",""],[1,"510","3","Ganges Barrage Construction","For Coastal Zones BDP2100 has suggested programmes like Construction of Ganges Barrage, Coastal Embankment Improvement Programme, Char Development and Settlement Project-V, Integrated Management of Drainage Congestion for greater Noakhali, Tidal River Management (30 yrs. duration), Estuary Land Development Programme (Hatiya-Dhamar Char-Nijhum Dwip and Urir Char Cross Dam projects).",""],[1,"510","3","Coastal Embankment Improvement Programme","For Coastal Zones BDP2100 has suggested programmes like Construction of Ganges Barrage, Coastal Embankment Improvement Programme, Char Development and Settlement Project-V, Integrated Management of Drainage Congestion for greater Noakhali, Tidal River Management (30 yrs. duration), Estuary Land Development Programme (Hatiya-Dhamar Char-Nijhum Dwip and Urir Char Cross Dam projects).",""],[1,"510","3","Char Development and Settlement Project V","For Coastal Zones BDP2100 has suggested programmes like Construction of Ganges Barrage, Coastal Embankment Improvement Programme, Char Development and Settlement Project-V, Integrated Management of Drainage Congestion for greater Noakhali, Tidal River Management (30 yrs. duration), Estuary Land Development Programme (Hatiya-Dhamar Char-Nijhum Dwip and Urir Char Cross Dam projects).",""],[1,"510","3","Integrated Drainage Congestion Management for Greater Noakhali","For Coastal Zones BDP2100 has suggested programmes like Construction of Ganges Barrage, Coastal Embankment Improvement Programme, Char Development and Settlement Project-V, Integrated Management of Drainage Congestion for greater Noakhali, Tidal River Management (30 yrs. duration), Estuary Land Development Programme (Hatiya-Dhamar Char-Nijhum Dwip and Urir Char Cross Dam projects).",""],[1,"510","3","Tidal River Management","For Coastal Zones BDP2100 has suggested programmes like Construction of Ganges Barrage, Coastal Embankment Improvement Programme, Char Development and Settlement Project-V, Integrated Management of Drainage Congestion for greater Noakhali, Tidal River Management (30 yrs. duration), Estuary Land Development Programme (Hatiya-Dhamar Char-Nijhum Dwip and Urir Char Cross Dam projects).",""],[1,"510","3","Estuary Land Development Programme","For Coastal Zones BDP2100 has suggested programmes like Construction of Ganges Barrage, Coastal Embankment Improvement Programme, Char Development and Settlement Project-V, Integrated Management of Drainage Congestion for greater Noakhali, Tidal River Management (30 yrs. duration), Estuary Land Development Programme (Hatiya-Dhamar Char-Nijhum Dwip and Urir Char Cross Dam projects).",""],[1,"510","3","Barind Water Management Programme","For Barind and Drought Prone Areas, Barind Water Management Programme (North Rajshahi Irrigation Project), Revitalization and Restoration of Chalan Beel has been proposed.",""],[1,"510","3","Chalan Beel Revitalization and Restoration","For Barind and Drought Prone Areas, Barind Water Management Programme (North Rajshahi Irrigation Project), Revitalization and Restoration of Chalan Beel has been proposed.",""],[1,"510","3","Integrated River Management Plan","River Management Programme, (Integrated River Management Plan, River Bank Improvement Project, Jamuna Land Development Programme), Sustainable Restoration of Connectivity of Major Navigation Route are proposed for the hotspot named Major Rivers and Adjoining Areas.",""],[1,"510","3","River Bank Improvement Project","River Management Programme, (Integrated River Management Plan, River Bank Improvement Project, Jamuna Land Development Programme), Sustainable Restoration of Connectivity of Major Navigation Route are proposed for the hotspot named Major Rivers and Adjoining Areas.",""],[1,"510","3","Jamuna Land Development Programme","River Management Programme, (Integrated River Management Plan, River Bank Improvement Project, Jamuna Land Development Programme), Sustainable Restoration of Connectivity of Major Navigation Route are proposed for the hotspot named Major Rivers and Adjoining Areas.",""],[1,"510","3","Sustainable Restoration of Major Navigation Route Connectivity","River Management Programme, (Integrated River Management Plan, River Bank Improvement Project, Jamuna Land Development Programme), Sustainable Restoration of Connectivity of Major Navigation Route are proposed for the hotspot named Major Rivers and Adjoining Areas.",""],[1,"510","3","Integrated Haor Management Programme","Integrated Haor Management Programme for Haor Region and Integrated Eastern Hills Management programme for CHT has suggested by BDP2100.",""],[1,"510","3","Integrated Eastern Hills Management Programme","Integrated Haor Management Programme for Haor Region and Integrated Eastern Hills Management programme for CHT has suggested by BDP2100.",""],[1,"510","3","Integrated Water and Sewage Management Programme","Integrated Water and Sewage Management Programme (Dhaka City), Improvement of Drainage Congestion and Flood Control for Chittagong City Corporation, Protection of River System around Dhaka city and Dhaka Integrated Flood Control Embankment cum Eastern Bypass projects has proposed for Urban Areas.",""],[1,"510","3","Chittagong City Drainage Congestion and Flood Control Improvement","Integrated Water and Sewage Management Programme (Dhaka City), Improvement of Drainage Congestion and Flood Control for Chittagong City Corporation, Protection of River System around Dhaka city and Dhaka Integrated Flood Control Embankment cum Eastern Bypass projects has proposed for Urban Areas.",""],[1,"510","3","Protection of River System around Dhaka City","Integrated Water and Sewage Management Programme (Dhaka City), Improvement of Drainage Congestion and Flood Control for Chittagong City Corporation, Protection of River System around Dhaka city and Dhaka Integrated Flood Control Embankment cum Eastern Bypass projects has proposed for Urban Areas.",""],[1,"510","3","Dhaka Integrated Flood Control Embankment cum Eastern Bypass","Integrated Water and Sewage Management Programme (Dhaka City), Improvement of Drainage Congestion and Flood Control for Chittagong City Corporation, Protection of River System around Dhaka city and Dhaka Integrated Flood Control Embankment cum Eastern Bypass projects has proposed for Urban Areas.",""],[1,"510","3","Rationalization of Existing FCD/FCDI Projects","BDP2100 has also proposed some projects around the Bangladesh i.e. Rationalization of existing FCD/FCDI projects and Development of Small-scale Water Reservoir and Revitalization of water bodies, khals etc.",""],[1,"510","3","Small-scale Water Reservoir Development and Water Body Revitalization","BDP2100 has also proposed some projects around the Bangladesh i.e. Rationalization of existing FCD/FCDI projects and Development of Small-scale Water Reservoir and Revitalization of water bodies, khals etc.",""]],"31":[[1,"358","7","River Dredging for River Revival","Top most priority would have to be attached towards river dredging to revive the rivers.",""],[1,"359","1","Enhanced Budget Allocation for Water Sector Projects","Water sector needs enhanced allocation in the national budget for several important on-going projects e.g. Teesta Barrage Project, Buriganga Restoration Project, Capital Dredging project and projects on Climate Change Adaptation and Mitigation Measures to fulfil the targets of vision 2021.","Ministry of Water Resources"],[1,"359","1","Processing of Major Water Resources Projects","A large number of big projects are being processed under the Ministry of Water Resources, i.e. Ganges Barrage Project, Mongla-Ghasiakhali Dredging, BEZA, Buriganga River Restoration Project, Urichar-Noakhali Cross Dam, CDSP-V, ORIO project in Bhola (Dutch assisted) and River Management Improvement Project.","Ministry of Water Resources"],[1,"359","1","Climate Service and Disaster Risk Reduction Programmes","Projects or Programme are to be taken on Climate Service, Disaster Risk Reduction, and Eastern bypass etc. may require especial emphasis during 7th plan.",""],[1,"359","10","River Management and Dredging Priority Programme","River management, commonly understood as dredging, would be given top most priority with feasibility assessment in case by case.",""],[1,"359","10","Coastal Land Reclamation Measures","Another priority is to take measures to reclaim land in the coastal areas.",""],[1,"360","3","River Dredging and Riverbank Protection Programme","Dredging would be carried out in a systematic and comprehensive way in combination with riverbank protection for non-destructive, easy and smooth passage of flood flow of the river system.",""],[1,"360","4","Canal Excavation and Re-excavation for Small-Scale Irrigation","Efforts should also be made to excavate/re-excavate the natural canals as that can help small scale surface water irrigation.",""],[1,"360","5","Development of Individual Hydrological Areas","it will also be necessary for Bangladesh to concentrate on the development of individual hydrological areas to meet short and intermediate term requirements.",""],[1,"360","6","Ganges Barrage Project with Ancillary Infrastructure","In 7th FYP period, government will pursue to (i) harness properly the benefits of the Ganges Water Treaty 1996 (ii) to save the Sundarbans and the south-west region of the country from salinity intrusion and (iii) to utilize the surface water in the wake of wide-spread arsenic contamination in groundwater.",""],[1,"360","7","River Channelization and Morphological Prediction Programme","Channelization and morphological prediction of major rivers reducing river erosion, thereby helping reduce internal migration caused by such erosion, and reclamation of agricultural land will be pursued under the plan.",""],[1,"361","1","River Channelization for Navigability and Riverbank Protection","knowledge and experience will be used for river channelization.",""]],"32":[[1,"490","4","Dhaka Sewerage Treatment Capacity Expansion","Increase the capacity or sewerage treatment plant of Dhaka city to cover 80 to 90% household.",""],[1,"490","4","Additional Sewage Treatment Plants for Tongi, Gazipur, and Narayangonj","Installing 3 additional Sewage Treatment Plants for Tongi, Gazipur, Narayangonj",""],[1,"490","8","Sludge Management System Development","Sludge Management System will be developed.",""],[1,"490","11","Dhaka City Drainage Rehabilitation","Drainage rehabilitation of Dhaka city through excavation of canals, if necessary to protect the city from urban flooding.",""],[1,"491","1","Drainage System Rehabilitation and Canal Excavation","Design & implement appropriate drainage plan or rehabilitation of existing drainage system with excavation of canals, if necessary, especially for Chittagong.",""],[1,"491","3","Environmentally Sound Sewerage Collection and Treatment Systems","Design & implement environmentally sound sewerage collection & treatment systems.",""],[1,"492","12","Wastewater Treatment Compliance Survey and Action Plan","Ministry of Industries MOI and MOE will conduct a comprehensive survey to determine compliance with this provision by WDF firms.","Ministry of Industries MOI | MOE"]],"33":[[1,"324","5","National Water Conservation Campaign","A countrywide campaign is, therefore, required to conserve water and use it judiciously and",""],[1,"325","1","Proper Land Use Planning System","institute proper land use planning system.",""],[1,"325","1","Mandatory Rainwater Harvesting and Water Use Efficiency Measures","Mandatory rain water harvesting and water use efficiency deserve higher priority.",""],[1,"326","2","Sustainable Irrigation Expansion and Surface Water Use","Ensure sustained agricultural growth through more efficient and balanced utilization of land, water and other resources, and encourage more use of surface water for irrigation and reduction of pressure on ground water while expanding irrigation facilities through improving existing irrigation system and related infrastructures.",""],[1,"326","2","Renewable Energy Promotion for Small-Scale Irrigation","Renewable energy (solar and wind power) is given more importance in the 7th FYP.",""],[1,"326","2","Solar Panel Installation for Rural Irrigation","Installations of solar panels for small scale irrigation in rural areas will be given priority;",""],[1,"329","9","Integrated Land Use Planning and Crop Zoning","Focus will be given on comprehensive land use planning through integration of economic, ecological, social and cultural values in production programme in order to develop options so that informed choices can be made.",""],[1,"329","9","Soil and Water Conservation, Land Development, Drainage and Flood Control Programme","In the seventh five year plan, emphasis will be broaden to include soil and water conservation, land development, drainage and flood control, and reclamation programme.",""],[1,"329","9","Crop Zoning-Based Production Programme","Production programme will be organized based on crop zoning.",""],[1,"330","2","Precision Agriculture Promotion","For resource conservation and judicious use of inputs, the Seventh FYP will give more focus on the Precision Agriculture (PA).",""],[1,"330","4","Well-Planned Irrigation Management System","Therefore, a well- planned irrigation management system is essential for gradual increase of cropping intensity as well as yield.",""],[1,"330","4","Modern Water Management Technology Promotion","Irrigation efficiency will be ascertained and modern water management technology will be promoted to enhance irrigation efficacy and water productivity through optimal use of available water resources.",""],[1,"330","4","Surface Water Irrigation Expansion and Groundwater Reduction","The government has laid special emphasis on the increased use of surface water and reduced use of groundwater in irrigation to protect the ecological balance and reduce irrigation expenses.",""],[1,"330","4","Conjunctive Surface and Groundwater Use","Thus, conjunctive use of surface and groundwater would be stressed.",""],[1,"330","4","Water Reservoir and Rainwater Harvesting Promotion","As part of the strategy creation of water reservoir/ rain water harvesting in rain fed/coastal/hilly areas will be encouraged, and small scale water resources systems will be developed (particularly through BADC/LGED/BWDB) along with monitoring the maintenance of the small scale water resources infrastructure at local levels by ensuring community participation and taking care of environmental and social issues.",""],[1,"330","6","Rainwater Harvesting for Irrigation","Rain water harvesting for irrigation",""],[1,"331","1","Solar-Powered Irrigation","Use of solar power for irrigation",""],[1,"331","2","Solar Panel Construction Over Canals and Water Bodies","Construction of solar panel over canal or water body",""],[1,"331","3","Deep Tube Well Irrigation Discouragement Policy","Discouraging the use of deep tube well for irrigation",""],[1,"331","4","Crop Diversification in Barind Area","Discouraging the cultivation of high water demand crop in Barind Area",""],[1,"333","2","Small-Scale Irrigation Technology and Surface Water Expansion","Expansion of small scale irrigation technology and surface water for irrigation;",""]],"34":[[1,"449","9","Rural Safe Water Supply and Sanitation Expansion","Increase access to safe water supply and sanitation to all rural people.",""],[1,"450","3","Rural ICT Infrastructure and E-Service Expansion","ICT & E-citizen Service and e-parishad services will be provided to ensure online services and dissemination of information to the people by strengthening ICT infrastructure in rural areas, by providing necessary access to the database of cooperative societies and human resource development.",""]],"35":[[1,"157","3","Arsenic-Free Tube-Well Provision","More arsenic free tube-wells have to be made available in these areas for ensuring safe health of the people of those districts.",""]],"36":[[1,"701","5","Child Water, Sanitation and Healthy Environment Access","providing access to children particularly in urban and remote settings to clean water and sanitation, and a healthy environment",""],[1,"702","4","Arsenic Mitigation and Alternative Drinking Water Systems","The specific objectives are to mitigate arsenic problem in drinking water by providing alternative systems",""],[1,"702","4","Sanitary Latrine Access Expansion","increase rural and urban slum access to sanitary latrines",""],[1,"702","4","Underserved Paurashava Water and Sanitation Service Expansion","expand water and sanitation services to cover currently underserved Paurashava areas",""],[1,"702","4","Improved Water Supply for Hard-to-Reach Areas","provide improved water supply to underserved, un-served and difficult to reach areas",""],[1,"702","4","Primary School Sanitation and Safe Drinking Water Provision","Primary schools will be ensured access to sanitation and safe drinking water.",""]],"37":[[1,"465","7","Natural Water Bodies and Environmental Resources Restoration","Ensure restoration of natural water bodies and other environmental resources",""],[1,"465","8","Artificial Groundwater Recharge Exploration","Explore the opportunities for environmental friendly artificial groundwater recharge in major cities.",""],[1,"465","21","Wetlands and Water Bodies Conservation and Development","Preserve, protect and develop the natural wetlands and water bodies",""],[1,"485","3","Ecologically Critical Area Designation for Dhaka Rivers","The rivers surrounding Dhaka has been declared as Ecologically Critical Areas (ECA) to restore riverine ecosystems.",""],[1,"490","2","Surface Water Resource Protection for Greater Dhaka","Protecting surface water resource base of greater Dhaka (Dhaka, Tongi, Gazipur, and Narayangonj) by taking appropriate actions for cleaning the river(s) Buriganga, Balu, and Turag & Sitalakhya.",""],[1,"490","10","Surface Water Supply Diversification and Groundwater Recharge Initiative","Shifting the dependence on water supply from groundwater to surface water, with improvement in surface water quality and increasing supply to the Saidabad water treatment plant (from the Meghna River) with the possibility to explore the opportunity of artificial and natural ground water recharge.",""],[1,"491","14","Groundwater Dependence Reduction Programme","On the basis of an objective and transparent survey on the availability of ground water, dependence of the water supplies on ground water requires to be lessened.",""],[1,"492","1","Mandatory Rainwater Harvesting and Conservation for Government Buildings","Rainwater harvesting and conservation may be made mandatory for all government buildings including school, cyclone shelters, and local government institution during 7th Five Year Plan",""],[1,"492","3","National Groundwater Availability Survey","Conducting a national wide survey on availability of ground water.",""],[1,"492","5","Rainwater Harvesting Options Exploration","Exploring options for rainwater harvesting",""],[1,"493","13","Environmentally Safe Dredging Guidelines","Developing guidelines for environmentally safe dredging that include appropriate distance from river banks and structures; spoil dewatering; disposal of contaminated sediments in appropriate locations; illegal dredging by developers without licenses (sand mining) to be stopped.",""],[1,"493","14","Waterway Buffer Zone Enforcement and Encroachment Removal","BIWTA to enforce the 50-metre buffer zone along rivers and canals; flood flow zones to be clearly marked and encroachment prevented (continue the programme to remove illegal structures in the waterways); protection of wetlands and beels from encroachment.","BIWTA"],[1,"493","15","Oil Recovery Programmes at Ship Repair Yards","Oil recovery programmes to be established at all ship repair yards, with waste oil stored, collected, and re-processed at refineries.",""],[1,"493","16","River Pollution Classification and Restoration Programme","Categorise rivers on the basis of pollution-load and taking-up programmes to restore the lifelines.",""],[1,"494","6","Waste Reception Facilities at Ports","Establishing proper Waste Reception Facilities at port(s) and a Contingency Plan to fight against oil spillage.",""],[1,"494","6","Oil Spill Contingency Plan","Establishing proper Waste Reception Facilities at port(s) and a Contingency Plan to fight against oil spillage.",""],[1,"494","7","Marine Biological Resources Inventory and Management Plan","Inventory of Marine Biological Resources and development of management plan for resources.",""]],"38":[[1,"358","5","Trans-boundary Water Sharing Negotiation","Trans-boundary water sharing issue would be pursued with the co- riparian country on a priority basis to address dry season water scarcity.",""],[1,"360","4","Transboundary River Water Sharing Arrangement","top-most priority would be given on water sharing of the Common/trans-boundary Rivers with the neighbouring country/countries following the model of the Ganges Treaty-1996.",""],[1,"360","5","Basin-wide Water Resources Development Initiative","Initiative would be started immediately to enter into agreements with co-riparian countries for sharing the waters of international rivers, data exchange, resource planning and long-term management of water resources under normal and emergency conditions of flood, drought and water pollution.",""],[1,"362","5","Resource Mobilization through Public-Private Partnerships and Donor Funding","creative measures will have to be undertaken to mobilize additional resources, particularly those that could lead to more private solutions which may call for Public Private Partnerships (PPPs) where feasible.",""]],"39":[[1,"356","3","Flood Control, Drainage, and Irrigation Projects","Through the FCD and FCDI projects, BWDB has created favourable environment for HYV rice production.",""],[1,"357","5","Small Scale Water Resources Development and Management","LGED has been mandated for development and management of small scale water resources for the command areas under 1000 hectares.","Local Government Engineering Department (LGED) | Department of Cooperatives"],[1,"358","10","Participatory Water Management Institutionalization","Sustainable operation and maintenance of BWDB/LGED FCD/FCDI projects is hinged on Participatory Water Management through Water Management Organization (WMO).",""],[1,"361","2","Participatory Water Management Approach","The approach would be followed in all water resources sector projects right from the identification up to monitoring & evaluation.",""],[1,"361","3","Operation and Maintenance of Completed Water Resources Projects","The completed projects of water resources sector especially the flood control, drainage and irrigation project would be properly operated and maintained with the participation of stakeholders so that the targeted benefits of the projects are ensured.",""],[1,"361","4","Command Area Development for Food Production","BWDB would continue to pursue command area development activities in surface water irrigation project and to explore expansion of irrigation, river protection and embankments.",""],[1,"361","6","Public-Private Partnership for Water Resources Development","As water resources development interventions are costly initiatives, public-private partnership model has to be explored whenever possible.",""],[1,"362","1","Small Scale Water Resources Development","LGED will continue to develop these with strategies i) ensuring participation, social inclusion and empowerment; (ii) promoting good governance at WMCA; (iii) services delivery; and (iv) caring for the environment and sustainable development.","LGED"],[1,"362","4","Water Resource Management for Agricultural Transformation","Besides, better water resource management facilitates agricultural transformation.",""]],"40":[[1,"462","8","Sectoral Environmental Legislation Review and Redrafting","Sectoral legislations have been reviewed and redrafted in light of Bangladesh's commitments expressed through signing and ratifying of a number of International Conventions and Protocols on environment.",""],[1,"462","9","Polluters Pay Principle Enforcement","'Polluters Pay Principle' has been adopted in order to ensure compliance of environment legislation.",""],[1,"463","3","Industrial Effluent Treatment Requirement","In order to control water pollution, the DoE has made it mandatory for industries to set up Effluent Treatment Plants to treat their waste before discharging to water bodies.","Department of Environment (DoE)"],[1,"463","3","Industrial Wastewater Compliance Enforcement","Enforcement is going on to bring the industries that are generating waste water under compliance.",""],[1,"463","3","Environmental Clearance Certificate Requirement","Proposed industries are required to obtain Environmental Clearance Certificates (ECCs) to ensure that the anticipated pollution load will be within acceptable limits.",""],[1,"463","3","Clean Air and Sustainable Environment Project","Clean Air and Sustainable Environment (CASE) project of the DoE has addressed a number of issues.","Department of Environment (DoE)"],[1,"463","4","Industrial Pollution Penalty Enforcement","To control environmental pollution from industries government imposes penalty against polluter as per section 7 of Bangladesh Environment Conservation Act, 1995.",""],[1,"464","5","Pollution Control Enforcement Enhancement","2. Enhance enforcement for pollution control",""],[1,"466","1","Environmental Pollution Monitoring and Control","Monitor, control and prevent environmental pollution and degradation related to air, water and soil",""],[1,"467","11","Environmental Improvement and Pollution Control","Effect environmental improvement and pollution control.",""],[1,"467","14","Environment Conservation Act Enforcement and Environmental Governance","The DOE is the technical arm of the Ministry engaged in implementation of Environment Conservation Act and Environment Conservation Rules to ensure sustainable environmental governance for achieving high quality of life for the benefit of present and future generation.","Ministry"],[1,"468","1","Competent and Transparent Clearance Process Administration","administer the clearance process competently and transparently",""],[1,"485","3","Mandatory Effluent Treatment Plant Enforcement","Liquid waste generating industries are now required to install effluent treatment plants which are subject to strict enforcement measures.",""],[1,"485","3","Polluter Pays Principle Implementation","The monitoring team of DOE is vigorously implementing Polluter's Pay Principle (PPP) in assessing the damage occurred by the polluters to the environment.","DOE"],[1,"485","3","Polluter Compensation Recovery Mechanism","Compensation for the damage to environment is also realized from the polluters.",""],[1,"486","6","Stricter Environmental Compliance Enforcement and Local Monitoring Committees","The GoB will ensure stricter enforcement of environment clearance conditions and effluent standards and establish local area committees to monitor environment compliance by the industries.",""],[1,"492","6","Zero Discharge Policy","Introduce zero discharge policy",""],[1,"493","2","Public Database for Industry Environmental Compliance","For effective monitoring and environmental compliance, a comprehensive public database will be developed for all firms.","DOE"],[1,"495","12","DoE Cadre Service Establishment","Professionalizing the recruitment of DoE officers through establishment of a cadre service on environmental conservation.",""],[1,"495","13","Environmental Management Cells Establishment","Establishing Biodiversity cell, Chemical Management cell and 3R cell in DoE in addition to Climate cell & Ozone cell already created.","DoE"],[1,"496","1","Implementation of the DoE Strategic Plan","Implementation of the DoE Strategic Plan prepared under BEISP project.",""],[1,"496","3","Environmental Training Institute and Compliance Training Programme","Comprehensive training programmes on rules & regulations, standards, monitoring, ETP & ATP for both public & private agencies through setting up environmental training institute.",""],[1,"496","4","Department of Environment Enforcement and Monitoring Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening enforcement and monitoring capacity of DoE.",""],[1,"496","5","DoE EIA Review Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening DoE capacity on EIA review with trained human resources.",""],[1,"496","6","Environmental Loss and Damage Assessment Methodology","Establishing criteria / methodology for assessment of loss & damage of the environment by various factors including effluent discharge and / or air pollution.",""],[1,"496","7","Standards Revision and Sampling and Monitoring Protocol Development","Revision of standards and development of protocol for sampling & monitoring.",""],[1,"496","8","Industrial Enforcement Monitoring Strengthening","Strengthening industrial enforcement monitoring with increase of frequency of inspection from regulatory agencies.",""],[1,"496","9","Vehicular Emission Enforcement Campaign Strengthening","Strengthening vehicular emission enforcement programme with increase of frequency of campaign.",""],[1,"496","11","Noise Level Control Enforcement Programme","Strengthening noise level control enforcement programme with promotion and awareness campaign involving.",""],[1,"496","12","Strategic Environmental Impact Assessment Introduction","There is also a need for introducing strategic EIA as a planning tool for sectoral level planning.",""],[1,"496","13","EIA Processing and Implementation Capacity Building","Strengthening the EIA processing & implementation through institutional capacity building.",""],[1,"496","14","Location Clearance Issuance for Red Category Projects","Issuance of location clearance after approval of EIA report for Red category projects.",""],[1,"496","15","Mandatory Environmental Clearance for Land Development","No land development activity to take place prior to environment clearance.",""],[1,"496","17","EIA Consulting Firm Enlistment","Enlistment of competent EIA consulting firms by the DoE for conducting EIA.","DoE"],[1,"496","19","Strategic Environmental Impact Assessment for Sectoral Planning","Strategic EIA/SEA for all sectoral planning including for exclusive economic zones.",""],[1,"496","20","EIA Compliance Across Development Ministries and Agencies","Achieving compliance to EIA practices by all development Ministries & agencies.",""],[1,"497","19","Strengthening Special Environmental Courts","To make the courts more effective the following programme can be adopted.",""],[1,"498","1","Court Performance Review and Judicial Reform","A review of the performance of our courts may be undertaken to revamp them.",""],[1,"498","5","In-House Environmental Units in Infrastructure Project Agencies","Establishing in-house environmental unit in each infrastructure project executing agency with staff and personnel of relevant multidisciplinary expertise.",""],[1,"498","6","Cooling Water Discharge Regulation for Power Stations","Establish regulations to control the discharge of cooling water from power stations.",""],[1,"498","7","Environmental Management System Establishment in Industrial Units","Establish Environmental Management System (EMS) in industrial units.",""],[1,"498","8","Zero Discharge Policy for Industry","Establish zero discharge policy with implementation plan for industry",""],[1,"503","11","DoE Enforcement and Surveillance Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening enforcement and surveillance capacity of DoE",""]],"41":[[1,"703","6","Alternative Farm and Non-Farm Livelihoods Support","They will be ensured alternative farm and non-farm based livelihoods.",""],[1,"703","6","Climate and Disaster Protection for CHT Communities","They will be protected from hazards caused by climate change and other natural calamities.",""],[1,"706","8","Preferential Access to Social Protection Programmes in Hill Districts","Social protection assistance will be provided in hill districts to strengthen people's capacity to cope with any sudden decrease in income due to damage to jhum crops caused by floods and drought.",""],[1,"707","3","Village/Mouza Community Forest Expansion","Village/mouza community forest will be created and expanded in the CHT to conserve biodiversity and the watersheds and ensure that people have access to water.",""],[1,"707","4","Community-Based Afforestation and Biodiversity Protection","A massive effort will be undertaken involving the local communities for afforestation over the region.",""],[1,"707","5","Integrated Watershed Management for Creeks and Water Bodies","Special initiatives will be undertaken to ensure the flow of water in creeks, water bodies and waterfalls by preserving the natural sources and integrated watershed management.",""]],"42":[[1,"462","15","3R Waste Management Strategy","3R Strategy has been formulated to streamline waste management system.",""],[1,"464","1","Urban Waste Management Programme","Waste management programmes are being implemented through the reduction of volumes and quantities of wastes, waste re-use and waste recycling.",""],[1,"465","2","Proper Waste Management System","Ensure Proper waste management system in place for good environmental health.",""],[1,"485","3","Waste Management Policy and Project Package","The Government has also taken a number of policies, strategies, regulations and projects on waste management.",""],[1,"485","3","Public-Private Waste Management Partnership and Source Segregation Initiative","A collaborative effort enhancing public- private partnerships, involving the community and establishing segregation techniques at sources, education and awareness towards waste management is a pressing need.",""],[1,"486","1","Waste Dumping Yard Completion","Waste Dumping Yard, which will be completed next year.",""],[1,"487","10","Polythene Disposal and Waste-to-Energy Measures","adoption of measures including discarding polythene, producing energy from wastes will be helpful.",""],[1,"487","11","Solid Waste Management Plan under the 4R Policy","Design and implement plans on solid waste management in accordance with the 4R policy (reduce, reuse, recycle, reclaim)",""],[1,"487","12","Neighborhood Waste Collection and Transfer System","Removal of neighbourhood dumping sites and introducing of private/community waste collectors to carry the segregated waste to central dumping sites or transfer stations.",""],[1,"487","13","Bio-fertilizer and Waste-to-Energy Development","Exploring possibilities for producing bio-fertilizer and energy from waste.",""],[1,"487","14","Bio-remediation and Eco-friendly Waste Treatment Innovation","Exploring and using new ideas or technologies, like bio-remediation, innovative and eco-friendly strategy, involving microbial agent (i.e. protozoa, bacteria, fungi etc.) as successful alternative of traditional (physical and chemical) treatment to clean up waste",""],[1,"487","15","Environmental Impact Assessment for Land Filling Site Selection","Judicious selection of land filling sites through undertaking of EIA",""],[1,"487","16","Polythene Ban Enforcement and Alternative Bag Promotion","Continue to enforce the ban on polythene, encourage the use of cotton and jute bags through economic investment.",""],[1,"491","2","Land Filling Site Criteria Establishment","Establishing criteria for land filling sites",""],[1,"491","4","Environmentally Acceptable Solid Waste Collection and Disposal System","Design & implement environmentally acceptable collection & disposal system of solid wastes.",""]],"43":[[1,"352","4","Social Forestry Programme","Social Forestry programme has got momentum in the last few years.",""],[1,"353","6","People-Oriented Afforestation Programme","Continue and expand people oriented afforestation programme for poverty alleviation and increased employment opportunity for forest dependent community including women;",""],[1,"354","6","People's Participation in Afforestation Programme","People's participation will be continued in afforestation programme in all marginal lands and buffer zone of forests.",""],[1,"354","6","Integrated Tree Plantation and Crop Cultivation","Integration of tree plantation and crop cultivation will be practiced.",""],[1,"354","11","Social Forestry Programme Expansion and Strengthening","Social forestry programme will continue for expansion and strengthening of upazila nurseries, union level nurseries, expansion and",""],[1,"355","1","Strip Plantation Expansion Programme","An estimated 20,000 km. of strip plantations will be raised during the plan period.",""],[1,"355","1","Grassroots Afforestation Coordination Mechanism","Local government bodies will co-ordinate the afforestation programme at the grass root level under this programme.",""],[1,"355","1","NGO-Led Afforestation Support and Extension Services","During the 7th Plan, NGOs will be more directly involved in afforestation programme.",""],[1,"355","2","Social Forestry Tree Planting for Fuelwood Supply","For the prevailing demand through social forestry, short/medium rotation fast growing tree species have to be planted along the roads and embankments, and on marginal and fellow lands with active participation of local people.",""],[1,"355","3","Non-Wood Forest Products Development Programme","Bamboo, agar tree, cane, murta, medicinal plants, honey, wax, golpata, etc. will be developed during the 7th Five Year Plan in a systematic way.",""],[1,"355","3","Private Sector Rubber Plantation and Production Facilitation","Rubber plantation and commercial production of rubber through private sector will be facilitated.",""],[1,"462","21","Forest Plantation Expansion","Against the set target of 302,000 hectares, about 65,814 hectares of plantations were raised in the last four years.",""],[1,"462","21","Coastal Afforestation Expansion","another 3,420 hectares will be raised in this year.",""],[1,"462","21","Coastal Green Belt Establishment","To establish Green belt along the coasts about 978 kilometre has been completed of estimated 2,280 kilometres of coast line",""],[1,"463","2","Social Forestry Programme","The Social Forestry Programme has also gained momentum in recent years, with about 500,000 poor people being involved in it.",""],[1,"464","12","Agro-forestry Promotion Programme","Promote multiple land use technology like agro-forestry to ensure increased productivity and supplement agricultural production;",""],[1,"464","13","People-Oriented Afforestation Programme","Continue and expand people-oriented afforestation Programme for poverty alleviation and increased employment opportunities including women;",""],[1,"466","13","People-Oriented Forestry Expansion Programme","Further promote the people oriented programmes covering forestry on marginal lands, char lands, road sides, etc.",""],[1,"467","10","Planned Forest Resource Expansion","Increase the country's forest resources in a planned manner and arrange to meet the demands for these resources;",""],[1,"477","7","National Social Forestry and Coastal Greenbelt Programme","A major nationwide Programme of social forestry has also been implemented and coastal 'greenbelts' has been planted as a key adaptation-mitigation strategy.",""],[1,"477","9","Social Forestry Programme Expansion","The social forestry programme on government and community land throughout the country will be expanded.",""],[1,"477","9","Coastal Greenbelt Afforestation Programme Expansion","Expansion of the 'greenbelt' coastal afforestation programme with mangrove planting along the shoreline is also suggested.",""],[1,"479","3","Coastal Afforestation Strip Plantation","GoB has also prioritized coastal afforestation strip plantation to capture atmospheric carbon within vegetation.",""],[1,"479","3","Participatory Afforestation Programme","International financing will be sought for participatory afforestation programme, with an aim to involve women and restore the already degraded forest areas.",""],[1,"491","10","Homestead Forestry with Horticulture Promotion","Encouraging homestead forestry with horticulture.",""],[1,"499","6","Afforestation and Reforestation Programme","Greater efforts will be geared up towards afforestation and reforestation activities",""],[1,"499","6","Biodiversity Conservation Activities","Greater efforts will be geared up towards afforestation and reforestation activities as well as, biodiversity conservation during the plan period.",""],[1,"499","7","Afforestation and Reforestation Programme","Greater efforts (which should exceed 6FYP period achievements) shall be taken for afforestation and reforestation activities during the plan period.",""],[1,"499","9","Participatory Forest Development and Agroforestry Integration","People's meaningful & informed participation will be incorporated in all forest development activities.",""],[1,"499","9","Integrated Tree Plantation and Crop Cultivation","Integration of tree plantation and crop cultivation will be practiced.",""],[1,"500","6","Coastal Afforestation and Enrichment Plantation","The existing afforestation and enrichment plantation will continue in the Coastal areas.",""],[1,"500","7","Coastal Green Belt Creation and Seedling Distribution Programme","To prevent the extent of damage by cyclones and tidal surges, Coastal Green Belt will be created and seedling will be raised to distribute or sell in the coastal zone.",""],[1,"500","9","Reed Land Planting Programme","Existing programme on reed land planting to continue.",""],[1,"500","13","Social Forestry Programme Expansion and Strengthening","Social forestry Programme to continue for expansion and strengthening of Upazila nurseries, union level nurseries, and strengthening of forest extension and nursery training centres.",""],[1,"501","1","Roadside and Embankment Tree Planting Programme","Short/medium rotation of fast growing tree species will be planted along the roads and embankments, and on marginal and follow lands with active participation of local people.",""],[1,"501","2","Social Forestry Expansion on Local Application","The amended provision for social forestry on application of local people to be utilized to bring new areas under tree coverage.",""],[1,"501","7","Village Forest Technical Back-up and Extension Services","supports were preceded from the government mainly in terms of technical back-up and extension services and will be continued.",""],[1,"501","8","Private Sector Plantation Credit Facility","Credit facilities will be provided in the 7th FYP to encourage the private sector to undertake rubber, teak, jackfruit and other high value crop plantation on a commercial basis.",""],[1,"502","1","Reforestation and Forest Protection Certification Streamlining","The mechanisms for certifying and approving reforestation and forest protection under carbon credit and REDD mechanisms will be rationalized and streamlined and be used to enable substantial forest restoration and coastal afforestation through partnerships with local communities, civil society and private sector.",""]],"44":[[1,"352","3","Wildlife Division and Protected Area Establishment","Accordingly initiatives have been taken to establish wildlife division and national park, botanical garden and eco-park in selected areas.",""],[1,"353","7","Protected Area Co-management Expansion","Strengthen and expand co-management system in all Protected Areas (PAs) to achieve meaningful participation of local people through CBO, local government bodies and government agencies in forest conservation;",""],[1,"353","8","Wildlife Protection and Illegal Trade Control","Protection of wildlife and control illegal trade of wildlife and trophies;",""],[1,"354","2","Natural Forest Moratorium and Zoning for Biodiversity Conservation","Moratorium on felling in the natural forests will continue.",""],[1,"354","8","Sundarbans Biodiversity Conservation and Wildlife Protection Measures","Due importance will be given to the Sundarbans Mangrove Forest for its biodiversity conservation.",""],[1,"354","8","Wildlife Conservation and Protection Measures for the Sundarbans","Different measures will be taken to conserve and protect wildlife with special attention to Royal Bengal Tiger.",""],[1,"354","8","Emergency Tiger Response Team and Village Tiger Response Team Operations","The activities of 'Emergency Tiger Response Team' and 'Village Tiger Response Team (VTRT)' constituted with the local peoples of surrounding villages will be continued for relaying stray tigers.",""],[1,"355","5","Protected Area Expansion and Forest Carbon Monitoring","The protected area (PA) coverage will be increased to 15 percent of the total forest land during the 7th Five Year Plan period.",""],[1,"355","6","Threatened Species and Fragile Ecosystem Protection Programme","Programmes will be taken to protect the threatened and endangered species of flora and fauna and the fragile ecosystems.",""],[1,"355","7","Forest Ecosystem Conservation and Eucalyptus Reduction","To conserve and protect forest ecosystems, efforts will be made to remove trees not suitable or detrimental to the environment of Bangladesh.",""]],"45":[[1,"50","25","Urban Wetland Restoration and Protection","Urban wetlands are restored and protected in line with Wetland Conservation Act",""],[1,"52","6","Natural Forest Felling Moratorium and Forest Enrichment Planting","The Forestry sub-sector strategy will include continuing moratorium on felling in the natural forests, increasing tree density of the existing forests and older plantations through 'enrichment planting' and",""],[1,"53","1","Assisted Natural Regeneration and Coastal Plantation Intensification","'assisted natural regeneration', and intensification of plantation activities in coastal zones.",""],[1,"53","1","Wildlife Conservation and Protection Measures","Different measures will be taken to conserve and protect wildlife with special attention to Royal Bengal Tiger.",""],[1,"53","1","Social Forestry Development","Social forestry development will continue to be an important strategy.",""],[1,"84","26","Urban Wetlands Restoration and Protection","Urban wetlands are restored and protected in line with Wetland Conservation Act",""],[1,"102","14","Inland River Systems and Ecosystems Maintenance","maintain the inland river systems and ecosystems for fishery, sediment transport, and inland shipping,",""],[1,"102","16","Integrated Coastal and Ocean Management Policy","an integrated Coastal and Ocean Management Policy would be put in place.",""],[1,"353","3","Forest Stand Quality Improvement Programme","During the 7th plan period emphasis will be given to increase tree density ≥70% by improving stand quality through different management interventions.",""],[1,"353","4","Forestry Sub-sector Development Initiatives","In this scenario development initiatives will be taken with following objectives:",""],[1,"353","5","Forest Ecosystem Conservation and Forestry Development Programme","Conserve and protect forest ecosystems for biodiversity and overall environmental stability, and implement forestry development programmes with due emphasis on climate change adaptation and mitigation;",""],[1,"353","11","Multiple Land Use Technology Promotion","Promote multiple land use technology to ensure increased productivity and supplement agricultural production, and encourage private plantation of rubber, orange and non-traditional fruits like chalta, olive, wood apple, cashew nut, amloki, horitaki, bohera, lotkon etc. and other high-value trees;",""],[1,"353","12","Eco-Tourism and Recreation Facilities Expansion","Expand facilities for eco-tourism and recreation.",""],[1,"354","3","Forest Quality Improvement and Enrichment Planting Programme","Necessary programmes will be taken to improve quality and increase tree density of the existing forests and older plantations through 'enrichment planting' and 'assisted natural regeneration'.",""],[1,"354","6","Integrated Tree Plantation and Crop Cultivation","Integration of tree plantation and crop cultivation will be practiced.",""],[1,"354","6","Degraded Sal Forest Rehabilitation Programme","Programme to rehabilitate the degraded Sal Forests will be taken up as part of important development activities.",""],[1,"354","10","Reed Land Plantation Programme","Under the 7th Five Year Plan 5000 ha of Reed lands will be planted.",""],[1,"355","8","Watershed Management and Wetland Conservation Programme","Watershed management, wetland conservation etc. will be initiated in the new area and also will be intensified in the old area for better conservation of nature in the country during the plan period.",""],[1,"466","6","Forest Restoration and Protection in Public Forest Lands","ecologically healthy native forests are restored and protected in all public forest lands (about 16% of land)",""],[1,"466","8","Forestry Extension Strengthening Programme","Strengthen forestry extension activities to transfer improved technology and research information to end-users, e.g., local people and private homesteads",""],[1,"466","10","Sundarbans Mangrove Conservation and Anti-Deforestation Measure","Conserve Sundarbans mangrove forest without any further deforestation and forest degradation.",""],[1,"466","11","Forestry Institutional Capacity Development and Community Participation","Develop institutional capabilities including human resource and involve local people as much as possible in forestry activities",""],[1,"466","14","Forest Land Conversion Restriction","Ensure no forest land shall be converted for non-forest use.",""],[1,"466","15","Protected Forest Restoration and Native Species Enrichment","Ensure no commercial plantation in protected forest area where only native species for enrichment and restoration purposes can be undertaken.",""],[1,"466","16","Inclusive and Rights-Respecting Protected Area Management","Ensure all PA management shall be inclusive of and respectful to the rights of the forest dwellers.",""],[1,"466","17","Community-Based Forest Protection Outsourcing","Consider out-sourcing forest protection measures, utilizing community members on the ground as forest stewards.",""],[1,"466","19","Biodiversity Treaty and Convention Compliance Actions","Initiate actions with regard to obligations under international treaties and conventions regarding conservation of biodiversity",""],[1,"466","20","Biodiversity Cooperation with Regional and International Institutions","Promote cooperation with regional and international institutions/organizations to address local, regional, and global biodiversity problems.",""],[1,"467","8","Forest Resource Conservation and Development","Manage forest resources, and conserve and develop forest land, forest resources and wildlife;",""],[1,"468","2","Government Forest Management and Conservation","The FD controls: 1) management of all the government forests to foster a steady supply of the forest products such as wood, fuel-wood, bamboo and other forest produces towards the demands of the members of the public; 2) protect and conserve the protected areas to meet the mandate of conserving the gene pool and biodiversity, including those of the wildlife, for the nation at large; 3) enhance the tree cover of the country; 4) undertake the social forestry activities towards the awareness raising and encourage the tree planting among the members of the public; 5) involve the members of public as participants in the conservation of protected areas; 6) identify and implement scientifically sound, economically viable and ecologically sustainable forestry management programmes; 7) implement the forestry policy through acts, rules and regulations.",""],[1,"499","8","Chokoria-Sundarbans Reserve Forest Restoration Programme","The 20 thousand acres of the denuded Chokoria-Sundarbans Reserve Forest shall be restored with time bound action and monitoring plan",""],[1,"499","10","Natural Forest Felling Moratorium","Moratorium on felling in the natural forest will continue.",""],[1,"499","10","Hill Forest Replanting and Scientific Management Programme","Existing scattered and denuded hill forests will be replanted to increase productivity.",""],[1,"500","1","Sundarbans Conservation Programme","Greater efforts shall be taken for sustainable conservation of Sundarbans and its resources during the plan period.",""],[1,"500","2","Community-Based Sundarbans Management with Property Rights Allocation","Measures will be taken to involve local community with allocating appropriate property rights in the management of the Sundarbans",""],[1,"500","3","Alternative Livelihoods for Sundarbans-Dependent Communities","Creation of alternative livelihood opportunities for the people, depending on the Sundarbans mangrove forest, to lessen anthropogenic pressure on the Sundarbans mangrove forest.",""],[1,"500","5","Sundarbans Reserve Forest Biodiversity Conservation Measures","Special attention will be given to the Sundarbans Reserve Forest (SRF) for its biodiversity conservation.",""],[1,"500","8","Sal Forest Restoration Programme","Immediate steps will be taken for restoration of the Sal Forest aiming specific targets.",""],[1,"500","8","Sal Forest Wildlife and Garo Community Support Programmes","Considering its wildlife and dwelling place of the Garo tribal community, necessary programmes will be implemented.",""],[1,"500","11","Eco-Parks and Recreational Green Space Development","Development and establishment of five new initiatives such as eco-parks, recreational garden along river or bay and botanical gardens, safari park, national park have already been initiated during the Fifth & Sixth Five Year Plan. Such activities will be continued under this Seventh Five Year Plan.",""],[1,"500","12","Regional Botanical Garden Establishment","Regional botanical garden will also be setup for uniform biodiversity conservation in the country.",""],[1,"501","3","Non-Wood Forest Products Promotion","More emphasis shall be given to non-wood forest products: bamboo, cane, murta, medicinal plants, honey, wax, golpata, during the Seventh Five Year Plan.",""],[1,"501","5","Protected Area Expansion and Management Programme","The protected area will be increased to 5 percent of the country during the Seventh Five Year Plan period.",""],[1,"501","6","Watershed Management and Wetland Conservation Initiative","Watershed management and wetland conservation will be initiated in the haor regions and hills districts and also will be intensified in the old areas for better conservation of nature during the plan period.",""],[1,"504","1","Endangered Species Risk Review and Protective Area Identification","Review IUCN Red list and other documents on the state of endangered and threatened species and to identify the risks specific to them and also geographic areas demanding special protective measures",""],[1,"504","2","Special Protection Measures to Reduce Existing Threats","Undertaking special protection measures to minimize the existing threats",""]],"46":[[1,"653","9","Marine Resource Management Programmes","The Seventh Five Year Plan will undertake specific programmes in the area of marine resource management which will include:",""],[1,"653","11","Integrated Coastal Resource Management Research Programme","Research Programme on Integrated Coastal Resource Management by ICZM",""],[1,"653","12","Marine Biological Resources Conservation Project","Long term project on conservation of marine biological resources",""],[1,"653","13","Protection of IUU Fishing in Bangladesh Waters Programme","Programme on protection of IUU (illegal, unreported and unregulated) fishing in Bangladesh waters",""],[1,"653","14","Pollutant Discharge Prohibition Programme","Programme on prohibition of pollutants discharge from ship breaking and other sources and their impacts",""],[1,"653","15","Deep-Sea Resource Survey","Deep-sea resource survey every five years.",""]],"47":[[1,"49","1","Environmental Protection in Public Investment","Additionally, the public investment programme will emphasize human resource development, enhancing social equity through inclusive growth and ensuring the sustainability of growth through continued macroeconomic stability and protection of the natural environment.",""],[1,"50","29","Integration of Environmental, Climate Change, and Disaster Risk Reduction Considerations into Project Design and Implementation","Environmental, Climate Change and disaster risk reduction considerations are integrated into project design, budgetary allocations and implementation process",""],[1,"54","3","Environmental and Climate Change Capacity-Building Programmes","Relevant programmes for environmental and climate change capacity building at local and national level will be the main interventions of this Plan.",""],[1,"54","3","Environmental and Climate Change Research Support","Government will offer greater attention to the areas in research for knowledge generation concerning environment and climate change.",""],[1,"78","5","Results-Oriented Environmental Management and Climate Change Strategy","A more focused and results- oriented strategy combining elements of policies, regulations, incentives, investment and capacity building are needed.",""],[1,"78","5","Integrated Climate Proofing of Development Strategy","An integrated approach to climate proofing of Bangladesh development strategy is the way to move forward.",""],[1,"80","5","Environmental Management and Climate Change Mainstreaming","the programmes in environmental management and climate change will be strengthened and incorporated in the mainstream economic policy management.",""],[1,"80","5","Climate and Environmental Policy Integration","The integration of climate change and environmental management issues in growth and fiscal policy management will be another high priority issue for the Seventh Plan.",""],[1,"85","1","Mainstreaming Environmental, Climate Change and Disaster Risk Reduction into Project Design and Implementation","Environmental, Climate Change and disaster risk reduction considerations are integrated into project design, budgetary allocations and implementation process",""],[1,"102","13","Climate Change Mainstreaming in Policies and Plans","give special priority to anticipated Climate Change impacts on all relevant matters, and adjust policies and plans,",""],[1,"104","1","Green Economy Transition","Bangladesh ... is committed to establish a 'green economy' of the future in the context of sustainable development goals",""],[1,"104","2","National Sustainable Development Strategy","To address the challenge of mainstreaming sustainable development across sectors and integrate economic, social and environmental objectives across sectors the Government has adopted the National Sustainable Development Strategy (NSDS).",""]],"48":[[1,"464","4","Environmental Management System for Sustainable Development","Ensure appropriate environment management system for sustainable development",""],[1,"465","3","Cleaner and Greener Cities Initiative","Promote activities for cleaner and greener cities",""],[1,"465","4","Environment-Friendly Development Interventions","Promote environment friendly activities in development of interventions.",""],[1,"465","5","Environmental Management Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the capability of public and private sectors to manage environmental concerns.",""],[1,"465","6","Urban Environmental Hazard Monitoring and Prevention","Improve major cities through monitoring and prevention of environmental hazards",""],[1,"489","4","Noise Pollution Control Activities","The following activities will be carried out to control noise pollution.",""],[1,"489","5","Noise Pollution Control Regulation Implementation and Enforcement","Implement and enforce the 'Noise Pollution Control Regulation-2006'",""],[1,"489","7","Urban Noise Monitoring and Reporting","Collect information/data on noise level in different divisional cities and report publication on it.",""],[1,"490","1","Coordinated Planning and Enforcement for Greater Dhaka","An environmentally sustainable greater Dhaka will be founded on coordinated planning and enforcement of plans for the Dhaka region as a whole (the districts of Dhaka, Gazipur, and Narayanganj).",""],[1,"490","12","Stop Encroachment on Greater Dhaka Environment","There has to be a stop form these encroachments.",""],[1,"490","14","Inter-Ministerial Steering Committee for Dhaka Environment Programmes","Forming an Inter-ministerial Steering Committee to oversee the processing and implementation of greater Dhaka environment programmes.",""]],"49":[[1,"461","3","Sustainable Land and Water Management Capacity Building","appropriate policy and institutional capacity building for sustainable land water management, biodiversity conservation, forest ecosystem restoration, climate resilient development and disaster management are crucial at all levels of government, especially with a greater emphasis at the local government level where most of the programmes are to be implemented",""],[1,"461","3","Green Growth Strategy","Seventh Plan will also incorporate a Green Growth strategy to harmonize economic growth for better environmental sustainability",""],[1,"462","12","Poverty-Environment-Climate Nexus Mainstreaming Capacity Strengthening","Efforts are underway to strengthen the Government's capacity to mainstream poverty-environment- climate nexus in the development project design, budgetary process, project implementation and monitoring process.",""],[1,"464","11","Poverty-Environment-Climate-Disaster Nexus Mainstreaming","Mainstream poverty-environment-climate-disaster nexus in the project design phase, budgetary process, project implementation and monitoring processes.",""],[1,"467","1","Environmental Management System for Climate Change Mitigation and Adaptation","Promote appropriate environment management system for mitigation and adaptation to climate change and climate vulnerability",""],[1,"471","2","Pro-Poor Climate Change Management Strategy","This will be achieved through a pro-poor Climate Change Management Strategy, which prioritizes adaptation and disaster risk reduction, and also follow the path of low carbon development, mitigation, technology transfer and the mobilization and international provision for investments in coping mechanisms and green technology.",""],[1,"474","4","Climate Change Adaptation Mainstreaming in Development Planning and Budgeting","The GoB has taken a simultaneous strategy to safeguard its current spending on projects under Annual Development Programme (ADP) from climate induced hazards and use such development practices to ensure adaptation co-benefits.",""],[1,"474","4","Mainstreaming Climate Change Adaptation and Disaster Risk Reduction in ADP Projects","The UNDP provided assistance to the GoB to mainstream CCA along with DRR, poverty alleviation and gender inclusion in all projects under ADP.",""],[1,"475","7","Mainstreaming of Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation","GoB will further mainstream DRR and CCA in policy and planning frameworks of all relevant ministries and departments.",""],[1,"476","7","Climate Change Adaptation Integration in Development Projects","Establish a culture of integrating CCA into all development projects so that adaptation co-benefits may be accrued from development spending.",""],[1,"495","5","Capacity Building for Mainstreaming Environment, Climate Change and Disaster Risk Management","Provide capacity building training on \"Mainstreaming Environment, Climate Change and Disaster Risk Management into Development Planning\" at local and central level.",""],[1,"495","11","Mainstream Environmental Management Across Sectoral Ministries and Agencies","Strengthening of all sectoral ministries and agencies to integrate environmental management and issues into their core operations.",""]],"50":[[1,"50","23","Urban Air Quality Improvement and Clean Air Act","Improve air quality in Dhaka and other large cities and enact Clean Air Act",""],[1,"50","24","Industrial Effluent Zero-Discharge Policy","Promote Zero discharge of industrial effluents",""],[1,"84","24","Urban Air Quality Improvement and Clean Air Act","Improve air quality in Dhaka and other large cities and enact Clean Air Act",""],[1,"84","25","Industrial Effluent Zero-Discharge Policy","Promote Zero discharge of industrial effluents",""]],"51":[[1,"463","3","Brick Kiln Phase-Out Programme","Traditional brick kilns are being phased out, and continuous air quality monitoring stations have been set up in various districts.",""],[1,"468","1","Air and Water Quality Management Improvement","Address major air and water quality management problems",""],[1,"483","6","National Implementation Plan for POPs Phase-Out","Execution of development programmes/projects on National Implementation Plan for the Phase out of POPs will be able to solve this problem.",""],[1,"483","7","E-Waste Rules and Guidelines","There is an urgent need to enact e-waste rules and prepare guidelines based on a baseline survey.",""],[1,"486","5","ISO 14000 Environmental Management Promotion and Plant Audit Programme","Promotion of ISO 14000 environmental management principles, plant audits; promotion of waste minimization through demonstration projects.",""],[1,"486","5","Waste Minimization Demonstration Projects","Promotion of waste minimization through demonstration projects.",""],[1,"487","1","Centralized Treatment Plant for Hazardous Industrial Waste","Establishment of a Centralized Treatment Plant for spent toxic, hazardous chemicals and sludge generated in industrial treatment plants under Public Private Partnership programme.",""],[1,"487","2","Division-wise Lead Acid Battery Recovery and Recycling Plants","Establishment of Division wise Lead Recovery & Recycling Plants for used out lead acid batteries.",""],[1,"487","3","PCB and Redundant Pesticide Recovery and Destruction Projects","Undertaking projects for Recovery and Destruction of PCB's & redundant pesticides (including DDT).",""],[1,"487","4","Mercury Pollution Assessment and Action Plan Development","Initiate assessment / studies to understand the magnitude of the mercury pollution in the country and develop an Action Plan.",""],[1,"487","5","Ship Decontamination and Authorized Ship-Breaking Compliance","Strict compliance to ensure that all ships imported for breaking are decontaminated prior to entering Bangladesh waters and that breaking only takes place in authorized zones after passing environmental checks.",""],[1,"488","5","Air Pollution Reduction Programmes","The following programmes will be initiated by the GoB under the 7th FYP to overcome air pollution:",""],[1,"488","6","Air Quality Management and Monitoring Expansion","Expanding air quality management activities, focusing on gross diesel polluters, and the extension of air quality monitoring to major cities.",""],[1,"488","7","Construction Site Emissions Control Enforcement","Strict enforcement to control dust and other emissions at the construction site",""],[1,"488","8","Brick Kiln Act Enforcement for Traditional Kiln Phase-Out","Strict enforcement of Brick Kiln Act 2013 for phasing out of traditional brick Kiln.",""],[1,"488","11","Brick Kiln Efficiency Improvement Project","In 2010, UNDP launched the Brick Kiln Efficiency Improvement Project to incorporate eco-friendly means of production.",""],[1,"489","1","National E-Waste Assessment and Action Plan Development","Initiating assessment / studies to understand the nature and magnitude of E-waste nationwide and developing an Action Plan.",""],[1,"489","3","Selected Electronic Waste Collection System","Establish efficient collection system for selected electronic waste.",""],[1,"489","12","Toxicological Laboratory Establishment for Adulteration Testing","Establishment of Toxicological Lab with facilities for testing adulteration on fruits, fishes etc. in each regional laboratory of DoE.",""]],"52":[[1,"344","6","Open Water Fisheries Management Measures","The current good practices of open water fisheries management such as replenishing stock and developing and implementing fisheries management regulations; preserving fish sanctuaries; banning fish catch during certain periods and ensuring community based fisheries management; protecting dry season water flows, restoration of habitat and fish species; integrated Coastal Fisheries Resource Management; maintenance of ecosystem health and management of pollution; coping with climate changes has yielded positive results.",""]],"53":[[1,"462","14","Community-Based Adaptation in Ecological Critical Areas","To conserve biodiversity in the Ecological Critical Area (ECAs), Community-based Adaptation approach has been implemented.",""],[1,"463","4","Biodiversity Conservation Programmes for Ecologically Critical Areas","Department of Environment has taken various programmes toward conservation of the biological diversity of Cox's Bazar-Teknaf Peninsula, Sonadia Island, St. Martin's Island and Hakaluki Haor ECAs with a view to ensuring conservation, management and sustainable use of the biological and other resources of the ECAs.",""],[1,"467","14","Ecologically Critical Area Declaration and Management","The DoE also has the legal authority to recognize and manage any ecosystem as an Ecologically Critical Area (ECA).","DoE"],[1,"485","4","Coastal and Wetland Biodiversity Management Project","the government has implemented the Coastal and Wetland Biodiversity Management Project",""],[1,"493","4","Ecologically Critical Areas and Wetland Management Programmes","The following programmes will be initiated to support the effectiveness of Ecologically Critical Areas (ECAs) and Wetland management.",""],[1,"493","5","Declared Ecologically Critical Areas Demarcation Finalization","Finalize demarcation of the declared ECAs",""],[1,"493","6","ECA and Wetland Management Replication and Restoration Programme","Sustaining & replication of ECA & wetland management project(s) in other areas with the ultimate objective of restoration and damage prevention.",""],[1,"493","7","ECA Protection and Restoration Management Plan","Develop ECA specific protection/ restoration management plan in consultation with local community and implement the plan in a time bound manner.",""],[1,"493","8","ECA Co-management Project Continuation and Replication","Sustaining and replication of ECA co-management projects.",""],[1,"493","9","Community-Based Adaptation for Ecologically Critical Areas","Sustaining and replication of community based adaptation of ECAs through biodiversity conservation and social protections.",""],[1,"493","10","Knowledge Centre for ECA and Wetland Management","Creating a knowledge Centre for ECA & Wetland management.",""],[1,"493","11","Wetland Ecosystem Identification and ECA Management","Identification of wetland ecosystems significant for biodiversity to be declared and managed as ECAs.",""]],"54":[[1,"579","18","Natural Resource Restoration and Protection Measures","Restoring or enhancing natural resources · Protecting forests, promoting forest-derived foods to benefit poor/ women",""],[1,"579","18","Secure Land and Productive Resource Rights for Vulnerable Groups","Securing ownership, access and management rights to land and other productive resources for poor or marginalised groups (e.g. ethnic minorities, emergency-affected populations)",""],[1,"579","18","Integrated Water Resources Management and Shock Mitigation","Pro-poor, efficient and integrated management of water resources including control for negative impacts, such as water-borne diseases · Risk mitigation and management of water-related shocks (e.g. droughts, floods, water insecurity) through adequate infrastructure, storage and flood control, supporting adaptation to the effects of climate change",""],[1,"579","18","Early Warning and Nutrition Surveillance Systems","Strengthening early warning and nutrition surveillance systems",""],[1,"579","18","Cross-Sectoral Resilience and Joint Programming","Increase collaboration with other sectors and joint programming to increase household/community resilience, especially in emergencies",""],[1,"579","20","Rights Protection and Non-Discrimination Monitoring","Protect, promote and monitor rights and non-discrimination: right to adequate food and to be able to feed oneself in dignity; and all other -related rights (employment, children's rights; women's rights; water and rights, focus on marginalized groups, poor households and women)",""],[1,"579","20","Refugee and Humanitarian Law Compliance in Protracted Crises","Uphold refugee and humanitarian law in protracted crises",""]],"55":[[1,"720","6","National Social Security Strategy Implementation for Women","The new NSSS is designed to addressing the specific concerns and vulnerabilities of women at different stages of the life cycle.",""],[1,"720","6","Social Insurance for Working Women","The introduction of the proposed social insurance is particularly important mitigation measure for risks faced working women.",""],[1,"724","4","National Social Security Strategy Implementation","For the Seventh Plan, the top most priority is to implement the NSSS.",""],[1,"724","4","Expanded Social Protection Spending","the Seventh Plan also projects to increase the average spending on social protection from 2.0% of GDP to 2.3%.",""]],"56":[[1,"708","5","Skills Building and Livelihood Support for Transgender People","The Government will, in conjecture with NGOs and the private sector, introduce provisions for skill building of transgender who prefer to build their lives around safer occupations in the form of either small entrepreneurship or small cooperative societies.",""],[1,"708","6","Inclusion of Sexual Minority Groups in Social Protection Mechanisms","Sexual minority groups will be integrated in the national social protection mechanisms including access to social health insurance or other transfers to ensure realization of human rights and fundamental freedom of those socially excluded that are most vulnerable.",""]],"57":[[1,"716","3","Expanded Multi-sectoral Violence Against Women Response Programme","The ongoing initiatives under the multi-sectoral Programme and institutional mechanisms would be expanded in more areas.",""],[1,"716","3","Women and Child Victim Support Services Expansion","It is necessary to take women's safety into account and promote various supports and services, i.e. one-stop crisis centre, forensic DNA laboratory, trauma counselling centre, women support centre, 24 hours toll free helpline (10921) for women and children victims of violence under multi-sectoral programmes.",""],[1,"716","3","Violence Against Women Prevention and Awareness Campaign","However, prevention would be emphasized and women's and community awareness of the economic, social and health impact of VAW would be enhanced.",""],[1,"716","3","Women's Legal Aid, Shelter, and Counselling Expansion","Information and support services for women in accessing legal support, shelter, and counselling would be expanded and support for women's economic self-reliance should continue.",""],[1,"716","3","Workplace and Institutional Anti-Sexual Abuse Policy Enforcement","Private and public institutions would be instructed to formulate and enforce policies to protect women from sexual abuse at work places/ educational institutions and other public places.",""],[1,"716","3","Law Enforcement Accountability Mechanism for Violence Against Women","Accountability mechanism would be developed and implemented for the law enforcing agency members in addressing VAW.",""],[1,"717","7","Community Orientation and Public Awareness Campaign on Violence and Sexual Harassment Prevention","Community orientation and motivation by using communication methods and media would be used to create public",""],[1,"718","1","Sexual Harassment Legislation and Enforcement Measures","Steps would be taken to enact legislation to address sexual harassment.",""],[1,"722","1","Equality Promotion Through Behaviour and Media Campaigns","behaviour, media and all other means to promote the culture of equality between girls and boys and their equal human rights is necessary, so that men do not grow up with a discriminatory view towards women.",""],[1,"722","1","Adolescent Clubs for Awareness and Protection","Establishing clubs for the adolescents all over the country will create awareness to reduce sexual harassment, child marriage, and other gender based violence, i.e. eve teasing.",""],[1,"722","2","Social Norm Change and Violence Against Women Reduction Measures","actions that enhances positive social norms and reduces VAW and other harmful practices.",""]],"58":[[1,"695","4","Child Legal Protection and Birth Registration Measures","Legal protection will be achieved by 1) creating a national platform for allowing children to express opinions on their needs; 2) enforcing and harmonizing laws against children abuse, trafficking, exploitation; 3) mobilizing municipal corporations to register all births; 4) eliminating child labour by instigating the National Plan of Action for Implementing the National Child Labour Elimination Policy 2010; and 5) ensuring children are removed from abusive and exploitative circumstances.",""],[1,"696","2","Child Rights Awareness Campaigns","The Government must persist in its efforts to empower children by scaling up awareness campaigns to ensure these laws become common knowledge to all and that every household is sensitized in the different risks children may face.",""],[1,"696","3","Services for Children at Risk Programme","Another programme, the \"Services for Children at Risk\" aims to strengthen the protection of children and the government's capacity to do so,",""],[1,"696","3","Child Helpline Programme","A Child-Helpline Programme is being implemented, 250 Community-based Child Protection Committees are being formed and 7 Integrated Child Protection Service Centres have already been established.",""],[1,"701","5","Child Rights and Development Support Measures","ensuring children's rights and advancement through the implementation of government policies and legislations",""],[1,"701","5","Child Protection from Abuse, Exploitation and Violence","protecting children from all forms of abuse, exploitation and violence",""],[1,"701","5","Child Participation in Programme Design and Evaluation","ensuring participation of children in defining their needs, developing programmes, implementing interventions, and evaluating their success",""],[1,"701","5","Public Support for Child Survival and Development","ensuring widespread public support for survival and development of children",""],[1,"702","6","Child Protection Measures","Measures will be taken to ensure right to protection from abuse, exploitation and violence for all children, particularly those who are vulnerable.",""],[1,"703","1","Child Protection Law Harmonization and Enforcement","Laws affecting children will be harmonized and enforced.",""],[1,"703","1","Training for Law Enforcement and Judicial Officers on Child Protection","Awareness amongst law enforcing officials and judicial officers ... will be undertaken.",""],[1,"703","1","Child Diversion Scheme as Alternative to Custodial Sentences","the development of a diversion scheme involving the courts, social workers and probation officers as an alternative to custodial sentences will be undertaken.",""],[1,"703","2","Universal Birth Registration Mobilization","The Municipal Corporations and Paurashavas will be mobilized to register all births.",""],[1,"703","2","Child Marriage Awareness Campaign","Awareness raising programmes through union Parishad members, and leaders of social opinion including Imams will be conducted to eliminate the practice of early marriage.",""],[1,"703","3","Child Labour Reduction and Worst Forms Elimination Measures","Effective measures will be taken to reduce child labour, and eliminate worst forms of child labour with a particular focus on child domestic workers, migrants, refugees and other vulnerable groups.",""],[1,"703","3","Policy for Children in the Formal Sector","In this context, a policy for children in the formal sector focusing on those caught up in the worst forms of child labour will be formulated.",""],[1,"703","3","Street Children Protection and Rehabilitation Support","Street children will be assisted in accessing their rights and protecting them from all forms of abuse and exploitation.",""],[1,"703","4","Child Abuse Recovery and Prevention Measures","To recover and remove children from abusive and exploitative circumstances, interventions will include developing community support for these children, providing livelihood alternatives, basic services and adoption, and implementing policies and legislation necessary for the prevention of abuse, discrimination, exploitation and violence.",""],[1,"703","4","Child Sexual Abuse and Trafficking Coordination Strengthening","Steps will be taken to increase efficiency to combat sexual abuse, exploitation and trafficking of children through enhanced coordination and cooperation.",""]],"59":[[1,"662","20","Support for Religious Centers and Institutions","The Ministry is responsible for assisting centres (mosques, churches, temples, pagodas and related academies and institutions) in undertaking research and promoting religious values, universal brotherhood and good citizenship",""],[1,"662","20","Religious Welfare Trusts Social Development Activities","Agencies within the Ministry, such as Islamic Foundation, Hindu Religious Welfare Trust and Buddhist Religious Welfare Trust are working within their domains to promote education, literacy, women empowerment under the broad umbrella of human and social development.","Islamic Foundation | Hindu Religious Welfare Trust | Buddhist Religious Welfare Trust"],[1,"663","1","Mosque-Based Child and Mass Literacy Programme","Through the Mosque-based Child and Mass Literacy Programme and the Temple-based Child Literacy and Mass Education Programme, primary school enrolment and literacy rate of adolescents and adults will be raised.",""],[1,"663","1","Temple-Based Child Literacy and Mass Education Programme","Through the Mosque-based Child and Mass Literacy Programme and the Temple-based Child Literacy and Mass Education Programme, primary school enrolment and literacy rate of adolescents and adults will be raised.",""],[1,"663","1","Pagoda-Based Pre-Primary Programme","The Pagoda-based Pre-Primary Programme will widen the reach of the Ministry in educating children.",""],[1,"663","1","New Mosque-Libraries","There will also be opportunities for the general people, especially in rural areas, to study Islamic text in 4500 new mosque-libraries.",""],[1,"663","1","Islamic Mission Complex Construction","The construction of Islamic Mission Complex in 3 hill districts will provide the poor and disadvantaged people with free education and medical care.",""],[1,"663","1","District and Upazila Mosque Construction","The Ministry has taken steps to construct mosques in district and upazila levels to improve and accommodate prayer services.",""],[1,"663","1","Religious Leaders Training and Capacity Building","To enhance the role of religious leaders in social development, proper training and capacity building will be implemented.",""],[1,"663","2","Primary School Enrollment and Adult Literacy Expansion","Increasing the enrolment of six 6+ Childs to primary school, increase the literacy rate of adolescent and illiterate adults and increase opportunity of disadvantaged poor learning of Holy Quran which uplift morality, social and religious values.",""],[1,"663","3","Free Access to Islamic and Socio-Economic Development Books","General People will get chance to study the Islamic & socio-economic development related books at free of cost to foster religious and social values and ideals.",""],[1,"663","4","Medicare Facility Infrastructure Development","Creating Medicare facilities by creating a permanent infrastructural facilities for each Centre.",""],[1,"663","5","Free Medicare Services for Poor and Disadvantaged People","Providing free Medicare service will be given to the poor and disadvantaged people.",""],[1,"663","6","Primary Religious Education Organization and Systematization","The religious education at primary level will be well organized & systemic.",""],[1,"663","7","Temple Financial Support and Library Establishment","Provide financial support for the temples and set up temple based libraries.",""],[1,"663","8","Publication of Religion Books and Restoration of Historical Temples","Publication of Religion books and repairing old & historical temples.",""],[1,"663","9","Buddhist Religious Books Printing and Supply Initiative","To enhance Religious knowledge on Buddhism for Buddhist Community of Bangladesh by Print and supplying Buddhist Religious Books.",""]],"61":[[1,"141","2","Targeted Extreme Poverty Reduction Programmes","the Seventh Plan poverty reduction strategy will accordingly build on this strategy while further sharpening the emphasis on extreme poverty.",""],[1,"141","2","Social Protection Reform for the Extreme Poor","Of particular importance is the need to reform and strengthen the social protection programmes in favour of the extreme poor.",""],[1,"141","2","Inclusion Strategy for Faster Extreme Poverty Reduction","A strong inclusion strategy will also help reduce extreme poverty at a faster pace than before.",""],[1,"143","5","Scale-Up of Targeted Livelihood Programmes for the Extreme Poor","The aim should now be to replicate on a wider scale - and suitably modified where applicable - these programmes to cover most extreme poor groups in the country so as to reduce extreme poverty significantly by the 7th Five Year Plan Period.",""],[1,"144","1","Replication of Successful Targeted Livelihoods Programmes","They include the following: (a) Replication of successful targeted livelihoods programmes;",""],[1,"144","1","Human Capital Development Support for the Extreme Poor","Support for human capital development for the extreme poor;",""],[1,"144","1","Expanded and Inclusive Social Protection for the Extreme Poor","Expanded and inclusive social protection programmes for the extreme poor.",""],[1,"144","1","Market Development and Access Facilitation for the Extreme Poor","promoting market development and facilitating extreme poor's access to the markets for employment and income generation, and empowering the extreme poor will also be given due priority.",""],[1,"144","2","Poverty Reduction Strategy Implementation","Implementation of the above poverty reduction strategy will be the most important element for containing and eventually reducing income inequality.",""],[1,"144","2","Human Development Access Gap Reduction Strategy","Human development strategy with emphasis on alleviating the access gap for the poor is one powerful instrument.",""],[1,"144","2","Poor Households Asset Accumulation Credit Access","Facilitating asset accumulation through better access to credit for the poor can be helpful for reducing income inequality.",""]],"62":[[1,"626","3","Electronic Public Grants Delivery System","Some progress has been made in expanding the use of National ID cards in availing of public services, especially in designing an \"electronic public grants (social safety net) delivery system.\"",""],[1,"626","3","Hard-Core Poor Database Linked to National Population Register","An initiative by Statistics and Informatics Division (SID), under the Ministry of Planning, is creating a hard-core poor database which is going to be linked with the National Population Register (NPR) to identify the most vulnerable, i.e., ultra-poor.","Statistics and Informatics Division (SID) | Ministry of Planning"],[1,"626","3","Pilot Projects for Hard-Core Poor Listing and NPR Integration","In creating a list of the latter and the NPR, the BBS has already carried out pilot projects in two districts - Manikganj and Tangail.",""],[1,"626","3","National ID Enabled E-Services Expansion","National Informatics Committee, being led by the Planning Minister, is exploring the scope for using National ID cards for availing of various e-services.",""],[1,"626","4","National Population Register Development","creation of a NPR, by engaging a diverse portfolio of concerned authorities, is the key to streamline citizen-to-government (C2G) and vice versa, i.e., G2C interactions.",""],[1,"626","4","Citizen Core Data Structure Use for Poverty Database Preparation","Citizen Core Data Structure (CCDS), prepared by the Cabinet Division, is being referred by the BBS in preparing the Bangladesh Poverty Database","Cabinet Division | BBS"],[1,"631","4","Comprehensive Civil Registry Linked to Service Delivery","Development of a comprehensive civil registry that is linked to all service delivery by the government, and preferably also by non-government service providers, will ensure inclusion.",""],[1,"631","4","Whole-of-Government Civil Registry Implementation Approach","A whole-of-government approach, possibly steered by the Cabinet Division, will be necessary to establish and use the civil registry across all service delivery organizations.","Cabinet Division"],[1,"631","4","Low-Cost Financial Inclusion Mechanisms","True financial inclusion mechanisms that provide low-cost mechanisms at citizens doorsteps for banking, money transfer including safety net payments and local and foreign remittances, credit including micro-credit, insurance including crop, health, life, disaster and other kind, must be formulated and popularized.",""],[1,"639","2","ICT-Based Social Security Management Information System","The NSSS will build an extensive network of management information system (MIS) based on ICT that will revolutionize the implementation of the social security system by delivering timely support to the marginalized population of the country.",""],[1,"639","3","Citizen Identification System for Poor Targeting","The Government has developed a uniform system of identification of citizens which is being used in the preparation of the hard-core poor database.",""],[1,"639","3","Inter-Ministerial Coordination for CCDS Beneficiary Targeting","Ministries need to coordinate among themselves under the guidance of the Cabinet Division to enhance use of CCDS for targeting beneficiaries and capturing their information in the database.",""],[1,"639","4","ICT-Based Social Safety Programme Management System","An entity, comprising of relevant officials, needs to be made responsible for identification of beneficiaries of all SSPs using an ICT-based SSP management system, where all nodes of SSP distribution will be linked gradually.",""],[1,"639","5","District and Local Portal Beneficiary Disclosure System","each district portal and subsequently upazila and union parishad portals should publish list of all eligible candidates for each type of SSP.",""],[1,"639","6","Mobile-Phone Based Social Benefit Payment System","SS payments: A system of mobile-phone based payment of benefits will be developed so that target beneficiaries are able to receive payment directly without any other interfaces.",""],[1,"640","1","Automated Cash Grant Delivery System","As the ICT usage matures and gains maximum coverage throughout the country, plans for automated delivery of cash grants will be considered, as solar-power ATMs can be introduced for expediency in local town centres where the literacy rates make such a Programme conceivable.",""]],"63":[[1,"671","10","Social Insurance System","Initiating a social insurance system that enables people to invest in their own social security, providing protection against the risks of old age, disability, social exclusion, unemployment and maternity.",""],[1,"672","11","National Social Insurance Scheme Expansion","Exploring possibilities of providing unemployment, sickness, maternity and accidental insurance as a part of the National Social Insurance Scheme (NSIS)",""],[1,"672","12","Financial Support Programme for Vulnerable Women","Implementing a programme of financial support to vulnerable women (widows, divorced, destitute, single mother, and unemployed single women) and facilitate their participation in the labour market.",""],[1,"672","13","Maternity Insurance through NSIS","maternity insurance through the NSIS as noted above",""],[1,"673","1","Comprehensive Pension System for the Elderly","Comprehensive Pension System for the Elderly: This reformed programme has four components:",""],[1,"673","2","Government Service Pension Continuation","Continue with the Government Service Pension with no change at this time.",""],[1,"673","3","National Social Insurance Scheme","Explore possibilities to establish a National Social Insurance Scheme (NSIS), to be managed under the Insurance Development & Regulatory Authority (IDRA) under the provision of the Insurance Act- 2010, based on the principle of employers and employees jointly paying contribution.","Insurance Development & Regulatory Authority (IDRA)"],[1,"673","4","Private Voluntary Pension Development Review","Review options to facilitate the development of Private Voluntary Pension (PVP), which are open to all citizens irrespective of occupation or formality of employment.",""],[1,"673","5","NSIS and PVP Contribution Financing","The NSIS and the PVP would be funded through employer and employee contributions.",""]],"64":[[1,"675","1","Senior Citizen Hospitality Complex","The Ministry of Social Welfare is going to create a new drive for old aged people with old home and palliative care, namely 'Senior Citizen Hospitality Complex', which will be first time of its kind in Bangladesh to provide international standard services for the senior citizens.","Ministry of Social Welfare"]],"65":[[1,"685","10","Small Bridges and Disaster Shelter Construction and Maintenance","Construction and Maintenance of small bridges/culverts, multi-purpose disaster shelters, cyclone shelters, flood shelters with a view to eliminating/ reducing disaster risks.",""],[1,"688","1","Disaster Shelter Construction and Community Resilience Programme","Massive efforts are underway to create shelters for disasters and to make communities more resilient.",""],[1,"688","1","Additional Coastal Cyclone Shelter Expansion","Besides, additional 400 shelters are targeted to be built by 2020 in all over the coastal belt.",""],[1,"688","1","ADB-Supported Resilient Housing Programme","The Government has targeted to build 97,000 resilient houses with support of Asian Development Bank in year 2015-2020.",""],[1,"688","1","Emergency Cyclone Recovery and Restoration Project","The Government has initiated the Emergency Cyclone Recovery and Restoration Project (ECCRP) to build multipurpose cyclone shelters.",""],[1,"688","1","Food Shelter and Disaster Search-and-Rescue Equipment Provision","MoDMR is also constructing food shelters, procuring search and rescue equipment for earthquakes and other disasters.","MoDMR"],[1,"688","5","Disaster Search and Rescue Equipment Procurement","Procurement of more equipment is under process.","MoDMR"],[1,"692","13","Disaster and Climate Resilient Infrastructure Investment Programme","Promote structural and non-structural investment like disaster and climate resilient housing, roads, embankments, flood and cyclone shelters and other infrastructure construction and risk reduction programmes at community level.",""],[1,"692","16","Earthquake-Resilient Building Retrofitting Programme","Encourage earthquake vulnerable building retrofitting for major cities especially public buildings",""],[1,"693","4","Search and Rescue Equipment Procurement","Procuring search and rescue equipment for earthquake and other disasters",""]],"66":[[1,"527","10","Restructuring of the Bangladesh House Building Finance Corporation","So restructuring of the entity into a more sustainable vehicle for provision of housing to the poor, with better targeted subsidies and stronger fundamentals and efficiency / productivity will be an important strategy to follow.",""],[1,"542","6","Housing Market Regulation and Facilitation Reform","The government's main role will be a regulator and facilitator rather than a provider of low-cost housing.",""],[1,"542","7","Land Market Legal and Regulatory Modernization","The government's role will increasingly be on modernizing the legal and regulatory framework and computerizing the land record system so as to encourage and support land markets that can respond to the variety of demands from different individuals, households and enterprises and investors.",""],[1,"542","8","Efficient Housing Market Regulatory Reform","For encouraging efficient private sector participation in housing delivery, an enabling framework for actors in the market will be created through continuous assessment of housing demand and supply as well as collection, analysis and dissemination of information about housing markets on a regular basis.",""],[1,"542","8","Housing and Land Use Legal and Regulatory Review","legal, financial and regulatory frameworks including land use, building codes, building control and building standards will be reviewed and adjusted from time to time.",""],[1,"542","8","Housing Registration System Simplification","Steps will be taken to simplify the procedure and improve the efficiency of the recording, registration, and mapping of house ownership and transactions.",""],[1,"542","8","Housing Taxation and Fiscal Incentive Reform","Appropriate fiscal measures, including taxation should be applied to promote adequate supply of housing and land",""],[1,"543","2","Housing Finance Mechanism Improvement Strategy","A comprehensive strategy will be developed and pursued together with finance for housing, in parallel to a housing policy and in particular the expansion of affordable housing.",""],[1,"543","3","Mortgage System Strengthening and Land Registration Computerization","Strengthening the foundations of the mortgage system by reinforcing the efficiency of mortgage collateralization and investing in the overhaul of the land registration system and early completion of computerization of land titling and land registration.",""],[1,"543","4","Housing Long-Term Resource Mobilization Measures","Enhance the mobilization of long term resources for housing: allow a diversification of institutional and National Savings Certificate (NSS) portfolios consider the creation of a market based refinancing facility, create \"housing Deposit Pension Scheme (DPS)\".",""],[1,"543","5","Mortgage Market Efficiency and BHBFC Restructuring","Stimulate the efficiency and the dynamism of the mortgage market by ensuring a level playing field and restructuring BHBFC.",""],[1,"543","6","Subsidy Rationalization and Targeted Assistance Policy","Consider rationalizing the mosaic of implicit subsidy mechanisms to develop a policy of well targeted assistance involving the leverage of public support by market resources",""],[1,"543","7","Real Estate Risk Assessment and Prudential Regulation Tools","Develop tools to assess and mange real estate related risks, including market monitoring and transparency and enhanced prudential regulation.",""],[1,"543","8","PPP Housing Implementation Facilitation","Ensure favourable environment for implementers with the provision of low cost, high tech and speedy execution in case of PPP in housing.",""]],"67":[[1,"446","9","Incremental Upgrading of Low-Income Areas","Incremental upgrading of low-income areas.",""],[1,"446","12","Incremental House Improvement Loan Facility","Provision for loans for incremental house improvements.",""],[1,"446","15","Pro-Poor National Urbanization Development","Develop a pro-poor national urbanization development taking into account carefully projected urban migration.",""],[1,"446","16","Low-Cost Housing and Construction Materials Industry Development","Develop low cost housing and construction material industry.",""],[1,"446","17","Compact Development with Basic Services and Facilities","Encourage compact development with all basic services and facilities.",""],[1,"542","8","Housing Support Measures for Poor and Vulnerable Groups","Step should be taken for periodic assessment of the requirements of government intervention to meet the specific needs of people living in poverty and vulnerable groups for whom traditional market mechanism fails to work; and implementation of legal and regulatory reforms for better operation of housing markets.",""],[1,"544","1","Basic Infrastructure and Service Delivery Support Mechanisms","it is necessary to establish support mechanisms to enable people living in poverty and the disadvantaged to have access to basic infrastructure and services.",""],[1,"544","1","Community Participation in Service Prioritization","Steps should also be taken to involve local communities, particularly women, children and persons with disabilities, in decision-making and in setting priorities for the provision of services.",""],[1,"547","2","Easing Access to Land and Housing for the Urban Poor","Easing access to basic services to land and housing used by the urban poor will be a strategic goal to achieve during the 7th plan period.",""],[1,"547","3","Lease-Based Tenure for Publicly Owned Urban Land","In urban and peri-urban areas the government should preferably not transfer land in freehold to occupants, rather choose leases as the instrument for granting tenure for publicly-owned land and especially local authority land;",""],[1,"547","5","Collective Tenure Security and Basic Lease Arrangements","Basic leases should be used along with group tenure arrangements, whereby block is registered under a lease agreement to the group or a local authority.",""],[1,"547","6","Private Land Lease Contract Promotion","Private land-owners should be encouraged to set up lease contracts with occupiers which protect the interest of all parties;",""],[1,"547","7","Scaling Up Poverty Reduction Action Plan","Scaling up of Poverty Reduction Action Plan (PRAP) for addressing poverty with lessons learnt from the relevant ongoing projects ; and",""],[1,"547","8","Community-Based Land Tenure Support and Cooperative Formation","Capacity is built in CBOs/NGOs to assist people in assessing and negotiating their lease conditions, setting up cooperatives associated with group tenure, assisting people in creating land administration rules for their group tenure and in sorting out their group tenure land disputes.",""],[1,"547","9","Special Zones for the Urban Poor","The local authority may zone specific land areas for micro- enterprises, farmer's markets, and areas for hawkers' stalls.",""],[1,"547","10","Special Zones for Low-Income and Informal Settlements","Special zones may also be created for low-income settlements and regularization of tenable informal settlements.",""],[1,"547","11","Block Boundary Recording and Land Information System","Block boundaries should be recorded in the national record system.",""],[1,"548","1","Participatory Informal Settlement Infrastructure Planning","Planning should take place in a participatory way with a view to involve the community and NGOs in servicing options.",""],[1,"548","1","Affordable Incremental Service Connection Infrastructure Design","The design of the infrastructure network should allow for individual, self-funded, incremental service connections and affordable capital, maintenance and user costs for services.",""],[1,"548","1","Infrastructure Network Partnership Financing Mechanism","Funding must be found for infrastructure network (sewerage, solid waste, roads, electricity and water), with individual households taking financial responsibility for their own connections.",""],[1,"548","2","Slum Upgrading and In-Situ Improvement Programme","An approach based on positive attitude and seeking to improve the lives of the slum/squatter dwellers through slum upgrading/improvement should be pursued to meet the sustainable development goal.",""],[1,"548","2","Basic Minimum Services for Slum Dwellers During Relocation","Even where slum clearance is considered essential in public interest, the slum dwellers are entitled to receive basic minimum services until proper relocation and resettlement provisions have been made.",""],[1,"548","2","Resettlement Guidelines for Affected Slum Dwellers","The local authority should draw up elaborate resettlement guidelines so as to reduce the impacts on and sufficiently compensate the livelihoods of the affected people.",""],[1,"548","2","Guideline-Based Relocation and Resettlement of Informal Settlements","All relocation/resettlement of dwellers of untenable slums/informal settlements should be implemented in accordance with the guidelines as prepared.",""],[1,"548","3","Low-Income Housing Loan Programme","The government should take up low-income housing loan programme for providing 'collective credit', that is, offering loans through community organizations for collective housing development.",""],[1,"548","4","Rental Housing Development Support","Development of rental housing, which caters for the needs of the majority of the low-income households, should be encouraged.",""],[1,"548","5","Slum and Informal Settlement Physical Improvement Programme","It is, therefore, necessary to undertake programmes for physical improvement of the slum/informal settlements through preparing community action plan that will greatly facilitate the integration of the settlements with the wider urban area and also improve quality of life of their residents.",""],[1,"549","2","Outsourcing of Upgrading and Service Delivery to NGOs or CBOs","Upgrading/improvement works and delivery of services may be contracted out to NGOs or CBOs as per PPR-2008 if such arrangement is necessary for the sustainability of the system.",""],[1,"549","3","Individual-Based Service Delivery","If possible, delivery of services should be made on an individual basis.",""],[1,"550","3","Urban Poor Social Protection Design Based on NSSS","The National Social Security Strategy (NSSS), 2015 of Bangladesh should be the basis for designing social protection for the urban poor.",""],[1,"550","5","Residential Flats and Plots Construction Programme","construction of 7000 residential flats, and 5000 plots, including those to be implemented through PPPs will be pursued during the 7th Plan.",""],[1,"551","8","Apartment Building Construction","Construction of apartment buildings",""],[1,"552","5","Dormitory Construction for Low-Income Garments Workers","It has also strategy for improving living condition of RMG workers and to promote the development of Garments sector for which CDA with collaboration of BGMEA (Bangladesh Garments Manufacturing and Export Authority) will be constructing a dormitory for the low income worker in the Garments Sector.",""],[1,"553","3","Urban Poor Services and Housing Development Programme","There are also programmes planned for improving services to the urban poor and promotion of housing development",""],[1,"556","8","Low-Cost Housing Support Scheme","the Housing Ministry provides support to low cost housing schemes","Housing Ministry"]],"68":[[1,"544","2","Support for Environmentally Sound Local Building Materials Industries","Appropriate steps should be taken to encourage and support the establishment and expansion of environmentally sound, local building materials industries.",""],[1,"544","2","Incentives and Credit for Sustainable Building Materials","Such supports may take the form of legal and fiscal incentives and provision of credit.",""],[1,"544","2","Promotion of Affordable and Accessible Building Technologies","The use of environmentally sound, affordable and accessible building technologies should be encouraged, and steps should be taken to facilitate transfer of such technologies.",""],[1,"544","2","Technology Transfer for Sustainable Construction","steps should be taken to facilitate transfer of such technologies.",""],[1,"544","2","Research and Development for Sustainable Building Materials","Special emphasis should be given on research and development activities for enhancing the local capacity for environmentally sound production of building materials and construction techniques.",""],[1,"550","6","Construction Materials Innovation and Building Code Update Programme","Housing and Building Research Institute will focus on bringing innovation including alternatives to traditional bricks with a target of achieving zero use of agricultural top soil for brick production, and standardization of construction materials through research.",""],[1,"550","6","Technology Dissemination and Extension Services for Green Building Materials","Special emphasis will be given for extension services to disseminate newly developed technologies and building materials which are agriculture and environment friendly, disaster resilient and affordable.",""],[1,"550","6","Pilot Low-Cost Multi-Storeyed Rural Housing Construction","on a pilot basis steps will be taken for construction of 75 low cost multi-storeyed residential building at different villages during the 7th Plan period.",""]],"69":[[1,"283","2","Digital Bangladesh Programme","The adoption and successful implementation of the Digital Bangladesh programme will also help raise labour productivity, reduce transaction costs, and improve market access as well as customer responsiveness.",""],[1,"302","1","ICT Strategy for the Seventh Plan","An important target for the services exports for the Seventh Plan will be to boost the penetration of Bangladesh into the global ICT market through a well thought out ICT strategy that looks at both domestic market and also the global market.",""],[1,"302","5","Bandwidth Price Reduction","The price of bandwidth needs to be reduced to facilitate increasing number of net users, enhancing demand for local content and applications and developing a connected Bangladesh.",""],[1,"302","5","Rural Telecommunications Network Development and Utilization Guideline Implementation","The Rural Telecommunications Network Development and Utilization Guideline 2010 will need to be implemented to make sure that the existing network infrastructures have been optimally utilized for commercial communication and key social services (e.g. education, health care, e-governance, etc.).",""],[1,"302","5","ICT and Banking Services Tax Policy Revision","the tax rates on ICT services and banking services are very high and may need to be revisited, especially to spur the expansion of ICT.",""],[1,"304","15","ICT Policy Review and Tax Policy Re-examination","the Government will review all ICT policies to ensure their consistency with private incentives for additional investment.",""],[1,"304","15","Rural Broadband Connectivity Rollout Partnership","the Government will invite private sector and not-for- profit sector for rolling out broadband connectivity in rural area.",""]],"70":[[1,"429","11","Vision 2021 Postal System Implementation","Bangladesh Post Office has adopted several steps for implementation of Vision 2021.",""],[1,"430","1","Post Office Automation Programme","Automation of 134 post offices.",""],[1,"430","2","Post e-Centre Rollout in Post Offices","Introduction of Post e-centre in 132 post offices.",""],[1,"430","4","IT-Based Postal Services Expansion","Providing information technology based developed postal services for each and every person;",""],[1,"430","10","Digitized ZIP Code Address System","Ensuring modern ZIP code based digitized address for every person as well as household;",""],[1,"430","12","ICT-Based Post Office Transformation","Transformation of all post offices into ICT based post offices;",""],[1,"430","13","Post Office Automation","Automation of all activities of post offices;",""],[1,"430","21","ICT-Based Postal Services Expansion","Introducing ICT based postal services along with traditional postal services.",""],[1,"430","24","ICT-Based Mail Transportation Supervision System","Bringing Mail transportation, collection and distribution under ICT based strict supervision;",""],[1,"430","25","ICT-Based Training Quality Improvement","Ensuring imparting of high quality ICT based training;",""],[1,"430","28","IT-Based Rural Post Office উদ্যpreneurship Initiative","Adopting activities for making at least one IT based entrepreneur in each of rural post offices.",""]],"71":[[1,"465","16","National Technology Research and Development Initiative","Undertake research and development for innovating technology in national perspective and application of modern technology",""],[1,"481","1","Research and Innovation Investment","Ensuring investment in research and innovation is a first step towards bridging the knowledge gap.",""]],"72":[[1,"645","3","ICT Policy and Institutional Reform Strengthening","a number of policies and institutional reforms will be needed to ensure that the ICT is a resilient institution that is built on strong policy and technical foundations with reliable and open access to all citizens, consistent with national security considerations.",""],[1,"645","5","ICT Policy and Regulatory Reform for Digital Service Delivery","Building on that, the Seventh Plan will review and institute additional policies and regulations in order to scale up and institutionalize ICT-based service delivery, administration and business productivity.",""],[1,"645","6","Tax Reform to Incentivize ICT Private Investment","Accordingly, the taxes will be reduced to make Bangladesh a competitive place for additional FDI inflows into the ICT",""],[1,"646","1","Intellectual Property Valuation Mechanisms","mechanisms for valuation of intellectual property are a high priority for the industry.",""],[1,"646","1","Whole-of-Government Policy and Legal Reform Approach","a whole-of-government approach, although difficult to orchestrate, is most effective for policy and legal reform.",""],[1,"646","2","ICT Public Investment and Financing Mechanisms","it is possible to mobilize finances in a flexible way.",""],[1,"652","4","Legal Framework Review for Science, Innovation, and Technology","Reviewing the legal framework having direct impact on the national science, innovation and technology activities in order to provide effective backward linkage support to industry and economic activities is protecting the consumers and environment;",""],[1,"654","1","E-Government Master Plan Development","Develop an e-government master plan",""],[1,"654","3","Investment Climate Incentives and Institutional Reform","Provide physical incentives & Institutional reform to create appropriate investment climate",""],[1,"662","10","Public-Private Partnership Strengthening Programme","Strengthening of public-private partnership programme.",""]],"73":[[1,"51","9","Cyber Security Institutionalization Measures","Robust cyber security measures are institutionalized",""],[1,"85","11","Cyber Security Institutionalization Measures","Robust cyber security measures are institutionalized",""],[1,"650","1","National Cybersecurity Capacity and Institutions Strengthening","specific steps will be taken to build national capacity and institutions to ensure protection from such criminal activities.",""],[1,"650","1","Centre of Excellence for Secure Software Development","investment would be made to establish Centre of excellences to develop nationally owned/developed software systems to ensure adequate level of security.",""],[1,"650","1","Open-Source Digital Backbone Development Partnership","Bangladesh will develop her own backbones in partnership with local universities.",""],[1,"650","2","Completion of Ongoing Digital Resilience Projects","While Bangladesh is building Tier-2 datacentres in 7 divisional headquarters, and already subscribed to an alternate international internet backbone, efforts would be made to complete the on-going projects in due time.",""],[1,"650","2","National Digital Asset Readiness and Capacity Assessment","An overall national readiness and capacity assessment of safeguarding digital assets in the face of disasters, natural or otherwise, would be carried out immediately and repeated in regular interval.",""],[1,"650","2","Tier IV Data Centre Establishment Project","Moreover, a project has been taken to establish Tier IV Data Centre.",""]],"74":[[1,"718","6","Access to Technology and Information Expansion","Access to modern technology related to business and jobs would be expanded at a low cost.",""],[1,"719","1","Media and ICT Access Expansion for Women","production or business opportunities would be increased through using media and ICT.",""],[1,"719","1","Mobile, Internet, and Radio Access for Women","Increased access to mobile phones, internet and radio etc., will help women in accessing information.",""],[1,"719","1","Strengthening of a2i Outreach to Young Girls","The a2i to reach young girls should be strengthened and be responsive to the needs of less educated persons.",""]],"75":[[1,"44","3","Beneficiary Rights and Digital Service Delivery Reform","At the same time, bottom up reforms were put in place to ensure the rights of intended beneficiaries.",""],[1,"44","5","Civil Service Innovation Fund for Service Delivery","Encouragement and policy support from senior officers at the ministry and directorate levels to take risks coupled with a Service Innovation Fund to incubate innovation in service delivery is recognizing, rewarding and catalysing new and promising ideas from field level officers in re-engineering, decentralization and public-private partnerships.",""],[1,"44","5","Government-Private-Civil Society Collaboration Mechanisms","mechanisms have been created by the government, private sector and civil society that allow people to come together for development.",""],[1,"45","5","Service Delivery Process Reengineering","Service delivery processes have been reengineered to provide greater access to common people, particularly those living in remote, rural areas.",""],[1,"45","5","Digital Centres Network","Digital Centres - over 5000 ICT based one stop outlets run by 'citizen entrepreneurs', one within 4 km of every citizen in Bangladesh- provide 4.5 million citizens access to public information and services (birth certificates, land records, passports, and application to various other government services) as well as private services (mobile financial services, insurance, various types of computer and vocational training, etc.) each month.",""],[1,"46","1","National Portal Integration and E-Service Expansion","The National Portal, the world's largest government portal with 2 million contents, has virtually integrated nearly 42,000 offices of the government in one address bangladeh.gov.bd and has become the boldest driver of progressive information disclosure by various government agencies.",""],[1,"46","1","Digital Centres Programme","The Digital Centres won ITU's World Summit on the Information Society (WSIS) Award in 2014 and the National Portal in 2015 - a rare feat by the same country in consecutive years.",""],[1,"46","1","Annual Electronic Service Delivery Commitment","Each Ministry has signed an Annual Performance Agreement (APA) with the Cabinet Division to launch a new electronic service every year - this one initiative alone could significantly and rapidly change the service delivery paradigm from one falling prey to unscrupulous middle-men to one that is driven by a culture of transparency, accountability and responsiveness.","Each Ministry | Cabinet Division"],[1,"51","4","Digital Government Payment Transfers","All G2P cash transfers and most P2G and B2G payments done digitally",""],[1,"51","5","Digital Public Service Delivery Expansion","Most vital government services are made available at all Digital Centres, through the national portal and over mobile devices; 100% of citizens and residents have digital ID that is used in service delivery",""],[1,"51","7","Open Government Data and Big Data Analytics for Public Decision Support","Open government data and big data analysis are regularly used in public decision support.",""],[1,"56","2","Digital Bangladesh Initiative Expansion","The strong progress with the implementation of the Digital Bangladesh Initiative during the Sixth Plan provides a solid foundation on which the Seventh Plan can build forward.",""],[1,"56","2","ICT Legal and Regulatory Framework","The Plan stresses on creating the enabling legal environment with the effective rules and regulations for greater use of ICT in every sphere of life.",""],[1,"85","6","Digital Government Payment Transfers","All G2P cash transfers and most P2G and B2G payments done digitally",""],[1,"85","7","Digital Public Service Delivery Expansion","Most vital government services are made available at all Digital Centres, through the national portal and over mobile devices; 100% of citizens and residents have digital ID that is used in service delivery",""],[1,"85","9","Open Government Data and Big Data Analysis for Public Decision Support","Open government data and big data analysis are regularly used in public decision support.",""],[1,"212","5","Union Information Centres","union information centres have improved transparency at the local level",""],[1,"212","5","a2i Local E-Governance Initiative","The a2i initiative has brought progress in the state of e- governance at the local level through the implementation of a well-designed programme of ICT, hardware and software, technical assistance and training programmes.",""],[1,"212","6","Digital Bangladesh ICT Expansion Initiatives","The Government has also taken numerous initiatives to implement the Digital Bangladesh vision.",""],[1,"213","2","Government ICT Skills Development and Unified Public Website Architecture","The two, interrelated objectives, are to (i) impart ICT skills to the Government officials, in order to (ii) bring all public websites and their information under a single architecture, adhering to a common design in terms of content and structure.",""],[1,"213","23","E-Purjee Collection Service through Union Digital Centers","E-Purjee can be collected from any UDCs located at the vicinity of the sugarcane producers.",""],[1,"437","1","One Stop Service Centre Expansion","One Stop Service Centre has been introduced in few City Corporations and Paurashavas.",""],[1,"437","10","Local E-Governance ICT Support Initiative","The a2i initiative has brought progress in the state of e-governance at the local level through the implementation of a well-designed Programme of ICT, hardware and software, technical assistance and training programmes.",""],[1,"445","3","Local-Level E-Governance ICT Programme","The Government will facilitate e-governance at the local level through a well-designed Programme of ICT, which involves providing adequate hardware and software, technical assistance and training programmes.",""],[1,"445","3","a2i Integration with Local Government Activities","more initiatives will be taken to integrate it further with the activities of the local Governments.",""],[1,"446","5","ICT Intervention Acceleration","Expedite ICT intervention",""]],"76":[[1,"663","10","Environment and Social Awareness Programmes","the Department of Mass Communication will conduct numerous environment and social awareness programmes.","Department of Mass Communication"],[1,"663","10","Digitization of Bangladesh Television and Bangladesh Betar","various mediums like Bangladesh Television and Bangladesh Betar will be digitized.",""],[1,"663","10","Digital Preservation of Mainstream Newspapers","Mainstream newspapers will be preserved in digital form for future reference.",""],[1,"663","10","Overseas Capacity Building for Sector Officials","officials will undergo capacity building with training abroad.",""],[1,"663","11","Expansion of FM Radio Stations and Modernization of Bangladesh Betar Facilities","During the 7FYP Bangladesh Betar shall adopt programmes of establishing more F.M based radio stations, expansion and replacement of existing old facilities by modern and digital technology.",""],[1,"664","1","Community Radio Network Expansion","Whole country will be covered by community radio network in future.",""],[1,"664","2","Bangladesh Television Infrastructure Expansion and Digital Modernization","Bangladesh Television (BTV), the state owned Television network in Bangladesh has been undergoing through development of infrastructure facilities, expansion and digital/ modernization process.",""],[1,"664","2","Licensing of New Television Channels","To create facilities to watch and enjoy television broadcast by more people in the rural area, the government has permitted license to 41 new television channels to operate.",""],[1,"664","2","Policy for Licensing FM Radio Stations and Private Television Channels","To strengthen private sector media coverage the Ministry of Information have taken up a policy to granting license to F. M Radio stations and private television channels as per existing rules.","Ministry of Information"],[1,"664","4","Bangladesh Betar Modernization Programme","Improve, up-grade, modernize and replace the existing logistic and technical facilities of Bangladesh Betar gradually for its responsible, uninterrupted service and CD quality radio programmes.",""],[1,"664","5","Digital Sound Recording and Archiving Upgrade","Improve the quality of sound recording by incorporating digital recording and digital archiving",""],[1,"664","6","Bangladesh Betar Studio Modernization","Establish new studio and improve studio facilities of Bangladesh Betar with full digital equipment",""],[1,"664","8","Digital Audio Broadcasting Media Campaign","Introduction of text message, video clips of artists along with Radio Programme by adopting digital Audio Broadcasting Techniques.",""],[1,"664","9","Satellite Radio Broadcasting Introduction","Introduction of satellite Radio broadcasting in the very near future.",""],[1,"664","10","SMS-Based Interactive Musical Entertainment Programme Expansion","Expansion of SMS based interactive and request oriented entertaining musical Programme.",""]],"77":[[1,"614","3","Knowledge Commercialization Incentives and Institutional Arrangements","Economic incentives and institutional arrangements to support the creation, acquisition and conversion of knowledge into usable form based on research and innovations by public and private enterprises.",""],[1,"617","3","University-Based ICT Incubator at CUET","Bangladesh's first university based incubator is being established at the campus of Chittagong University of Engineering and Technology (CUET).",""],[1,"617","5","ICT Special Purpose Facility and IT Park Development","To establish special purpose facility to meet unique infrastructure requirement of the ICT industry, Kaliakoir Hi-Tech Park, Janata Tower Software Technology Park and Jessore Software Technology Park are being implemented.",""],[1,"617","5","Private Software Technology Park Approval","BHTPA has already approved 3 (three) private Software Technology Parks.",""],[1,"617","5","Proposed IT Village and City Park Development","Moreover, STP/HTP/IT parks have been proposed: Mohakhali IT Village, Silicon City Rajshahi, and Electronic city Sylhet.",""],[1,"617","5","District IT Park Project and Training Incubation Centres","\"Twelve (12) IT park Project \" of Unique design in Dhaka, Comilla, Chittagong, Cox's bazar, Gopalganj, Jamalpur, Mymensingh, Sylhet, Rangpur, Khulna, Barisal & Nator District and \"IT training incubation centre\" in different places.",""],[1,"632","1","ICT Export Expansion Strategy","The government's target is to expand ICT exports to $5.0 billion by FY2020.",""],[1,"632","1","ICT Research and Development Investment","Policies will need to focus on expanding ICT infrastructure, improving incentives by lowering taxes on ICT products, greatly expanding the ICT skills base and investing in ICT-related research and development.",""],[1,"633","3","Technology Parks and BPO Center Expansion","To this end, more Hi-Tech Parks and Software Technology Parks will be established throughout the country.",""],[1,"633","3","District and Sub-district BPO Center Development","Besides, Business Process Outsourcing (BPO) centers will be set up in district and sub-district level.",""],[1,"633","3","Union Digital Center Conversion to BPO Centers","Steps will be taken to gradually convert the potential Union Digital Centers into Business Process Outsourcing centers by providing high speed connectivity and other necessary infrastructure.",""],[1,"633","4","Innovation Ecosystem and Startup Incubation Initiative","For this purpose, an innovation ecosystem comprising of required infrastructure, well trained human resources and supportive policy regime will be established.",""],[1,"633","4","Tech Startup Nurturing Programme","Hence, steps will be taken to nurture the tech startups in Bangladesh.",""]],"78":[[1,"259","8","Scaling Up Infrastructure Investment","It is recognized by the Government and has prioritized scaling up infrastructural investment in the annual budgets.",""],[1,"259","8","Large Transformational Infrastructure Projects","the Government has undertaken a number of large transformational projects in the areas of energy, power, deep sea port, railway, expressways, and bridges.",""],[1,"262","5","Private Sector Investment Enabling Environment Reform","In facilitating development of the private sector and SME, the primary role of the government will have to be to create investment friendly law and order situation, supportive legal and regulatory framework and appropriate macroeconomic policies.",""],[1,"262","5","Prioritized Public Investment for Structural Bottlenecks","These will need to be complemented by prioritized public investment designed to ease various structural bottlenecks pertaining to physical and infrastructural facilities, energy, and technology.",""],[1,"265","4","Social Mitigation Measures for Price Alignment Reforms","and measures to mitigate adverse social consequences of reforms needed to align domestic to international prices.",""],[1,"267","5","Corporate Tax Incentive Reform","corporate tax regime with appropriate incentives",""],[1,"267","5","Intellectual Property Rights Strengthening","strong intellectual property rights",""],[1,"267","5","Rule of Law Strengthening","rule of law",""],[1,"267","5","Financial System Development and FERA Modernization","a developed financial system, including modernization of Foreign Exchange Regulation Act (FERA) 1947",""],[1,"267","7","Liberalized Investment Policy Regime","A liberalized investment policy regime, which offers scope for international firms to have unlimited stake in the local firm.",""],[1,"267","8","Joint Ventures with Established Global Value Chain Actors","Joint ventures with established actors within the GVC will allow the diffusion of technology, which ultimately boost the export potential of the local firm.",""],[1,"267","9","Local Firm Innovation and Technology Upgrading Support","Local firms must have the capacity to innovate and acquire a basic level of technological standard, so that such types of cooperation are possible.",""],[1,"268","3","Investment Climate Improvement Measures","The Government must recognize that the FDI sector is an integral part of the economy - essential to restructuring the economy and raising national competitiveness .- by putting in place market economy institutions and a sound legal framework; building an advanced and integrated infrastructure, particularly transport and ports; removing complexity in land entitlements and mutations, and developing a quality workforce.",""],[1,"268","4","Adequate Power Supply Provision","Provision of adequate power supply,",""],[1,"268","7","Tax and Customs Administration Reform","reforms in tax and customs administration,",""],[1,"268","8","Contract Enforcement Legal Reform","legal reforms that ensure enforcement of contracts,",""],[1,"268","9","Special Economic Zone Expansion","setting up more special economic zones to overcome the land constraint,",""],[1,"273","1","Special Economic Zones Development Programme","Bangladesh can implement Special Economic Zones (SEZs) as a way of catalysing the desired private sector investment to propel the economy towards 7-8% rate of GDP growth.",""],[1,"273","2","Special Economic Zones Development Programme","The government plans to develop five special economic zones in to attract both foreign and domestic investments.",""],[1,"274","3","Sub-sector Study Programmes","The Commission has undertaken a set of sub-sector study programmes for the interest of Bangladesh economy; some of those subsectors are the Agro- Processing Industry, Dairy Products, sanitary and phyto-sanitary measures (SPS) and Technical Barriers to Trade (TBT) Impact in the Import Policy, Natural Flower, Ship Building, Jute Industry, Melamine Industry, Motorcycle Industry and Cement industry.",""],[1,"274","3","BTC Planning Cell and Office Building Development","During the tenure of the 7th FYP BTC will develop a planning cell and construct a permanent office building to assess the supply gap of essential commodities.",""],[1,"274","4","CCI&E Online Trade Registration and Digitalization System","The Office of the Chief Controller of Imports and Exports (CCI&E) aims to promote national trade and generate more revenue by provision of online facilities to allow submission of application for an import, export & indenting registration to the CCI&, by digitalizing of all existing records, formulation of Import Policy Order 2015-2018 that is under progress, Integration of online payment facility and digital signature into the system and implementation of online module system by IFC.",""],[1,"274","7","Consumer Rights Protection Regulatory Body","The Directorate of National Consumer Rights Protection (DNCRP) has been established as a regulatory body to safeguard consumer rights by implementing Consumers Rights Protection Act-2009, conducting surveys of products, goods and/or services regarding consumer safety, providing suggestions and recommendation to the government in the preparation of policies for consumer protection.",""],[1,"280","3","Electricity Supply Expansion and Power Sector Reform Programme","During FY11-15, the government, therefore, adopted a strong and well-rounded reform programme to increase the supply of electricity involving substantial investment, sector reforms and regional trade in electricity.",""],[1,"280","3","Continued Power Supply Expansion and Cost Reduction Efforts","So, continued efforts are needed to expand power supply and reduce the average cost of production over the 7th FYP period.",""],[1,"281","2","Female Employment Regulation and Support Measures","proper employment regulations to facilitate the participation of female workers (e.g. maternity leave, skill development, child care facilities, etc.) have to be put in place in most areas of employment.",""],[1,"281","2","RMG Worker Safety and Working Conditions Improvement","Thanks to recent coordinated efforts of the Government with the Apparel Manufacturers, and the buyer-driven initiatives.",""],[1,"281","3","Business Law Improvement for Contract Enforcement","there is still much to be done in improving business laws to ensure enforcements of contracts.",""],[1,"281","3","State-Owned Enterprise Rationalization","Scaling down the coverage and size of SOEs is still needed to provide impetus to private enterprises which often face uneven competition from SOEs in procurement of raw materials and breaking into export markets (e.g. jute textiles).",""],[1,"281","7","Industrial Estate Environmental Infrastructure","Other goals include installing Central Effluent Treatment Plants and dumping yard and infrastructure development of the park for establishment of Active Pharmaceutical Ingredient (API) Industries",""],[1,"282","4","Sugar Mill Production Capacity Strengthening and Sustainability Programme","This organization is committed towards the strengthening and sustaining of the production capacity of the existing sugar mills, to meet the local demand by producing white sugar from imported raw sugar, reduce dependency on private sector and stabilize the domestic market and benefit the consumers.",""],[1,"282","4","Organic Bio-fertilizer and Biogas Production Initiative","BSFIC also aims to produce environment friendly organic Bio- fertilizers, Bio- gas that will reduce fuel consumption, increase sugar cane production and also consider using molasses to produce alcohol/spirit.",""]],"79":[[1,"7","4","Private Investment Mobilization and PPP Promotion","The Plan will be implemented by mobilizing the private investment, with focus on PPP initiative and FDI attracting, where public investment will create the investment climate for a favourable pro-business growth.",""],[1,"11","4","Private Investment Mobilization through PPPs and FDI Attraction","The Plan will be implemented by mobilizing the private investment, with focus on PPP initiative and FDI attracting, where public investment will create the investment climate for a favourable pro-business growth.",""],[1,"12","4","Capital Formation and Investment Mobilization Strategy","The 7th Plan will pursue a strategy for capital formation by mobilizing higher domestic and foreign investment and harnessing the labour force by utilizing demographic dividend for achieving 7.4% annual average growth rates.",""],[1,"12","4","Investment Climate and Infrastructure Improvement Measures","Improving the investment climate in favour of quality infrastructure and manufacturing, expanding market opportunity through world trade, improving efficiency of the financial sector, managing the land constraint and improvements of governance are other critical areas that would receive increased attention for accelerating growth, environmental sustainability and social advancement.",""],[1,"12","5","Private Sector Support Policies and Programmes","the planning process, therefore, involves focus on policies and programmes to support the private sector",""],[1,"12","5","Medium-Term Public Investment Programme","the planning process, therefore, involves focus on policies and programmes to support the private sector and also to formulate a strong medium-term public investment programme.",""],[1,"48","2","Public and Private Investment Scaling","Both public and private investment rate will need to increase.",""],[1,"48","2","Public Investment Efficiency Improvement","Additionally, the efficiency of domestic investment, particularly in the public sector, will be important for realizing the maximum benefits out of the limited public sector investments.",""],[1,"48","6","Seven-Year Plan Investment Financing Framework","Total investment over the 5 year of the 7th Plan will amount to Tk. 32 trillion in constant FY16 prices (the first year of the Plan).",""],[1,"48","6","Private Sector Investment Mobilization","As during the 6th Plan, private sector investment will continue to play its dominant role, accounting for 77% of the total planned investment.",""],[1,"48","6","Foreign Investment Inflow Expansion","the role of FI would need to increase significantly.",""],[1,"48","6","Foreign Investment Inflow Target","Increasing the inflow of FI in Bangladesh to 3% of GDP would be critical for achieving the financing of the investment target of the 7th Plan.",""],[1,"48","6","External Financing for Private Investment","Thus, the external financing for private investment, comprising primarily private FDI and external borrowing in foreign currency by the private sector, will increase markedly in the 7th Plan as compared with the 6th Plan.",""],[1,"49","1","Public Investment Programme Priorities","Public investment priorities will emerge from the key 7th Plan targets with respect to real GDP growth, poverty reduction and social protection for the poor and the vulnerable.",""],[1,"53","6","Public-Private Partnership Strategy Reform","Reform the PPP strategy with a view to achieving stronger progress under this approach in the 7th Plan;",""],[1,"90","6","Inclusive Growth and Employment-Generating Investment Strategy","The strategy of the 7th FYP is to ensure that the growth acceleration does occur by putting place the right combination of investment in human and physical capital supported by the right package of policies.",""],[1,"97","5","Investment Reallocation Toward Infrastructure and Manufacturing","Improving composition of investment in favour of infrastructure and manufacturing.",""],[1,"97","5","Foreign Direct Investment Mobilization for Infrastructure","The massive demand for infrastructure investment will also have to be met from FDI, which calls for a radical improvement in the investment climate.",""],[1,"99","4","Infrastructure Public-Private Partnership Financing Framework","Improving the investment climate and developing appropriate policy and regulatory framework will be critical to attract private investment, both domestic and foreign, in infrastructure.",""],[1,"113","2","Increase National Investment Rate","higher growth in the 7th Plan is also predicated upon a substantial increase in the investment rate in the economy from the current level of about 28.9% of GDP to more than 34.4% by the end of the Plan, averaging 32% of GDP per year during the Plan period.",""],[1,"113","3","Foreign Direct Investment Mobilization","foreign direct investment is expected to play a bigger role under this Plan.",""],[1,"114","6","National Investment Climate Improvement Policies","Public investment in nationally important mega projects and national policies to improve the overall environment for investment will be critical in boosting investors' confidence (both national and foreign).",""],[1,"116","1","Public-Private Partnership Pipeline Expansion for Infrastructure Investment","The Government expects that the Public Private Partnership (PPP) in infrastructure investment will gain momentum, particularly in power generation, as the PPP office under the Prime Minister's Office are putting effort to build up a larger pipeline for PPP projects.","Prime Minister's Office"]],"80":[[1,"302","4","Continuation of Service Sector Deregulation Policy","The Government will continue this policy during the Seventh Plan.",""],[1,"303","9","Non-Labour Export Services Expansion","Increase the growth of non-labour export services focused specifically on ICT, international transport and tourism",""],[1,"304","9","Private Investment Incentive Policy Reform for Services","Improve the incentive policies for boosting private investment in services.",""],[1,"304","10","Public Investment in Key Service Sector Infrastructure","Increase public investment in key service sector infrastructure.",""],[1,"304","11","Service Industry Skills Development","Strengthen the skills base for the service industry",""],[1,"304","12","Strengthening of Prudential Regulation Implementation","Strengthen implementation of prudential regulations to boost service quality, increase public safety, improve compliance and ensure accountability of service providers.",""],[1,"304","13","Public Institution Strengthening for Service Sector Development","Strengthen public institutions to support the growth of services sector and improve service quality, safety and accountability.",""],[1,"304","14","Service Sector Deregulation and Regulatory Reform","the deregulation drive to motivate greater private provision of services sector activities will continue.",""],[1,"304","14","Regulatory Consultation and Feedback Mechanism for Service Providers","Each line Ministry concerned with regulating a particular service will undertake dialogue with concerned service providers through public meetings with business chambers and conduct special purpose surveys as necessary to obtain specific feedback on regulatory burden or other constraints.",""],[1,"304","14","Policy and Institutional Reform Based on Consultation Findings","The findings of these consultations and surveys will be used to reform policies and institutions as relevant.",""],[1,"304","14","Foreign Investment Promotion in Export-Oriented Services","Foreign investment in export oriented services will be promoted, especially with a view to importing technology and thereby increasing service quality and export competitiveness.",""],[1,"304","14","Technical Skills Import Facilitation for Priority Services","Import of technical skills in the area of aviation, international shipping, ICT and tourism will be facilitated.",""],[1,"304","14","Foreign Joint Venture Promotion","Wherever possible, joint venture with foreign partners will be encouraged.",""],[1,"307","1","Strengthening the Services Sector Regulatory Framework","the Seventh Plan will seek to strengthen the regulatory framework for services sector",""],[1,"307","2","Services Sector Regulatory Framework Review and Modernization","all regulatory authorities dealing with transport, trade, education, health, tourism and ICT will be asked to look at the adequacy and relevance of all concerned regulatory issues, both prudential and enabling, with a view to upgrading and modernizing the regulatory framework for services sector.",""],[1,"308","2","Specialized Task Forces to Review Service Regulatory Agency Capacity","The Seventh Plan will commission specialized task forces to review the capacity of each of these agencies with a view to determining specific ways these agencies can be strengthened to improve export competitiveness of aviation, shipping services, tourism and ICT.",""],[1,"312","3","Regulatory and Incentive Policy Improvement for Services Investment","The improvements in regulatory and incentive policies will spur the expansion of private domestic and foreign investment.",""],[1,"312","3","Complementary Public Infrastructure Investment for Services Sector Expansion","Yet, complementary public investments in fixed infrastructure will be a critical determinant for expansion of private investment in services.",""],[1,"312","4","Services Sector Modernization Investment Expansion","To secure the modernization of the services sector both public and private investment will need to go up as a share of GDP.",""],[1,"312","4","Regulatory and Incentive Reforms for Private Investment","Along with reforms of regulations and incentives for private investments, these complimentary public investments will be necessary to spur the expansion of private investment.",""]],"81":[[1,"52","2","Prudential Regulation Enforcement for Service Quality and Safety","Strengthening implementation of prudential regulations to boost service quality, increase public safety, improve compliance and ensure accountability of service providers;",""],[1,"52","2","Overseas Employment Recruitment Monitoring and Enforcement","Strengthen monitoring and enforcement services on overseas employment related recruitment services and vii) Strengthening public institutions to support the growth of services sector and improve service quality, safety and accountability.",""],[1,"52","2","Public Institution Strengthening for Service Sector Support","Strengthening public institutions to support the growth of services sector and improve service quality, safety and accountability.",""],[1,"52","3","Support for Banking, Financial, and Social Sector Development","The strategy will also continue to support the development of banking and financial activities, education, health, transport and trading.",""],[1,"102","7","Maritime Industry Development and Maintenance","maintaining existing (e.g., ship building) and developing new maritime industries;",""],[1,"102","11","Competitive Tourism Industry Development","(vii) creating a competitive tourism industry, including ecotourism and marine cruises,",""],[1,"102","12","Domestic Fleet and Port Connectivity Expansion","further increasing revenue from shipping and commerce by the expansion of domestic fleet and destinations, transhipment and transit provisions, linking neighbouring states to the sea-ports, etc.",""]],"82":[[1,"429","2","Diversification of TSS Manufacturing and Assembly Activities","TSS management took initiatives for diversification of the activities of TSS and established four Manufacturing/Assembling units for PSTN land telephone sets, Mobile Phone Battery, Mobile Phone Battery Charger and Digital Electric Meter.",""],[1,"429","2","Affordable Laptop and Notebook Assembly","To provide Laptop/Notebook at an affordable price, TSS assembles Laptop/Notebook so that the people can buy them at a competitively lower price.",""],[1,"429","2","Maintenance-Free Battery Manufacturing Proposal","It also has a proposal for manufacturing Maintenance Free VLRA Battery and other types of Battery which can be used in mobile industry.",""],[1,"429","2","Digital PABX Supply and Installation","TSS is a well- known and long reputed supplier of Digital PABX of different brands.",""],[1,"429","2","Optical Network Unit Supply and Installation","Beside these, TSS is going to supply and install Optical Network Unit (ONU) and related equipment to different exchanges of BTCL.",""]],"83":[[1,"470","4","Industrial Policy and Enterprise Reform Programme","MoI has sought to accelerate industrialization through formulating appropriate industrial policy, reforming and renovating state owned enterprises, developing SMEs, micro and cottage industries, protecting standards of products and intellectual property rights and enhancing productivity.","MoI"],[1,"470","4","Eco-friendly Industrial Infrastructure Development and Regulation","MoI is also entrusted with establishing, developing, and regulating eco-friendly and safe industrial infrastructure.","MoI"],[1,"480","7","Energy-Efficient Manufacturing Upgrade Support","Large RMG and textile manufacturers can tap into multilateral expertise and funding to switch to cost-effective production that reduces energy costs.",""],[1,"480","10","Industrial Greenhouse Gas Emissions Reduction Measures","GoB will increase efforts to reduce greenhouse gases from manufacturing industries such as cement and steel rerolling.",""],[1,"480","10","Dairy Sector Emissions Reduction Incentives","Further incentives will be given to reduce emissions in the dairy sector.",""],[1,"480","10","Low-Carbon Development Strategy Development","LCD strategy will be developed in collaboration with relevant ministries and agencies along with mainstreaming the National Action Plan on Short-lived Climate Pollutants in all the relevant mitigation sectors.",""]],"84":[[1,"717","3","Growth and Employment Strategy Implementation","Implementation of the growth and employment strategy of the Seventh Plan will create new jobs for the growing labour force.",""],[1,"717","3","Private Sector Wage Equality Regulation and Monitoring","The private sector will be regulated and monitored in enforcing equal wage and benefits for women and men as per Labour laws and the ILO Conventions.",""],[1,"717","3","NSSS Implementation for Women's Formal Employment","The implementation of NSSS will be a major step forward to encourage women participation in the formal work force.",""],[1,"717","5","Women’s Self-Employment Support Initiative","The large number of micro-finance users, the unemployed school graduates and dropouts, and the unpaid family labourers are the main groups who will contribute to family and for growth, if they are introduced to simple time saving and green technology, information about markets, source of finance and training.",""],[1,"717","5","Private Sector and Civil Society Support for Women’s Self-Employment","Ensuring support from private sector, NGOs, business associations and media is also important.",""],[1,"717","6","Women Entrepreneurship Support and Business Development Services","Women entrepreneurship needs to be supported and entrepreneurs are to be prepared to qualify for institutional finance, i.e. they have to be prepared with required paper work, business planning, financial management and such other.",""],[1,"717","6","Women Entrepreneurs Business Capacity and Finance Linkage Support","Bangladesh Women Chambers of Commerce and Industry and some others are working to develop business capacity of women entrepreneurs and linking them with the banks and PFIs.",""],[1,"717","6","District-Level Entrepreneur Support Initiatives","All chambers and associations would be encouraged to take similar initiatives for entrepreneurs at the district levels.",""],[1,"717","6","Business Incubator Expansion by Chambers and Associations","Business incubator services would be expanded by the chambers and associations.",""],[1,"717","6","Trade Fair and Value Chain Participation Support","Opportunities to participate in trade fairs and higher levels of the value chains would be created.",""],[1,"717","6","Women in Value Chains Technology and Input Support","Scope for women at different levels of the value chain of different products would be identified, disseminated and supported with technology and inputs.",""],[1,"717","6","Ethnic Crafts Promotion Initiative","Ethnic crafts would be promoted.",""],[1,"721","1","Women’s Access to Employment, Skills, and Entrepreneurship Support","Providing women with greater access to employment guarantee schemes, skills development, technology, entrepreneurship support and training would continue.",""],[1,"722","2","Gender Wage Gap Reduction and Workplace Bias Elimination","narrowing of wage gap between similarly qualified male and female workers; elimination of all types of biases against female staff at the work place;",""]],"85":[[1,"283","11","Technology Dissemination Cell for Industrial Development","Collect information on industrial development and arrange for technology dissemination through the Technology Dissemination Cell, set up at the Ministry of Science and Technology.","Ministry of Science and Technology"],[1,"284","6","R&D Incentives and Green Technology Transfer Support","Arranging for incentives to be given for research and development, acceptance and transfer of environmentally friendly appropriate technology.",""],[1,"284","6","Market-Oriented Technology Development Institutional Reform","At the same time, develop market-oriented institutional structure in overall technological development.",""]],"86":[[1,"240","3","Manufacturing Sector Industrial Upgrading","A high level of industrial sophistication meeting internationally recognized standards of product quality, within a compliant production environment, must be attained by the manufacturing sector to be globally competitive.",""],[1,"240","3","Open and Seamless Trade Facilitation Regime","It must also be supported by a trading regime that is open and seamless in the movement of import-export cargo",""],[1,"245","6","Selective Bonded Import Facility Expansion","Moreover, the Government has been selectively according bonded import facilities to more emerging exports (e.g. agro-processing, ship building).",""],[1,"245","6","Extension of Bonded Import Facilities to Dual-Market Industries","In future, this facility may not be limited to 100% export-oriented industries only but extended to industries producing for both domestic and export markets.",""],[1,"245","6","Duty Drawback Scheme Revamp","Further, the Duty Drawback Scheme is expected to be revamped to ensure world-priced inputs to exporting firms without long lags and high transaction costs for reimbursements.",""],[1,"251","6","Tariff Regime Restructuring for Export Diversification","Bangladesh would have to restructure its tariff regime in order to gradually phase out effective protection levels and anti-export bias.",""],[1,"252","3","Bali Package Implementation for Preferential Market Access","Bangladesh seeks full implementation of Bali package so that the decision can be operationalized properly and much desired commercially preferential market access is achieved.",""],[1,"252","4","WTO Negotiations for TRIPS Waiver Extension on Pharmaceuticals","Bangladesh remains engaged in negotiations in the WTO to extend TRIPS waiver for pharmaceuticals products beyond 2016.",""],[1,"253","4","Trade Facilitation through Rules of Origin Simplification and Preferential Trade Cooperation","simplification of RoO with India and a selective cooperation in the form of a PTA/general trade cooperation agreement with China would be the preferred solutions to facilitate exports to these countries.",""],[1,"253","4","Compliance Support for Japanese Product Standards","Surely, Bangladesh can have a larger share of $35 billion Japanese apparel market if it can remain compliant with Japanese product standards.",""],[1,"254","7","Comprehensive Trade Policy","The Comprehensive Trade Policy (CTP) of Bangladesh aims to achieve accelerated and sustainable economic growth by an integrated trade approach.",""],[1,"254","11","Export Production Network Strengthening","To strengthen production networks of existing and new export products, thereby improving Bangladesh's position in global value chains.",""],[1,"254","12","Trade and Investment Competitiveness Enhancement","To increase Bangladesh's international competitiveness by creating a conducive environment for private sector trade and investment including reliable infrastructure, an effective transport network, coherent and enforceable trade-related policies and strengthened institutions;",""],[1,"255","1","Trade Agreement Negotiation and Market Access Expansion","To create favourable market access conditions through taking maximum advantage of existing trade agreements and engaging actively in the exploration of new bilateral and regional trade and investment agreements;",""],[1,"255","4","Establish Ministry of Commerce as National Trade Policy Authority","To establish MoC as the national competent authority and apex organisation in all matters relating to trade policy formulation.","MoC"],[1,"255","7","Export Policy Strengthening for Export-Led Growth","Export Policy is geared towards strengthening export-led growth leading to job creation, poverty reduction, and higher growth.",""],[1,"255","7","Market Access Expansion for Non-Traditional Export Markets","CTP incorporates initiatives for expanding market access to non-traditional markets, and through PTAs and FTAs at regional or bilateral levels.",""],[1,"255","8","Import-Export Policy Linkage Reform","Two major areas of reform include establishing better linkages between import and export policies",""],[1,"255","8","Ministry of Commerce Trade Policy Coordination Capacity Strengthening","and enhancing the capacity of the MoC to steer and coordinate trade policies and trade instruments.","MoC"],[1,"255","9","Central Coordination Policy Mechanism for Export Promotion","the CTP will serve as the central coordinating policy mechanism to steer public sector initiatives augmenting export and dismantling any anti-export bias of the policy regime",""],[1,"255","10","Enhanced Integrated Framework Trade Capacity Building Initiative","The main objective of the EIF is to support LDCs in trade capacity building and integrating trade issues into overall national development strategy.",""],[1,"255","11","Implementation of the DTIS Action Matrix","The next step will be implementation of the Action Matrix.",""],[1,"256","1","National Trade Portal Setup","Ministry of Commerce is in the final stages of setting up a National Trade Portal (NTP set to be launched in August, 2015.","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"256","7","Export Diversification Strategy","The government's focus on export diversification as a cornerstone of its export policy will continue and intensify during the Seventh Plan period and beyond.",""],[1,"257","2","Export Competitiveness Improvement Measures","Ensuring export competitiveness in general - by addressing border barriers (e.g. tariffs) and beyond-the border constraints (e.g. trade infrastructure, energy and telecommunications, regulations, finance).",""],[1,"257","3","Trade Regime Reform to Reduce Anti-Export Bias","Eliminating or reducing the built-in anti-export bias that still remain will be key to switching the incentive regime in favour of exports.",""],[1,"257","4","Reduction of Anti-Diversification Bias in Trade Policy","This particular feature of anti-diversification bias could be unique to Bangladesh and will be addressed during the Seventh Plan.",""],[1,"257","10","Goods-to-Services Export Diversification","Goods-to-services diversification - seeking opportunities to expand non-merchandise exports.",""],[1,"260","5","Trade and Transport Logistics Infrastructure Investment","Through adequate investments in trade and transport logistics and infrastructure to facilitate growth of trade and investment, and by aggressively pursuing trade facilitation at the land and sea borders, by the close of the 7th Plan, Bangladesh is expected to improve its ranking in all of the component indicators of Ease of Doing Business by moving up at least 25% over its current rank (Table 2.8).",""],[1,"260","5","Trade Facilitation at Land and Sea Borders","Through adequate investments in trade and transport logistics and infrastructure to facilitate growth of trade and investment, and by aggressively pursuing trade facilitation at the land and sea borders, by the close of the 7th Plan, Bangladesh is expected to improve its ranking in all of the component indicators of Ease of Doing Business by moving up at least 25% over its current rank (Table 2.8).",""],[1,"262","1","Export Duty Drawback Scheme","In addition to the duty drawback scheme that accords to all exporters, the RMG exporters enjoy the special privilege of paying only a nominal income tax on their earnings.",""],[1,"262","1","Concessional Income Tax Treatment for RMG Exports","The income tax is fixed at a low level on total gross earnings of the RMG sector as a withholding tax, which is also the final tax.",""],[1,"262","1","Annual Cash Subsidy for Non-Traditional Exports","the government offers direct cash subsidy to exports of non-traditional items, announced on an annual basis, with the rate varying from 5% on jute goods to 20% on potatoes in FY2014.",""],[1,"265","3","Export Diversification Policy Package","A strategy for diversification of exports must include a policy package that is multifaceted and comprehensive covering constraints at the borders, behind the borders (supply side), and beyond the borders (market access issues).",""],[1,"265","4","Tariff and Non-Tariff Barrier Reduction and Customs Facilitation","Addressing constraints at the borders implies a focus on tariff and non-tariff barriers to imports and exports, as well as better customs facilitation;",""],[1,"265","4","Anti-Export Bias Policy Reform","against a background of appropriate macroeconomic framework (including low inflation, realistic exchange rate, low fiscal and external deficits), anti-export bias policies, and measures to mitigate adverse social consequences of reforms needed to align domestic to international prices.",""],[1,"265","5","Export Diversification Support Measures","Addressing constraints behind the borders implies addressing supply side constraints (Infrastructure, trade-related Institutions, policy constraints, including adequate business regulatory framework, and investment policy regime), competitiveness constraints (standards, packaging, quality, and delivery in time), and needed support incentives (fiscal incentives and credit incentives) for export diversification, including emphasis on R&D for developing improved products or moving up the value chain.",""],[1,"265","6","Export Growth Support through Market Access, Infrastructure, and Trade Institutions","Addressing constraints beyond the borders implies addressing market access barriers to export growth.",""],[1,"266","5","Integration into Asian Production Networks and Value Chains","Bangladesh should be vigorously looking for opportunities to integrate with Asian production networks and value chains, during the 7th FYP period.",""],[1,"267","5","Import Liberalization Reform","import liberalization",""],[1,"272","1","Foreign Currency and Exchange Regime Liberalization","In the first place there is a huge deregulation agenda, especially in the area of foreign currency regulation.",""],[1,"272","1","Simplification and Digitalization of Regulatory Procedures","the government's regulatory policies in the areas of foreign currency transactions, licensing, accreditation, import of trained foreign experts, visas, and foreign investments have to be vastly simplified and digitalized.",""],[1,"274","1","Export Market Diversification and Promotion Programme","To expand and diversify exports, Export Promotion Bureau (EPB) has set a goal of achieving export earnings at US$ 60 billion by FY 2016-FY2020 through the exploration of ten new export markets, addition of at least ten new products in the export basket, capacity building of EPB officials and establishment of a permanent Fair Complex to oversee the organization of trade fairs.",""],[1,"274","1","Trade Fair and Market Exploration Missions","Sending marketing mission for exploration of new markets, participation in International Trade Fairs for market exploration, issuing GSP certificates through automation system and increasing supply side capacity of the exporter by removing hindrances in the supply chain are some crucial programmes to be adopted.",""],[1,"274","2","Trade Liberalization Policy Advisory and Tariff Rationalization","The Commission will continue its activities to making appropriate policy recommendations for trade liberalization.",""],[1,"274","2","Unfair Trade Remedies and Safeguards Function","Moreover, the Commission is designated to perform works on issues related to unfair trade such as issues related to dumping, subsidy & countervailing, safeguard measures.",""],[1,"274","2","Competition and Market Access Policy Recommendations","The Commission will continue to make policy recommendations to the government on inducing greater competition in industrial production; encouraging efficient use of resources in the economy, obtaining greater market access through bilateral, regional and multilateral trade agreements including WTO issues.",""],[1,"275","1","Export Promotion Bureau Strengthening as Trade Promotion Organization","The strategy would be to make EPB more effective as a TPO over the next five years.",""],[1,"275","1","Trade Regulatory and Border Process Improvement","there is a critical need to improve the regulatory framework and processes at and behind the border, covering a wide range of efficiency improvements, such as,",""],[1,"280","2","Trade Liberalization and Anti-Export Bias Reduction","a much faster pace of trade liberalization and commensurate measures to minimize if not eliminate anti-export bias of the existing trade regime.",""]],"87":[[1,"120","1","Foreign Direct Investment Facilitation for Traditional and New Sectors","In order to facilitate FDI in the traditional and new sectors, the government is accelerating the process of setting up Special Economic Zones under both public and private sector initiatives.",""],[1,"120","1","Special Economic Zone Allocation to Foreign Investors","It also plans to hand over SEZs to investors exclusively from Japan, China, India and other countries in order to accelerate investment from those countries.",""],[1,"129","9","Special Economic Zones Establishment","special emphasis will be given to the alleviation of the infrastructural bottlenecks through establishment of SEZs in various parts of Bangladesh",""],[1,"155","9","Lagging Districts Manufacturing Promotion Support","Manufacturing activity needs to be promoted in the lagging districts.",""],[1,"155","10","Industrial Investment Incentives for Lagging Districts","Industrial policy would incorporate enough flexibility for incentivizing investment in lagging districts with the help of tax breaks, lower interest rate and similar other policy interventions.",""],[1,"155","11","Special Economic Zones in Lagging Districts","Lagging region would get priority while setting up special economic zones.",""],[1,"156","1","Special Investor Incentive for Industrial Park Investment","Promulgation of special incentive for prospective investors would proceed simultaneously to encourage faster investment in this industrial park.",""],[1,"160","1","Investment-Friendly Environment and Infrastructure Constraint Reduction","the government's role will be to create the investment friendly environment and ease infrastructure constraints for the private sector to come forward with the desired levels of investment.",""],[1,"160","1","Regulatory Reforms for Private Savings and Investment","Through public sector investment in infrastructure and social development and through regulatory reforms conducive for private savings and investment, the Government will try to achieve the economic and social development objectives established under the Plan.",""],[1,"160","2","Special Economic Zones Serviced Land Access Initiative","In addition major initiatives will be taken to broaden and accelerate the implementation of other major highways and bridges, power sector projects, and providing access to serviced land to foreign and domestic investors in the context of the Special Economic Zones (SEZ) initiative.",""],[1,"161","1","Foreign Direct Investment and External Financing Expansion","increasing the inflow of FDI in Bangladesh to 3% of GDP from current levels of about 1% would be critical for achieving the financing of the investment target under the Seventh Plan.",""],[1,"202","2","Private Investment Policy and Regulatory Framework","For private investment this consistency requires adoption of right policies, regulations and institutions that guide private investment in the required sectors.",""]],"88":[[1,"119","4","Export-Led Growth Strategy","The 7th Plan aims to reach the export target of US$54.1 billion with export growth averaging about 12% per annum over the Plan period.",""],[1,"119","5","RMG Export Growth Strategy","As in the past, RMG sector will continue to lead the export growth strategy under the Plan.",""],[1,"119","5","RMG Sector Export Expansion Investment","The envisaged US$20 billion increase in the RMG sector exports over the Plan period will require massive amounts of investment in this sector along with investment in growth supporting infrastructure like power/electricity, land for setting up industries, transport, port etc.",""],[1,"119","5","Footwear and Leather Export Sector Development","The other potential export sector is footwear and leather products, which is growing at a healthy pace and the growth rate is expected accelerate with new factories likely to coming into operation, and growing interest of foreign investors in the footwear sector.",""],[1,"119","6","Non-Traditional Export Expansion Support","some non-traditional exports like light engineering (bicycle and electronic products), Information Technology (IT), home textiles, agricultural and food processing, pharmaceuticals and shipbuilding have good potentials and expected to expand rapidly under the 7th Plan.",""],[1,"122","4","Export Proceeds Retention Liberalization","Bangladesh Bank has already increased the level of retention of export proceeds by the exporters as part of its ongoing exchange market liberalization.","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"122","4","Further Increase in Export Proceeds Retention","Bangladesh Bank will consider further increases in the percentage of export proceeds that could be retained by the exporters in order to reduce cost of inputs and make manufacturing and exports more competitive.","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"142","7","Labour-Intensive Manufacturing and Export Diversification Strategy","In manufacturing the effort will concentrate on labour intensive manufacturing with focus on export diversification.",""],[1,"142","7","Formal Services Expansion and Non-Factor Services Export Promotion","The services sector is projected to grow faster than GDP based on emphasis to formal services including exports of non-factor services (tourism, shipping and ICT).",""]],"89":[[1,"243","5","SME Refinancing Window","In order to support the SME activities, Bangladesh Bank has established a refinancing window which includes Tk. 600 crores coming from BB, $125 million equivalent from the ADB, and Yen 5000 million by the Government of Japan.","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"243","5","Cluster-Based SME Programmes","different financial institutions are also specifically focusing on cluster based SME programmes.",""],[1,"262","3","SME Niche Identification and Support Services Mobilization","This will mean exploring market opportunities on a sustained basis and mobilizing the required support services for the promotion of these industries once such niches are identified.",""],[1,"262","4","SME Foundation Capacity Strengthening","The capacity and activities of the SME Foundation needs to be strengthened to this end.",""],[1,"262","4","National SME Census","Also, a national SME census needs to be conducted through Bangladesh Bureau of Statistic (BBS) in order to create a comprehensive information repository regarding the SME sector.",""],[1,"263","2","Differentiated Indirect Tax and Graduated Turnover Tax System for SMEs","A graduated system of turnover tax can be designed for the SMEs for this purpose.",""],[1,"263","6","Comprehensive SME Credit Policy","The comprehensive credit policy for SMEs developed by the Bangladesh Bank constituted a key element of the Plan measures.","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"263","7","Area and Cluster-Based SME Credit Disbursement","Following Bangladesh bank and SMEF guidelines, area and cluster approach is to be adopted in SME credit disbursement.",""],[1,"263","8","SME Census and Identification Card System","To strengthen targeting of SME credit, the Plan provided for (i) a census of SMEs containing detail information on inputs, output, technology and management, (b) issuing identification card with",""],[1,"264","1","SME Registration and Database Development","registration number to the SMEs, (iii) creating a database of SMEs and updating it periodically, and (iv) creation of detail upazila level map of SMEs to identify cluster.",""],[1,"264","2","SME Loan Product Development Requirement","The financial institutions will be required to develop loan products that relate better to specific type of credit needed in SMEs.",""],[1,"264","3","Subsidized Credit for Clusters and Disadvantaged Regions","Provision of subsidized credit to clusters, disadvantaged groups and backward regions with close monitoring.",""],[1,"264","4","Bank Official Training and SME Cell Establishment","Training of bank officials and setting up of SME cells for identifying potential borrowers, loan disbursement, monitoring use of credit and collection of loan.",""],[1,"264","5","Wholesale Credit to Partner NGO-MFIs for Small and Micro Enterprises","PKSF will continue to wholesale credit to its partner NGO-MFIs for small and micro enterprises.",""],[1,"264","6","SME Credit Wholesaling Loan Programme","SME Foundation will continue providing loans at single digit interest rates to local SMEs through its credit wholesaling programmes.",""],[1,"264","7","SME Credit Disbursement Expansion","credit disbursement to SMEs has been geared up following Bangladesh Bank guidelines",""],[1,"264","7","SME Database Development","A prerequisite for this is the creation of SME database",""],[1,"264","9","National SME Cluster Development Action Plan","SME Foundation has identified 177 SME clusters scattered throughout Bangladesh, and is now formulating a National SME Cluster development action plan for improving the competitiveness of the SME Clusters.",""],[1,"264","10","Support for Women Entrepreneurs through SME Foundation","SME Foundation has been working to bring women entrepreneurs into mainstream development process.",""],[1,"265","1","Women Entrepreneurship Development Programme","Women entrepreneurship development programme of SME Foundation will be prioritized and strengthened under the 7th Plan.",""],[1,"265","1","Institutional Capacity Building for Women Chambers and Trade Bodies","Other activities include institutional capacity building of women chambers and trade bodies, formulating gender action plan, encouraging bankers to finance women entrepreneurs, conducting study and survey on women entrepreneurs, organizing women entrepreneur conferences and skill development programme, national SME women entrepreneurship award, SME product fair for women entrepreneurs, etc.",""],[1,"265","1","Gender Action Plan Formulation","Other activities include institutional capacity building of women chambers and trade bodies, formulating gender action plan, encouraging bankers to finance women entrepreneurs, conducting study and survey on women entrepreneurs, organizing women entrepreneur conferences and skill development programme, national SME women entrepreneurship award, SME product fair for women entrepreneurs, etc.",""],[1,"265","1","Financing Support for Women Entrepreneurs","Other activities include institutional capacity building of women chambers and trade bodies, formulating gender action plan, encouraging bankers to finance women entrepreneurs, conducting study and survey on women entrepreneurs, organizing women entrepreneur conferences and skill development programme, national SME women entrepreneurship award, SME product fair for women entrepreneurs, etc.",""],[1,"265","1","Women Entrepreneur Study and Survey","Other activities include institutional capacity building of women chambers and trade bodies, formulating gender action plan, encouraging bankers to finance women entrepreneurs, conducting study and survey on women entrepreneurs, organizing women entrepreneur conferences and skill development programme, national SME women entrepreneurship award, SME product fair for women entrepreneurs, etc.",""],[1,"265","1","Women Entrepreneur Conferences and Skills Development Programme","Other activities include institutional capacity building of women chambers and trade bodies, formulating gender action plan, encouraging bankers to finance women entrepreneurs, conducting study and survey on women entrepreneurs, organizing women entrepreneur conferences and skill development programme, national SME women entrepreneurship award, SME product fair for women entrepreneurs, etc.",""],[1,"265","1","National SME Women Entrepreneurship Award","Other activities include institutional capacity building of women chambers and trade bodies, formulating gender action plan, encouraging bankers to finance women entrepreneurs, conducting study and survey on women entrepreneurs, organizing women entrepreneur conferences and skill development programme, national SME women entrepreneurship award, SME product fair for women entrepreneurs, etc.",""],[1,"265","1","SME Product Fair for Women Entrepreneurs","Other activities include institutional capacity building of women chambers and trade bodies, formulating gender action plan, encouraging bankers to finance women entrepreneurs, conducting study and survey on women entrepreneurs, organizing women entrepreneur conferences and skill development programme, national SME women entrepreneurship award, SME product fair for women entrepreneurs, etc.",""],[1,"281","7","SME Development and Industrial Estate Expansion","The Corporation is mostly committed towards the setting up and development of SMEs in the country other for creating, employment opportunity and to help increasing GDP growth through the establishment and extension of Industrial Estates in various districts of the country.",""],[1,"281","7","Modern Beekeeping and Honey Production Support","to meet the national demand of honey and increased production of quality honey through modern bee-keeping technology.",""]],"90":[[1,"615","5","Digital Technology for Private Sector Productivity and Competitiveness","Making the private sector and market more productive and competitive through the use of digital technology.",""],[1,"617","6","Annual Fairs, Exhibitions, Workshops, and Road Shows for Local Enterprises","Progress has made in arranging annual fairs, exhibitions and targeted workshops for local enterprises and organizing road shows and other interactive programmes such as seminars.",""],[1,"618","1","ICT-Based MSME Promotion Initiative","the promotion of ICT based model targeting micro, small and medium enterprises (MSMEs) will play important role in fostering entrepreneurships in the country",""],[1,"618","1","Software Company Growth Potential Study","SME Foundation has undertaken a project to study growth potentials of software companies and constraints limiting the exploitation of those potentials",""],[1,"630","1","Review of ICT Tax Regime","Accordingly, the Government will review the tax regime for ICT and ensure that the taxation regime is friendly to the ICT and is supportive of the implementation of the Digital Bangladesh vision.",""],[1,"631","5","ICT Productivity Tools Adoption Incentives","Appropriate productivity tools will be adopted alongside incentives for quick adoption.",""],[1,"631","6","IT/ITES Industry Expansion and Skills Development","A collaborative approach is necessary to develop technical and soft skills necessary for the sector, generate employment for local, foreign and outsourced jobs.",""],[1,"631","6","ICT Infrastructure Development for IT/ITES Growth","Additionally, establishment of necessary infrastructure, special focus on international brand image of the country, and access to finance for entrepreneurs is required to tap into the imminent demographic dividend.",""],[1,"632","1","ICT Export Expansion Strategy","The government's target is to expand ICT exports to $5.0 billion by FY2020.",""],[1,"632","1","ICT Tax Incentive Reform","Policies will need to focus on expanding ICT infrastructure, improving incentives by lowering taxes on ICT products, greatly expanding the ICT skills base and investing in ICT-related research and development.",""],[1,"633","2","EEF-IT and SIF Support to Private and Public Sectors","The Government will continue to provide support to both private and the public sectors through the EEF-IT and the SIF respectively.",""],[1,"646","4","ICT Technology Parks Software Capability Development","The government will continue its efforts to develop the software capabilities through ICT Technology Parks.",""],[1,"646","4","Private Investment Incentives for Software Development","Private investment in software development will be promoted through public research grants and tax incentives.",""],[1,"646","4","Commercialization and Scale-Up Support for R&D Innovations","Provision for necessary public funding will be made to commercialize and scale up of the new and innovative products and services developed through R&D initiatives in both public and private sectors.",""],[1,"646","5","ICT Export Marketing and Branding Initiative","a key policy effort to support the expansion of ICT exports is to market and brand Bangladesh ICT products for the international markets.",""],[1,"652","5","Private Sector Research and Development Promotion","Attracting more private sector in supporting, leading and performing research and development;",""],[1,"653","19","R&D Funding for ICT and Science and Technology","Provide funding for R&D in ICT & Science and Technology",""],[1,"654","2","Product Innovation and Creation Ecosystem Support","Support product innovation & creation ecosystem",""]],"91":[[1,"44","3","Agricultural Input, Extension, Credit, and R&D Support","Policy driven resources were made available from the top to support availability of inputs, extension services, credit to farmers and R&D to meet the challenges for increasing productivity and sustainability.",""],[1,"44","3","IT-Enabled Agricultural Extension and Technology Diffusion","Bank accounts were opened for as small as Tk. 10, beneficiary cards were issued and beginning was made to leverage IT enabled services for extension services, crop protection and technology diffusion.",""],[1,"52","4","Agricultural Commercialization and Productivity Support","the overall strategy for 7th FYP will be to accelerate the process of transformation from already existing semi-subsistence farming to commercialization of agriculture.",""],[1,"52","4","Agricultural Diversification, Value Addition, and Agro-processing Promotion","This strategy will require achieving productivity gains, diversification, value addition and agro-processing commensurate with national environmental protection and climate change adaptation strategies.",""],[1,"52","4","Agricultural Technology, Extension, and Small Farmer Credit Support","for the crop sub-sector, encouraging agricultural growth through various policy changes/adjustments ranging from applying new technology and extension services to providing credit to small farmers will be intensified.",""],[1,"52","5","Agricultural Extension and Research Capacity Strengthening","A very important part of the strategy for the agriculture sector as a whole will be strengthening extension and research capacity of different Departments, Institutes, and Universities.",""],[1,"142","7","Agricultural Diversification and Productivity Improvement","Additionally, emphasis will be placed on agricultural diversification, an area where the performance of the Sixth Plan was lagging.",""],[1,"155","7","Expansion of Agricultural and Fisheries Storage Facilities","Storage facilities for agricultural and fisheries would be increased according to the demand of such facilities in lagging districts where economic activities are mostly agricultural in nature.",""],[1,"155","7","Rural Storage Facility Enhancement","Such facilities would be enhanced in the remote areas so that farmer gets most benefit from such facilities.",""],[1,"316","6","Agricultural Production Diversification Incentive Policy Regime","the Government is mindful of the need for maintaining a policy regime to incentivise and motivate farmers to diversify agricultural production toward increased production of cash crops.",""],[1,"317","6","Sustainable Agricultural Growth through Efficient Resource Use","Ensure sustained agricultural growth through more efficient and balanced utilization of land, water and other resources.",""],[1,"317","8","Promotion of Non-Crop Agricultural Activities","Promote non-crop agricultural activities related to forestry, livestock and fisheries.",""],[1,"321","3","Post-Harvest Management, Processing, and Storage Investment for Potato and Vegetables","It will be difficult to sustain the growth of production of these high-value and labour-intensive crops unless investment is made in the post-harvest management (a 10% reduction of post-harvest loss would add 10% additional food for the nation), processing and storage to stagger marketing of the crops throughout the year to match the demand that remains stable across the season.",""],[1,"322","4","Agricultural Productivity and Diversification Programme","These will need to come from increasing agriculture-product diversification and consumption for improving nutrition; increasing resource use efficiency and judicious use of agricultural inputs; promoting science-led agricultural technology systems and dissemination of improved technology; reducing loss of arable land; minimizing yield gap; production, distribution and preservation of quality seeds; reduce output loss through technology based weather prediction and forecasting and better crop disease management and bio-control of pest; shifting where feasible to higher-value crops for commercialization including increasing quality horticultural crop production; reducing instability and production costs; popularizing of good agricultural and IPM practices; linking farm-produces with market so as to overcome the issue of low price of products at farm level, low investment in agriculture and inadequate credit support to farmers; facilitating increased private investments in agriculture and agro-processing value chains alongside public investments, and more public private partnerships; ensuring safety and quality agro-produces; expanding irrigation and farm mechanization with appropriate technology including better use of renewable energy; developing resilience to climate change impacts; expanding agriculture to the newly accrued coastal land and marine islands; identifying and removing structural bottlenecks have to be in place.",""],[1,"323","5","Agricultural Commercialization and Value Chain Development","Crop agriculture is mainly operated yet at subsistence or semi- commercial level, which needs to be commercialized with high value crops such as aromatic rice, vegetables and fruit production and processing.",""],[1,"323","5","Good Agricultural Practices for Production and Post-harvest Management","Good agricultural practices need to be employed for production and post-harvest management.",""],[1,"323","5","Smallholder Market Integration Support","small holders need to be enabled to integrate in the markets to effectively contribute to the production of high value crops.",""],[1,"323","5","Agricultural Credit and Service Access Expansion","they need better access to credit and other agricultural services - such as extension, information and local market infrastructures and services.",""],[1,"323","5","Private Investment in Agriculture Value Chain Development","there needs to be more private participation and investments in the agriculture value chain development.",""],[1,"323","5","Jute Production Market Support","Fair price and market access to encourage farmers will be ensured to further intensify jute production in order to satisfy domestic and export demand.",""],[1,"324","2","Agro-Processing Value Chain Support","To ensure that their production and export potential are fully realized, the government needs to continue its current commitment to investing in manufacturing and infrastructure, but more so in facilitating private participation in different aspects of those value chains.",""],[1,"325","2","National Farmers' Database Development","Finally, in order to achieve the objectives of 7th FYP, a national farmers' database need to be developed for smooth implementation of agricultural policy, protecting the rights of farmers and intellectual properties developed by the farmers.",""],[1,"325","3","Agricultural Supply Chain Extension and Market Linkage Initiative","The development vision for agriculture under the 7th Five Year Plan is to ensure food and nutritional security, enhancement of sustainable intensification and diversification of climate resilient agricultural production with increased commercialization, and livelihood improvement through technological innovations and use, strengthening of research and extension system, developing supply chain extension, value addition of agricultural products, and linking farming community with markets, both local and global.",""],[1,"325","5","Agro-based Industrial Expansion and Agricultural Export Promotion","Develop agriculture as a basis for agro-based industrial expansion while encouraging export of such agro-processed/agricultural commodities, particularly aromatic and premium quality rice, potatoes, vegetables and fruits keeping in view domestic production and consumption needs and ensuring fair market price of the produces for sustainable and profitable agriculture;",""],[1,"327","1","Agricultural Growth Support Measures","All out support will be provided to achieve the stipulated objectives in the field of crop production, yield gap minimization, expansion of irrigation facilities, quality seed production & distribution, Good Agricultural Practices (GAP), farm mechanization, quality horticultural crop production and popularization of IPM practices.",""],[1,"330","3","Agricultural Diversification and Horticultural Crop Expansion","Agricultural diversification will allow shifting from cereal-cereal cropping patterns to cereal and non-cereal based high value cropping patterns with value added product, including expansion of horticultural crops, promoting sugar beet production and processing it as sugar crop.",""],[1,"330","3","Small and Marginal Farmer Market Linkage Support","Policy support will also be provided to small and marginal farmers in selling their surplus products at remunerative prices by linking them with domestic and international markets.",""],[1,"330","3","High-Value Crop Development and Value Chain Expansion","Agricultural diversification will also achieved by further development of jute, cotton, quality tea production for local consumption and exports as well as that of aromatic rice and commercial flower cultivation, their marketing, and development of associated value chains.",""],[1,"331","5","Good Agricultural Practices Protocol Development and Promotion","Protocol development for Good Agricultural Practices (GAP) suitable for Bangladesh agro-ecological and socio-economic conditions should be the major priority as required under the new Agricultural Policy.",""],[1,"331","7","Agro-Processing Facility Development and Capacity Expansion","Development of agro-processing facilities can prevent postharvest losses and enhance farmers' income.",""],[1,"331","7","Refrigerated Transport for Agricultural Produce","efforts will be made to make available refrigerated compartments in train and also refrigerated vans for the transport of agriculture produces",""],[1,"332","1","Agro-Business Support Programme","The process of supporting agro-business will be continued and strengthened during the Seventh Plan period.",""],[1,"332","2","Agricultural Value Chain Development","In the seventh five year plan the approach will be applied to other crops such as aromatic rice.","MOA"],[1,"332","2","Agricultural Marketing Efficiency Improvement","The main effort will be to improve the efficiency of agricultural marketing to reduce market distortions and the cost of marketing, and to ensure that farmers get proper price for their produce and consumer gets quality products.",""],[1,"332","2","Phytosanitary Capacity Development for Traceability","For quality control and ensuring traceability, phytosanitary requirements, Department of Agricultural Marketing (DAM) will need to be involved and its capacity developed.","Department of Agricultural Marketing (DAM)"],[1,"332","2","HORTEX Value Chain Promotion Board","the establishment of HORTEX, a private board for value chain promotion for high value commodities, is an important institutional development.",""],[1,"332","2","Private Sector-Led Value Chain Development","Strengthening the institutional capacity and reducing financial and regulatory constraints to address the complex production and marketing constraints including developing a viable private sector led value chain will be an important strategic issue to address.",""],[1,"332","2","Agricultural Technology Support Services Strengthening","For value chain development augmentation of required technological support services should also be strengthened.",""],[1,"332","3","Agricultural Credit Access Improvement","the government through its various agencies is trying to improve access and availability of credit at lower interest rate especially for production of pulse, oilseed and spice crops.",""],[1,"333","10","Priority Support for Marginal and Small Farmers","Marginal and small farmers will receive priority attention;",""],[1,"333","21","Agricultural Business Development Initiative","Promote business development initiative in agriculture;",""],[1,"333","22","Agricultural Price Support and Input Subsidy","Continuing price support and input subsidy to farmers;",""],[1,"333","28","Homestead Agricultural Value Addition Support","Supporting homestead agricultural value addition strategies;",""]],"92":[[1,"479","2","Promotion of Electrified Irrigation Pumps","GoB has been promoting electrified irrigating pumps in place of diesel based pumps for greater efficiency in agriculture.",""],[1,"479","2","Alternate Wet and Dry Irrigation Promotion","To conserve water in paddy production, the Department of Agricultural Extension has been promoting 'alternate wet and dry' method for irrigation in paddy fields.","Department of Agricultural Extension"],[1,"479","2","Solar Irrigation Systems Facilitation Programme","Infrastructure Development Company Limited (IDCOL) has already been facilitating solar based irrigation systems, for environment friendly agro-based economy.",""],[1,"479","2","Solar Irrigation Pump Financing Target","IDCOL also has a target to finance 1,550 solar irrigation pumps by 2017.",""]],"93":[[1,"327","3","Integrated Pest Management Programme Expansion","Integrated Pest Management (IPM) programme will be intensified and expanded in order to safeguard crops from pest and combat environmental degradation due to pesticide uses.",""],[1,"327","3","Organic Farming and Organic Inputs Promotion","Organic farming along with use of crop residues, compost, and animal waste has been popularized but need more effort.",""],[1,"327","3","Public Plant Protection Services and Pesticide Quality Control","the public sector programmes are confined to qualitative and quantitative aspects of plant protection: pest's surveillance, monitoring and early warning against pest attacks, advisory service to farmers, traders and others dealing with pesticides and quality control of pesticides marketed by the private sector.",""],[1,"327","5","Agricultural Technology and Machinery Development","Hence, more food has to be produced with lesser resources, and in this situation it will be critical to increase the efficiency of production through the application of science and technology.",""],[1,"328","1","Efficient Micro-Irrigation and Conservation Agriculture Support","technology, efficient micro irrigation system, conservation agriculture, site specific nutrient management based on soil test for macro and micro-nutrient should receive special attention.",""],[1,"328","1","Agro-Meteorological Information for Crop Planning and Pest Management","More agro-meteorological information would be utilized for crop production planning and pest and disease management strategy.",""],[1,"328","1","Remote Sensing-Based Agricultural Production and Damage Estimation","Efforts will be made to base the 7th and subsequent Plans on accurate estimates of agricultural production and crop damages using Remote Sensing tools for which expertise exists with CEGIS.",""],[1,"329","10","Quality Seed Production and Distribution Strengthening","The concerned agencies under the MOA, BADC and Horticulture Centres of DAE, will be further strengthened in order to ensure production of quality seeds/quality planting material at all stages of its production- breeder, foundation and certified seed and encouraged farmer to produce quality seed and farmer to farmer seed exchange.","MOA | BADC | Horticulture Centres of DAE"],[1,"329","10","Biotechnology-Based Seed Production Expansion","Seed production activities through biotechnology will be expanded.",""],[1,"329","10","Hybrid Seed Production Infrastructure Support","Emphasis will be given on creating facilities and infrastructure support for hybrid seed production, marketing and development.",""],[1,"329","10","Farmer Seed Production and Technical Assistance Programme","Farmers will be given training and technical assistance to extend improved methods of seed production, testing, storage and post-harvest management.",""],[1,"330","1","Bio-fertilizer Production and Use Promotion","Emphasis/support will be given for the production of bio-fertilizers and facilitating their increased use.",""],[1,"330","1","Fertilizer Subsidy Rebalancing for Balanced Use","Rebalancing of fertilizer subsidy for encouraging balanced use of fertilizers has given some results.",""],[1,"330","1","Balanced Fertilizer Use Promotion Measure","it is, therefore, important to adopt pragmatic measure to encourage farmers using balanced fertilizers to maintain soil fertility.",""],[1,"333","7","Seed, Pesticide, and Fertilizer Quality Monitoring","Ensuring quality of seed, pesticide and fertilizer through proper monitoring;",""],[1,"333","13","Community Seed Production, Storage and Distribution","Promote community seed production, storage and distribution;",""],[1,"333","14","Rice Yield Gap Minimization Techniques Promotion","Promotion of Rice Yield Gap Minimization (RYMG) techniques;",""],[1,"333","15","Green Growth Agriculture Promotion","Promotion of green growth agriculture by intensifying IPM, IDM, ICM, AWD and organic farming;",""],[1,"335","1","Plant Quarantine Strengthening","plant quarantine activities will be strengthened to render an efficient service.",""],[1,"465","17","Promotion of Environmentally Friendly Alternative Technologies for Agricultural Inputs and Food Preservation","Promote environmental friendly alternative technology for fertilizer and pesticides use and grain and food preservation",""],[1,"488","2","Integrated Pest Management Network Expansion","The GoB will expand network of integrated pest management (IPM) with environmental awareness, education and behaviour change.",""],[1,"488","3","Support Programmes for Organic Food Producers","Authorities will support programmes for organic food producers.",""],[1,"488","4","Vermi Post, Composting, and Organic Farming Promotion Programme","The GoB will undertake programmes on vermi post, composting and organic farming through piloting and promotional activities.",""]],"94":[[1,"340","3","Animal Productivity and Value Addition Promotion","To promote sustainable improvements in animal productivity of milk, meat and egg including products processing and value addition;",""],[1,"340","5","Private Sector Participation and Investment in Livestock Development","To facilitate increased private sector participation and investments in livestock production, livestock services, market development and export of livestock products and by-products.",""],[1,"340","6","Livestock Entrepreneurship Development Support","To facilitate development of entrepreneurship for livestock commercial production.",""],[1,"340","7","Poultry and Livestock Sector Support Package","The target for achieving the goals and objectives will be to raise production levels to meet the growing demand through policy support, institutional capacity building, regulatory streamlining, and easing access to credit, increased private participation, providing training on poultry and livestock management, introduction of insurance for livestock farmers, and direct public investments.",""],[1,"340","15","Livestock Extension Service Reform and Expansion","Front line extension services of DLS would be updated and extended and resource allocations to it would be increased and would be reformed to enhance its role as a provider of public goods services, viz. regulatory measures, quality assurance and control, monitoring function, food safety function, disease surveillance, while private sector, NGOs and CBOs (Community Based Organizations) would be encouraged to provide more of the livestock services viz. veterinary services, vaccination.",""],[1,"341","1","Dairy Supply Chain Development and Cooperative Dairy Promotion","In order to reduce the demand and supply gap, the supply chain based production, processing and marketing of milk and milk products, including co-operative dairy development (Milk Vita model), would be promoted.",""],[1,"341","1","Integrated Smallholder Dairy Farming Promotion","Smallholder dairy farming integrated with crop and fish culture would be promoted.",""],[1,"341","2","Livestock Productivity Improvement Programme","For bridging the demand-supply gap, production of better beef breeds, improvement in cattle fattening system, more breeding of the \"Black Bengal goat\", along with more hygienic avatar system, will be undertaken with necessary knowledge transfer for increased productivity at farm level.",""],[1,"341","2","Special Projects for Buffalo and Sheep Farming Development","Besides buffalo, sheep farming would also be developed in selected high potential areas through special projects.",""],[1,"341","3","Poultry Sector Support and Quality Control Measures","While this needs to continue, successful pro-poor models would be replicated.",""],[1,"341","3","Bangladesh Livestock Research Institute Strengthening","Bangladesh Livestock Research Institute (BLRI), which has been declared as the National Reference Laboratory for detection of Avian Influenza virus and other emerging diseases, would be strengthened to international standards with adequate trained manpower.",""],[1,"341","4","Indigenous Breed Conservation and Utilization Programme","Conservation and utilization programme of potential indigenous breeds for subsistence semi-commercial farming would be a priority.",""],[1,"341","4","Livestock Product Quality Assurance and Certification Unit","An autonomous unit/institute would be established for quality assurance and certification of livestock products, vaccines and biologics.",""],[1,"341","4","Artificial Insemination Strengthening for Breed Development","Artificial Insemination (AI) is a useful instrument for breed development, which would be further strengthened.",""],[1,"341","5","Livestock Research Capacity Enhancement","Research capacity of BLRI and Universities/Institutes, including human resource capacity, would be enhanced to address national priority and untapped potential of regional livestock resources, and to ensure safe production of animal products and by-products, animal protein supplement, feed additives, premixes, probiotics and mineral and vitamin supplements as inputs for poultry and livestock development.",""],[1,"341","5","Private and NGO Support for Livestock Research","Private and NGO initiatives in livestock research would be encouraged and supported.",""],[1,"341","6","Private and Community-Based Veterinary Services Development","Policy support will be provided to accelerate the development of private and community-based veterinary services, including compliant private veterinary diagnostic centres, clinics and hospitals.",""],[1,"341","6","Veterinary Quality Control Agency Establishment","An autonomous Quality Control Agency would be established to ensure quality of veterinary drugs, vaccines, feeds, feed ingredients and breeding tools and materials.",""],[1,"341","7","National Fodder Development Programme","Long term fodder development programme would be taken throughout the country, including large scale private sector participation, to minimize the acute shortage of feeds and fodder.",""],[1,"341","7","Community-Based Fodder Cultivation Strategy","A strategy would be developed for community- based fodder cultivation along roads and highways, rivers and embankments, in Khas lands and in combinations with crops.",""],[1,"341","7","Animal Feed Act Implementation","An Animal Feed Act would be approved and implemented to ensure feed quality.",""],[1,"342","1","Autonomous Hides and Skins Quality Control Agency","An autonomous agency would be needed for quality control and certification of hides and skins",""],[1,"342","1","Slaughter and Tannery Environmental Regulation","environmental legislation on slaughter and tannery operations would be framed and enforced",""],[1,"342","1","Hides and Skins Handling Training for Traders and Butchers","butchers and merchants (Farias, Beparis and Aratdars) would be trained on basic knowledge of flaying, curing and storing for improved management and quality of hides and skins",""],[1,"342","2","Animal Products Marketing and Value Chain Development","Traditional animal products marketing system will be improved through linking products to market and processors as well as value chain development activities will be facilitated.",""],[1,"342","3","Affordable Bank Financing for Smallholder Dairy Producers","Smallholder dairy producers and entrepreneurs will be facilitated through allowing access to bank financing at an affordable rate of interest which will be farmers friendly.",""],[1,"342","4","Poultry and Livestock Input Subsidy for Marginal Farmers","it is reasonably required to give subsidy in poultry and livestock inputs (feeds, etc.) for respective marginal farmers.",""]],"95":[[1,"344","7","Aquaculture and Fisheries Regulatory Frameworks","During the implementation of 6th FYP, a number of regulatory frameworks have been developed to harness the potentials of aquaculture and fisheries resources.",""],[1,"346","1","Inland Aquaculture Extension Service Strengthening","The main support needed and provided for sustainable development of inland aquaculture is nationwide extension service by the DOF presently down to Upazila level.",""],[1,"346","1","Fish Hatchery Quality Control and Regulation","The challenge is one of quality control and regulating of the private hatcheries for quality and imparting training to the private hatchery and nursery operators.",""],[1,"347","4","Laboratory Capacity Enhancement for Quality Assurance","it will be highly essential that the laboratory capacity of DOF and other GoB agencies are enhanced, not only by procuring equipment, but also with trained manpower and provision of operating expenses.","DOF | other GoB agencies"],[1,"347","5","Private Processing Plant Quality Control Laboratory Requirement","the processing plants should be compelled to establish and manage own QC labs",""],[1,"347","5","National Quality Control Accreditation System","an international accreditation system should be established networked to both GoB, industry-operated and NGO-promoted QC labs",""],[1,"348","3","Fisheries Research Upgrade","Fisheries research need to be upgraded to continue the flow of technology generation.",""],[1,"348","3","Inter-Ministerial Coordination and Legal Framework for Fisheries","These need to be coordinated and a necessary legal framework needs to be formulated.",""],[1,"348","3","Fish Quality Assurance Measures","Quality assurance in fish harvesting, processing, marketing and export need to be especially emphasized and appropriate actions undertaken.",""],[1,"348","4","Fish and Shrimp Self-Sufficiency and Food Safety Improvement","The 7th plan will also promote increased participation of women in fish cultivation.",""],[1,"349","4","Purebred Brood Fish Maintenance and Hatchery Support","Purebred brood fish of commercially important indigenous fish species will be maintained in the selected Fish Seed Multiplication Farms of the DOF, research stations of the BFRI, other GoB establishments and promoting private and NGO hatcheries with facilitation and monitoring support by the DOF and BFRI.","DOF | BFRI"],[1,"349","5","Brood Fish Distribution to Hatcheries","Brood fish from the above source will be distributed to the GoB hatcheries and selected private and NGO hatcheries to produce good quality fish seed and fries of commercially important and endangered species.",""],[1,"349","6","Hatchery and Fry Quality Certification and Marketing Regulation","Operation of hatcheries, nurseries and supply of spawn and fry, in which private sector is the key player, will be constantly monitored by GO-NGO collaboration and public private partnership.",""],[1,"349","7","Fish and Shrimp Feed Quality Monitoring and Certification","Production, import and marketing of fish and shrimp feed, feed ingredients, minerals and vitamin premix, and other inputs, in which private sector is the key player, will be constantly monitored by GO-NGO.",""],[1,"349","9","Promotion and Regulation of Pen and Cage Aquaculture","Pen culture and Cage culture will be further promoted but guided and monitored for species selection, location, target group identification, and feed and input use etc.",""],[1,"350","5","Extension Support and Research-Extension Linkage Strengthening","Extension support and research extension linkage will be strengthened.",""]],"96":[[1,"448","2","Cooperative-Based Milk Production Expansion","The Department of Co-operatives has been expanding cooperative based milk production in Greater Faridpur, Barisal and Khulna District for Reduction of Poverty and Socio-economic Development.","The Department of Co-operatives"],[1,"448","2","Youth and Women Dairy Skills and Credit Support","These projects provided support to 4,250 specially selected unemployed youth and women through providing training on cross breed cow management and provided credit support for buying two heifers for each family.",""],[1,"449","3","Dairy Cooperative Breed Development and Milk Production Expansion","Breed development and increase in milk production through Cooperatives in all over the country including fallow land in char areas, thereby reducing dependency on imported milk.",""],[1,"449","10","Agricultural Cooperative Marketing and Branding Support","Direct marketing of agricultural products through cooperatives and awareness building and motivational activities for cooperative members on different aspects of production including quality and hygiene will be encouraged.",""],[1,"450","3","Dissemination of Modern Agricultural, Livestock and Fisheries Technologies","In order to alleviate poverty, modern agricultural, livestock and fisheries technologies will be disseminated to the stakeholders as a strategy.",""]],"97":[[1,"674","3","Food Distribution Coordination with Stock and Fair Price Policies","Food distribution through OMS and as disaster relief will be coordinated with the Government's Food Stock Policy and the fair price policy.",""],[1,"678","4","Smart Food Grain Buffer Stock Maintenance","Considering the population size, smart buffer stock of food grains to make up anticipated production and stock losses due to periodic calamities will be maintained.",""],[1,"678","4","ICT-Based Public Food Stock and Distribution System","In order to maintain efficient stock information and appropriate distribution management, ICT based Public Food stock and distribution system will be introduced in 7th Plan.",""],[1,"678","4","Household Food Grain Stock Promotion","Besides, household level food grain stock will be promoted, especially vulnerable community in the disaster prone areas of the country are to be encouraged for preservation and storage up to emergency survival level food grains.",""],[1,"678","5","Non-distortionary Food Grain Market Intervention Programme","The Government now plans for a more non-distortionary food grain market intervention Programme to accelerate market price stability, encourage market competition and improve food security, yet not discouraging private sector trade and storage.",""],[1,"678","6","Public Food Grain Stocking and Distribution Alignment","For improving social access to food, public food grain stocking and distribution systems will have to be aligned with the Social Security Strategy.",""]],"98":[[1,"697","4","Non-Farm Income Generation and Rural Development Expansion","the expansion of non-farm income generating opportunities and rural development",""],[1,"697","4","Sustainable Tourism Development Initiative","the development of a sustainable tourism industry",""],[1,"703","3","Livelihoods Support for Extreme Poor Households","Extreme poor households, where the occurrence of child labour is highest, will be covered by livelihoods interventions for adult earners.",""],[1,"703","6","CHT Access to Basic Services and Livelihoods Programme","The ethnic communities of the CHT will be ensured access to education, health care, food and nutrition, employment, and overseas employment, and protection of rights to land and other resources.",""],[1,"703","6","Alternative Farm and Non-Farm Livelihoods Support","They will be ensured alternative farm and non-farm based livelihoods.",""],[1,"705","7","Agriculture Research and Development Centres in the Hill Districts","The Government will establish Agriculture Research and Development Centres, hubs of knowledge and extension , in the three Hill Districts to introduce advanced varieties of fruits, vegetables, flowers, and medicinal plants that are suitable for growing in hilly terrain and also commercially profitable in local and international markets.",""],[1,"705","7","Special Farmer Programme for Horticulture and Home Gardens","The Government will introduce a special programme among farmers to popularize growing these fruits, vegetables, flowers, and medicinal plants, and will arrange micro-finance for farmers to create horticulture/vegetable gardens and home gardens.",""],[1,"705","7","Area-Specific Agro-Ecological Development Planning","Development approaches will be designed based on area specific agro ecological potential and access to markets and other services.",""],[1,"705","8","Rural Non-Farm Income Generation Expansion","Income generating activities through small and cotta e industries, trading, poultry and livestock rearing, beekeeping, mushroom cultivation, and others will be expanded.",""],[1,"705","8","Social Forestry and Hill Area Livelihood Support","The income of poor people will be enhanced through social forestry in hill areas, cultivation of fruits and medicinal plants, and expanding non-farm employment opportunities.",""],[1,"706","2","Alternative Livelihoods Programme for Jhum Cultivators","Special programmes/projects will be undertaken to promote alternative livelihoods options and reduce dependency on traditional livelihoods like jhum cultivation at a level that is sustainable and socially acceptable.",""],[1,"706","3","Rural Market Infrastructure and Market Access Improvement","Proper market infrastructure and rural road and market facilities will be developed so that farmers/producers can achieve a better price from selling their products.",""],[1,"706","3","Agricultural and Local Product Market Access Reform","Measures will be taken to eliminate barriers so that agricultural and other local products have easy access to national and international markets.",""],[1,"706","3","Post-Harvest Management and Value Chain Development Programme","A special programme will be developed to strengthen post-harvest management, value chain development, processing, packaging, and market access, and to engage private sector market linkages.",""],[1,"706","3","Private Investment Promotion for CHT Product Processing and Marketing","Private investment in processing, packaging, and marketing CHT products and services will be encouraged.",""],[1,"706","5","Ethnic Community Labour Mobility Support","The Government will make special arrangements targeting ethnic communities to prepare them to take up the opportunities provided by national and global labour markets, including overseas employment, and thus enable them to increase their income.",""],[1,"706","9","Microfinance Expansion for Poor People and Farmers","Micro-finance activities for poor people and farmers will be expanded (in place of micro-credit) and vocational training provided to the poor.",""],[1,"706","10","Ecotourism and Community-Based Tourism Development","Tourism, especially ecotourism and community-based tourism will be encouraged as a means of income generation for the local people.",""],[1,"706","10","Private Investment for Sustainable Tourist Spots and Facilities","Private local investment will be encouraged to develop sustainable tourist spots and facilities in Rangamati, Bandarban and",""]],"99":[[1,"323","4","Technology Transfer and Dissemination Strengthening","Technology transfer/dissemination activities need to be strengthened by revitalizing the District Technical Committee (DTC), Regional Technical Committee (RTC), Agricultural Technical Committee (ATC) & National Agricultural Technical Coordination Committee (NATCC) and operationalizing these committees.",""],[1,"325","3","Agricultural Research and Extension System Strengthening","The development vision for agriculture under the 7th Five Year Plan is to ensure food and nutritional security, enhancement of sustainable intensification and diversification of climate resilient agricultural production with increased commercialization, and livelihood improvement through technological innovations and use, strengthening of research and extension system, developing supply chain extension, value addition of agricultural products, and linking farming community with markets, both local and global.",""],[1,"326","4","Digital Repository and Database for Farmers' Indigenous Innovations","Promote farmer's right through digital repository by achieving farmer's indigenous innovations, farmer's creativity under intellectual property laws and protect their intellectual properties and establish a database for indigenous technologies owned by the rural farming community.",""],[1,"332","2","Government Extension Agency Capacity Building","due emphasis on capacity building of government extension agencies for which necessary steps will be taken.",""],[1,"332","4","Agricultural Extension Services Strengthening","The following priority strategy will be adopted for extension services:",""],[1,"333","1","Research-Extension-Farm Linkage Strengthening","Strengthening research-extension-farm linkages;",""],[1,"333","8","Agricultural Extension Services Improvement","Improving extension services, through qualitative demonstration, field days, and agricultural exhibition;",""],[1,"333","9","Field-Level Decentralization of Authority","Strengthening field level activities through delegation of authority from headquarters to field level;",""],[1,"333","17","Extension Agency Human Resources Development Programme","Strengthening human resources development programme of extension agencies through higher education, training and exposure visit;",""],[1,"333","18","MIS-Based Knowledge Management and E-Agriculture Strengthening","Strengthening MIS (ICT) based knowledge management system and e-agriculture;",""],[1,"333","19","Village-Level Agriculture Information and Communication Centres","Establishing more Agriculture Information and Communication Centre (AICC) at village level;",""],[1,"333","20","Expansion of Farmer's Information and Advisory Centres","Establishing more Farmer's Information and Advisory Centre (FIAC) at union level;",""],[1,"335","5","Farmer Training and Demonstration for Agricultural Extension","Extension department have been organizing training and demonstration for farmers on agricultural, social and environmental development in their technology transfer process.",""],[1,"335","5","Agricultural Training Institution Support and Improvement","these institutions are Central Extension Resources Development Institute (CERDI) transforming to the National Agriculture Training Academy (NATA) in Joydebpur, Graduate Training Institute (GTI) attached to Bangladesh Agricultural University (BAU) in Mymensingh and 16 Agricultural Training Institutes (ATIs) located throughout the country; although the training facilities vary considerably among the institutes, they are generally inadequate and need support for overall improvement.",""],[1,"335","5","ICT Skills Development Through Agriculture Information Centres","The computer labs of Agriculture Information Centres can be used for producing ICT skilled human resources at local level.",""],[1,"335","5","ICT and MIS Tools for Reducing the Agricultural Information Gap","Modern ICT/MIS tools would",""],[1,"336","1","Farmer Information and Advisory Centre Expansion","Farmer's Information and Advisory Centre (FIAC) has been established at union level linking farmers and extension official through ICT/MIS.",""]],"100":[[1,"326","3","Women’s Participation in Homestead-Based Agriculture and Agro-Food Value Chains","Encourage wider women participation in homestead based agricultural production, post-harvest management, agro/food processing, marketing and decision making for ensuring women empowerment;",""],[1,"333","23","Mainstreaming Women in Agriculture","Women will require access to information, credit and other business development services in order to capitalize on the new market opportunities along changing or emerging value chains.",""],[1,"333","23","Women’s Capacity Building for Agricultural Leadership","Capacity building is required to ensure that women remain active and assure important positions in leadership and decision making in economic organizations.",""],[1,"333","23","Special Policies for Women’s Control over Income-Generating Activities","Special policies and provision are often required to ensure that women have control over important income generating activities:",""],[1,"333","24","Women-Friendly Technology and Business Environment Development","Developing women friendly technology and business environment;",""],[1,"333","26","Women’s Small-Scale Entrepreneurship Capacity Development","Capacity development of women for small-scale entrepreneurships;",""],[1,"334","1","Women Agricultural Workers Recruitment and Innovation Participation Initiative","Recruit more women agricultural workers and increase their participation in the technology innovation;",""],[1,"334","2","Protection of Women and Children from Agricultural Health Hazards","Protection of women and children from health hazards during agricultural operation.",""],[1,"718","3","Women-Focused Agricultural Extension Services","The extension services of all the government agencies (livestock, fisheries, agriculture etc.) would take specific measures in reaching women with support for training on technology, market information, production techniques, sources of raw materials, etc.",""],[1,"718","3","Women Extension Worker Recruitment","Employing women as extension workers is useful in reaching women and opening new employment opportunities for women.",""],[1,"718","3","Seed and Fertilizer Distribution Through Women Farmer Groups","The distribution of seeds and fertilizer through women farmer groups will help grassroots level women who are gradually being responsible for farming.",""],[1,"718","3","NGO Partnership for Agricultural Support","Partnership with NGOs has proven to be effective and should be continued.",""]],"101":[[1,"680","1","Safe Food Supply Risk Assessment and Prevention","Priority will have to be given to assessment and prevention of risks involved in the distribution of safe food along the entire channel from production to consumption.",""],[1,"680","3","Food Safety Coordination and Enforcement Strengthening","Greater coordination on food safety management with concerted efforts of all stakeholders needs to be ensured.",""],[1,"680","3","Food Safety Awareness and Behaviour Change Communication","Simultaneously, communications for awareness and behavioural change for the mass people would be strengthened.",""],[1,"680","3","Food Safety Monitoring and Regulatory Enforcement","Furthermore, Production and market monitoring along with enforcement of regulatory framework and strengthening institutional capacity have to be ensured with utmost priority.",""],[1,"680","3","Food Safety Authority Establishment and Activation","In this regard, formation and activation of the Food Safety Authority as provisioned in the newly enacted Food Safety Law (2013) needs to be expedited.",""]],"102":[[1,"270","2","Institutional Capacity Enhancement for MoEWOE and Subordinate Bodies","An enhancement in technical and organizational capacity of the Ministry of the Expatriates' Welfare and Overseas Employment (MoEWOE) and its subordinate bodies will be required through following institutional reforms:","Ministry of the Expatriates' Welfare and Overseas Employment (MoEWOE)"],[1,"270","3","Strengthening of Expatriate Welfare and Overseas Employment Management","The existing set up of the MoEWOE should be strengthened by taking into consideration the changing aspects and condition of international migration.",""],[1,"270","4","Establishment of New Labour Wings","To accomplish the goals of Perspective Plan at least 50 new Labour Wings are need to open immediately to strengthen welfare services of expatriates' and expand overseas market.",""],[1,"270","5","Department of Expatriates' Welfare Establishment","a separate full-fledged department named 'Department of Expatriates' Welfare' is very much needed to ensure welfare services and marker expansion of Bangladeshi workers.",""],[1,"270","7","Grassroots Expansion of District Employment and Manpower Offices","Take initiatives for specific expansion measures of the District Employment and Manpower Office (DEMO) at the grass-root level.",""],[1,"270","7","Strengthened Local Body Collaboration with DEMOs","Collaboration of local bodies with the DEMOs are to be strengthened.",""],[1,"270","8","Market-Driven Skills Development for Overseas Workers","Market driven skill development programmes with international standardization",""],[1,"271","1","Mutual Skills Recognition Diplomacy","The diplomacy regarding mutual skill recognition should also be promoted.","MoEWOE"],[1,"271","2","Sufficient Resource Allocation for MoEWOE and Subordinate Bodies","Sufficient resource allocation should be ensured for the MoEWOE and its subordinate bodies to fulfil the development priorities and promises given by the Government.","MoEWOE"],[1,"271","3","Youth Migration Participation and Skills Training Support","participations of youth living in lagging regions can be promoted, providing quality skill trainings at minimum cost",""],[1,"271","3","Migration and Remittance Cost Reduction Measures","ensure further reduction of migration and remittance transfer cost",""],[1,"271","3","Remittance Productive Investment Facilitation","facilitate remittances into productive investments",""],[1,"271","4","Bangladeshi Diaspora Engagement and Investment Facilitation Measures","The contribution of Bangladeshi Diaspora should be further strengthened by incorporating them in various development activities through effective measures including facilitation of different socio- economic activities, promotion of financial and investment incentives through popular financial instruments, revenue gain through tourism and utilization of their knowledge networks by recognizing and acknowledging their contributions.",""],[1,"271","5","Migration Diplomacy and Negotiation Capacity Strengthening","Negotiation capacity with effective migration supported diplomacy should be strengthened through continues training and interface with a view to develop research and survey-based professional expertise to support initiatives to explore new markets and destinations, strengthen associations in destination countries, periodic review of bilateral and multilateral employment agreement and generate greater oversight of working conditions and breaches of contract to ensure protection of expatriate workers including special emphasis on female migrant workers, eliminate fraudulent recruitment activities and ensure standard and ethical practices.",""],[1,"271","6","Comprehensive Digitization of the Migration Process","Comprehensive digitization of the migration process is also required for the effort to demonstrate results related to sound planning and management of labour migration as well as for the social protection of the workers and recruitment agent regulation.",""],[1,"271","7","Migrant Information and Awareness Campaigns","Widespread campaigns with purposive information kit, explained in simple language, on the costs and benefits of jobs abroad, migrant's rights and responsibilities, choice of placements abroad, the public and private support systems that are available to them can minimize risks associated with migration.",""],[1,"271","8","Returned Migrant Rehabilitation Loan Support","Probashi Kallayan Bank is currently providing 'rehabilitation loan' to those returned migrants who are destitute, marooned and victim of unexpected circumstances.",""],[1,"272","1","Education and Tourism Infrastructure Investment","Second, substantial investments are needed in education and tourism infrastructure.",""],[1,"298","3","Migrant Worker Support Services","This is a welcome development and benefitted from a range of government support services including remittance facilitation, government level dialogue with host countries to protect the interests of the migrant workers, tax exemption, and information sharing.",""],[1,"298","3","Strengthening the Ministry of Expatriates' Welfare and Overseas Employment","In this context, more initiatives including strengthening the Ministry of Expatriates' Welfare and Overseas Employment will be needed during 7th FYP period.","Ministry of Expatriates' Welfare and Overseas Employment"],[1,"303","11","Overseas Employment Growth Maintenance","Maintain the growth of overseas employment",""],[1,"307","13","Overseas Employment Recruitment Monitoring and Enforcement","Strict monitoring and enforcement of the recruitment process of overseas employment.",""],[1,"307","14","Overseas Employment Law Enforcement","Enforcement of laws and regulations related to overseas employment.",""],[1,"308","4","Migration Mainstreaming in National Development Planning","Bangladesh is moving to integrate migration across the national development planning process.",""],[1,"308","4","Migration Dialogue and Cooperation Engagement","Bangladesh has been making pronounced efforts to enhance dialogue and cooperation in migration and development by hosting several high-level events15, and assuming the Chairmanship of the Global Forum on Migration and Development (GFMD) in 2016.",""],[1,"308","6","Strengthening of the National Skill Database and Migration Information System","Besides the maintenance and strengthening of the relevant structures e.g. the National Skill Database and the Migration Information System, there is an urgent need for building a comprehensive evidence base on",""],[1,"309","3","Remittance Regulatory Framework Improvement","Governments ought to and can play a key role to help reducing remittance costs",""],[1,"309","4","Diaspora Investment Attraction Policies","Policies to attract direct foreign investment will also encourage investment resources from the diaspora.",""],[1,"309","6","Labour Migration Promotion and Migrant Skills Development","The Seventh FYP is concerned with promoting labour migration, including from lagging districts, and improving the skills base for the development of new overseas labour market opportunities for Bangladeshi nationals, ensuring the protection of migrant workers' human and labour rights.",""],[1,"310","2","National Skill Database and Labour Market Information System Consolidation","A key step in this regard is the consolidation of the National Skill Database, including data on migrant workers, and of labour market information systems to assess the demand for different categories of workers in overseas markets.",""],[1,"310","3","Migrant Worker Protection and Ethical Recruitment Measures","Interventions to ensure the protection of migrant workers' human and labour rights should target not only potential and actual migrant workers and recruitment agencies, but also employers and relevant public institutions.",""],[1,"310","3","Migrant Information Dissemination and Post-arrival Assistance","Besides continued support to potential and actual migrants through the dissemination of information and post-arrival assistance, the capacities of consular networks could be strengthened so to enable them to provide effective referral services.",""],[1,"310","3","Consular Network Capacity Strengthening","the capacities of consular networks could be strengthened so to enable them to provide effective referral services.",""],[1,"310","3","Wage Earners Welfare Fund Board Reform","the ability of the Wage Earners Welfare Fund Board to support the needs of migrant workers and its transparency need to be enhanced through multi- stakeholder participation within the Board.",""],[1,"310","3","Migrant Reintegration Endowment Fund","an endowment fund could be established.",""],[1,"310","3","Victim Identification and Anti-trafficking Assistance","Better identification of victims of human trafficking through fraudulent recruitment is necessary to provide adequate assistance and prevent other workers from falling into similar exploitative conditions.",""],[1,"310","3","Private Recruitment Agency Regulation","This is linked to strict regulation of private recruitment agencies in addition to continued efforts to provide potential and actual overseas workers with information, building the capacity of border officials and sensitizing and building the capacity of employers to identify formal intermediaries committed to ethical recruitment.",""],[1,"310","3","Border Official Capacity Building for Migration Control","building the capacity of border officials",""],[1,"310","3","Employer Sensitization on Ethical Recruitment","sensitizing and building the capacity of employers to identify formal intermediaries committed to ethical recruitment.",""],[1,"310","3","Vigilance Task Force Strengthening","The Government's Vigilance Task Force can be further strengthened to combat irregular migration, in accordance with the Overseas Employment and Migrants Act, 2013.",""],[1,"310","3","International Migration Protection Treaty Accession and Legal Harmonization","joining the existing relevant international instruments relating to the protection of migrants' human and labour rights, smuggling and trafficking in persons should be pursued and followed by the harmonization of national policies and laws with those standards.",""],[1,"311","1","Skills Policy for Migrants and Population Dynamics","Such assessments should also consider the national population dynamics.",""],[1,"312","2","Migration Mainstreaming and Capacity-Building Programme","The Programme on Mainstreaming Migration seeks not only to support the establishment and consolidation of intra-governmental mechanisms for coordination on migration and development but also to continue assisting governments in building capacities to design, implement and monitor the national migration and development policies and strategies.",""],[1,"312","2","Intra-Governmental Migration Coordination Mechanism","The Programme on Mainstreaming Migration seeks not only to support the establishment and consolidation of intra-governmental mechanisms for coordination on migration and development",""],[1,"312","2","National Migration Policy Capacity Support","to continue assisting governments in building capacities to design, implement and monitor the national migration and development policies and strategies.",""],[1,"312","2","Migration Legal Provisions Sensitization and Capacity-Building Initiative","There is an urgent need to sensitize the population and build the capacity of government, civil society and private sector actors to implement the existing legal provisions.",""],[1,"312","2","Colombo Process Participation and Best-Practice Sharing","Bangladesh participates actively in the Colombo Process for Asian labour-sending countries, and contributes to the process through both sharing its best practices and reviewing and implementing its recommendations.",""]],"103":[[1,"126","1","Basel III Banking Regulation Implementation","Bangladesh has started preparation to implement the BASEL-III framework for bank companies from 2014 in line with the global standard.","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"126","1","Bank Supervision Capacity Strengthening","Efforts have also been made to improve the supervision capacity of the regulator, the Bangladesh Bank, through a range of technical assistance.","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"128","1","Banking Sector Governance and Supervision Strengthening","Bangladesh Bank and the government will strengthen significantly banking sector governance and supervision in order to reduce the lending rate without creating market distortions.","Bangladesh Bank | the government"],[1,"128","2","Financial Sector Reform Programme","In order to establish stable financial markets and service systems, continuous reforms ranging across financial sector policies, financial infrastructure, regulatory and supervisory institutions will be undertaken.",""],[1,"128","3","State-Owned Bank Supervision Reform","The government will formulate strategy and implement identified measures for better supervision of state owned banks.",""],[1,"128","3","Insurance Regulatory Authority Capacity Strengthening","The capacity of the Insurance Development and Regulatory Authority will be strengthened through providing manpower and promulgating relevant rules and regulations.",""],[1,"208","2","Financial Sector Strengthening Reform","These critical areas for intervention include: (c) financial sector;",""],[1,"210","5","Broad Financial Sector Reform Measures","the Sixth and Seventh Plan contain a slew of reform measures directed at the overall financial sector.",""]],"104":[[1,"701","5","Child Participation in Programme Design and Evaluation","ensuring participation of children in defining their needs, developing programmes, implementing interventions, and evaluating their success",""],[1,"701","5","Support for Duty Bearers, Parents and Caregivers","ensuring support of duty bearer, parents and other care givers on whom children have to depend",""],[1,"701","5","Public Support for Child Survival and Development","ensuring widespread public support for survival and development of children",""],[1,"702","5","National Child Participation Platform","it would be necessary to create a national platform for allowing children to express opinions on their needs and expectations and means of addressing them.",""],[1,"703","1","Child Protection Social Awareness and Community Mobilization Campaign","A widespread social awareness campaign and community mobilization on protection issues will be undertaken to foster positive attitudes towards children, particularly girls, and bolster the positive attitude of parents and decision-makers on the need to protect children regardless of the socio-economic environment.",""],[1,"703","3","Multi-Stakeholder Coordination for Street Children Rehabilitation","Coordination between government agencies, NGOs working on child issues, parents and community people will be required for an effective rehabilitation and development of street children.",""],[1,"703","5","Public Advocacy and Child Rights Coordination","The Ministry of Women and Children Affairs will conduct public advocacy and coordinate interventions for children's well-being and rights.","Ministry of Women and Children Affairs"],[1,"703","5","Inter-Ministerial Child Rights Coordination Committee","An inter-ministerial coordination committee consisting of government ministries with children's portfolios and organizations representing children's mandate will be chaired by the Secretary of the Ministry of Women and Children Affairs and will coordinate implementation of the Children Act 2013, CRC, CEDAW, and the World Fit for Children Plan of Action.","Ministry of Women and Children Affairs"]],"105":[[1,"467","5","Environmental Policy Coordination and Monitoring by MoEF","The Ministry has a critical role in policy and coordination of the implementation of action plans in various sectors.","MoEF"],[1,"467","14","Institutional Assessment and Strategic Planning for the DoE","DoE has enforced an institutional assessment and strategic plan with five focuses: 1) enforce the Environment","DoE"],[1,"468","1","Department of Environment Capacity Building","Build DOE's capacity",""],[1,"473","9","Strengthening Environment, Forestry and Climate Change Capacities Project","One of the key initiatives of the Ministry of Environment and Forests is the implementation of a project entitled \"Strengthening the Environment, Forestry and Climate Change Capacities of the MoEF and its Agencies\" funded by the USAID and with technical assistance from Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations.","Ministry of Environment and Forests"],[1,"473","10","Climate Change Focal Point Coordination and Training","focal points have been designated in each ministry and a few specialized and relevant agencies. MoEF has trained them to ensure proper integration of climate change issues at the national level.","MoEF | Planning Commission"],[1,"473","14","Capacity Enhancement Training for Government Officials","Most of the officials need immediate capacity enhancement trainings in order to equip themselves to act as per mandate of the BCCSAP and project designing under ADP.",""],[1,"474","3","Institutional Coordination for Climate Change Response","To ensure an effective multi-dimensional response system, proper coordination among relevant institutions is a must.",""],[1,"474","7","National Institutional Framework for Climate Change Adaptation Readiness","In order to design an effective CCA strategy, developing a national institutional framework for allocating roles and responsibilities for different ministries is paramount.",""],[1,"474","8","Institutional Strengthening for Climate Mainstreaming","Institutional capacity of units within different ministries and departments should be strengthened so that climate change may be integrated into development projects and initiatives.",""],[1,"474","8","Institutional Setup Upgrading for Whole-of-Government Climate Action","Investment in the up-gradation of current institutional setup to utilize the whole-of government approach is also required.",""],[1,"476","8","Institutional Leadership Strengthening for Climate Coordination","Revitalize and strengthen institutional leadership for improved coordination: Sluggish institutional arrangement towards implementing BCCSAP and the prevailing bottleneck in inter-agency coordination has been hindering integration of CCA with development projects, an institutional revitalization and strengthening is an immediate necessity.",""],[1,"476","8","Capacity Building for Climate Coordination Arrangements","The current institutional arrangement requires a thorough examination, the prevailing capacity involving technical know-how of officials, financial and coordination strength will be built to make the arrangement more functional.",""],[1,"476","10","Climate Fiscal Cell Establishment","GoB will consider establishing a climate fiscal cell in the Finance Division of the MoF.","Finance Division of the MoF"],[1,"480","6","Institutional Capacity Building for Opportunity Analysis","The Government will facilitate institutional capacity through training.",""],[1,"480","6","Formalized Process for Assessing Technological Opportunities","The process of analysing opportunities from technological advancements will be formalized and implemented.",""],[1,"480","8","LCD Anchor Institution Coordination Mechanism","The GoB will identify an anchor institution, and it will be empowered on LCD.",""],[1,"495","3","Stakeholder Capacity Enhancement and Institutional Extension","Enhance capacity of the relevant stakeholders along with vertical and horizontal extension of local and central level institutions.",""]],"106":[[1,"34","23","Emergency Cyclone Recovery and Restoration Project","Emergency Cyclone Recovery and Restoration Project",""],[1,"78","6","Disaster Management Programmes","The disaster management programmes have generally performed well in the recent years and the progress continued under the Sixth Plan.",""],[1,"685","9","Risk Reduction Programme","Institutional Feeding programme, Rural Infrastructure Maintenance programme, Risk Reduction Programme, Road Maintenance Programme, House Building Grants etc.",""],[1,"685","13","National Disaster Response Mechanism Strengthening","Establish, strengthen and improve the national disaster response mechanism.",""],[1,"686","1","Disaster and Climate Change Risk Reduction Mainstreaming","Mainstreaming Disaster and Climate Change risk reduction integration efforts within government, NGOs and private sector and effective response mechanism across the whole country will help to achieve sustainable development from national to community level.",""],[1,"686","4","Integrated Disaster Risk Management and Recovery","Disaster management would involve the management of both risks and consequences of disasters that would include prevention emergency response and post-disaster recovery.",""],[1,"686","5","Community Involvement for Disaster Preparedness Programmes","Community involvement for preparedness programmes for protecting lives and properties would be a major focus.",""],[1,"686","6","Community Disaster Preparedness Training and Public Awareness","Non-structural mitigation measures such as community disaster preparedness training advocacy and public awareness must be given a high priority;",""],[1,"686","20","Preparedness and Emergency Response System Strengthening","Utilizing technical and traditional analysis to strengthen preparedness and emergency response systems including early warning",""],[1,"687","1","Disaster Risk Reduction and Management System","The objectives of this Act are substantial reduction of the overall risks of disasters to an acceptable level with appropriate risk reduction interventions; effective implementation of post disaster emergency response; rehabilitation and recovery measures; provision of emergency humanitarian assistance to the most vulnerable community people; strengthening of institutional capacity for effective coordination of disaster management involving government and non-government organizations, and establishing a disaster management system capable of dealing with all hazards in the country.",""],[1,"687","2","Department for Disaster Management Strengthening","Following its enactment, the Government has set up the Department for Disaster Management (DDM)with a more robust and wider role focusing on comprehensive disaster management, and has been responsible for implementation of the national disaster management related policies and plans at all levels.",""],[1,"687","5","Disaster Impact Reduction and Disaster Management Improvement","The Government has expressed its commitment to reducing the harsh impacts of disasters and improves disaster management.",""],[1,"687","6","Disaster Management Policy Implementation and Guidance Framework","The Disaster Management Act (2012) has been implemented and a Disaster Management policy has been approved.",""],[1,"687","6","Disaster Management Policy for Hazard Preparedness","The Disaster Management Policy will provide guidance, plan and help prepare for all types hazards and disaster.",""],[1,"687","6","Department of Disaster Management Establishment","Department of Disaster Management was also established to implement DM Act 2012.",""],[1,"688","3","Cyclone Preparedness Volunteer Programme","Cyclone Preparedness Programme (CPP) has now a total of 55,260 volunteers including 16,455 female volunteers.",""],[1,"688","3","Urban Disaster Volunteer Formation Initiative","government has undertaken initiatives to form a total of 70,260 thousand urban volunteers by 2020.",""],[1,"688","3","Cyclone and Flood Preparedness Volunteer Expansion","Volunteerism for disasters has been enhanced by enhancement of the cyclone preparedness programme and creation of the flood preparedness programme implemented by Ansar & VDP.",""],[1,"688","4","Emergency Response and Communication Centre and Disaster Management Research and Training Institute","An Emergency Response and Communication Centre (ERCC) and a National Disaster Management Research and Training Institute (NDMRTI) will be established under the Urban Resilience Project.",""],[1,"689","1","Disaster Needs Assessment Capacity Strengthening","Needs Assessment capacity of DDM has been strengthened through development of SOS and D-Form Guidelines and training of DRRO, PIOS, and UNOs.","DDM | DRRO | PIOS | UNOs"],[1,"689","1","Humanitarian Coordination Architecture Reform","Joint Government-Development Partner cooperation for effective disaster response and recovery strengthened through the reformed humanitarian coordination architecture which includes the LCG-DER, Humanitarian Coordination Task Team (HCTT) and the humanitarian clusters.",""],[1,"689","4","Whole-of-Government Disaster Risk Reduction Collaboration","It is not possible for government alone to tackle disaster unless strong collaboration among all the relevant stakeholders such as government, NGOs, researchers, scientists, civil society, private sector, media etc. are established and maintained.",""],[1,"689","6","Disaster Management Monitoring and Accountability System","Monitoring and accountability systems are essential to ensure implementation.",""],[1,"690","5","Sendai Framework Implementation","The Sendai Framework is fundamental to the vision and ambition of the Government of Bangladesh and thus requires full implementation.",""],[1,"690","8","Integrated Disaster Risk Reduction Measures","Prevent new and reduce existing disaster risk through the implementation of integrated and inclusive economic, structural, legal, social, health, cultural, educational, environmental, technological, political and institutional measures that prevent and reduce hazard exposure and vulnerability to disaster, increase preparedness for response and recovery, and thus strengthen resilience.",""],[1,"690","11","Disaster Risk Governance Strengthening","Strengthening disaster risk governance to manage disaster risk;",""],[1,"690","12","Disaster Risk Reduction for Resilience Investment","Investing in disaster risk reduction for resilience;",""],[1,"690","13","Disaster Preparedness Enhancement","Enhancing disaster preparedness for effective response.",""],[1,"691","1","Technical Assistance Optimization for Resilience","Careful consideration of how TA can be most effectively used to support lasting increases in resilience must be made and a strong commitment to change ensured",""],[1,"691","3","Disaster Management Regulatory Framework Upgrade","Upgrade the disaster management regulative framework.",""],[1,"691","4","Mainstreaming of Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation","Risk reduction and climate change adaptation principles (with sustainability) are mainstreamed within all development programmes, plans and policies.",""],[1,"691","8","National Capacity Strengthening for Disaster Response Management Support","Strengthen national capacity for response management support to local disaster management committees",""],[1,"691","10","Go-NGO and Private Sector Disaster Risk Reduction Coordination","Establish Go- NGO and private sector coordination for disaster risk reduction",""],[1,"691","11","Multi-Sectoral Coordination System","Establish multi sectoral coordination system",""],[1,"691","13","Regional Network Establishment and Strengthening","Establish & strengthen the regional networks",""],[1,"691","16","Implementation of the Disaster Management Act and Decentralized Disaster Governance","Under the 7th FYP, the Disaster Management Act of 2012 will be institutionalized and implemented to achieve adequate decentralization throughout the Government and accountability for delivery.",""],[1,"691","16","Regional Disaster Management Cooperation","Regional cooperation will be further strengthened for disaster management.",""],[1,"691","17","SoD and DM Act Reform","Reform the SoD and DM Act and its rules, if needed in line with post MDG and Sendai Framework for DRR.",""],[1,"691","18","National Plan for Disaster Management 2016-2020 Publication","Publish the National Plan for Disaster Management 2016-2020 in line with post MDG and Sendai Framework for DRR.",""],[1,"691","19","National Disaster Management Policy Implementation","Approve and implement the National Disaster Management Policy.",""],[1,"691","20","Disaster Coordination Mechanisms Activation","Activate disaster coordination mechanisms at national and local level.",""],[1,"692","1","Disaster Management Research and Training Institute","Establish and activate the Disaster Management Research and Training Institute to develop capacity and provide technical assistance across all relevant government agencies including the DMCs.",""],[1,"692","2","Integration of DRR and CCA into Government Planning Frameworks","Integrate DRR and CCA for resilience approaches and principles within the planning and policy frameworks of all Government institutions, provide technical assistance, monitor and report on implementation.",""],[1,"692","3","Disaster Management Integration in District Development Plans","Integrate DM in district development plans and provide capacity development training including UDMCs.",""],[1,"692","4","DRR and CCA Training Curriculum Integration","Inclusion of DRR and CCA issues in the training curriculum for local government, public representative officials, Bangladesh Ansar & VDP, religious leaders, scouts, etc.",""],[1,"692","5","Gendered Disaster Resilience Mainstreaming","Implement a gendered approach to disaster resilience in all Government planning, policy frameworks and programmes.",""],[1,"692","6","Private Sector Disaster Resilience Partnership Framework","Establish effective partnerships for disaster resilience with the private sector focused on roles, responsibilities, investment priorities and incentives, including regulation.",""],[1,"692","7","Policy Framework for Slow-Onset Disaster Management","Develop policy framework for addressing slow onset disasters such as water logging in south-west, river bank erosion etc.",""],[1,"692","12","Sectoral Disaster Management Financing and Local Disaster Management Fund","Allocate adequate sectoral financing of disaster management through line ministries and establish the Local DM Fund.",""],[1,"692","12","Disaster Management Implementation Monitoring and Reporting","Monitor and report on implementation.",""],[1,"692","14","Risk Reduction Action Plan and Contingency Planning","Promote RRAP (Risk Reduction Action Plan) and contingency planning across agencies and for all unions/cities/wards and monitor its implementation and practice.",""],[1,"692","15","Hazard-Based Contingency Planning","Encourage different hazard based contingency planning like chemical and technological hazards, road and water safety, nuclear and radiological risk, biological hazards, landslide etc.",""],[1,"692","19","National Emergency Operations Centre Establishment and Operationalization","Establish the National Emergency Operations Centre (EOC) and fully operationalize it.",""],[1,"693","1","National Emergency Response Coordination Mechanism Framework and Guidelines","Develop national emergency response co-ordination mechanism framework & guidelines",""],[1,"693","2","Debris and Dead Body Management Guidelines Implementation Capacity","Finalize, approve, disseminate and create capacity for implementation of critical guidelines and plans on debris management, dead body management etc.",""],[1,"693","3","Incident Management System Implementation Capacity and Rollout","Finalize, approve, disseminate and create capacity for implementation of an Incident Management System.",""],[1,"693","7","National Volunteers Organization Development","Develop National Volunteers organization",""],[1,"693","8","Volunteer Equipment, Training, Certification, and Compensation Programme","Provide equipment, training programmes for CPP, Urban volunteers, scouts certification & award programmes for volunteers, compensation programmes for dead or injured volunteers.",""],[1,"693","10","Community-Level Drill Promotion","Promote community level drills.",""],[1,"693","13","Mutual Aid Agreements for Emergency Response","Mutual Aid-Agreements between Public-Private Partners for emergency Response",""],[1,"693","14","Emergency Response Coordination Guidelines","Develop guidelines on co-ordination mechanism for GO-NGO and private sector for emergency response and strengthening GO-NGO and private sector co-ordination for emergency response",""],[1,"693","18","Post-Disaster Recovery and Reconstruction Capacity Development","Develop dedicated capacity within MoDMR and DDM to lead and coordinate post disaster recovery and reconstruction","MoDMR | DDM"],[1,"693","20","Build Back Better Recovery and Reconstruction Integration","Integrate \"build back better\" principles into recovery and reconstruction policies, plans and financial projections.",""],[1,"693","23","Monitoring and Support Mechanism","Establish an effective monitoring and support mechanism",""],[1,"693","26","Monitoring and Evaluation Guideline Development","Prepare monitoring and evaluation guideline",""],[1,"693","27","Multi-Sectoral Coordination Guidelines for Post-Disaster Recovery and Development","Develop guidelines on multi sectoral co-ordination for post disaster recovery and development activities",""],[1,"694","2","Comprehensive Disaster Resilience Communication Strategy","Design and implement a comprehensive communication strategy to enable proactive communication to vulnerable communities, across government and to the wider DM community to support awareness raising for effective disaster resilience.",""],[1,"694","4","DRR-CCA Indicator Framework Development","Overall performance of the various plans, programmes and projects will be tracked by developing focused and specific DRR-CCA indicators.",""]],"107":[[1,"176","11","Development Partner Partnership for Foreign Assistance Effectiveness","one of the key strategies of the Seventh Five Year Plan will be to ensure effective partnership with development partners to ensure better use and results of foreign assistance.",""],[1,"177","2","Local Consultative Group Coordination Platform","Anchored in the JCS, Local Consultative Group (LCG) is the main platform for coordination between the government and DPs is Bangladesh.",""],[1,"177","2","Joint Cooperation Strategy for Aid Effectiveness","Bangladesh has established a formal mechanism of partnership with development partners working in Bangladesh through the signing of a Joint Cooperation Strategy (JCS) in 2010.",""],[1,"177","3","Joint Cooperation Strategy and Local Consultative Group Strengthening","During the 7th Five Year Plan period, government will continue its efforts to strengthen the JCS and the LCG, keeping up with the evolving partnership needs.",""],[1,"177","4","ERD Capacity Development Strategy Implementation","GoB should have highly trained, efficient and dynamic in house coordination officers, who will be capable to set forth the implementation of the ERD capacity development strategy which was recently initiated, run the Aid Information Management System and house the LCG secretariat.",""],[1,"177","5","National Development Cooperation Policy","A national Policy on Development Cooperation is being prepared to guide development cooperation in Bangladesh from a wider, strategic perspective.",""],[1,"177","5","Alignment of Development Partner Country Assistance Strategies","The 7th FYP envisages that all DPs align their country assistance strategies with the goals and sectoral targets of the Government.",""],[1,"177","5","Line Ministry Leadership in LCG Sectoral Working Groups","Leadership of government line Ministries in the LCG sectoral working group is key to ensure development partners' policy alignment and system harmonization.",""],[1,"177","5","ERD Foreign Assistance Coordination Work Plan","Economic Relations Division (ERD) as the principal gateway to development assistance issues should map comprehensive work plan to reach out to all government line Ministries to ensure that they all are on the same wavelength when dealing with foreign assistance.","Economic Relations Division (ERD)"],[1,"178","1","Aid Data Transparency and Sharing System","This 7th FYP stipulates that all aid data be made public and the Aid Information Management System (AIMS) should be the principal means of data sharing by DPs in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"190","3","Joint Cooperation Strategy for Aid Effectiveness","The overall goal of Joint Cooperation Strategy (JCS) is to make aid in Bangladesh more effective by creating common platforms for national and sectoral dialogues as well as a country owned change process for improving delivery of aid.",""],[1,"190","3","Strengthened Results Framework Dialogue and Development Partner Support","The process, however, needs to be improved with stronger dialogue and input from the Development Partners on the RF with a view to making that sharper and more focused on areas of mutual interest.",""],[1,"190","3","Technical and Financial Support for GED Monitoring and Evaluation","The Development Partners should also stand ready to support GED to improve the M&E effort with technical inputs in the areas of their competence as well as through financial support.",""]],"108":[[1,"624","5","Digital Land Management System and Land Information Service Centres","Implementation of digital land management system in 45 upazilas under 7 districts and establishment of 20 land information service centres in 20 different upazilas through another project titled, \"Strengthening Governance Management Project, Component B,\" is underway.",""],[1,"624","5","PPP-Based Computerization and Outsourced Land Record Services","This project will be implemented under PPP's build-operate-transfer (BOT) basis, retaining overall control of the government.",""],[1,"624","5","Private Sector Distribution of Khatiyan and Map Services","In this case, the services relating to distribution of khatiyans and maps will be channelled through private organizations.",""],[1,"626","7","Digital Land Management System","Digital land management system has been introduced in order to make land administration and management transparent and accountable by making land records available online, through conducting satellite technology based digital survey, preparation of digital maps and ledgers.",""],[1,"626","7","Authoritative Land Records Pilot Project","A pilot project is being implemented in three upazilas to introduce \"Authoritative Land Records\" (ALR).",""],[1,"627","1","Computerization of Land Management in Dhaka District","A total of 5 upazilas under Dhaka district have been chosen as pilot projects under a Programme titled \"Computerization of Land Management of Dhaka District.\"",""],[1,"627","1","Digitization of Land Survey, Record Preparation and Preservation Project","Steps have been taken to implement computerization of existing mouza maps and khatiyan across 55 districts under another project titled \"Digitization of Land Survey, Record Preparation and Preservation Project, 1st Phase.",""],[1,"635","3","ICT-Based Land Market Efficiency Improvement","The steps taken under Sixth Plan to improve the functioning of the land market through ICT will be strengthened further in the Seventh Plan through the following steps:",""],[1,"635","4","Digital Land Records Modernization Reform","The reform will enhance public access to land records, transparent land transactions and efficient collection of land revenue through modernization of all land records.",""],[1,"635","4","Transparent Khas Land Distribution Mechanism","Marginalized citizens will be allowed to establish their legal rights on khas land through transparent distribution mechanism.",""],[1,"636","2","Work Culture Transformation in Land Management Agencies","Hence, efforts will be undertaken to gradually transform the work culture of relevant agencies.",""],[1,"636","2","ICT-Based Land Management Modernization","To this end, modern technology will be introduced to support improved work-processes of the relevant agencies.",""],[1,"636","2","Leadership and Management Skills Training Programme","Additionally, skill-training Programme for the management of these agencies to build leadership skills such as negotiation and communication skills will be organized.",""]],"109":[[1,"230","2","Election Commission Performance Enhancement","Thus, under the 7th FYP, the following activities will be pursued to enhance the performance of the EC:",""],[1,"230","3","Support for the Election Commission's Impartial Operations","The Government will offer all necessary support to EC to carry out its operation impartially and effectively.",""],[1,"230","4","Operational Capacity and Technology Upgrade","Greater efforts will be given to improve its capacity and promote better use of technology to undertake its operation.",""],[1,"230","5","Election Campaign Finance Monitoring and Control Capacity Enhancement","Measures will be taken to improve EC's capacity to monitor and control campaign contribution and spending of parties and candidates during local and national elections.",""],[1,"230","6","Candidate Database and Affidavit Disclosure System","EC will further strengthen its database of all candidates in both local and national elections so that citizens can review the personal affidavits of all candidates and formulate an informed decision.",""]],"110":[[1,"697","3","Ethnic Peoples Rights and Empowerment Programme","This will be achieved by providing them with improved health and education services, promoting their employment, as well as protecting their rights to land and other resources.",""],[1,"697","3","Chittagong Hill Tracts Accord Implementation","One of the chief strategies is to fully implement the 1997 Chittagong Hill Tracks (CHT) accord.",""],[1,"697","6","Legal Protection and Rights Framework for Ethnic Communities","Legal protection ensured by 1) implementing the UN Declaration on the Rights of Ethnic groups Peoples 2007 and ratify the ILO Convention 1969, 2) formulating a land policy to deal with land disputes involving ethnic communities and finally 3) ensuring the participation of local governments in the management of natural resources.",""],[1,"697","7","Implementation of the Chittagong Hill Tracts Accord","Recent progress in continuing the implementation of this accord includes the transferring of 5 new institute functions under the Hill District Council's authority.",""],[1,"703","6","Ethnic Population Rights and Social Inclusion Strategy","The government is committed to ensuring socio-economic and political rights, fundamental human rights, and social security, while enabling tribal people to retain their social, cultural, and traditional identities.",""],[1,"704","1","Chittagong Hill Tracts Development Consultation Process","be formulated for the development of the CHT through a consultation process with key stakeholders.",""],[1,"704","3","Implementation of the CHT Peace Accord","The government is committed to implementing the remaining provisions; all measures will be taken to implement the Peace Accord within the period of the 7th Five Year Plan.",""],[1,"704","3","Strengthening Decentralization and Devolution in the CHT","Decentralization and devolution will be will be further strengthened.",""],[1,"704","3","Support for CHT Development Institutions","The Ministry of CHT Affairs, CHT Regional Council (CHTRC), and three HDCs will be support the development of the CHT.","Ministry of CHT Affairs | CHT Regional Council (CHTRC) | three HDCs"],[1,"704","3","Amendment of the Land Commission Act 2001","The Land Commission Act 2001 will be amended to make it functional and acceptable.",""],[1,"704","3","Resolution of Land Disputes in the CHT","The Government will make every effort to expedite the process to resolve land disputes in the three districts of the CHT.",""],[1,"704","3","Phased Withdrawal of Army Camps","Phased withdrawal of army camps will continue.",""],[1,"704","3","Consultative Land Survey in the CHT","A land survey will be carried out in consultation with the key stakeholders.",""],[1,"704","3","Ethnic Community Responsive Government Programmes","The Government programmes will be tailored to meet the needs and concerns of the ethnic communities.",""],[1,"704","5","Implementation of the UN Declaration on the Rights of Indigenous Peoples","The Government will consider implementing the UN Declaration on the Rights of Indigenous Peoples 2007 and ratifying the ILO Convention 1969.",""],[1,"704","5","Ratification of ILO Convention 1969","The Government will consider implementing the UN Declaration on the Rights of Indigenous Peoples 2007 and ratifying the ILO Convention 1969.",""],[1,"704","6","CHT Peace Accord Implementation","The Government will ensure full implementation of the CHT Peace Accord signed in 1997.",""],[1,"704","6","Strengthening of CHT Governance Institutions","The Ministry of CHT Affairs, CHT Regional Council, and three Hill District Councils will be strengthened to support the development of the CHT.","Ministry of CHT Affairs | CHT Regional Council | three Hill District Councils"],[1,"704","6","Transfer of Remaining CHT Subjects and Departments","As per the provisions of the CHT Peace Accord, the remaining subjects/departments will be transferred to HDCs in terms of administration, finance, and development fund in letter and spirit and with allocation of finance.",""],[1,"704","7","Land Dispute Resolution and Secure Tenure Reform in the CHT","The Land Commission will resolve the land disputes in the CHT following the amended Land Commission Dispute Resolution Act 2001 to ensure the rights to land.",""],[1,"704","7","Community Land Ownership Protection in the CHT","Community ownership of land in the CHT will be honoured.",""],[1,"704","7","Consultative Land Survey in the CHT","A land survey will be carried out in consultation with the key stakeholders as per the provisions of the CHT Peace Accord.",""],[1,"704","7","Ethnic Land Dispute Policy Formulation","An appropriate land policy will be formulated which can deal with land disputes involving ethnic groups.",""],[1,"704","7","Secure Land Tenure System","A secure land tenure system will be introduced.",""],[1,"704","8","Ethnic Community Participation and Support Programme","The Government will ensure participation of local people in development activities and management of natural resources and will recognize the traditional customs and knowledge of the various ethnic peoples.",""],[1,"705","3","Chittagong Hill Tracts Perspective Plan Formulation","The Government will formulate a Perspective Plan for the development of CHT through a consultation process with key stakeholders.",""],[1,"705","4","Accelerated Development Programme for the Chittagong Hill Tracts","Additional finance will be allocated on priority basis for implementation of programmes/projects to reduce poverty and to attain middle income status by 2021.",""],[1,"705","4","Centralized Channeling of Chittagong Hill Tracts Development Funds","All funds of line Ministries for CHT development will be channelled through the Ministry of CHT Affairs.","line Ministries | Ministry of CHT Affairs"],[1,"705","4","Inclusive Participation in Development Projects in CHT Areas","Representatives of the ethnic groups will be included in development projects undertaken in their areas.",""],[1,"705","5","Strengthened Coordination of Development Work in the CHT","Coordination of development works will be strengthened through the Ministry of Chittagong Hill Tracts Affairs.","Ministry of Chittagong Hill Tracts Affairs"]],"111":[[1,"719","4","Public Sector Gender Mainstreaming Capacity Building","Training, orientation and knowledge development would be provided to all women employed in the public sector.",""],[1,"719","4","Training Institution Strengthening for Gender Mainstreaming","The capacity of the existing training institutions would be increased with experienced faculty and other resources in the area of gender mainstreaming to both women and men.",""],[1,"719","4","Women’s Leadership Training and Performance Monitoring","Leadership training and performance monitoring against defined results would be available to women on a priority basis.",""],[1,"723","3","Gender Analysis Training and Capacity-Building Programme","The capacity of PLAU and DWA should be enriched so that their staff are able to monitor performance and can guide other agencies and ministries, if needed.",""],[1,"723","3","Additional Gender Analysis Courses in Education Institutions","the education institutions should be encouraged to initiate additional courses to develop technical knowledge on how to address gender in different sectoral operations.",""],[1,"723","5","Gender Strategy Capacity Building and Mainstreaming Programme","Orientation of the policy makers and training and capacity building of existing staff contingent in different institutions has to be continued and expanded.",""],[1,"723","5","Gender Integration in Institutional Training Programmes","All training programmes of different institutions should integrate gender issues that are relevant to the sectors' or departments' operation with specific actions identified and monitoring of the same.",""],[1,"723","5","Private Sector Gender Mainstreaming Incentive","Private sectors should be encouraged to incorporate gender perspectives in their operation and employ gender specialists, if needed.",""]],"112":[[1,"690","1","Decentralization Capacity, Financing, and Responsibility Delegation Reform","Mechanisms to build capacity, finance and delegate responsibility needs to be improved.",""],[1,"694","3","Business Process Reform in Relevant Ministries and Departments","Review and reform business processes within relevant ministries and departments focusing on financial management, monitoring and evaluation, human resource management, incentive structures and coordination / collaboration skills.",""],[1,"710","4","Gender Mainstreaming Across Sectoral Interventions","First, gender will be mainstreamed into all sectoral interventions.",""],[1,"710","4","Removal of Gender Bias in Society and Institutions","Second efforts will be taken to remove all biases against women in society but also in policies, programmes, institutions.",""],[1,"712","6","Gender Responsive Budgeting Mainstreaming","steps have also been taken to incorporate gender dimensions in the formal budgeting process.",""],[1,"713","1","Gender-Sensitive Development Project Guidelines","guidelines has also been issued to ensure that development projects are prepared and reviewed in a gender sensitive way.",""],[1,"713","6","Gender Equality and Women's Empowerment Agenda","Gender equality and women's empowerment agenda for the 7th FYP is based on pursuing strategies and actions that not only enhance women's capabilities and access to resources and opportunities but also address the control over resources, decision making, reducing the barriers in structures and institutions and aim at changing social norms and protecting their rights are critical to integrate within the plan.",""],[1,"713","6","Gender Monitoring, Oversight, and Accountability Mechanisms","Establishing monitoring, oversight and accountability mechanisms is equally important.",""],[1,"714","2","Women's Advancement Enabling Environment","Create an enabling environment for women's advancement:",""],[1,"714","8","Institutional Capacity, Accountability and Oversight Improvement","Improve institutional capacity, accountability and oversight",""]],"113":[[1,"722","3","Sex-Disaggregated Progress Reporting System","To ensure results from actions related to gender equality all reporting of national progress including those related to Post 2015 agenda would be based on sex disaggregated data to allow a better understanding the progress in the area of gender equality and women's empowerment.",""],[1,"722","5","Strengthening Institutional Mechanisms for Women's Advancement","The existing institutional mechanism for women's advancement will be made more effective with accountability, capacity and authority.","NCWCD | MOWCA | DWA | PLAU | IMED | BBS | OAG | Planning Commission"],[1,"723","1","Gender-Disaggregated Data and Gender Equality Monitoring System","The BBS will be tasked with generating gender disaggregated data synchronized with the national and sectoral indicators and the reporting needs for CEDAW, SDG and such others.",""],[1,"723","1","Gender Equality Results Monitoring by IMED","IMED would have accountability to monitor gender equality results",""],[1,"723","1","Gender Budget Audit by the Office of the Auditor General","the Office of the Auditor General (OAG) should be given responsibility of auditing gender budget expenditure.",""],[1,"723","1","Gender Equality Research Support by BIDS","Bangladesh Institute of Development Studies (BIDS) can be assigned to necessary gender equality research",""],[1,"723","4","Transparent Monitoring Mechanisms for Gender Equality Results","Transparent monitoring mechanisms established and implemented to measure impact of public policies and programmes: The review of 7th FYP programmes should incorporate monitoring of gender equality results.",""],[1,"723","4","IMED Gender Equality and Women's Empowerment Monitoring","IMED monitoring should integrate monitoring of progress of women's empowerment and gender equality based on project/ Programme targets.",""],[1,"723","4","Strengthened Gender Budget Monitoring Across Agencies","More rigorous monitoring of the gender budget is essential across agencies, sectors and field level.",""],[1,"723","4","OAG Gender Equality Expenditure and Results Oversight","The OAG should be assigned to monitor expenditure and results in the area of gender equality.","OAG"],[1,"723","4","Transparent Procedures for Open Meetings and Financial Disclosure","Transparent procedures at different levels would include holding open meetings, issuing publicly available financial disclosure statements, and conducting budget review.",""],[1,"724","3","National Gender Equality Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","For establishing good monitoring and evaluation (M&E) mechanism, it is critical to have a list of agreed gender equality indicators at the national level for measuring the progress of gender equality.",""],[1,"724","3","Sectoral Key Performance Indicator Monitoring System","At the sectoral level, a few key performance indicators (KPI) in each sector would be identified and monitored.",""],[1,"724","3","GED Indicator Finalization Support","The GED of the Planning Commission would finalize the indicators with support from sectoral ministries.","GED of the Planning Commission | sectoral ministries"],[1,"724","3","Stakeholder Results and Indicator Communication for Implementation","All relevant stakeholders working in the sector should be informed of the expected results and indicators so that they are also active in implementing actions and monitoring for those results.",""]],"114":[[1,"170","2","Diversification of Government Financing Sources","the government would need to diversify its sources of financing with proper mix of domestic and external financing, and on both fronts identify market based additional sources of financing.",""],[1,"170","2","Shift Toward Long-Term Government Securities and Infrastructure Bonds","On the domestic borrowing front, dependence on National Savings Schemes and short-term treasury bills should give way to long-term treasury bills and bonds, infrastructure bonds, etc. with proper secondary market and a well-developed yield curve.",""],[1,"170","3","Government Financing and Debt Management Strategy","These strategic transformations should be done on the basis of a comprehensive Government Financing and Debt Management Strategy to be prepared by the Debt Management Wing of the Ministry of Finance.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"170","3","Expanded External Concessional Borrowing and Sovereign Bond Financing","On the external front, the access to traditional concessional borrowing from official bilateral and multilateral sources should be increased and at the same time complemented with additional borrowings in the form of sovereign bonds of various maturities and other sources of financing.",""],[1,"170","3","Mobilization of Concessional External Financing for Infrastructure Investment","In addition to the traditional access to multilateral institutions like the World Bank and ADB, the new Asian Infrastructure Bank is also expected to help mobilize concessional external financing for infrastructure investment in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"170","3","Launch of First Sovereign Bond","The government should try to establish its relations with the international capital market by launching its first sovereign bond soon because external and domestic conditions are favourable for such a launch.",""],[1,"171","1","Sovereign Bond Financing","To meet up the short-fall, the non-concessional windows of both multilateral agencies and international capital market through issuance of sovereign bonds may play significant role.",""],[1,"171","1","Long-Term Domestic Bond Market Development","Similarly, the Government would make efforts to develop the long-term domestic bond market by issuing longer maturity Government bonds and bills, and thereby reduce its dependence on borrowing through the National Savings Schemes.",""],[1,"173","1","Prudent Public Debt Management Strategy","Government's public debt management strategy under the Seventh Plan will continue to be guided by prudent fiscal management, with the overall fiscal deficit limited to no more than 5% of GDP",""],[1,"173","2","Prudent External Borrowing Strategy","The external financing strategy under the Plan will essentially maintain the current strategy of prudent external borrowing on best possible terms with maximum utilization of concessional official bilateral and multilateral borrowing.",""],[1,"173","2","Concessional Financing for Major Infrastructure Projects","Many of the infrastructure projects in the transport and energy sector (like Matarbari Power Hub; Dhaka Metro Rail; Karnaphuli River Tunnel etc.) can be financed from concessional borrowing.",""],[1,"173","2","Climate Change Mitigation Project Financing","Bangladesh can also implement projects to mitigate the adverse effects of climate change which can be funded under relevant multilateral initiatives.",""],[1,"173","2","Acceleration of Donor-Funded Project Implementation","There is also scope for accelerating the pace of donor funded project implementation and reduce the very large aid pipeline which currently stands at more than $19 billion (about 6 years of aid utilization).",""],[1,"173","3","External Financing Diversification Strategy","The external financing strategy under the Plan would also entail broadening of the sources of external financing, creating greater scope for private investors to secure external financing on better terms through reduced country/sovereign risk, and continued reliance on official bilateral and multilateral sources for financing large public sector projects or achieving social sector objectives under the Plan.",""],[1,"173","4","Domestic Public Debt Management and Borrowing Diversification","reliance on domestic financing will increase and the level of outstanding domestic public debt would continue to increase.",""],[1,"174","1","Domestic Interest Payment Reduction Measures","efforts will be made under the Seventh Plan to slow down the growth of domestic interest payments by reducing dependence on high cost borrowing.",""],[1,"174","6","Debt Management Reform","Accordingly, debt management reforms will be undertaken to make public borrowing cheaper and also help develop domestic bond market.",""],[1,"174","6","Interest Rate Rationalization for National Savings Instruments","The Government will also continue to keep rationalizing the interest rate structure of national savings instruments in line with interest rate developments in the money/bond market.",""],[1,"178","3","Reduce Reliance on External Financing","there will be a significant further reduction in the reliance on external financing of the budget during the Plan period",""],[1,"178","3","Sustain External Debt and Debt Service Reduction","The sustained reduction of external debt and debt service payments in relation to GDP and exports of goods and remittances, respectively, would certainly reduce Bangladesh's vulnerability to external shocks",""],[1,"178","4","Domestic Financing Source Rationalization","The sources of domestic financing and the interest rates paid on non-bank borrowing would need to be rationalized with the developments in the market-based interest rate structure",""],[1,"178","4","Domestic Bond Market Development","Development of domestic bond market with proper development of the regulatory regime and the demand and supply side of the domestic bond market will be important for diversifying the domestic financing sources.",""]],"115":[[1,"79","7","Judicial Financial and Legal Support","Financial and legal support to the judiciary to strengthen its capacity to ensure faster disposal of civil and criminal cases.",""],[1,"208","2","Judiciary Strengthening Reform","These critical areas for intervention include: (b) judiciary;",""],[1,"214","1","Computerized Court Case Recording and Tracking System","Basic initiatives have been taken to improve the judiciary such as the computerized court case recording and tracking system.",""],[1,"214","1","Judicial Information Access Website","Information is also accessible to people through the website.",""],[1,"214","1","Court Case Management and Criminal Justice Coordination Committees Pilot","A pilot has been undertaken in lower courts regarding case management committees and criminal justice coordination committees.",""],[1,"214","1","NGO-Facilitated Access to Justice and Legal Awareness","The Government has enabled NGOs to facilitate access to the judicial system by the poor, women and vulnerable people and in building awareness among them.",""],[1,"214","1","Alternative Dispute Resolution Strengthening and Regulation","The Government has taken measures to strengthen alternative dispute mechanisms by regulating them with formal and traditional laws.",""],[1,"217","1","Judicial Performance Improvement Programme","to improve the quality of institutional performance within the judiciary system, a pragmatic set of activities are articulated under the Seventh Plan so that the overall performance of the judiciary is improved.",""],[1,"217","3","Ombudsman Appointment and Resourcing","An Ombudsman will be appointed with sufficient resources as guaranteed by the Article 77 of the Constitution of the People's Republic of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"217","4","Supreme Court Judge Recruitment Reform","A clear, transparent recruitment process and specific criteria for the Supreme Court judges will be established.",""],[1,"217","5","Court Administrative Procedure Streamlining","Measures will be taken to streamlining administrative procedure of the court.",""],[1,"217","6","Computerized Court Case Recording and Tracking System","Computerized court case recording and tracking system will be introduced which will allow all information to be accessible to citizens through websites.",""],[1,"217","8","District-Level Case Management and Coordination Committee","A \"Case Management & Coordination Committee\" will be established for civil and criminal matters at the district level.",""],[1,"217","9","Court Backlog Reduction Measures","Measures will be taken to slow down the rate at which backlog of cases are growing.",""],[1,"217","10","Bar Council Lawyer Accountability and Integrity Measures","Bar Council will be required to take effective steps to ensure the accountability of the lawyers and also to maintain integrity.",""],[1,"217","11","Local Justice Capacity Building for Violence Against Women Response","Violence against women will become a key focus of local justice institutions, requiring greater investment in capacity building at the district and upazila level",""],[1,"217","12","Land Dispute Mitigation Initiatives","Ministry of Land and Ministry of Law, Justice and Parliamentary Affairs will conceptualize and undertake new initiatives to mitigate land disputes, which has an undue effect on judicial effectiveness.","Ministry of Land | Ministry of Law, Justice and Parliamentary Affairs"],[1,"217","13","Annual Recruitment of Judicial Officials","Evaluate and implement the recommendation of the Law Commission of recruiting adequate number of judicial officials every year for the next five years to address the 3 million case-backlog in the judiciary.",""],[1,"217","14","Village Courts Scaling-Up and Strengthening Strategy","Scaling-up and strengthening of the village courts - formulation and implementation of a national strategy together with an investment plan to ensure greater access to the disadvantaged sections of the population.",""],[1,"218","1","Village Court Dispute Resolution Mechanism","The local Government will encourage citizens, particularly in rural areas to avail the village court mechanism to resolve disputes without resorting to formal justice institutions.",""],[1,"218","2","National Legal Aid Services Organization Capacity Enhancement","The Government will enhance the capacity of National Legal Aid Services Organization (NLASO) through management systems and procedures, as well as human resources, particularly in supporting the poor and women.",""],[1,"218","3","NGO and Government Agency Legal Aid Partnership Strategy","NLASO will develop a strategy for engaging with NGOs and other Government agencies to promote access to justice; through this partnership, they will set targets for jointly providing quality legal aid, especially for the poor, women and marginalized, with each agency transparently reporting on their own activities.","NLASO | NGOs | other Government agencies"],[1,"218","4","District Legal Aid Officer Appointment","The NLASO will appoint District Legal Aid Officers in 64 districts.",""],[1,"218","6","Legal Basis for Alternative Dispute Resolution","A legal basis for ADR will be created, building on the current legislation, to establish an extra tier of mediation under ADR.",""],[1,"218","7","Local ADR Capacity Building and Public Awareness Initiative","The Government will undertake initiatives for improving the capacity of ADR at the local level regarding mediation, as well as public awareness.",""],[1,"218","9","Judicial Reform Support Investment","To ensure the effective completion of the activities mentioned above for judicial reform, it is needless to say that the administration of justice will require adequate investment.",""],[1,"218","10","Judiciary Digitization Initiative","This digitization will cover all the necessary equipment for the Judges and Court stuff, hardware and connectivity support and relevant software support.","Supreme Court | ICT Ministry | Access to Information (a2i) of PMO"],[1,"218","11","E-Judiciary Development Team and Coordination Mechanism","For establishing e-judiciary in Bangladesh there must be linking of PMO and Supreme Court for establishing e-judiciary team within a2i programme comprised of judges of subordinate judiciary to come up with a work plan in terms of long term development of e-judiciary system in every jurisdiction of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"218","12","Crime Data Database System","a process should be introduced where in all data relating to crime, criminals, prison etc. be prepared and kept in the database for future use.",""],[1,"218","13","Judiciary Digital Staffing Arrangement","In every district there must a Programmer and some Assistant Programmers to look after the digital activities of the Judiciary.",""],[1,"219","1","Judiciary Infrastructure Development","There must be infrastructural development of both the Supreme Court and subordinate Judiciary to cover the accommodation for ejlash and offices of all section a Court.",""],[1,"219","3","Judicial Pay Structure Reform","Towards this end, pay of the Judge of the both tiers must be increased.",""],[1,"219","4","District Judicial Complex Construction Programme","Therefore, there should be infrastructural development in terms of judicial complex in every district.",""],[1,"219","4","Judicial Transport Safety Provision","Besides, there must vehicle facilities for all judges in every tire to ensure their safety of transportation and movement.",""],[1,"623","7","Online Court Case Status and Digital Cause List System","Mechanisms are also being established for online status check of court cases.",""],[1,"624","1","Judicial Web Network Connectivity Initiative","initiative has been adopted to connect all subordinate/lower courts with the Bangladesh Supreme Court, through a web network to store important data, track case and modernize information exchange system.",""],[1,"642","2","Judicial Case Management Digitization","eliminating pending cases through digitization of case and court management process",""],[1,"642","2","ICT Integration in Legal Process","improving legal enforcement system through integration of ICTs in all stages of legal process, e.g., digitization of case record management",""],[1,"642","3","Digital Case Management System","To expedite case management process, the present system would be transformed into a digital system, starting from filing, recording of presence to witness and evidence production.",""],[1,"642","3","Automated Court Cause List Generation","This will automatically generate cause list of the day in the respective court with specified time.",""],[1,"642","3","Online and Mobile Court Fee Payment System","Court and other process fees should be paid online or through mobile phones.",""],[1,"642","4","ICT-Based Judicial Case Management System","A modern record keeping, filing and maintaining case proceedings using ICT based management system will be introduced to strengthen the judiciary governance mechanism.",""],[1,"642","5","Digital Court Information and E-Filing System","The websites of courts at all levels would be developed which will ideally provide information on: general court information, cause lists, roster, court fees, case status, orders etc.",""],[1,"642","5","Court Digital Data Archiving and Backup System","All digital data will be archived and will be backed up each day to two different locations in the same jurisdiction and to a third in a relatively disaster-free area, saving them from destruction by unforeseen calamities.",""],[1,"642","6","Online and SMS Legal Case Information Service","Case and court procedure related information will be made available online or sent using SMS.",""],[1,"642","6","Local Government Information Access Point Filing Support","Agencies will maintain liaison with the local government institutions to use their information access points as their first face for filing any plea.",""],[1,"642","6","Proactive Information Disclosure Policy","The Information Commission has put in place a Proactive Information Disclosure Policy to specify the requirement for government institutions in complying with the RTI Act, 2009.","Information Commission | Cabinet Division"],[1,"642","6","RTI Compliance Monitoring Mechanism","it is important that the Commission, in collaboration with the Cabinet Division, monitors compliance of all government institutions.","Information Commission | Cabinet Division"]],"116":[[1,"144","5","Land Administration and Land Market Reform","there is an important need to strengthen the land administration regime and related land market through a range of institutional, regulatory and fiscal policy reforms.",""],[1,"145","1","Land Records Computerization and Transaction Simplification Reform","computerization of land records; simplification of land transactions and land registration.",""],[1,"528","2","Computerization of Land Records Management","Government has taken steps to simplify the titling and registration of property through starting of computerization of land records management, but that effort needs to be accelerated.",""],[1,"635","5","Land Administration and Land Use Policy Review","The relevant authorities will conduct further investigations to sift through the evidences taking into consideration latest technological advances and develop a new set of policies for proper land administration and land use.",""],[1,"635","5","Stakeholder Review Process for Land Policy and Legal Frameworks","A review process will be initiated to consider how the stakeholders of those policies and legal",""],[1,"636","1","Independent Review and Advisory Body","A high-powered independent body will be established to give recommendations for next steps based on such a review and through a consultative and inclusive process.",""]],"117":[[1,"453","16","Land Use Planning and Management Project","Land Use Planning and Management Project in the Upazillas of Bangladesh",""],[1,"466","12","GIS-Based Land Use Mapping and Analysis Capacity Development","Develop capacity of national government and regional/local offices to map and analyse land use through data-driven approaches/GIS",""],[1,"491","11","Land Conversion Regulation and Binding Land Use Planning","Regulating conversion of lands & introducing binding land use plans.",""],[1,"494","2","Land Zoning and Proper Land Use Planning","Land zoning and proper land use plan is considered an utmost necessity.",""],[1,"494","3","National Land Zoning and Land Use Planning Action Plan","Undertaking an action plan to complete the land zoning & land use plan for the entire country and DoE to consult the above stated plan(s) prior to making decisions on the award of Site clearance & Environment Clearance.",""]],"118":[[1,"54","1","Local Government Legal Framework","i) A Local Government Legal Framework (LGFL) - This single legal instrument (LGFL) will cover all units and tiers, irrespective of urban and rural, regarding their formation, function, jurisdiction, taxation, finance, budget account, electoral process, and central-local and local-local relationships;",""],[1,"54","1","Local Government Capacity Building Programme","ii) Building the capacity of local governments through assignment of appropriate officials, technical assistance and training programmes;",""],[1,"54","1","Local Planning and Budgeting Capacity Development","iii) Developing planning and budgeting capacities at the local level to help design and implement local level programmes;",""],[1,"54","1","Local-National Planning Linkage Technical Assistance","iv) Fostering initiatives to provide technical assistance to link local level plan to the national medium to long term planning.",""],[1,"72","3","Public Administration and Local Government Strengthening","The focus on strengthening public administration and local governments will be a key priority for the Seventh Plan.",""],[1,"77","5","Devolution of Health and Education Service Responsibilities to Local Governments","stronger efforts are needed to implement the Sixth Plan's recommendation to devolve service responsibilities in health and education to the local governments",""],[1,"77","6","Government Coordination and Decentralization Reform","Greater decentralization, with responsibilities and budgets actually divided between the different institutions and levels will help this coordination process considerably.",""],[1,"79","5","Local Government Institutional Strengthening and Fiscal Autonomy Reform","Strengthening of the local government institutions based on a well-defined legal framework that assigns responsibilities along with commensurate financial autonomy.",""],[1,"156","8","Local Government Institution Strengthening for Development Delivery","Local government institutions such as Union Parishads and Upazila Parishads should be strengthened to conduct development activities of the government through these institutions.",""],[1,"208","2","Local Government Strengthening Reform","These critical areas for intervention include: (d) local government.",""],[1,"212","5","Local Planning and Budgeting Capacity Strengthening","Efforts to improve planning and budgeting capacity at the local level have been initiated.",""],[1,"212","5","Local Government Transparency and Accountability Measures","Some measures have been taken to increase the transparency and accountability of local Governments.",""],[1,"212","5","Local Government Training and Technical Assistance Programme","Training and technical assistance programmes have been undertaken which has helped improve the capacity of local Governments.",""],[1,"436","2","Strengthening Local Government Institutions","The government is committed to establish strong local government institutions at various level through active participation of the elected representatives in the administration as well as development activities.","Local Government Division"],[1,"436","2","Local Government Development and Service Delivery Activities","Local Government Division is implementing various development and service-oriented activities for poverty alleviation and to make the rural people's life more comfortable, sound and meaningful.","Local Government Division"],[1,"436","4","Local Government Institution Capacity-Building and Training Programme","For enhanced good governance both technical and investment projects have been taken through which capacity of the LGIs elected representatives and staffs are enhanced through training.",""],[1,"436","4","LGI Staff Training Manual Development and Training Rollout","Training manuals for LGI staff have been developed and some training is underway.",""],[1,"437","2","Local Government Institutional Strengthening","Strengthening Local Govt. institutions is an important mandate for Local govt. Division.","Local govt. Division"],[1,"437","8","Local Government Training and Technical Assistance Programme","Training and technical assistance programmes have been undertaken which has helped improve the capacity of local Governments.",""],[1,"437","9","Local Planning and Budgeting Capacity Improvement","Some efforts to improve planning and budgeting capacity at the local level have been initiated.",""],[1,"438","3","Local Government Project Planning and Implementation","LGD is also responsible for planning and implementation of development projects in the local level, conducting survey/ research regarding local government and arranging training programme for enhancing knowledge and efficiency of the elected representatives.","LGD"],[1,"438","3","NILG Training and Research Programme","To strengthen the governance at the local level, National Institute of Local Government (NILG) under LGD is imparting training to elected public representatives and related officers and staff and doing research on local government matters.","LGD"],[1,"440","2","City Corporation Formation and Governance Arrangement","City Corporation shall be formed with composition of (a) Mayor, (b) Councillors, same number as government defined ward numbers through gazette notification and (c) Female councillors, as defined number reserved for female.",""],[1,"440","3","Paurashava Formation and Composition Reform","Paurashavas shall be formed with composition of (a) Mayor, (b) Councillors, same number as government defined ward numbers through gazette notification and (c) Female councillors, as defined number reserved for female.",""],[1,"441","3","Governance Improvement Programme for Municipalities","LGED is continuing its Governance Improvement Programme through 4 major projects in 80 Paurashvas and City Corporations; Municipal Government Support Project (MGSP) financed by World Bank in 26, Northern Bangladesh Integrated Development Project (NOBIDEP) by JICA in 18 Paurashavas, Urban Governance Improvement and Infrastructure Project (UGIIP)-3 by ADB in 31 and City Governance Project (CGP) by JICA in 5 Paurashavas and City Corporations.",""],[1,"441","6","Municipal Capacity Development Support","MSP and UGIIP are providing support in capacity development of Municipalities in different phases covering 183 Paurashavas and City Corporations out of 335 Paurashavas and City Corporations through Municipal Support Unit (MSU) of LGED.",""],[1,"441","6","Performance-Based Municipal Project Allocation","Performance based allocation of these projects improved the implementation process.",""],[1,"442","8","Strengthening Decentralized Local Government and Public Participation","The key issues that will be focused on during the 7th Plan period include the regulatory environment that will be able to operate within a strengthened and decentralized local government, with scope for adequate public participation in local government decision making and overcoming the poor institutional and financial capacities of the urban local bodies.",""],[1,"443","2","Model Local Government Tax Schedule Framework","The Government may frame model tax schedules and where such schedule have been framed, the LGIs shall be guided by them in levying tax, rate, toll or fees.",""],[1,"443","3","Gradual Increase in Block Grants to Local Government Institutions","The proportion may be increased gradually commensurate with capacity development and assessment of results.",""],[1,"443","4","Local Government Participation in National Project Formulation","Participation of LGIs in national projects needs to be ensured during the formulation of the projects.",""],[1,"443","6","Local Government Service Reform","To address the issue with renewed commitment, a long pending proposal to create a 'Local Government Service' may be reviewed afresh with a long-term vision of sustained professionalism at the LGI levels.",""],[1,"444","1","Updated LGI Capacity Development Policy Framework","The LGI capacity development needs an updated policy framework and an independent resource pool.",""],[1,"444","1","Expanded LGI Capacity Development Training Modules","Besides standard training modules, the updated capacity development approach should include new focus such as:",""],[1,"444","8","Local Government Strengthening Programme","The Government acknowledges that strengthening the local Government is pivotal for improving public service delivery.",""],[1,"444","9","Local Government Legal Framework Development","A Local Government Legal Framework (LGLF) will be created so that Bangladesh can create a strong enough LGI system.",""],[1,"444","10","Local Government Performance Accountability Framework","Increasing the transparency and improving the accountability of local Governments by establishing indicators and standards for measuring performance in service delivery at local level, broadening the role of oversight institutions which would perform financial and service delivery audits, and investigating irregularities and make the reports available to public.",""],[1,"444","11","Local Government Capacity-Building Programme","Building the capacity of local Governments through assignment of proper officials, technical assistance and training programmes.",""],[1,"445","1","Local Planning and Budgeting Capacity Development","Developing planning and budgeting capacities at the local level to help design and implement local level programmes.",""],[1,"445","4","National Tax Revenue Sharing Formula","A comprehensive tax sharing formula will be adopted in the National Tax Policy for sharing national tax revenue between national and local Governments.",""],[1,"445","5","Local Participation in National Project Formulation","Participation of LGIs in local components of the national projects will be ensured during the formulation of the projects at national level.",""],[1,"445","5","Local Inclusive Development Initiative","Concept of Inclusive development will be initiated at local level among the Govt. agencies, Private Sector with the help of Local Govt. Institutions.",""],[1,"649","4","Scaling Up Field-Level Service Delivery Through Local Government Institutions","First, massive scaling-up on multiple fronts of field-level service delivery through local government institutes will be done.",""],[1,"649","4","Review of Legal and Policy Framework for Local Government Institutions","Secondly, the Government will review the legal and policy framework guiding those institutions as well as assessment of their capacity to ensure that these services are accessible to the disadvantaged groups.",""],[1,"649","4","Beneficiary Capacity Assessment and Capacity-Building Support","Third, capacity of the beneficiary groups will be assessed and built if required.",""],[1,"649","4","Disaggregated Data Mobilization for Participation Monitoring","Fourth, disaggregated data indicating specific usage by disadvantaged groups and other priority groups like women will be mobilized to monitor participation.",""],[1,"660","8","Private and Local Government Support for Cultural Development","Private sector as well as the local government bodies will be encouraged to contribute their resources and efforts for cultural development;",""]],"119":[[1,"18","11","Prudential Regulations Strengthening","Strengthen Prudential Regulations",""],[1,"48","1","Prudent Macroeconomic Management","The 7th Plan will continue the emphasis on prudent macroeconomic management.",""],[1,"48","1","Inflation Reduction Policy","the objective of higher growth will be balanced with efforts to further reduce inflation to 5.5% by FY20.",""],[1,"48","5","Tax Policy and Administration Reform and Modernization","Financing of this national Plan will require increased private and public sector savings, rapid income growth for the private sector and increased revenue mobilization through reform and modernization of tax policy and tax administration.",""],[1,"48","5","Public Resource Efficiency and Subsidy Transfer Improvement","Prudent spending of public sector resources for better public service delivery and subsidy/transfer programmes, and improved efficiency of public sector enterprises will be important for public sector resource efficiency and productivity.",""],[1,"79","8","Public Bank Reform to Reduce Non-Performing Loans","Reform of public banks to reduce non-performing loans and bad lending decisions.",""],[1,"79","9","Tax Modernization Project Implementation","Stronger implementation of the Tax Modernization Project with a special focus on strengthening income tax collections.",""],[1,"82","12","Prudent Macroeconomic Policy Mix","instituting a prudent macroeconomic policy mix",""],[1,"98","4","Macroeconomic Stability Maintenance Policy Mix","Much of the fiscal, monetary, and exchange rate policies are in place to sustain the record of prudent yet growth-friendly macroeconomic policies during the 7th FYP.",""],[1,"99","1","Banking Sector Strengthening and Supervision Reform","The efficiency and financial health of the banking sector must be strengthened by easing controls over the interest rate, through better banking supervision and oversight by the Bangladesh Bank, and through corporatization of public banks.","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"99","1","Stock Market Regulatory Authority and Market Entry Facilitation","The stock market management is being improved by establishing a strong regulatory authority, and providing a better enabling environment for new entrants to the stock market.",""],[1,"100","5","Land Market Reform Measures","Measures will have to be taken to correct these problems on a priority basis in order to accelerate the growth effort.",""]],"120":[[1,"234","3","Universal Machine Readable Passport and Visa Issuance","In order to provide Machine Readable Passport (MRP) to all Bangladeshi citizens according to the International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO) guideline and to issue & extend the validity of Machine Readable Visa (MRV) is the main function of DIP.",""],[1,"234","3","Simplification of Bangladesh Visa Issuance Process","the simplification of the process of obtaining Bangladesh visas will facilitate foreign professionals' employment within the country and promote transfers of knowledge and technologies.",""],[1,"234","3","Simplification of Passport Issuance for Bangladeshi Nationals","Simplification of the issuing of passports to Bangladesh nationals will also help to accelerate export of labour to the overseas markets.",""],[1,"234","4","Travel Document Security and Authenticity Measures","To ensure security& authenticity of travel documents- passport and visa;",""],[1,"234","5","Electronic Passport Introduction","To introduce Electronic Passport (e-passport) by 2020;",""],[1,"234","6","Modern Training Centre Establishment","To establish a modern training Centre for improvement of skill & professional knowledge;",""],[1,"234","7","Passport and Visa Information Website Service","Provide passport and visa related information on the website.",""]],"121":[[1,"174","7","Enhanced Plan Implementation Capacity, Governance, and Results-Based M&E","Accordingly, the Government will be paying enhanced attention to implementation capacity, governance and result-based monitoring and evaluation (M&E) under the Plan.",""],[1,"184","1","Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation System","the Sixth Five Year Plan marked a decisive shift from the earlier approach of undertaking monitoring and evaluation (M&E) of the plan and associated programmes by tracking spending to a more results based M&E system which jointly assesses public spending and achievement of objectives.",""],[1,"184","3","Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation Institutional Reforms","the Seventh Five Year Plan translates this priority in concrete terms by outlining institutional reforms and activities that will be implemented by policymakers between 2015 and 2020 to move towards an effective results-based M&E.",""],[1,"184","3","Development Results Framework for Plan Monitoring","the GoB acknowledges that a comprehensive Development Results Framework is required for monitoring results of the Seventh Five Year Plan.",""],[1,"184","3","Macro-Level Monitoring and Evaluation System Strengthening","the focus of the exercise is on the various aspects of macro level M&E system.",""],[1,"185","1","Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation System","While the Seventh Plan takes specific steps to move towards a results-based M&E and strengthen the process initiated during 6th FYP.",""],[1,"185","2","Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation Institutional Reform","Thus, to mitigate such institutional, structural and policy deficits, which undermines the overall state of results-based M&E system within the public sector, the principle strategy of the GoB will be to undertake major institutional reforms and implement a comprehensive set of activities that will create a conducive environment for an effective M&E culture.",""],[1,"185","3","Adaptive Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","The M&E framework should be best seen as a dynamic process.",""],[1,"185","5","National Monitoring and Evaluation Framework Development","the Planning Commission rightly focuses on developing a nation-wide M&E framework in coordination with the Ministry of Finance and the line ministries","Planning Commission | Ministry of Finance | the line ministries"],[1,"185","5","Medium-Term Budgetary Framework Coordination Mechanism","the adoption of the medium-term budgetary framework (MTBF) as the main instrument for coordination with national planning and fiscal management",""],[1,"185","5","Line Ministry Monitoring and Evaluation Strengthening","the role of M&E at the line ministry level also gains significance","the line ministries"],[1,"185","5","Planning Commission M&E Capacity Strengthening","to further strengthen the capacity of the Planning Commission in guiding the overall M&E process","Planning Commission"],[1,"186","2","IMED Institutional Reform and Capacity Development Programme","GoB will undertake a thorough review of the present functions, accountabilities and capacities of IMED.",""],[1,"186","3","Project Impact Assessment and Micro-Level Monitoring Enhancement","The GoB will also use IMED to undertake impact assessment of project with the help of both experimental and non-experimental data so that M&E at the micro-level moves beyond simply tracking the financial and physical completion of the projects.",""],[1,"186","3","IMED Collaboration with Non-State Actors","IMED will be encouraged to develop collaboration with non-state actors, such as experts and think-tanks.",""],[1,"186","4","Strengthening Line Ministry M&E Capabilities","the M&E capabilities of the line ministries themselves will be strengthened.",""],[1,"186","4","Reforming Planning Commission Coordination Units","In addition to reforming the coordinating units in the Planning Commission, the M&E capabilities of the line ministries themselves will be strengthened.",""],[1,"186","5","Results-Based M&E Capacity Building for Line Ministries","First, a comprehensive training modules and manuals will be developed that are demanded by the civil servants for effective understanding and operationalization of the result-based M&E system.",""],[1,"186","5","Line Ministry M&E Strategy Development Plan","Second, a capacity building plan will be developed which will pinpoint how line ministries will design an M&E strategy, so that sufficient incentives are available for staffs to effectively undertake M&E for all its projects.",""],[1,"186","5","Results-Based M&E Good Practice Review","Third, revision of existing good practice for a results-based M&E from relevant international experience so that some lessons can be drawn to improve the existing results based M&E system of line Ministries.",""],[1,"187","4","Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation Unit Institutionalization","A dedicated Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation (RBM) Unit will be institutionalized within GED to carry out these responsibilities.",""],[1,"188","1","GED Monitoring and Evaluation Capacity Strengthening","Analysis and Monitoring Wing of GED will be redefined to make Seventh Plan related M&Es as a key part of its accountability.",""],[1,"188","1","GED Technical Assistance Support","To deliver this accountability, GED will require technical assistance that could be funded through donor support.",""],[1,"188","1","GED Capacity Building Programme","On the whole, over the Seventh Plan time interval, the capacity of GED will be built up with range of activities aimed at improving staffing, skills and technology.",""],[1,"188","2","Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation Unit","The proposed Unit should keep in front the following key objectives in order to establish an effective Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation Unit:",""],[1,"188","3","Results Framework Development and Finalization","To cooperate with other stakeholders in the Planning Commission and across government in developing and finalizing a Results Framework against which can track achievement of the Government of Bangladesh in terms of economic and social policies and strategic priorities (as expressed in the Seventh Five Year Plan) can be reported;","Planning Commission"],[1,"188","4","National Statistical Data Flow and Monitoring Support","To work with the Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics and other data providers to develop and ensure adequate and timely flows of data from the National Statistical System that will allow meaningful monitoring of the indicators included in the Results Framework;","Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics"],[1,"188","5","Sectoral Performance Monitoring Coordination","To coordinate with line Ministries and other service providers to ensure the availability of supplementary quantitative and qualitative information to facilitate the monitoring of sectoral performance relevant to the indicators in the Results Framework;","line Ministries | other service providers"],[1,"188","6","Five-Year Monitoring and Evaluation Plan","To develop in discussion with stakeholders and implement a 5-year M&E Plan in alignment with national development plan timeframe, including both major thematic evaluations and smaller-scale programme or large project evaluations, that will further illuminate the progress being made towards the achievement of the outcomes and impacts envisaged in the Results Framework;",""],[1,"188","7","Regular Government Reporting and Policy Briefing Mechanism","To institute a series of regular reports to the Prime Minister, the Cabinet, the National Economic Council and the ECNEC on an annual basis, supplemented by ad hoc policy briefs on matters requiring the attention of and action by the Government, and to ensure that its regular reports are both published and drawn to the attention of the media and the relevant committees of Parliament;",""],[1,"188","8","Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation System","To promote a results-based approach to monitoring and evaluation across government system.",""],[1,"188","9","Results Framework Development and Consultation Process","the GED has taken a lead to design a Results Framework for the Seventh Five Year Plan in collaboration with BBS, IMED and line ministries.","GED | BBS | IMED | line ministries"],[1,"189","2","Monitoring and Evaluation Data Repository System","Thus, to aid the creation of such database, the following activities will be undertaken.",""],[1,"189","3","DRF Monitoring and Evaluation Database Development","To facilitate the monitoring processes described earlier, the DRF M&E database will be developed and maintained throughout the Seventh Five Year Plan cycle.",""],[1,"189","4","Expert Assessment on DevInfo-Based Monitoring Dissemination","Hence, within the first year of the Seventh Plan time frame, an expert assessment on the aforementioned issue will be undertaken and the recommendations will be implemented within the second year of the Seventh Plan.",""],[1,"189","5","Web-Based Monitoring Data Repository and Portal","The M&E Unit under GED will firstly develop the data repository based on DRF of 7th Five Year Plan and the Government's commitment to the International Development Framework like MDG/SDG and extend into a web-based system.",""],[1,"189","6","DevInfo-Based DRF Monitoring System","The DevInfo will be used to bring together all the information tailored to the DRF outcomes, outputs, and focus areas that will support monitoring of the Seventh Five Year Plan.",""],[1,"190","1","Stakeholder Partnership for Monitoring and Evaluation","A solid M&E effort involves building partnerships with stakeholders including NGOs, CSOs and independent academic/research institutions.",""],[1,"190","1","Outsourced Monitoring and Evaluation Support","These institutions have professional and analytical strengths that can be tapped by the GED and IMED to outsource a significant amount of the M&E effort, particularly at the early years when in-house capacity is constrained.",""],[1,"190","1","Hands-on M&E Capacity Building for Staff","Additionally, this partnership can result in hands-on training for GED, BBS and IMED staff through their active involvement with the M&E exercise.",""],[1,"190","2","GED Collaboration with Research Institutions for M&E and Capacity Building","The GED has already started collaboration with a range of research institutions in the context of the Sixth Plan.",""],[1,"190","3","National Monitoring and Evaluation Coordination under the Sixth Plan","At the macroeconomic level, the Sixth Plan and its implementation provided the platform for coordinating the national level M&E effort.",""],[1,"190","4","Seventh Plan Annual Progress Reporting Process","The annual review process will introduce with the preparation of the Seventh Plan Annual Progress Report.",""],[1,"190","5","Seventh Plan Mid-Term Review","The third annual review will be replaced by the Seventh Plan Mid Term Review.","GED"],[1,"190","6","Independent External Evaluation of the Seventh Plan","The final review or evaluation will be conducted by an independent and external evaluator to assess the relevance, efficiency, effectiveness, impact and sustainability of the Seventh Plan's contribution.",""],[1,"191","1","Final-Year Plan Evaluation and Stakeholder Validation","evaluation will be conducted in the final year of the Seventh Plan to allow incorporation of the results and lessons learned into the subsequent national development planning.",""],[1,"191","2","M&E Review and Dissemination Mechanism","The findings of M&E will be reviewed through workshops with stakeholders.",""],[1,"191","3","Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation System Strengthening","the government will ensure that the information used for M&E is trustworthy and credible.",""],[1,"212","2","Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","The Government has also facilitated improvements in the 'planning and budgeting framework' and adopting a better 'results based monitoring and evaluation framework'.",""],[1,"212","4","Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation Institutionalization","Efforts are also underway to institutionalize arrangements at GED to undertake periodic results based M&E exercise at the macroeconomic and sectoral levels.",""],[1,"212","4","Project-Specific Results-Based Monitoring Strengthening","IMED continues to focus on physical and financial aspects of project implementation.",""],[1,"215","3","Annual Performance Agreement System","Under the system an Annual Performance Agreement is signed between the Secretary of the concerned Ministry/Division and the Cabinet Secretary.",""],[1,"215","3","Government Performance Management System","To this end, the Government has already formulated a framework of performance management called Annual Performance Agreement (APA).",""],[1,"215","3","Cabinet Division GPMS Implementation Unit","Furthermore, the Government has established a separate Unit in the Cabinet Division headed by a Secretary and this Unit has been entrusted with the responsibilities inter alia of implementing the Government Performance Management System (GPMS).",""]],"122":[[1,"7","3","SDG Implementation Initiation","the launch of UN's post-2015 Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) which ultimately provide us opportunity to initiate implementation of SDGs",""],[1,"13","1","Domestic Resource Mobilization Capacity Strengthening","For that to happen, we will have our capacity for domestic resource mobilization further strengthened.",""],[1,"13","1","Development Result Framework Monitoring System","Overall implementation process of the Plan will be monitored by GED using a Development Result Framework (DRF), comprising of a total of 88 indicators spreading over 14 thematic areas.","GED"],[1,"13","2","Sector Strategy and Plan Framework for Thirteen Development Sectors","In line with the 7th Five Year Plan, there will be Sector Strategy/Plan of these thirteen development sectors.",""],[1,"13","2","Public Investment Management Synchronization","The mismatch between the sectoral divide, followed by the Ministry of Finance and the Planning Commission, for Public Investment Management (PIM) is synchronized for the first time in the planning history to ensure efficient use of public resources for better development outcome.","Ministry of Finance | Planning Commission"],[1,"13","2","Sectoral Strategy Compliance in Project and Programme Formulation","Finally, it is expected that the concerned Ministries/Divisions and implementing agencies will follow the sectoral strategies while formulating project and programmes during the 7th FYP period to guarantee that projects/programmes that are used as a tool to attain the objectives of the Plan.","concerned Ministries/Divisions"],[1,"13","3","Seventh Five Year Plan Preparation and Monitoring Project","The logistics support from 'Preparation and Monitoring of Medium Term Development Plans (Seventh Five Year Plan)' project of GED as well as technical inputs and support from the UNDP financed 'Support to Sustainable and Inclusive Planning' project is laudable.",""],[1,"48","5","Annual Budget Alignment with Seventh Plan Objectives","Annual Budgets will be formulated in a manner consistent with the realization of the Seventh Plan objectives.",""],[1,"51","10","Results-Based Monitoring and Evaluation Strategy","The 7th Plan emphasizes the need for adopting an effective results-based Monitoring & Evaluation (M&E) strategy which can help monitor the implementation of the plan and associated programmes.",""],[1,"51","11","Unified Sectoral Classification for Planning and Budgeting","The chapters on the sectoral development strategies of the 7th FYP have been structured to align with the recently adopted 14 uniform sectoral divisions.",""],[1,"94","3","Institution Strengthening for Long-Term Growth Support","the 7th FYP strategies are geared to pay greater attention to the establishment of stronger institutions to support and sustain higher growth over the longer term.",""],[1,"94","4","Seventh Five-Year Plan Growth Target","The 7th FYP will strive to achieve this",""]],"123":[[1,"128","5","Public Investment Quality and Tender Transparency Measures","Transparency in tendering process and ensuring quality at different phases of project implementation, and making contractors responsible even after the delivery of projects will be key to ensuring quality of project implementation.",""],[1,"211","6","Programme- and Results-Based Planning Reform","The Planning Commission has taken measures to move away from the existing project-by-project approach to a more programme and results based approach that is better linked with the Plan and the Medium-Term Budgetary Framework (MTBF).",""],[1,"211","6","Project Quality Improvement Measures","Measures have been implemented to bring improvement in project quality through more realistic project design, better assessment of implementation capacity, and more realistic costing.",""],[1,"211","7","Strengthening Project Director Financial Authority","The Government has taken actions to increase financial authority of project director for accelerating the ADP implementation.",""],[1,"211","7","Timely and Quality Public Procurement Improvement","Greater efforts are geared to ensure procurement of goods and services on a timely basis with due regard to qualitative and governance aspects of procurement.",""],[1,"211","7","Results-Based Project Implementation Reform","Greater attention has been given to make project implementation results-based and not just a matter of speedier use of public funds.",""],[1,"221","2","Public Investment Management Reform Road Map Implementation","under the Seventh Plan, the Government intends to implement reform options discussed under the \"A Public Investment Management Review and Reform Road Map for Bangladesh\".",""],[1,"221","3","Multi-Year Public Investment Programme","The introduction of a multi-year Public Investment Programme (PIP) to ensure a close match between approved projects and the availability of financial resources.","Finance Division | Ministry level | MDAs | line ministries"],[1,"221","4","Project Design, Appraisal and Approval Strengthening","Strengthening project design, appraisal and approval capacities and systems to increase the quality of the investment portfolio.","Planning Commission"],[1,"222","1","PIM Reform Institutionalization Mechanisms","To achieve this objective, the Government will establish a dedicated PIM Reform Unit within the Programming Division and a joint technical committee between the Planning Commission and the Ministry of Finance.","Planning Commission | Ministry of Finance"],[1,"222","2","Revenue Administration Reform Programme","The Government will undertake comprehensive reform programmes for the revenue administration, especially the National Board of Revenue (NBR) to improve existing low tax-GDP ratio.",""],[1,"222","3","Integrated Financial Management Information System (IFMIS) Introduction","The Government will introduce a modern Integrated Financial Management Information System (IFMIS) capable of producing timely, comprehensive and reliable financial statements in line with international accounting and reporting standards (IPSAS, GFSM 2014).",""],[1,"222","4","Treasury Securities Market Deepening Initiative","Initiatives will be taken to deepen the treasury securities market for reducing the cost of borrowing of the government.",""],[1,"222","4","Medium-Term Debt Management Strategy Update","Medium Term Debt Management Strategy (MTDS) will be updated regularly and public debt will be kept within sustainable limit under Debt Sustainability Analysis (DSA) framework.",""],[1,"222","4","Regular Public Debt Statistics Publication","Debt statistics will also be published regularly for greater transparency of government's fiscal position.",""],[1,"222","5","Treasury Single Account Strengthening and Cash Forecasting Reform","the existing Treasury Single Account (TSA) will be further strengthened with gradual phase out of special accounts and preparing cash forecasting model.",""],[1,"222","6","Budget and Accounting Classification System Rollout","A new Budget and Accounting Classification System (BACS) will be adopted with a view to improve efficiency in budgeting and accounting.",""],[1,"222","7","PFM Legal and Regulatory Framework Review","A comprehensive review of PFM legal and regulatory framework will be undertaken.",""],[1,"222","8","Non-Funded Government Pension System Reform","Initiatives will be taken to reform the existing non-funded pension system of the Government.",""],[1,"222","9","State-Owned Enterprise Financial Management Improvement","Steps will be given to improve the financial management of the State Owned Enterprises (SOEs) with special focus on their reporting and oversight.",""],[1,"222","10","Local Government Financial Management Improvement","Steps will be taken to improve the financial management of the local government bodies with special focus on their reporting, financial oversight and audit.",""],[1,"222","11","IT-Based Public Financial Management Solutions","Special attention will be given to introduce more IT based solutions in PFM area for improving transparency and efficient delivery of public services.",""],[1,"222","13","Strategic and Policy-Based Budgeting Reform","Institutionalization of a more strategic and policy based approach to budgeting, including through further rollout of Medium Term Strategy and Business Plans (MTSBP).",""],[1,"223","1","Line Ministry Forward Baseline Estimates Development","Further development of line ministry Forward Baseline Estimates (FBEs) to prioritize spending based on available fiscal space.",""],[1,"223","2","Performance-Based Ministry Resource Allocation Linkage","A credible and reliable linkage will be established between allocation of resources of a ministry and its performance.",""],[1,"223","3","Procurement Transparency and Accountability Initiative","The Government will undertake initiatives to improve transparency and accountability associated with procurements.",""],[1,"223","4","Citizens' Budget Publication","Publication of a citizens' budget immediately after the budget speech.",""],[1,"223","5","Open Data Portal for Public Finance Data","Greater transparency of public finance data in user-friendly and editable formats, such as through an Open Data Portal.",""],[1,"223","6","Improvement of Analytical Budget Reporting","The Government will further improve the quality of the analytical reports published during national budget like child budgeting, gender budgeting, district budgeting, etc.",""],[1,"223","7","Auditing Standards Improvement Measures","The Government will undertake necessary measures to improve auditing standards.",""],[1,"223","8","Public Disclosure of Audit Reports and Follow-up Actions","The Government will make all recent audit reports public on its website in a user friendly and accessible format, as well as clearly indicate how these audits have been followed up, particularly in holding the officials involved accountable.",""],[1,"223","9","Strengthening the Office of the Comptroller and Auditor-General","The Government will provide necessary support to improve the effectiveness of the Office of the Comptroller and Auditor-General to enable it to discharge its constitutional obligation more efficiently as an independent body with appropriate budget discretion and authority over human resources.",""],[1,"227","4","Direct Tax Collection Improvement Measures","the following activities will be undertaken under the 7thFYP to improve the state of direct tax collection:",""],[1,"227","5","Taxpayer Asset Ownership Monitoring and Income Assessment Measures","The Govt. will undertake measures to improve the monitoring of the ownership of all sizable physical and financial assets of taxpayers and determining the income generation out of those assets.",""],[1,"227","6","Broadening Tax Revenue Sources","Thus, the Govt. will support the tax administration to broaden its sources for revenue mobilization by identifying, adopting and implementing practices that are useful for such objectives",""],[1,"227","7","Equal Tax Treatment of Household Income Sources","Treating all sources of income equally for the tax purpose without discrimination for the households: This would imply taxation of capital gains from land, real estate/housing, and stock market.",""],[1,"228","1","Direct Tax Coverage Expansion","Under the 7th FYP time interval, the government aims to improve direct tax to GDP ratio to 5% by improving tax coverage by bringing a larger share of eligible population under its tax net.",""],[1,"228","4","Public Budget Committee Hearing Expansion","Increasing the number of hearings open to the public, particularly of important budgetary committees such as the Public Accounts Committee.",""],[1,"228","5","Inclusive Policy Debate Standards","Promoting standards for policy debate, in terms of allowing time and space for parliament (and if possible experts and other stakeholders such as prominent think tanks) to give opinions on policies, with the public generally informed regarding these processes",""],[1,"228","6","Public Accounts Committee Response and Public Reporting Mechanism","The Government will develop mechanisms to ensure timely responses to recommendations from the Public Accounts Committee, and provide easily accessible and comprehendible data for the public, including a progress report from the PAC",""],[1,"228","7","Parliamentary Secretariat Capacity Strengthening and Legal Implementation","Build on the existing capacity of the Parliamentary Secretariat, and ensure effective implementation of the Parliament Secretariat Act 1994 & Rules.",""],[1,"228","9","Public Sector Transparency and Accountability Improvement Measures","Moreover, under the 7th FYP, the Government will undertake the following activities to improve its effectiveness:",""]],"124":[[1,"177","6","Right to Information Disclosure Framework","The government is proactively creating enabling environment for disclosure of public documents with the enactment of Right to Information Act and establishment of the independent Information Commission;",""],[1,"213","3","Public Information Provision in Bangla","The NPF offers public information in the vernacular language Bangla, which can be easily understood and used for collecting information relating to citizens livelihood - agriculture, health, education, law and human rights, tourism and history, human resources, development & engineering, environment & disaster management.",""]],"125":[[1,"118","6","Public Revenue Mobilization Effort","A part of the increased national savings would also come from the public sector through increased revenue mobilization efforts.",""],[1,"128","5","Tax Policy Reform and Tax Administration Modernization","Resource mobilization by the public sector will continue to remain a major challenge and will require steadfast implementation of tax policy reforms (in both VAT and direct tax fronts), modernization of tax administration, and reform of the NBR tax administration.",""],[1,"129","9","NBR Tax Revenue Mobilization","Mobilization of resources, particularly with greater focus on sustainable increase in NBR tax revenue, will be essential for financing the Plan",""],[1,"144","2","Progressive Personal Income Tax Reform","This calls for both increased public spending on social sectors (health, education, sanitation, water supply and social protection) and very importantly a well-designed personal income taxation system that taxes all sources of income at a progressive rate.",""],[1,"146","6","Personal Income Tax Collection Enhancement","Increasing the effective income tax rate to even 10 percent in the next 3-5 years to the top 10 percentile who own 35 percent of the national income will yield 3.5 percent of GDP instead of 1 percent of GDP now.",""],[1,"146","7","Tax Base Broadening and Tax Administration Reform","This will require closing of loopholes that lets capital gains escape the tax net, treating all sources of personal income equally for taxation purpose, and improving tax administration and compliance.",""],[1,"146","7","VAT Modernization and Productivity Improvement","The modernization of VAT and improving its productivity can yield an additional 1.8% of GDP.",""],[1,"146","7","Modern Property Tax Introduction and Local Government Assignment","Additionally, the introduction of a modern property taxes and assigning this to the local governments can be a substantial boost for their fiscal autonomy while providing fiscal resources.",""],[1,"160","3","Tax Policy and Administration Reform and Modernization","Financing of this National Plan will require increased private and public sector savings, rapid income growth for the private sector and increased revenue mobilization through reform and modernization of tax policy and tax administration.",""],[1,"163","3","Revenue Mobilization Strategy","This positive turnaround both in terms of non-ADP spending and financing of a larger proportion of ADP by own savings will only be possible if the strategy for revenue mobilization is realized as Planned.",""],[1,"165","8","Transfer Pricing Incorporation in Income Tax Ordinance","Incorporating transfer pricing in the Income Tax Ordinance, 1984",""],[1,"165","9","Alternative Dispute Resolution in Tax and Customs Acts","Incorporating Alternative Dispute Resolution (ADR) in Income Tax, VAT and Custom Acts",""],[1,"165","10","Direct Tax Code Drafting","Drafting of a new Direct Tax Code",""],[1,"165","11","Customs Act Reform","Drafting of a new Customs Act",""],[1,"166","1","Income Tax Zone and Tax Office Expansion","Establishing 13 new Income Tax Zones, 2 Tax Appeal Zones and 85 Circle Offices",""],[1,"166","2","Automated TIN Registration and National ID Linkage","Automation of TIN registration and linking TIN with National ID",""],[1,"166","4","Q-Cash E-Payment Tax Collection","Payment of taxes using the Q-Cash network under the platform of e-payment of NBR",""],[1,"166","5","Taxpayer Information and Service Centres","Establishing taxpayer information and service centres at all divisions.",""],[1,"166","6","Enhanced Taxpayer Services","Providing enhanced taxpayer services through spot assessment, income tax fair etc.",""],[1,"166","8","Incentive-Based Tax Compliance System","Introducing incentive based taxation system through tax cards, certificates etc. for tax compliance",""],[1,"166","9","Central Intelligence Cell Strengthening for Tax Evasion Combat","Strengthening the Central Intelligence Cell (CIC) for combating tax evasion",""],[1,"166","10","VAT Commissionerate Expansion","Establishing 4 new VAT Commissionerates and 3 VAT Appeal Commissionerates,",""],[1,"166","11","Custom House and Bond Commissionerate Establishment and Customs Wing Merger","Setting up of 1 new Custom House (ICD), merger of Import and Export Wings of Chittagong Custom House, setting up of a full-blown Bond Commissionerate at Chittagong",""],[1,"166","12","ASYCUDA World System Installation in Customs Stations","Installing ASYCUDA World System in all Custom Houses and 4 Land Custom Stations",""],[1,"166","13","Online Customs-Bangladesh Bank Connectivity for Anti-Money Laundering","Online connectivity between the customs database and Bangladesh Bank database for combating money laundering",""],[1,"166","14","Customs Database Development","Developing customs database",""],[1,"166","15","Pilot E-filing of VAT Returns at Large Taxpayers Units","E-filing of VAT returns on a pilot basis at Large Taxpayers Units (LTUs)",""],[1,"167","3","Land Transaction Revenue Policy Reform","Government will ensure policy reform for increasing the revenue earnings from land transactions.",""],[1,"168","2","Tax Administration Strengthening and Computerization","The need for strengthening of the tax administration, its computerization and improvement in efficiency is integral to achieving these targets.",""],[1,"168","2","Income Tax Base Expansion and Withholding Coverage","Expansion of the income tax base and bringing more individuals and companies under the tax net and under the withholding mechanism would be necessary to drive the revenue growth and to achieve levels enjoyed by our neighbouring countries.",""],[1,"168","2","Formalization Incentives for the Informal Sector","Initiatives and incentives by the government to formalize these activities would greatly enhance the tax potential on the domestic side while making it possible to achieve the targets set under the Seventh Five Year Plan.",""],[1,"168","3","Strengthening Tax Evasion Detection Units","This needs to be addressed by strengthening tax evasion detecting unit like the Central Intelligence Cell (CIC) and other intelligence units of the NBR.","National Board of Revenue | Central Intelligence Cell (CIC)"],[1,"168","3","Inter-Agency Tax Evasion Combat Coordination","The NBR should work together with the Bangladesh Bank and the Anti-Corruption Commission for combating tax evasion.","National Board of Revenue | Bangladesh Bank | Anti-Corruption Commission"],[1,"168","3","Alternative Dispute Resolution for Revenue Cases","Following the South African model, the NBR has introduced the Alternative Dispute Resolution (ADR) mechanism to settle disputes out of the court system.","National Board of Revenue"],[1,"168","3","Expansion of Alternative Dispute Resolution for Arrear Revenue Collection","The ADR mechanism will be further popularized and strengthened to collect arrear revenue.",""],[1,"168","6","VAT and Supplementary Duty Act Implementation","Effective Implementation of VAT and Supplementary Duty Act 2012",""],[1,"168","7","Transfer Pricing Incorporation in Income Tax Ordinance","Incorporating transfer pricing in the Income Tax Ordinance, 1984",""],[1,"168","8","Alternative Dispute Resolution in Tax and Customs Acts","Incorporating Alternative Dispute Resolution (ADR) in Income Tax, VAT and Custom Acts",""],[1,"168","9","Direct Tax Code Drafting","Drafting of a new Direct Tax Code",""],[1,"168","10","Customs Act Drafting Reform","Drafting of a new Customs Act",""],[1,"168","12","Taxpayer Asset Ownership Monitoring and Income Assessment","Broadening of the taxpayers' base- This will require monitoring of the ownership of all sizable physical and financial assets of taxpayers and determining the income generation out of those assets.",""],[1,"169","1","Tax Base Broadening Initiative","Broadening of the tax revenue sources- Traditionally there has been an excess dependency on taxing financial institutions and a few large non-financial corporations.",""],[1,"169","3","Equal Tax Treatment for Household Income Sources","Treating all sources of income equally for the tax purpose without discrimination for the households.",""],[1,"169","4","TIN Registration Automation and National ID Linkage","Automation of TIN registration and linking TIN with National I.D.",""],[1,"169","5","Integrated Revenue Management Programme","An integrated revenue management programme seeks to connect the three departments at transactional level by linking the taxpayer identification numbers i.e. TIN and BIN in the database.",""],[1,"169","6","Integrated Revenue Management Digitalization Programme","This programme will seek to set up a country-wide integrated ICT platform to capture all tax payment information from tax returns, banks, TDS deductors, third party collection agencies etc.",""],[1,"169","7","E-Filing of Income Tax Returns","E-Filing of income tax returns.",""],[1,"169","8","Withholding Tax Expansion and Enforcement","Aggressive imposition and expansion of withholding taxes, particularly on individual taxes which could potentially improve tax compliance, expand the income tax base and address administrative issues pertaining to tax collection efforts through increased transparency and efficiency.",""],[1,"169","9","Taxpayer Education and Outreach Programme","The taxpayer education programme will make available a menu of offerings through remote outlets like websites, internet etc. as well as through customers facing one to one or group interface with the NBR Customer Service Wing.",""],[1,"169","10","New VAT Act Implementation","Implementation of the new VAT Act.",""],[1,"169","11","VAT Base Expansion","Expanding VAT base especially on businesses and organization.",""],[1,"169","12","VAT Compliance Incentive for Small Businesses","Incentivizing VAT payment with benefits for small businesses to bring them into the VAT coverage as well as promoting increased formalization of businesses currently operating in the informal sector.",""],[1,"169","13","VAT Administration Functional Reform","Reform of the VAT administration along functional lines",""],[1,"169","14","Tax Administration Automation and Central VAT Registration System","Automation of the whole tax administration through Central Data base including Central VAT Registration; electronic submission and return processing",""],[1,"169","15","Taxpayer Education and Information Campaign on the New VAT Law","Comprehensive taxpayers' education and information campaign about the new VAT law and Rules.",""],[1,"169","16","VAT Law Implementation and VAT Administration Modernization","significant progress is being made on the VAT front in terms of the new VAT Law, which is already enacted in December 2012, and administrative restructuring and modernization of VAT administration.",""],[1,"169","17","Bond Administration Refocusing and Separation Reform","the government will consider bond administration can be separated from full customs administration and also lined its performance with investment, industrialization and trade.",""],[1,"170","1","Statistics and Research Department Strengthening","efforts will be made to implement the recommendations of the diagnostic report.","NBR"],[1,"170","1","Tax Compliance Social Recognition Programme","Efforts will also be made to enhance tax compliance through social recognition programme.",""],[1,"178","2","National Board of Revenue Modernization Plan","Effective implementation of the NBR modernization Plan including automation of the VAT and direct tax administration will be preconditions for the success of the domestic revenue mobilization strategy.",""],[1,"178","2","Tax Administration Automation Reform","The revenue targets established for the national Board of Revenue is ambitious, but supported by proper policy and administrative reforms and automation of tax administration the targets are certainly attainable.",""]],"126":[[1,"437","3","Administrative Decentralization and City Corporation Expansion","There is a vision of the Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina to transform some of the big Divisions into smaller Divisions and transform the new Divisions and big districts Headquarters into City corporations (Dhaka Division will be divided into 3 Divisions: Dhaka, Faridpur, Mymensingh).",""],[1,"444","1","Specialized Urban Local Government Institutions","There is also a need for specialized institutions to address the needs of urban local governments.",""],[1,"446","1","Citizen Participation in Municipal Governance Reform","Institutionalize citizen participation (civil society, NGOs, CBOs) in municipal business through appropriate changes in legal framework.",""],[1,"446","2","Municipal Administrative and Management Reform and Staff Training","Introduce improved administrative and management practices and procedures; impart training to municipal staff; change prevailing culture and perception;",""],[1,"446","3","Municipal Revenue Enhancement and Capital Budget Planning Reform","Augment revenue raising, improve municipal financial system and capital budget planning",""],[1,"446","7","Alternative Service Delivery Mechanisms","Alternate service delivery mechanisms (public-private partnerships, community-based and self- help project).",""]],"127":[[1,"719","3","Women's Political Participation Support and Monitoring Mechanisms","Women's political orientation would be enhanced through apprenticeship, training, and campaigns and by establishing support and monitoring mechanisms to increase their participation as contestants in regular seats.",""],[1,"719","3","Training and Monitoring for Women Public Representatives","Some projects have introduced training of women public representatives and citizens and monitoring of women's role in different committees.",""],[1,"719","3","Uniform Implementation of Women's Participation Approaches","Steps should be taken so that these approaches are uniformly practiced.",""],[1,"719","3","Enforcement of RPO 2013 in Party Registration Criteria","The provisions of RPO 2013 related to women's participation and representation in political parties would be ensured by enforcing it within the registration criteria",""],[1,"719","5","Women's Representation Institutionalization in Public Institutions","Women's representation together with appropriate training and capacity building support would be institutionalized in public institutions.",""],[1,"719","5","Gender Strategy Requirement for Private Sector Institutions and Trade Bodies","Private sector institutions and trade bodies would also be instructed to develop their own gender strategies and ensure more women's representation at different levels.",""],[1,"719","5","Women's Representation Incentives and Board Participation Measures","It could be considered as criteria for qualifying for different incentives by the private sector.",""],[1,"719","5","Mandatory Women's Participation in Delegations and Committees","Women's participation in delegations and committees for trade and other important negotiations and development initiatives would be made mandatory and private sector to be encouraged /incentivised to have women on the Boards.",""],[1,"719","6","Enforcement and Expansion of Women's Representation Quotas","The existing quota provisions for women's representation in different services will be enforced and/or increased by taking specific measures, especially as the availability of qualified women increases with improvements in women's educational attainments.",""],[1,"719","6","Assessment of Quota Provisions for Different Groups","Also an assessment of the quota provisions for different groups, the performance of these groups and, future possibilities would be considered.",""],[1,"720","1","Orientation and Training for Women in Governance Bodies","clear TOR and orientation and training for women on their roles in such bodies as well as orientation of their male counterparts.",""]],"128":[[1,"560","4","Health Care and Family Planning Service Expansion","The Perspective Plan stipulates necessary actions to increase coverage of all types of health care and family planning services, to strengthen health administration and to increase the number of skilled professionals in the HNP sector.",""],[1,"562","3","Health and Nutrition Improvement Strategy for the Poor","the Government emphasizes reducing severe malnutrition, high mortality and fertility, promoting healthy lifestyles, and reducing risk factors to human health from environmental, economic, social and behavioural causes with a sharp focus on improving the health of the poor.",""],[1,"563","1","Health Services Improvement and Primary Health Care Support","The first component aims to improve health services, such as maternal and child health, and support the service delivery system including primary health care.",""],[1,"565","2","Primary Health Care Referral and Facility Upgrading","The provision of Primary Health Care (PHC) under HPNSDP included an emphasis on establishing a functional referral system at Upazila and district levels to improve the continuity of care and included appropriate upgrading and equipping Upazila Health Complexes (UHC) and Community Clinics (CC).",""],[1,"565","2","Urban Primary Health Care Service Delivery Collaboration","HPNSDP aimed to tackle the problem of service delivery in urban areas through collaboration with the Local Government Division (LGD) as it is the local government institutions that are responsible for providing PHC service delivery to the urban population.","Local Government Division (LGD)"],[1,"565","2","MOHFW-LGD Health Coordination Mechanism","There has been slow progress in establishing a coordinating mechanism between MOHFW and the LGD.","MOHFW | LGD"],[1,"565","3","Community Based Health Care Initiative","Community Based Health Care (CBHC) initiative is to improve overall health status of the rural community by providing health, family planning and nutritional services through community participation and by establishing a functional linkage among the public facilities at union and upazila level through effective referral.","MOHFW | DGHS"],[1,"565","4","Community Clinic Service Delivery and Reporting System","During the last four years of implementation, a total of 12,895 CCs have been made functional, with newly recruited 13,240 Community Health Care Providers (CHCP) and provision of adequate medicines.",""],[1,"565","4","Community Oversight and Web-Based Health Reporting System","12,895 Community Groups (CGs) and 37,731 Community Support Groups (CSGs) are associated with the running and community oversight of the CCs.",""],[1,"566","1","Community Clinic-Based Health Service Expansion","The HPNSDP through implementation of CC based services including conduction of deliveries in certain CCs, keeping separate toilets and other facilities for women at the public hospitals, provision of nutrition corners and establishment of SCANUs in public hospitals, etc. has increased access of the poor women to HNP services.",""],[1,"566","2","Public Health Service Network Programmes under the 7th FYP","Recognizing the challenge, the Government has undertaken programmes under the 7th FYP to address many of them.",""],[1,"566","4","Community Clinic and Upazila Health Complex Improvement","improvements in the community clinics and Upazila Health Complexes are essential.",""],[1,"566","4","Community Health Care Revitalization Initiative","The revitalization of community health care initiative integrated in a wider Upazila Health System promises better access for the poor women to health care services at the grass roots level.",""],[1,"566","4","Community Participation in Primary Health Care","Involvement of communities through Community Management Group and Community Support Groups is another praiseworthy initiative.",""],[1,"566","4","Health Workforce and Drug Supply Optimization","the challenge of further improving and consolidating gains from the CC based health care initiatives require better use of existing HR and rational use of supplied drugs.",""],[1,"566","4","Facility-Based Health Service Expansion","the possibility of a move towards more facility-based services away from the domiciliary approach will be more focussed.",""],[1,"566","4","Health Facility Referral System Strengthening","Strengthening the referral system across facilities at different levels to improve the continuity of care is another area that needs to be looked at.",""],[1,"566","5","Primary Health Care System Sustenance Measures","during the 7th FYP period required steps will be taken for sustenance of this PHC system.",""],[1,"567","1","Community Clinic Field-Level Coordination and Supervision Improvement","The elaborate guidance jointly issued by the DGHS and DGFP for field-level co-ordination and supervision therefore need better compliance for turning the CC into an effective first service-contact.","DGHS | DGFP"],[1,"567","2","Drug List Review for Community Clinics","Reviewing the drug list for CCs to ensure rational dispensing of drugs by service providers at CCs.",""],[1,"567","3","CBHC Mainstreaming into Primary Health Care Delivery","The CBHC initiative will need to be mainstreamed with the primary health care system of DGHS's regular service delivery mechanism.",""],[1,"567","6","Strengthening and Consolidating Union Health and Family Welfare Centres","The HPNSDP called for strengthening and further consolidating the functioning of the UHCs, union health and family welfare centres/sub-centres through providing adequate human resources, drugs, and other medical aids.",""],[1,"568","3","Hard-to-Reach Area Health Service Incentive Policy","Policy introducing both financial and non-financial incentives for hard to reach areas has been developed.",""],[1,"568","3","Monitoring and Supervision Transport Support for Health Managers","motorcycles and bicycles have been distributed among upazila level managers and family planning inspectors to enhance and facilitate monitoring and supervision.",""],[1,"569","3","Urban Primary Health Care Strengthening","The Government will take additional steps to ensure urban health services, especially PHC.",""],[1,"569","4","District-Specific and Tribal-Friendly Health Services","the Government will implement measures to institute district-specific and tribal-friendly health services.",""],[1,"570","1","Gender-Friendly Health Service Access Improvements","The 7th FYP will address these issues to ensure a more equitable and gender-friendly access to health services.",""],[1,"574","18","Health Service Access Expansion for Disadvantaged Populations","The health service delivery system will ensure that the poor, marginalized and geographically disadvantaged population are able to access and utilize health services.",""],[1,"574","18","Institutional Arrangements for Urban Slum and Street Dweller HNP Services","To particularly provide HNP services to urban slum and street dwellers, proper institutional arrangements will be made to",""],[1,"576","1","Collaborative CHT Health Service Delivery System","The problem with service delivery in the CHT will be tackled in collaboration with MOCHTA and other relevant authorities.","MOCHTA"],[1,"576","1","District-Specific Health Service System for Hill District Councils","District-specific health service system will be developed along with institutional arrangements for respective Hill District councils to facilitate the system operation.",""],[1,"576","1","Tribal-Friendly Health Services for Plainland Populations","Tribal-friendly health services will be ensured through appropriate initiatives for tribal population residing in plain lands.",""],[1,"576","4","Disability Advocacy and Coordinated Service Expansion","During the 7th FYP period, the exponential increase in the prevalence of ASD across the country including other disability issues will be properly addressed through appropriate advocacy campaign, effective coordination among concerned ministries, departments, and NGOs for proper preventive, curative and rehabilitative services including expansion of services to cater the need of different types of disabled along with making health-facilities disable-friendly.",""],[1,"576","5","Mental Health Service Delivery Plan","To address this problem, a comprehensive mental health service delivery plan will be developed with the aim of gradual expansion of service to address the growing need of psychological aspects of health.","MOHFW"],[1,"577","2","National Institute for Physical and Geriatric Medicine and Rehabilitation","a National Institute for Physical and Geriatric Medicine and Rehabilitation is proposed to be set up during the 7th FYP.",""],[1,"577","2","Multi-sectoral Geriatric Health Care Collaboration","MOHFW will also promote multi-sectoral collaboration with other ministries (e.g., Ministry of Social Welfare), NGOs, CSOs, etc. for improving geriatric health care.","Ministry of Social Welfare"],[1,"586","4","Population Planning and Human Development Services","the NSDS calls for population planning, providing quality education and training, and providing quality health and sanitation services and nutrition for all.",""]],"129":[[1,"568","4","Antenatal Care Promotion and Health Personnel Quality Improvement","The Government will pursue strategies to further encourage ANC visits by pregnant women to ensure safe and sound delivery and will also enhance quality of health personnel.",""],[1,"568","5","Maternal, Neonatal, Child and Adolescent Health Newborn Care Strengthening","Four priority interventions have been incorporated in Maternal, Neonatal, Child and Adolescent Health (MNCAH) to strengthen new-born care.",""],[1,"568","5","Expanded Programme on Immunization Strengthening Under Reach Every Community Strategy","Under the Reach Every Community Strategy routine, Expanded Programme on Immunization (EPI) has further been strengthened in low performing 32 districts and 4 City Corporations.",""],[1,"573","7","Adolescent and Reproductive Health Care","To ensure adolescent and reproductive health care",""],[1,"575","3","Community Skilled Birth Attendant Mentoring and Expansion","proper technical mentoring and supervision will be introduced.",""],[1,"575","3","Midwife Deployment to Union and Upazila Posts","Newly trained dedicated midwives will be deployed in newly created posts at the union and upazila level to augment service delivery.",""],[1,"575","3","Comprehensive Emergency Obstetric Care Access Expansion","new initiatives will be undertaken to ensure access of CEmOC, particularly for hard to reach areas.",""],[1,"575","3","Newborn Care Partnership and Coordination Initiative","Strategic partnerships with DPs, NGOs and the private sector will be built to strengthen and expand new-born care.",""],[1,"575","6","Gender- and Adolescent-Friendly Health Services","Gender and adolescent friendly services together with availability of proper information for the adolescent will be ensured to protect themselves from health hazards.",""],[1,"575","6","Health Facility Maintenance and Privacy Improvement","Health facilities will be maintained properly and women will be given their due privacy and confidentiality regarding health matters.",""],[1,"581","5","Regional Family Planning Service Strengthening","Existing family planning services will thus be strengthened through delivering regional packages in less performing divisions/pockets.",""],[1,"581","5","Long-Acting Permanent Contraception Shift","Method-mix of contraceptive use will be shifted to long acting permanent method (LAPM).",""],[1,"581","5","Contraception Demand Reduction and Service Collaboration","The unmet need for contraception will be reduced along with the tendency to discontinue contraception through improved collaboration with health department and others to ensure services of technical personnel like doctors and nurses.",""],[1,"581","6","Gender Equality in Family Planning","Gender equality will be particularly ensured during the 7th FYP period in family planning.",""],[1,"582","1","Population and Family Planning Service Improvement","Population and family planning services will thus be improved by promoting delay in marriage and child bearing among other interventions.",""],[1,"582","1","Youth Marriage and First-Birth Delay Initiative","Newly-wed couples, especially adolescents, will be targeted to delay the first birth.",""],[1,"582","1","Reproductive Health Counseling Expansion","Counselling on population control and reproductive health and behaviour will be continued and expanded in health care centres.",""],[1,"582","1","Women's Reproductive Decision-Making Empowerment","Steps will be taken to ensure women's decision making over reproductive health through proper education and information.",""],[1,"582","1","Inclusive Health Services for Women Beyond Reproductive Age","Services for women beyond reproductive age will be addressed to ensure a more equitable and gender-friendly access to health services.",""],[1,"582","6","Contraceptive Access Expansion","Increase contraceptive prevalence rate to arrest population growth by making services and contraceptives available to people at minimum cost and using door to door service wherever required.",""],[1,"582","7","Population and Family Planning Services Improvement","Improve population and family planning services through following interventions:",""],[1,"582","8","Delayed Marriage and Childbearing Promotion","Promote delay in marriage and child bearing, use of post-partum FP and FP for appropriate segments of population;",""],[1,"582","9","Family Planning Awareness Building through IEC Activities","Strengthen FP awareness building efforts through Information, Education and Communication (IEC) activities with special emphasis on mass communication and considering local specificities;",""],[1,"582","10","Differentiated Family Planning Service Delivery","Use different service delivery approaches (including domiciliary services) for different geographical regions and segments of population having low CPRs;",""],[1,"582","11","Eligible Couples Registration and Counseling System","Register eligible couples with particular emphasis on urban areas to establish effective communication and counselling;",""],[1,"582","12","Compensation for Contraceptive Service Providers","Compensate for lost wages for long acting and permanent method contraceptive performance;",""],[1,"582","13","Postpartum and Post-abortion Family Planning Service Strengthening","Strengthen FP services especially post-partum and post abortion FP and demand generation through effective coordination of services with DGHS;","DGHS"],[1,"582","14","Male Participation in Contraception Advocacy","Strengthen advocacy for male participation in permanent and other methods of contraception.",""],[1,"582","15","Population Management Roles Awareness Initiative","Create awareness of all relevant ministries of their roles in population management with MoHFW as the lead Ministry.","MoHFW"]],"130":[[1,"714","12","Lifecycle-Based Women’s Healthcare Expansion","Life cycle based disease prevention and curative healthcare services: Considering the current realities of women in Bangladesh, a lifecycle based healthcare system including tertiary care should be accessible to women within affordable cost.",""],[1,"714","12","Gender-Responsive Health Service Reform","The health care system would be made more responsive to differential needs of women and men aiming at reducing discrimination and ensuring equal benefits.",""],[1,"714","12","Health Information and Motivation Campaigns","One important initiative will be to undertake information and motivational campaigns to inform households, both women and men about the need and availability of preventive care and screening services.",""],[1,"714","12","Expansion of Low-Cost Health Care Coverage","Coverage of the existing low cost health care services will be expanded to include the poor of the remote and vulnerable areas.",""],[1,"714","12","Primary Health Care Immunization Support","The ongoing primary health care services would ensure equal immunization support for both girls and boys who are not covered yet.",""],[1,"714","12","Maternal, Antenatal, and Postnatal Care Expansion","Similarly, immunization, maternal and ante-natal care for pregnant women and post-natal care for both mother and child would be ensured through increased facilities as well as information and motivation both in rural and urban areas.",""],[1,"714","12","Reproductive and Sexual Health Service Expansion","Reproductive and sexual health care services including counselling would be expanded.",""],[1,"714","12","Women-Friendly Hospital Expansion","Expansion of women friendly hospitals in all districts by enhancing services in all sadar hospitals and medical college hospitals including outputs of reproductive health care will be done.",""],[1,"714","12","Women and Children Service Registration and Tracking System","The system for registration and tracking of services for women and children at the community clinics and all hospitals would be made more effective.",""]],"131":[[1,"578","7","Nutrition Scaling-Up Enabling Environment Strengthening","The 7th FYP will address the impeding factors related to nutrition and strengthen the enabling environment for scaling up nutrition.",""],[1,"578","8","National Nutrition Services Operational Plan","Nutrition Programme of the MOHFW has been mainstreamed within the DGHS and DGFP through a new operational plan for National Nutrition Services (NNS) will be used to provide regular nutritional services.","MOHFW | DGHS | DGFP"],[1,"578","8","Expansion of Nutrition Service Capacity at Health Facilities","The responsibilities and capacities of relevant sectors and institutions, i.e. Upazila health complexes and district hospitals, will be expanded and developed accordingly to manage severely malnourished cases.",""],[1,"578","9","Nutrition-Fortified Crop Extension Services","Ministry of Agriculture provides extension services for different crops fortified with nutrition elements, newly developed by research institutes of Bangladesh.","Ministry of Agriculture"],[1,"578","9","Golden Rice Expansion","A new variety of rice namely, 'Golden Rice', fortified with beta carotene as Vitamin A supplement is a major achievement, which will be extended in suitable areas.",""],[1,"578","9","Nutrition Stakeholder Coordination Arrangements","During the 7th FYP period, the roles and responsibilities of the stakeholders for nutrition will be specified, and arrangements of appropriate coordination and synergistic action will be made.",""],[1,"578","9","Cabinet Committee Support for Food Security and Nutrition Coordination","Policy guidance and inter/intra ministerial linkages can be facilitated through existing cabinet committees and coordination structures that address food security/ nutrition within the Ministry of Food and Disaster Management and others.","Ministry of Food and Disaster Management"],[1,"578","9","Urban Nutrition and Food Safety Collaboration","MOHFW will collaborate with the Ministry of LGRD&C and the Ministry of Food and Disaster Management to address nutrition and food safety issues within urban contexts.","MOHFW | Ministry of LGRD&C | Ministry of Food and Disaster Management"],[1,"579","3","Nutrition and Hygiene Education in School Curriculum","Incorporate nutrition and hygiene education in curriculum, including school vegetable garden and cooking demonstrations",""],[1,"579","3","School Health and Nutrition Days","Ensure regular Health and Nutrition Days in the schools calendar",""],[1,"579","3","School Feeding Nutrition Promotion","Promote and protect good dietary practices among children in places where there are school feeding programmes",""],[1,"579","5","Hand-Washing and Hygiene Promotion","Contribute to increased levels of hand-washing and hygiene",""],[1,"579","5","Safe Drinking Water Provision","Ensure availability of safe drinking water",""],[1,"579","5","Sanitary Facilities Expansion","Improve availability of sanitary facilities in different settings",""],[1,"579","5","Water Access for Women in Agriculture and Fishing","Prioritise the availability of water to women for agriculture and fishing",""],[1,"579","7","Food Availability and Food Safety Improvement Measures","Ensure improving availability of diverse foods of quality · Promote best practice to ensure food safety in agriculture sector, food processing industries, food distribution system and in food value chain · Ensure adequate food safety regulatory framework in place and monitored",""],[1,"579","10","Diversified Food Production and Nutrition-Sensitive Agriculture Extension","Improve production of diversified food (source of animal protein) · Empower women to access agriculture extension services, resources · Incorporate basic nutrition into agriculture extension training and tasks · Build agriculture extension and agriculture input supply system to ensure nutrition is considered in planning and implementation",""],[1,"579","13","Women’s Empowerment for Household Decision-Making","Emphasis on empowerment of women to make decisions about their own and their children's wellbeing",""],[1,"579","13","Fully Paid Maternity Leave Implementation","Ensure 6-month fully paid maternity leave is implemented in all sectors",""],[1,"579","15","Fortified Staple Food Availability and Marketing Standards","Increase availability of fortified staples e.g. salt and oil · Adhere to high standards in advertising/marketing, focus on children",""],[1,"579","18","Early Warning and Nutrition Surveillance Systems","Strengthening early warning and nutrition surveillance systems",""],[1,"579","18","Cross-Sectoral Resilience and Joint Programming","Increase collaboration with other sectors and joint programming to increase household/community resilience, especially in emergencies",""],[1,"579","18","Nutrition-Sensitive Monitoring and Evaluation System","Monitoring & evaluation systems include nutrition relevant indicators",""],[1,"580","1","Gender-Responsive Nutrition Mainstreaming","Under the 7th FYP, efforts will be taken to mainstream gender issues in nutrition programmes.",""],[1,"580","1","Multidimensional Child and Maternal Malnutrition Response","To that end, the Government will consider a multidimensional approach to address the intergenerational health impact.",""],[1,"580","1","Nutrition Awareness Campaigns","Among other things, such an approach will include awareness on child/women nutrition, food value and food diversity.",""],[1,"580","1","Iron-Folic Acid Supplementation for Women and Girls","Iron-folic acid supplementation among pregnant, lactating women and adolescent girls to cover iron-deficiency anaemia will be undertaken through health and family planning facilities.",""],[1,"580","1","Infant and Young Child Feeding Strategy Implementation","The national strategy for infant and young child feeding will be implemented.",""],[1,"580","1","Vitamin A Capsule Distribution for Children","Existing half-yearly Vitamin A capsules distribution for children will be continued.",""],[1,"580","1","Post-Partum Vitamin A Distribution Scale-Up","Post-partum Vitamin- A distribution to improve vitamin A status of neonates through breast milk will be scaled up.",""],[1,"580","1","Salt Iodization Monitoring Strengthening","Monitoring of salt iodization will be strengthened.",""],[1,"580","1","Zinc Promotion for Diarrhoea Treatment","Zinc for treatment of diarrhoea will be adequately promoted.",""],[1,"580","1","Intestinal Parasite Treatment Expansion and Deworming Programme","Expansion of intestinal parasite treatment, including the distribution of albendazole tablets, along with a separate deworming programme will be considered.",""],[1,"580","1","IMCI Zinc Tablet Provision","With the coverage of IMCI, zinc tablets are expected to be freely provided to children with diarrhoea.",""],[1,"580","2","Nutrition Capacity Building and Community Awareness Programme","Capacity building and awareness: To improve the knowledge base and capacity of health personnel regarding nutrition, health and family planning workers as well as agricultural extension workers will be appropriately trained in nutrition education.",""]],"132":[[1,"44","2","Community Clinic Basic Healthcare Delivery","more than 13,000 Community Clinics deliver quality basic healthcare in close proximity of rural communities.",""],[1,"55","2","Health Service Delivery Improvement and Governance Reform","The Plan places special emphasis on the following areas on health: i) To improve service delivery and utilize the vast health network, innovative approaches will be explored, including field-based service delivery, decentralization of the management of facilities, providing autonomy to hospitals by protecting the interests of poor; ii) The health service delivery system will ensure that the poor and marginalized population are able to access and utilize such services; iii) Since a considerable portion of the population turn to the private sector for health services, proper regulation to protect the people from malfeasant practices is considered very crucial in the Plan; iv) To make better and effective use of government trained Community Skilled Birth Attendants (CSBAs), proper technical mentoring and supervision will be introduced; iv) Recognizing the epidemiological transition, massive health promotion and prevention efforts for impending non-communicable diseases will be carried out; v) Gender and adolescent friendly services together with availability of proper information for the adolescent will be ensured; v) special emphasis will be placed on tribal health, autism, mental health, geriatric care, and health education; vi) In addition to addressing service delivery issues, the 7th FYP will also take into account the deficiencies in governance and management of the health sector.",""],[1,"55","2","Community Skilled Birth Attendant Mentoring and Supervision","To make better and effective use of government trained Community Skilled Birth Attendants (CSBAs), proper technical mentoring and supervision will be introduced;",""],[1,"55","2","Non-Communicable Disease Health Promotion and Prevention Campaign","Recognizing the epidemiological transition, massive health promotion and prevention efforts for impending non-communicable diseases will be carried out;",""],[1,"55","2","Gender and Adolescent-Friendly Health Services","Gender and adolescent friendly services together with availability of proper information for the adolescent will be ensured;",""],[1,"55","2","Targeted Health Services and Education for Priority Groups","special emphasis will be placed on tribal health, autism, mental health, geriatric care, and health education;",""],[1,"55","3","National Nutrition Services Operational Plan","Nutrition Programme of the MoHFW has been mainstreamed within the DGHS and DGFP through a new operational plan for National Nutrition Services (NNS) will be used to provide regular nutritional services.","MoHFW | DGHS | DGFP"],[1,"55","3","Expansion of Nutrition Sector Responsibilities and Capacity Development","The responsibilities of relevant sectors and institutions will be expanded and capacity developed accordingly.",""],[1,"55","3","Strengthening of Community and Hospital Nutrition Capacity","Capacities of the Community Clinics, Upazila health complexes and district hospitals will be further strengthened to adequately manage severely malnourished cases.",""],[1,"55","4","Delay Marriage and Childbearing Promotion","i) Promoting delay in marriage and child bearing, use of post-partum FP and FP for appropriate segments of population;",""],[1,"55","4","Family Planning Awareness and IEC Campaign","ii) Strengthening FP awareness building efforts through Information, Education and Communication (IEC) activities with special emphasis on mass communication and considering local specificities;",""],[1,"55","4","Male Participation in Contraception Advocacy","iii) Strengthening advocacy for male participation in permanent and other methods of contraception.",""],[1,"77","7","Government Health Insurance Programme","The implementation of the Government's health insurance programme will also help.",""],[1,"78","2","Nutrition Programme Strengthening and Outreach Expansion","Sixth, the nutrition programmes need additional efforts. Outreach programmes need to be strengthened.",""],[1,"85","5","Community Health Clinic Teleconsultation Service","25% Community Health Clinics provide teleconsultation with specialists in urban areas",""]],"133":[[1,"715","2","Expanded Reproductive Health and Family Planning Services","Counselling on population control and reproductive health and behaviour would be continued and expanded in all health care centres.",""],[1,"715","2","Community-Based Family Planning Outreach","Community based family planning services would be continued and expanded to cover urban poor women and men.",""],[1,"715","2","Modern Contraceptive Promotion and Access Support","Motivational work in urban slums and remote areas for use of modern contraceptives and availability of modern contraceptives at a low cost especially in remote areas would be ensured.",""],[1,"715","3","Reproductive Health Information, Education, and Counselling Services","Information and education is necessary to enhance women's control over their own reproductive health. Counselling services would be made available in all health care centres for men, women and couples.",""]],"134":[[1,"625","3","UISC Telemedicine Service Rollout","with support from the Directorate General of Health Service (DGHS), 30 UISCs have introduced telemedicine services.","Directorate General of Health Service (DGHS)"],[1,"625","3","Mobile Emergency Medical Advice Service","each Upazila Health Complex has a mobile phone so people can easily seek emergency medical advice.",""],[1,"625","4","Mobile Phone Health Care Programme","Ubiquity of mobile phones across all district and upazila hospitals has made it possible to launch a \"mobile phone health care\" Programme.",""],[1,"625","4","Telemedicine Service Expansion","18 hospitals have introduced telemedicine services.",""],[1,"625","4","Health Facility Digital Connectivity and Online Reporting System","A total of 800 health institutions have received computer supplies and have been brought under the internet service.","DGHS"],[1,"625","4","DGHS Online Reporting System","This has enabled introducing an online reporting system by the DGHS.","DGHS"],[1,"625","4","Upazila Health Complex Video Conferencing and Monitoring System","All upazila health complexes have been provided webcam which are being used to conduct video conferencing and at the same time, also acting as a monitoring tool.",""],[1,"625","4","Community Clinic Digital Equipment Provision","All 12,557 community clinics have a mini laptop with a built-in webcam.",""],[1,"638","6","Health Sector E-Monitoring System","A proper e-monitoring system will be established to monitor attendance, absenteeism and quality of service delivery.",""],[1,"638","6","ICT-Based Health Education for Service Providers","Health education will be arranged to service providers using ICT.",""],[1,"638","6","Medical Faculty Connectivity for Remote Care","Medical faculties will be connected to address remote medical needs.",""],[1,"638","7","National Telemedicine Service Expansion","Telemedicine, particularly mobile phone based solutions, could be launched at a national scale to provide medical information, consultation and services.",""],[1,"638","7","Clinic and Hospital Standard Operating Procedures","Standard operating procedures will be developed for clinics and hospitals.",""],[1,"638","7","Automated Patient Information and Queue Management System","Patients' information and queue management protocol will be automated using the CCDS.",""],[1,"638","7","Digital Patient Payment and Accommodation Facilitation Measures","measures would be explored so that patients do not spend a significant amount of time in paying bills or in arranging accommodation.",""],[1,"638","7","Essential Drug Availability Monitoring","Availability of essential drugs would be monitored.",""],[1,"638","7","Disability-Inclusive Health System Design","It is also imperative to design systems by considering persons with disabilities.",""]],"135":[[1,"708","4","Universal HIV Treatment, Care and Support Services","People infected and affected by HIV/AIDS will be given universal access to treatment, care and support services.",""],[1,"708","4","HIV Prevention Services for Key Populations","There will be increased coverage on interventions (basic educational, counselling, referral and legal supportive services) for key populations including people living with HIV, along with implementation of services to prevent new HIV infections.",""],[1,"708","4","Public Information Campaign on HIV Treatment Availability","The Government will inform about the availability of effective treatment for adequate and timely antiretroviral treatment, since unawareness may discourage people from getting tested.",""],[1,"708","7","Multi-Sector HIV/AIDS Response Coordination and Management Strengthening","Coordination mechanisms and management capacity at different levels will be strengthened to ensure an effective multi-sector HIV/AIDS response.",""],[1,"708","7","HIV/AIDS Strategic Information and Research Strengthening","Also strategic information systems and research for an evidence based response will be strengthened.",""],[1,"708","8","HIV Response Legal and Policy Support","The Government will make laws and policies that facilitate the HIV response and work with uniformed services and health care workers to increase knowledge and tolerance.",""],[1,"714","12","HIV Testing, Counselling, and Awareness Scale-Up","HIV testing and counselling would be scaled up among key populations and high risk groups and awareness amongst migrant labourers and their spouses need be promoted.",""],[1,"714","12","Prevention of Mother-to-Child Transmission Scale-Up","Prevention of Mother to Child Transmission services will be scaled up for HIV infected women.",""]],"136":[[1,"700","4","Integrated Education Programme for Children with Disabilities","developing an integrated education Programme for visually impaired children, 2) expanding existing institutions for hearing impaired and mentally retarded children, 3) establishing new institutions to provide access to more children with disabilities at primary, secondary and tertiary levels and 4) collaborating with NGOs and private sector to develop and implement the improvements in the education sector.",""],[1,"700","5","Lifelong Health Support Service for Disability","Implement a lifelong health support service by 1) strengthening early detection of symptoms of disability, 2) undertaking nutrition programmes for pregnant women, 3) appointing trainee doctors, nurses and other caregivers to deal with disability issues and 4) introducing support services of assistive devices and equipment at the health centres.",""],[1,"700","6","Disability Accessibility and Inclusion Measures","taking measures to provide persons with disability access to all physical facilities, information and communication",""],[1,"700","6","Disability Decision-Making Empowerment Initiative","improving their decision making power at national and community level",""],[1,"700","6","Community-Based Rehabilitation Programme","introducing community based rehabilitation (CBR) programmes in rural areas",""],[1,"700","8","Disability Welfare Projects and Service Expansion","the Department of Social Services (DSS) has introduced new projects and strengthened existing ones to improve the welfare of PWD.","Department of Social Services (DSS)"],[1,"700","8","Integrated Education Programme for the Visually Impaired","These include the Integrated Education Programme for the Visually Impaired project, the establishment of a hostel for visually impaired children, and the expansion of the PROYASH institute dedicated to the wellbeing of persons and children with special needs.",""],[1,"700","8","Hostel for Visually Impaired Children","These include the Integrated Education Programme for the Visually Impaired project, the establishment of a hostel for visually impaired children, and the expansion of the PROYASH institute dedicated to the wellbeing of persons and children with special needs.",""],[1,"700","8","Expansion of the PROYASH Institute","These include the Integrated Education Programme for the Visually Impaired project, the establishment of a hostel for visually impaired children, and the expansion of the PROYASH institute dedicated to the wellbeing of persons and children with special needs.",""],[1,"709","4","Expansion of Inclusive Education Institutions for Children with Disabilities","Along with an expansion of integrated education Programme for visually impaired children, existing institutions for hearing impaired and mentally retarded children will be expanded.",""],[1,"709","4","Establishment of New Special Education Institutions","New institutions will be established to provide access to more children with disabilities at primary, secondary and tertiary levels.",""],[1,"709","4","Multi-Stakeholder Disability Education Collaboration and Teacher Training","A collaborative effort involving the government, NGOs and the private sector will be encouraged to expedite an expansion of existing institutions, establish new institutions and undertake teachers' training on disability.",""],[1,"709","5","Early Disability Detection and Primary Medical Rehabilitation","Action will be taken in the health sector to: (i) strengthen early detection of symptoms of disability and provide primary medical rehabilitation;",""],[1,"709","5","Nutrition Programme for Pregnant Women","Action will be taken in the health sector to: (ii) undertake a nutrition programme for pregnant women;",""],[1,"709","5","Training and Deployment of Caregivers for Disability Services","Action will be taken in the health sector to: (iii) appoint trainee doctors, nurses and other caregivers to deal with disability issues;",""],[1,"709","5","Assistive Devices Support Services at Health Centres","Action will be taken in the health sector to: (iv) introduce support services of assistive devices and equipment at health centres.",""],[1,"709","6","Disability Access and Inclusion Measures","Measures will be taken so that persons with disabilities can have access to all physical facilities and information and communication.",""],[1,"709","6","Community-Based Rehabilitation Services for Persons with Disabilities","Services like early detection and timely medical intervention, fitment of artificial aids and appliances, educational services in special and integrated schools, vocational rehabilitation including micro-credit will be provided to persons with disabilities through community based rehabilitation programmes.",""],[1,"709","7","Organization and Empowerment of Persons with Disabilities","it is necessary to support the organising of people with disabilities in order to make them 'visible' and to empower them to make their voices heard.",""]],"137":[[1,"567","5","Health, Population and Nutrition Coordination Improvement","Conscious efforts are being made to improve both inter and intra agency coordination.",""],[1,"567","6","Health Care Quality Improvement and Accreditation Mechanism","HPNSDP included TQM for quality improvement activities as a comprehensive approach.",""],[1,"567","6","Health Facility Quality Governance and Standards Development","Health Economics Unit as the focal point of UHC formed a Core Committee for developing an outline for improvement of quality.",""],[1,"568","2","Private Sector Health Service Regulation and Accreditation","To enhance the private sector service delivery and prevent mishaps and mistreatment, a strong and effective regulatory structure to address quality issues and enforce standards is a priority for the remainder of the HPNSDP.",""],[1,"568","2","Private Sector Medical Pricing and Quality Enforcement","According to the National Health Policy, measures will be taken to develop and apply necessary rules and regulations in order to ensure availability of proper and quality medical care for the patients of private sector.",""],[1,"568","3","Diversification of Health Service Delivery through Public-Private Partnerships","The Government will explore diversification of service provisions including public-private partnerships",""],[1,"570","3","Health Sector Coordination System","Assuming strategic stewardship and governance role by MOHFW for policy management and setting up a coordinating system for synergistic, effective and efficient contribution of public, non-public including private sector and health NGOs.","MOHFW"],[1,"570","4","Health Regulatory and Supervisory Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening MOHFW's regulatory and supervisory roles through revising the mandates of the regulatory bodies and capacity building for enforcement of standards.","MOHFW"],[1,"570","5","MOHFW NGO and Private Sector Engagement Strengthening","Facilitating and strengthening MOHFW's engagement with the NGO and private sector, based on comparative advantage.","MOHFW"],[1,"570","6","Update Health-Related Legal Frameworks","Reviewing and updating the existing health related legal frameworks to include the health consumers' rights in the Consumer Rights Protection Act (2009).",""],[1,"570","7","Legal Framework Review Taskforce","Constituting a Taskforce to assess the need for (i) new law/ordinance, (ii) revising any existing ones and (iii) determining measures to improve existing legal framework.",""],[1,"570","8","Strengthening Health Ministry Regulatory and Supervisory Functions","The HPSNDP, along with the 6th FYP, illustrated the Government's commitment to strengthen the regulatory and supervisory role of the MOHFW and delegating the stewardship role.","MOHFW"],[1,"570","8","Improving Nutrition and Population Sub-Sector Coordination","Another area needing attention is the institutional arrangements and coordination related to the nutrition and population sub-sectors, which need to be more effective and synergistic.",""],[1,"570","8","Strengthening Cross-Sector Nutrition Coordination","Under the nutrition sub-sector, weak coordination between sectors combined with heavily centralized coordination within sectors continue to pose a significant challenge.",""],[1,"572","1","Systematic Human Resources Strategy Development","To guide activities and improving upon the HR situation in Bangladesh, the MOHFW has undertaken the initiatives for developing a systematic HR Strategy.","MOHFW"],[1,"572","5","Health Human Resource Strengthening and Planning, Monitoring and Evaluation Programme","the Government will conduct a number of programmes to strengthen human resources and conduct proper Planning, Monitoring and Evaluation inclusive of governance and stewardship.",""],[1,"572","6","Strengthening of the Directorate General of Drug Administration","Directorate General of Drug Administration will be strengthened to deal with these issues.",""],[1,"573","2","Health Financing Strategy","To tackle financing issues, a Health Financing Strategy (2012-32) has also been developed for addressing this issue of reducing out of pocket expenditure.",""],[1,"573","3","Research Coordination for Public Benefit","Well-coordinated efforts are needed to ensure that the findings of the research are utilized to benefit the people.",""],[1,"573","8","Community Participation Strengthening for Programme Implementation","To strengthen community support and involvement to obtain better results in implementation of programmes",""],[1,"574","16","Health Sector-Wide Approach Continuation","Bangladesh is currently implementing the third SWAp, and will follow the Sector-Wide Approach (SWAp) as the Government has already stated its policy of continuing with the SWAp in the HNP sector.",""],[1,"574","16","Fourth HNP Sector Programme Implementation","Past experience and lessons learned will surely aid in the implementation of the necessary actions during the 7th FYP period through the upcoming 4th HNP Sector Programme.",""],[1,"574","17","Health Service Delivery Improvement and Decentralization Reform","To improve service delivery and utilize the vast health network, various innovative approaches will be explored.",""],[1,"575","2","Private Health Sector Regulatory Mechanism","An effective regulatory mechanism will thus be developed.",""],[1,"575","2","Informal Health Service Delivery Utilization Study","The possibility of utilizing the vast informal sector of health service delivery, which is particularly important for hard to reach rural areas, will be explored.",""],[1,"577","4","Health Sector Governance and Management Strengthening","the 7th FYP will also take into account the deficiencies in governance and management of the health sector.",""],[1,"577","4","Health Workforce, Financing, Surveillance, and Supply Systems Improvement","Issues related to the inadequacies in the health workforce, finance, surveillance, drugs and equipment, information and research will be addressed.",""],[1,"577","10","Directorate General of Drug Administration Strengthening","Strengthen Directorate General of Drug Administration for ensuring production and dispensing of quality drugs, promotion of rational use of drugs and elimination of harmful and useless drugs",""],[1,"577","10","Bangladesh Pharmacy Council Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen Bangladesh Pharmacy Council to support regulatory role of DGDA",""],[1,"578","1","Health Care Financing Strategy Implementation","Ensure proper implementation of Health Care Financing Strategy 2012 to strengthen financial risk protection and extend health services and population coverage.",""],[1,"578","1","Health Financing Expansion and Prepayment Initiative","Increase public sector contribution in health sector with appropriate initiatives to increase development partners' assistance and decrease out of pocket expenditures with prepayment initiative like health insurance.",""],[1,"578","2","Regulatory Mechanism Review and Strengthening","Strengthen stewardship role, regulatory functions through review of existing regulatory mechanisms in terms of number, structure, mandate and capacity.",""],[1,"578","3","Health Sector Regulatory Reform for Universal Coverage","Develop and implement proper regulations required to ensure quality, equitable health services of public sector and gradual shift in public sector's role from service delivery to stewardship and regulation for ensuring universal coverage in health.",""],[1,"578","5","Bangladesh Institute of Health Management Establishment","Establish Bangladesh Institute of Health Management",""],[1,"582","16","Health, Nutrition and Population Sector Development Programme","The Government of Bangladesh (GOB) is currently implementing the 3rd Health, Nutrition and Population (HNP) sector programme entitled \"Health, Nutrition and Population Sector Development Programme (HPNSDP)\", which will be completed in June 2016.",""],[1,"582","16","Sector-Wide Approach for HNP Sector Development","The HNP sector development initiatives in Bangladesh have been following the sector-wide approach (SWAp) since 1998 as part of implementation mechanism of MOHFW's development activities.","MOHFW"],[1,"582","16","Sector-Wide Approach for 7th FYP HNP Programmes","the HNP sector's development programmes of the 7th FYP will also be implemented following the SWAp mechanism.",""],[1,"583","1","Fourth Health, Nutrition and Population Sector Programme","the 4th HNP Sector Programme will be implemented from July 2016 for a period of five years through to June 2021 without any interruption between the current and next sector programme.",""],[1,"583","2","Strategic Investment Plan Preparation","MOHFW is already in the midst of preparation of the Strategic Investment Plan (SIP) in connection with the development of a Programme Implementation Plan (PIP) for the 4th Sector Programme.","MOHFW"],[1,"583","3","Health, Population and Nutrition Sector Resource Allocation and Service Delivery Enhancement","The Seventh Plan stipulates adequate development resources for the health, population and nutrition sector.","Ministry of Health and Family Welfare"]],"138":[[1,"143","3","Health Insurance Pilot Scheme","Time has come for Bangladesh to start on a pilot basis some type of a health insurance scheme.",""],[1,"143","3","Health Financing Strategy Implementation","The implementation of this health financing strategy will be a major priority during the Seventh Plan.",""]],"139":[[1,"695","4","Child Health Improvement Measures","Improved health will be achieved through 1) controlling communicable and non-communicable diseases as well as increasing behavioural change communications in schools about health and healthy practices; 2) increasing food and nutrition intakes of children; and 3) ensuring access to safe water and sanitation to reduce environmental health hazards for children.",""],[1,"695","4","Early Childhood Development and Education Access Expansion","The children's access to good quality education will be strengthened through early childhood development strategies and access to formal and non-formal education.",""],[1,"696","3","Early Detection and Screening for Child Autism","Emphasis has been placed on early detection and screening of child autism to help this disability at an early stage.",""],[1,"701","5","Child Health Services Provision","providing health services the children need",""],[1,"701","5","Child Food and Nutrition Access Support","ensuring access to food and nutrition they need",""],[1,"701","5","Girls' Education and Development Opportunities","providing access to girls to education, training and development opportunities",""],[1,"701","7","Safe Childbirth and Child Health Programme","The programme areas include arrangements for safe child birth, eradication of polio, elimination of measles and neonatal tetanus, improvement of nutrition and strengthening the school health programme.",""],[1,"701","7","Health Expenditure Efficiency and Governance Reform","The actions will include maximizing the efficiency and cost-effectiveness of health expenditure and improving governance.",""],[1,"702","1","School Health Education and Adolescent Health Strategy","Necessary measures will be taken to include such issues in school syllabus.",""],[1,"702","1","Adolescent Health Awareness and Counseling Programme","Activities will be undertaken to develop an adolescent health strategy including counselling, building awareness for adolescents on hygienic practices, nutrition, puberty, RTI/STD and HIV/AIDS.",""],[1,"702","1","Regional Immunization Coverage Improvement Measures","Minimizing regional disparities in immunization coverage will be addressed to reduce disparities in vaccination coverage through effective programmatic interventions.",""],[1,"702","2","Maternal and Child Nutritional Supplementation","Provision of nutritional supplement for pregnant and lactating mother will be uncompromisingly implemented.",""],[1,"702","2","Vitamin A Deficiency Control Programme","To control vitamin A deficiency and contain the prevalence of night blindness, vitamin A supplements will be distributed to children with vitamin A deficiency, measles, persistent diarrhoea or severe malnutrition and to postpartum women within 6 weeks of delivery.",""],[1,"702","2","Universal Salt Iodization Programme","Ongoing efforts to control iodine deficiency disorders through universal salt iodization will continue.",""],[1,"702","2","Anaemia Control Strategy","Strategies to control anaemia will include iron-foliate supplementation, anathematic treatment, fortification and BCC to increase the consumption of iron-rich foods and promoters of iron absorption.",""],[1,"702","2","Health Care Strategy for Children with Disabilities","A strategy will be developed to address the health care needs of children with physical and mental disabilities.",""],[1,"702","3","Early Childhood Development Awareness and Community Childcare Programme","The intervention for early childhood development will include an awareness raising programme for parents to make them aware of early childhood development benefits, promote community- based childcare centres for clusters of families where literate mothers are trained to become caregivers and design facilities for early learners.",""],[1,"715","1","Nutrition Awareness and Education Campaign","It would include awareness on child/women nutrition, food value and food diversity.",""],[1,"715","1","Micronutrient Supplementation and Deworming Programme","Together with this, the ongoing iron acid supplementation during pregnancy to cover iron-deficiency anaemia, postpartum vitamin A supplementation, treating intestinal parasites, distribution of albendazole tablets, and vitamin A campaign for children and separate deworming Programme would be strengthened and expanded.",""]],"140":[[1,"697","8","Tribal Health, Nutrition and Population Plan","The Tribal Health, Nutrition and Population Plan (THNPP) were formulated as part of the Health, Population and Nutrition Sector Development Programme (HPNSDP)",""],[1,"698","1","Ethnic Minority Health, Nutrition and Population Services","ensure ethnic minorities have access to the health, nutrition and population services.",""],[1,"704","9","Tribal Health, Nutrition and Population Plan Strengthening","Steps will be taken to make Tribal Health, Nutrition and Population Plan (THNPP) more effective in order to ensure ethnic communities have",""],[1,"705","1","Expansion of Health Service Coverage in Remote Areas","The network of health services will be expanded so that people living in remote and inaccessible areas come under the coverage.",""],[1,"705","1","Disease Prevention and Sanitation Support for Hill Tracts","Government will take measures to prevent malaria, diarrhoea and other diseases in hill tracts and provide sanitation facilities to the people.",""]],"141":[[1,"639","1","National Health Data Consolidation and Standardization System","National data on health indicators will be consolidated and updated.",""],[1,"639","1","Electronic Health Record Development","The electronic health record (EHR) being prepared by the DGHS will be developed to maintain an integrated system.","DGHS"],[1,"639","1","National Health Geographic Database Completion","The geographical database will be completed.",""],[1,"639","1","Health Data Standardization and Disease Surveillance Coordination","Health data would be standardized using the CCDS and cooperation among large health facilities in disease surveillance ought to be strengthened.",""]],"142":[[1,"465","1","Environmental Health Capacity Building","Build capacity in the area of environmental health through both public and private sectors.",""],[1,"483","3","Medical Waste Management Compliance and Handling System","Strict compliance of Medical Waste Management Rules along with a good management of in-house and off-the-house practice is badly needed to solve the problem.",""],[1,"483","3","Local Government Medical Waste Management Role","Moreover, there is a need of strong role from local government agencies for off-the-house management of medical waste.",""],[1,"487","7","Medical Waste Management Improvement Measures","GoB will take measures to improve medical waste management in the country by delivering specific disposal training and with strict enforcement of separate collection & disposal systems.",""],[1,"487","8","Infectious Waste Treatment Centres in Divisional Cities","GoB will establish environmentally acceptable treatment centres for infectious wastes in each divisional city.",""],[1,"487","9","Medical Waste Management Compliance and Enforcement","Strict compliance of Medical Waste Rules along with in-house and off-the-house management should be established.",""]],"143":[[1,"223","10","Banking and Capital Market Governance Reform","The Government also acknowledges that while tax revenue has witnessed substantial rise, the scopes of tax evasion has also increased. Thus, the Govt. intends to improve the state of economic governance by undertaking the following activities:",""],[1,"223","11","Bangladesh Bank Autonomy Review","Under the 7th FYP time interval, the Government will review the issue of the independence of the Bangladesh Bank and the amount of autonomy it wants to convey to the regulator.",""],[1,"223","11","Central Bank Capacity and Prudential Regulation Strengthening","A fully autonomous regulator capable of hiring quality staff it needs, procuring the technology it requires strengthening its effectiveness, and implement prudential norms is essential to prevent financial irregularities observed during 2009 and 2014.",""],[1,"223","11","Sound Monetary Policy Formulation and Implementation","An effective and autonomous Central Bank is also essential to formulate and implement sound monetary policies.",""],[1,"224","1","Public Bank Supervision Strategy and Regulatory Compliance Measures","The Government will also formulate a strategy and implement identified measures for better supervision of public banks.",""],[1,"224","2","Gross Non-Performing Loan Reduction Measure","Under the 7thFYP time interval, the government will ensure that the Gross-NPL of both state owned and private banks do not cross 10%.",""],[1,"224","3","NBFI Deposit Insurance Coverage Expansion","the Govt. will undertake measures to bring the depositors of NBFI under the umbrella of insurance coverage.",""],[1,"224","4","NBFI Support Policy and Reporting Simplification","A more comprehensive investment friendly policy of Bangladesh Bank for NBFIs, more coordination with Banks, easy and simplified procedures of reporting to Bangladesh Bank etc. will be formulated to support the growth of NBFIs.","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"224","5","NBFI Loan Disbursement Monitoring Mechanism","The NBFIs will put in place a better monitoring mechanism to streamline their loan disbursement methods with focus on low risk industrial segments in order to minimize the risks associated with their assets.",""],[1,"224","6","Separation of Lending and Leasing Operations","The government will take measures to ensure that these two different operations are not mixed, or else, it might distort the basic financial norms.",""],[1,"224","7","NBFI Client Protection and Transparency Support","The government will support clientele protection by ensuring the availability of relevant information for each NBFI, so that greater transparency prevails in the sector.",""],[1,"225","2","Stock Exchange Demutualization Reform","Demutualization of stock exchanges.",""],[1,"225","3","Regulatory Coordination for Financial Stability","Enhanced coordination between regulators to enhance financial stability.",""],[1,"225","4","Institutional Investor Demand and Mutual Fund Industry Promotion","Enhancing institutional investor demand and promote the mutual fund industry.",""],[1,"225","8","Accounting and Auditing Standards Upgrade","Upgrading of accounting and auditing standards to enhance market confidence.",""],[1,"225","9","Independent Financial Reporting Council","Establish an independent Financial Reporting Council to adopt and monitor International Accounting Standards (IAS) and International Standards of Auditing as well as license accountants and auditors.",""],[1,"225","10","Audit Committee Establishment","Establish an Audit Committee to supervise companies' internal controls, accounting policies, and compliance with IAS.",""],[1,"225","12","Self-Regulatory Organization for Securities Market Oversight","The government will establish a strong Self-Regulatory Organization (SRO) to monitor and discipline their members to minimize the involvement of the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC).",""],[1,"225","13","SRO Oversight and Commercial Practice Reform","The industry will be instructed to define the role of SROs in oversight and adopt international best commercial practices.",""],[1,"225","14","Market Integration with International Best Practices","The SEC will be consulted to officially recognize many of the SRO's and begin the process of integrating Bangladesh's markets with international best practices.",""],[1,"225","15","DSE Capital Improvement Programme Review and Delisting Reform","A demutualized DSE will be instructed to review its capital improvement programme to determine what new investments are necessary and the DSE will delist the defunct shares and debentures.",""],[1,"225","16","Regulatory Framework Improvement Activities","Finally, the government will undertake the following activities to improve quality of the regulatory framework:",""],[1,"225","17","Regulatory Coordination and Independence Support for Financial Regulators","The SEC and BB will develop an MOU or protocol on the collection and sharing of supervisory information, risk assessments and coordinating supervisory activities, and in enforcing conduct requirements.",""],[1,"226","1","Securities and Exchange Commission Funding and Regulatory Capacity Reform","Thus, the SEC will be afforded broader access to its fund without tight Government expenditure approval and paid competitive.",""],[1,"226","1","SEC Regulatory Process Standardization","It will adopt clear and consistent regulatory processes and should eliminate anomalies in the case of SEC prosecution of criminal cases.",""],[1,"226","1","SEC Staff Code of Conduct and Professional Standards Mechanism","The GoB will put in place mechanisms so that staff of the regulator maintains the highest professional standards including standards of confidentiality by adhering to a comprehensive Code of Conduct.",""],[1,"226","2","Self-Regulatory Organization Oversight Programme","The GoB will cooperate with the SEC to put in place an on-going programme to oversee them because of staffing and capacity limitations.",""],[1,"226","3","Strengthening Regulatory Enforcement Powers","The GoB will take necessary measures to ensure the regulator has broad powers for inspection, investigation and surveillance and to review bank account information and implementation of an effective compliance programme.",""],[1,"226","3","Special Capital Market Tribunal Establishment","To this end, the Government will form a working group of relevant personalities from the Ministry of Law and SEC to take measures to establish a Special Capital Market Tribunal.","Ministry of Law | SEC"],[1,"226","4","Cross-Border Regulatory Cooperation and Information Sharing Mechanism","The Regulator will be given the authority to share both public and non-public information and should establish information sharing mechanisms that set out when and how they will share such information with domestic and foreign counterparts.",""],[1,"226","5","Strengthen Securities Disclosure and Investor Protection Oversight","The Government will ensure that there is full, timely and accurate disclosure of financial results and other information that is crucial to investors' decisions.",""],[1,"226","5","SEC Oversight of Takeovers and Rule Amendments","Holders of securities in a company will be treated in a fair and equitable manner by allowing effective SEC oversight of takeovers and amendment of rules.",""],[1,"226","5","International Alignment of Accounting and Auditing Standards","Accounting and auditing standards will be made internationally acceptable and of a high quality.",""],[1,"226","5","Implementation of IFRS and ISA","IAS (IFRS) and ISA need to be implemented.",""],[1,"226","6","Collective Investment Scheme Regulatory Framework","The regulatory system will set eligibility criteria and regulation standards governing the legal form and structure of collective investment schemes and the segregation and protection of client assets for those who wish to operate a collective investment scheme.",""],[1,"226","6","Collective Investment Scheme Disclosure Requirements","Regulation will be required disclosure, as set forth under the principles for issuers, which is necessary to evaluate the suitability of a collective investment scheme for a particular investor and the value of the investor's interest in the scheme.",""],[1,"226","7","Market Intermediary Regulation and Prudential Standards","Regulation will provide for minimum entry standards for market intermediaries and require demonstrating proficiency.",""],[1,"227","1","Market Intermediary Risk Management and Failure Resolution Procedure","Furthermore, the Government will also put in place a procedure for dealing with the failure of a market intermediary in order to minimize damage and loss to investors and to contain systemic risk.",""],[1,"227","2","Regulatory Supervision of Securities Exchanges and Trading Systems","There will be ongoing regulatory supervision of exchanges and trading systems, which will aim to ensure that the integrity of trading is maintained through fair and equitable rules that strike an appropriate balance between the demands of different market participants.",""]],"144":[[1,"367","9","Transmission and Distribution System Development","Development of transmission and distribution system in line with generation.",""],[1,"385","7","Transmission and Distribution Network Development and Renovation","The Generation & Distribution Utilities plan has proceeded in line with implementation capacity and needs.",""],[1,"392","4","Transmission and Distribution Development Programme","Even so, massive transmission and distribution development programmes are to ensure uninterrupted power distribution and achieve the target of power supply for all.",""],[1,"392","5","Electricity Transmission Infrastructure Expansion","Transmission infrastructure will be added in the tenure of 7th FYP (2016-2020) are given below:",""],[1,"393","4","Rural Electrification Distribution Expansion Plan","Through the Bangladesh Rural Electrification Board (BREB), the Government is committed to providing rural electrification and also to reduce regional disparity.",""],[1,"393","6","Electric Distribution Line Expansion and Upgrading","Expansion/up-gradation of electric distribution line (Km)",""],[1,"393","17","Urban Power Distribution Improvement Programme","The power distribution companies serving urban centres have also adopted major programmes to ensure smooth distribution of power in the urban areas, especially to the major cities of Dhaka, Chittagong, Khulna, Rajshahi, Sylhet and Barisal.",""],[1,"393","17","Power Distribution Network Expansion Plans","The Bangladesh Power Development Board, the Dhaka Power Distribution Company, Dhaka Electric Supply Company and the West Zone Power Distribution Company have all adopted substantial distribution plans.",""],[1,"393","17","Transmission and Distribution Loss Reduction and Customer Service Improvement","Emphasis is also placed on reducing T&D losses and to improve customer service.",""],[1,"393","23","Electric Distribution Line Expansion and Construction","Expansion/Construction of electric distribution line (Km)",""]],"145":[[1,"376","4","Renewable Energy Investment and Incentive Support","Through this policy the Government is committed to facilitate both public and private sector investment in renewable energy projects to substitute indigenous non- renewable energy supplies and scale up contributions of existing renewable energy based electricity productions.",""],[1,"376","4","Sustainable and Renewable Energy Development Authority Establishment","A nodal agency, the Sustainable and Renewable Energy Development Authority (SREDA), has been established and is expected to start working soon.",""],[1,"377","1","Rooftop Solar PV Deployment","Roof top solar PV systems are also being introduced in the country with the current installed capacity estimated at 32 MW.",""],[1,"377","1","Renewable Energy Expansion and Financing Mechanism","Mini-grids and grid-connected MW-scale solar PV plants are also being explored.",""],[1,"377","1","Renewable Energy Generation Target","The Government's plan is to generate 800MW of power through renewable energy by FY2017 with a target of 10% of the total electricity to be met from renewable resources by FY2020.",""],[1,"381","1","Biogas Utilization Policy","Biogas utilization policy may also define how Primary Energy, namely pipeline gas, LPG and Biogas can be best mixed.",""],[1,"383","21","Renewable Energy Programme Development and Implementation","Administrative and technical capacities also need to expand in a number areas related to domestic gas exploration, negotiation of IOC investments, development and implementation of renewable energy programmes and the implementation of DSM initiatives.",""],[1,"391","6","Renewable Energy Power Generation Scale-Up","the Seventh Plan recognizes that continued efforts will be needed to accelerate the implementation of scalable power generation through renewable energy.",""],[1,"391","6","Off-Grid Renewable Energy Supply for Non-Grid Areas","This will be especially important to meet the demand in areas where grid supply is not possible during the Seventh Plan.",""],[1,"391","6","SREDA Renewable Energy Promotion Institution","The establishment of SREDA provides a strong dedicated institution to promote renewable energy.",""],[1,"391","6","Solar and Wind Power Development Focus","The Seventh plan will focus on two main areas of renewable energy: solar and wind power.",""],[1,"391","7","500 MW Solar Programme","For the Seventh Plan the Government has adopted the 500WM Solar Programme broken down into 340MW of commercial purpose and 160MW of social sector.",""],[1,"392","1","Solar Energy Deployment Projects","Commercial projects are: (a) Solar Park (grid connected); (b) Solar Irrigation; (c) Solar Mini-grid/micro-grid; and (d) Solar rooftop.",""],[1,"392","1","Social Infrastructure Electrification Projects","The social projects are: (a) Rural health centres; (b) Remote educational institutes; (c) Union e-Centres; (d) Remote Religious Establishment; (e) Off-grid Railway Stations; and (f) Government & Semi-Government Offices in the off-grid areas.",""],[1,"392","2","Wind Resource Mapping Project","As a first step, a wind resource mapping project has been taken up by the Government to prepare bankable wind data.",""],[1,"392","2","Wind Resource Assessment Process","Government has initiated process to carry out Wind Resource Assessment (WRA) at Feni, Chittagong, Cox's Bazar, Barguna and Kurigram.",""],[1,"392","2","15 MW Wind Power Plant Installation","In addition to the wind assessment study, a 15 MW Wind Power Plant will be installed at the most suitable site.",""],[1,"392","2","Renewable Energy Development Technical Assistance Project","A Technical Assistance Renewable Energy Development Project has been taken for Wind Resource Assessment (WRA) at Anowara, Chittagong.",""],[1,"392","2","Wind Resources Mapping Technical Assistance Project","Another Technical Assistance Project for Wind Resources Mapping project has been taken at Inani, Anowara, Sitakundo, Chandpur, Rajshahi, Gaibandha & Kuakata.",""],[1,"392","2","Independent Power Producer Wind Projects","Keeping the wind resource mapping pending two IPPs (100 MW & 60 MW) have been taken for implementation.",""],[1,"477","7","Climate Change Mitigation Awareness and Low-Carbon Growth Measures","The Government also realizes that there should be more awareness about the importance of climate change mitigation.",""],[1,"477","7","Renewable Energy Promotion for Solar Homes and Biogas","Due emphasis should be given to the promotion of renewable energy, particularly solar homes and biogas plants.",""],[1,"478","1","Revision of Energy and Technology Policies and Incentives","energy and technology policies along with incentives will be revised.",""],[1,"478","3","Mandatory Solar-Based Renewable Units for New Electricity Consumers","Urban power authorities in major cities have mandated new electricity consumers to install solar-based renewable units to cover 3% of estimated power demand for the particular house or building.",""],[1,"478","4","LED and Solar Street Lighting Replacement","GoB also plans to replace conventional street lights with LED and solar lights.",""],[1,"478","4","Energy Efficiency Appliance Certification and Promotion","Energy efficient appliances will be certified through BSTI, and their use will be highly encouraged.",""],[1,"478","4","Sustainable and Renewable Energy Development Authority Establishment","Sustainable and Renewable Energy Development Authority (SREDA) has already been set up to serve as a nodal agency for the promotion and development of sustainable energy, comprising of renewable energy, energy efficiency and energy conservation.",""],[1,"479","1","Renewable Technology Promotion Fund","The Government has also allocated about BDT 400 crore to promote renewable technologies in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"479","3","Gender-Friendly Energy Efficiency Pathway","GoB is committed to developing a pathway for addressing gender friendly energy efficiency with special emphasis on LCD.",""],[1,"480","7","Review of Energy Demand Management Tax and Tariff Structures","The existing tax and tariff structures will be reviewed to better manage energy demand.",""],[1,"480","7","Non-Pecuniary Energy-Saving Incentive Measures","GOB will also seek to employ non-pecuniary means to encourage energy saving, and interact with targeted programmes involving private sector institutions.",""],[1,"480","7","Targeted Private Sector Energy-Saving Programmes","GOB will also seek to employ non-pecuniary means to encourage energy saving, and interact with targeted programmes involving private sector institutions.",""],[1,"480","7","Clean Technology Fund Investment Opportunity Identification","The emergence of clean tech funds necessitates identifying specific investment opportunities.",""],[1,"480","7","Eco-Friendly Building Construction Incentives","The Building sector can be motivated to construct more eco-friendly buildings that require less energy.",""],[1,"480","7","Review and Pursue Energy-Saving Investment Opportunities","Potential opportunities for investments like these will be reviewed and pursued accordingly.",""],[1,"481","2","Nationwide Improved Cook Stove Introduction","Full introduction of improved cook stove all over the country will be the best option in this respect.",""],[1,"489","10","Improved Cooking Stove Campaign and Programme","Continuing massive campaign & programme on improved cooking stove.",""],[1,"489","13","Solar Lantern and Renewable Energy Rollout","Support the roll out of solar lanterns or other renewable energy options, to prevent use of kerosene lamps and other polluting technologies.",""],[1,"506","3","Cleaner Coal Power Transition","To counter the effects of a possible shortfall in natural gas, the Government has planned to switch to coal as the primary fuel source.",""],[1,"506","4","High-Efficiency Super-Critical Coal Power Investment","GoB has decided to pay extra amounts for high efficiency super-critical gasifier technology involving coal as the primary fuel.",""],[1,"506","5","500 MW Solar Programme","The '500 MW Solar Programme', started in 2012, outlines the government's plan to make the best possible use of solar energy.",""],[1,"506","6","Wind Power Project Development","To further utilize wind potential, Bangladesh Power Development Board (BPDB) has signed a contract for a 60 MW wind power project with a consortium.","Bangladesh Power Development Board (BPDB)"],[1,"506","6","Wind Resource Mapping Initiative","BPDB has also initiated steps to commission a wind map for Cox's Bazaar, Kutubdia, Khepupara, Feni and","Bangladesh Power Development Board (BPDB)"],[1,"507","1","Off-Grid Wind-Solar Hybrid Power Project at Hatiya Island","One such ongoing project is a 7.5 MW off Grid wind-solar hybrid system at Hatiya Island, Noakhali.",""],[1,"507","2","Renewable Energy Policy Subsidy Revision","The Renewable Energy Policy has been revised to provide subsidies to renewable energy sectors.",""],[1,"507","2","Tax and Licensing Incentives for Renewable Power Plants","The government is considering waiving of income taxes for foreign and local investors for 15 years, and waiving of licenses for installation and operation of renewable power plants with less than 5 MW capacity.",""],[1,"507","2","Sustainable Energy Focal Point Mandate","It will serve as a focal point for sustainable energy development and promotion.",""],[1,"507","2","Renewable Energy Development Agency Coordination","Government agencies and departments like Bangladesh Power Development Board (BPDB), Rural Electrification Board (REB), Local Government Engineering Directorate (LGED) and others are involved in renewable energy development in Bangladesh.","Bangladesh Power Development Board (BPDB) | Rural Electrification Board (REB) | Local Government Engineering Directorate (LGED)"],[1,"507","2","Green Financing Policy Guidelines","To encourage investment and green financing, Bangladesh Bank has formulated policy guidelines for banks and non-financial institutions.","Bangladesh Bank"]],"146":[[1,"53","4","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Programme","Energy efficiency and conservation will be enhanced across the industry from generation to the consumer end.",""],[1,"53","5","Industrial Gas Efficiency Through Cogeneration and Tri-generation","Industrial users of gas as well as captive generators will have to increase efficiency through cogeneration/tri-generation.",""],[1,"76","4","Industrial Energy Efficiency and Conservation Targets","In line with the Government precedence to the promotion of Energy Efficiency (EE) and Energy Conservation (EC) programmes, the different energy saving targets has been set to improve efficiency of industrial Boiler, Captive Power Generator and industrial furnaces/kilns in order to ensure energy conservation.",""],[1,"99","3","Energy Supply Expansion and Demand Management Strategy","The strategy needs to provide a balanced approach that looks at both supply increases through new investments and demand management.",""],[1,"367","13","Power Sector Efficiency and Loss Reduction","Improving power sector efficiency and reducing transmission and distribution losses.",""],[1,"371","6","Repowering of Gas-Based Old Power Plants","steps have been taken to generate additional 700-800 MW power through repowering gas based old power plants",""],[1,"371","6","Conversion of Simple Cycle Power Plants","Actions have been taken to convert Ghorashal, Baghabari, Shikalbaha and Shahjibazar simple cycle power plants",""],[1,"372","2","Gas Demand Side Management and Energy Efficiency Programme","Demand Side Management (DSM) through Energy Efficiency and Conservation (EEC) improvement will be a key focus of the gas sector in the Seventh Plan to conserve the shrinking gas resources.",""],[1,"377","5","Improved Cooking Stove Dissemination","Improved Cooking Stove: As part of the Government's efforts to disseminate cleaner and more sustainable energy to all, Improved Cooking Stove (ICS) can play an important role.",""],[1,"378","3","Holiday Staggering Programme in Commercial Areas and Markets","Holiday staggering programme in commercial areas and markets.",""],[1,"378","6","Simple Cycle to Combined Cycle Power Plant Conversion","Conversion of Simple Cycle power plant to Combined cycle Power Plant",""],[1,"378","7","Incandescent Bulb Replacement with Energy-Efficient Lighting","Replacement of inefficient incandescent bulb with energy efficient CFL/ LED bulb.",""],[1,"378","8","Government and Semi-Government CFL/LED Lighting Adoption","Use of CFL/LED in Government & semi-government offices.",""],[1,"378","9","Street Lighting Modernization Program","Conventional street lights will be replaced by LED and solar subsequently",""],[1,"378","10","Replacement of Single-Cycle Plants with CCGT for Base Load Operation","Replacement of single cycle plants by CCGT for base load operation",""],[1,"378","11","Power Plant Repowering for Capacity and Efficiency Improvement","Re-powering of inefficient and old power plants for capacity & efficiency improvement",""],[1,"378","12","Performance Improvement of Inefficient Power Plants","Performance improvement of inefficient power plants",""],[1,"378","13","National Prepaid and Smart Metering Rollout","Introduction of quality pre-paid and smart metering all over the country",""],[1,"378","14","Improved Rice Parboiling System in Rice Mills","Use of Improved Rice Parboiling System in the rice mills",""],[1,"378","15","Improved Cook Stove Promotion Programme","Use of Improved Cook Stoves in the rural areas and Improve gas stoves in the urban areas",""],[1,"378","16","Intelligent Motor Controller Energy-Saving Adoption","Use of energy saving Intelligent Motor Controller (IMC)",""],[1,"378","18","Energy Conservation Curriculum Integration","Incorporation of Energy Conservation issues in the academic curriculum of School/Madrasas/Colleges",""],[1,"378","19","Incorporation of Energy Conservation and Efficiency in the National Building Code","Include Energy Conservation and Energy Efficiency issues in the National Building Code",""],[1,"378","23","Industrial Gas Efficiency Review and Technical Remediation Study","Reviewed and assessed the existing efficiency of the major gas users and identify the inefficient gas users' causes of low efficiency, recommend the technical aspects to remedy the inefficiency of the identified major gas users with cost- benefit analyses.",""],[1,"378","27","Energy Standard and Energy Star Labelling Programme","Implementation of energy standard & energy star labelling programme through BSTI",""],[1,"378","29","Energy Conservation and Energy Efficiency Programme","Energy Conservation & Energy Efficiency Programme: The Government accorded high priority to the promotion of Energy Efficiency (EE) and Energy Conservation (EC) programmes during the Sixth Plan.",""],[1,"379","1","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Planning Framework","The \"Energy Efficiency and Conservation Map\" and \"Energy Efficiency Action Plan\" have been prepared, and preparation of \"Energy Efficiency and Conservation Master Plan\" with support from Government of Japan is under process.",""],[1,"379","1","Energy Savings Target Implementation Programme","Time-bound targets for energy savings have been set and programme implementation is well underway.",""],[1,"380","2","Demand-Side Energy Management and Conservation","In this policy, the following items would need to be delineated: i) Gas Allocation Policy, ii) Domestic gas exploration policy, (iii) Domestic coal utilization; iv) Energy import) Demand side management and energy conservation, vi) Improved Cooking Stove (ICS); and vii) Energy subsidy and pricing.",""],[1,"380","2","Improved Cooking Stove Promotion","In this policy, the following items would need to be delineated: i) Gas Allocation Policy, ii) Domestic gas exploration policy, (iii) Domestic coal utilization; iv) Energy import) Demand side management and energy conservation, vi) Improved Cooking Stove (ICS); and vii) Energy subsidy and pricing.",""],[1,"382","3","Gas Conservation and Energy Efficiency Measures","The policy effort involves substitution of low thermal efficient gas-fired power plants with more energy efficient plants; incentives for adoption of improved fuel use efficiency and energy conservation technology in industry; and conserving gas consumption by households through proper metering and pricing based on volume of gas consumed rather than a monthly flat rate per stove.",""],[1,"383","21","Demand-Side Management Initiative Implementation","Administrative and technical capacities also need to expand in a number areas related to domestic gas exploration, negotiation of IOC investments, development and implementation of renewable energy programmes and the implementation of DSM initiatives.",""],[1,"388","8","Interim Action Plan for Improvement of Energy Efficiency and Conservation","Interim Action Plan for Improvement of Energy Efficiency and Conservation",""],[1,"394","1","Operational Efficiency Improvement for Generation Plants","Adoption and implementation of a proper O&M is of highest priority.",""],[1,"394","2","Gas Power Plant Repowering and CCGT Conversion","efforts are currently underway for repowering some of the Ghorasal units.",""],[1,"395","2","Demand Side Management Policy","The Government will continue its emphasis on energy conservation by working on both supply and demand sides.",""],[1,"395","6","Energy Management Programme","the sustainable component of SREDA is entrusted with three main pillars: (1) energy management Programme, (2) energy efficiency labelling Programme, and (3) energy efficiency building Programme.",""],[1,"395","6","Energy Efficiency Labelling Programme","the sustainable component of SREDA is entrusted with three main pillars: (1) energy management Programme, (2) energy efficiency labelling Programme, and (3) energy efficiency building Programme.",""],[1,"395","6","Energy Efficiency Building Programme","the sustainable component of SREDA is entrusted with three main pillars: (1) energy management Programme, (2) energy efficiency labelling Programme, and (3) energy efficiency building Programme.",""],[1,"395","6","Financial Incentive Schemes for Energy Conservation","SREDA will be empowered to offer financial incentive schemes for promoting the programmes to conserve power system in the range of 1,000MW during the Seventh Plan.",""],[1,"395","6","Energy Manager and Energy Auditor Certification Mechanism","The Energy management Programme includes (i) certification mechanism of Energy Manager and Energy Auditor, and (ii) designation of large energy consumers in industry and building sectors that have obligations to nominate energy managers, implement the energy management for energy saving, prepare and submit annual energy reports and improvement plan to SREDA, and implement the energy audit periodically.",""],[1,"395","6","Designation of Large Energy Consumers for Energy Management Compliance","The Energy management Programme includes (i) certification mechanism of Energy Manager and Energy Auditor, and (ii) designation of large energy consumers in industry and building sectors that have obligations to nominate energy managers, implement the energy management for energy saving, prepare and submit annual energy reports and improvement plan to SREDA, and implement the energy audit periodically.",""],[1,"395","7","Energy Efficiency Labelling Programme","The energy efficiency labelling Programme intends to promote sales of high efficiency products in the market, mainly home appliances such as room air-conditioner, refrigerator/freezer, TV, motors, lighting, and fan, through officially certified five star rating labels on them.",""],[1,"395","7","Energy-Efficient Building Programme","The energy efficiency building Programme is designed to introduce energy efficiency building equipment and appliances in accordance with the New National Building Code requirement and upcoming energy efficiency building guidelines in next five years.",""],[1,"396","1","Building Code Adoption for Energy-Efficient and Low-Impact Buildings","Building Code, a voluntary Programme under development to be used as a guideline for the design and construction of upper-grade energy efficiency and conservation and low environment impact buildings, will be adopted for the implementation.",""],[1,"396","2","Power Conservation Incentive Mechanisms","A range of incentives has been proposed including preferential taxation, subsidy and low-interest financing.",""],[1,"396","2","SERDA Institutional Strengthening","Concerted efforts will be needed to make SERDA fully functional with a clear mandate to implement the Government's power conservation strategy.",""],[1,"397","4","Power Sector Efficiency and Conservation Policies","Several new policies have been adopted to conserve power and improve the operational efficiency of the power sector.",""]],"147":[[1,"53","4","Coal-Based Power Plant Development","Most of the new generation would come from coal based power plants with state of the art technology that minimizes impact on environment and ensures high efficiency.",""],[1,"53","4","Rooppur Nuclear Power Project First Plant Commissioning","Rooppur Nuclear Power Project's first plant (1000 MW) will be commissioned immediately after 2020.",""],[1,"53","5","Primary Energy Supply Diversification Strategy","The strategy during the 7th Plan will be to meet the shortfall in domestic gas with coal, particularly imported and LNG while moving ahead with accelerated exploration of hydrocarbons in the offshore and the deep sea.",""],[1,"53","5","Regional Hydropower Cooperation Initiative","Regional cooperation will also be pursued, in particular, to harness hydropower.",""],[1,"75","4","Marine 2D Non-Exclusive Multi-Client Seismic Survey","Petrobangla has initiated to conduct marine 2D Non-Exclusive Multi-Client Seismic Survey within the sovereign offshore areas of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"75","5","Floating Storage and Re-gasification Unit LNG Import Facility","necessary steps have been taken to add about 4 million ton per annum (MMTPA) imported LNG by installation of a Floating Storage and Re-gasification Unit (FSRU) at Moheshkhali on Build Own Operate Transfer (BOOT) basis.",""],[1,"75","5","Land-Based LNG Terminal Development","Moreover, the Government is going to undertake two land based LNG terminal in the country.",""],[1,"76","1","Land-Based LNG Terminal Development","The land based LNG terminal would be completed within 5-7 years.",""],[1,"76","2","Barapukuria Coal Mine Production Expansion","Recently rate of coal production from Barapukuria has been increased significantly due to application of modern coal extracting method.",""],[1,"76","2","Barapukuria Underground Mining Extension Feasibility Study","Beside, feasibility study for extension of existing underground mining operation of Barapukuria Coal Mine towards the southern and the northern side of the basin without interruption of the present production is being undertaken.",""],[1,"76","3","Coal Bed Methane Feasibility Study Project","A Coal Bed Methane (CBM) feasibility study project has been undertaken to evaluate the methane gas reserve as well as to examine the commercial viability for extraction of CBM from Jamalganj coal field which is about one kilometre deep.",""],[1,"370","5","Onshore Gas Exploration by Petrobangla","Petrobangla should undertake most of the onshore exploration on its own at relatively lower cost.",""],[1,"370","5","Offshore Gas Exploration under Production Sharing Contracts","At the same time effort should be made for offshore exploration under Production Sharing Contract (PSC) with reputed International Oil Companies (IOCs).",""],[1,"370","6","Gas Development Fund for Upstream Exploration and Development","To support BAPEX for undertaking seismic survey and exploration works, in 2009 the Government took the initiative to establish the Gas Development Fund (GDF), where 15 percent of the gas tariff is utilized for upstream exploration and development activities.",""],[1,"370","6","Petrobangla Subsidiary Gas Exploration Projects","Currently, subsidiary companies of Petrobangla have been implementing 13 projects amounting Tk. 22.84 billion with this fund.",""],[1,"370","6","Petrobangla Own-Financed Gas Projects","Besides, Petrobangla and its subsidiary companies have been implementing 8 projects amounting Tk. 12.23 lakh with own financing.",""],[1,"370","7","Strengthening BAPEX Technical Capacity","Efforts have also focused on strengthening the technical capabilities of BAPEX.",""],[1,"370","8","Accelerated Onshore Gas Survey, Exploration, and Development","the active survey/exploration/development movement has to be further accelerated even in these \"difficult areas\" to meet the national gas demand and contribute to the economic growth.",""],[1,"370","8","Foreign Investment Attraction for Natural Gas Exploitation","the Government has made efforts to attract foreign investments through International Oil Companies (IOCs) to exploit its natural gas.",""],[1,"372","4","Liquefied Natural Gas Import Terminal Development","Petro Bangla has started working on LNG import.",""],[1,"373","1","Land-Based LNG Terminal Development","the Government is going to undertake two land based LNG terminal in the country.",""],[1,"381","2","Gas Exploration and Development Investment","Therefore, Bangladesh will urgently need to focus on investment for exploration and development.",""],[1,"381","2","LNG Import Supply Security Measure","Subsequently, LNG import should be considered to ensure smooth supply of natural gas.",""],[1,"381","3","Onshore and Offshore Oil and Gas Exploration","Therefore, both onshore and offshore oil and gas options should be pursued.",""],[1,"381","6","LNG Supply Diversification and Co-purchasing Measures","In order to mitigate the very high unit price and to have bargaining power, it is critical for Bangladesh to take various measures, such as diversification of gas suppliers, and co- purchasing of natural gas with other countries.",""],[1,"381","6","Pursuit of Additional LNG Supply Sources","Bangladesh may pursue: i) in addition to the current negotiation with Qatar, pursue other LNG supply sources;",""],[1,"383","21","Domestic Gas Exploration Capacity Expansion","Administrative and technical capacities also need to expand in a number areas related to domestic gas exploration, negotiation of IOC investments, development and implementation of renewable energy programmes and the implementation of DSM initiatives.",""],[1,"383","21","IOC Investment Negotiation Capacity","Administrative and technical capacities also need to expand in a number areas related to domestic gas exploration, negotiation of IOC investments, development and implementation of renewable energy programmes and the implementation of DSM initiatives.",""]],"148":[[1,"719","2","Women's Renewable Energy Access Expansion","Women's expanded access to renewable energy would be ensured in both grid and off- grid areas to facilitate their economic gains as well as conservation of resources.",""],[1,"719","2","Women's Access to Solar, Biogas, and Improved Cookstoves","The energy policy would consider and enhance women's access to solar power, bio-gas, improve cook-stoves etc.",""],[1,"719","2","Women's Rural Market Corner Infrastructure Expansion","Women's access to rural market corners and such infrastructure have proved to be beneficial and can be expanded in collaboration with the local government institutions (e.g. municipalities, city corporations).",""]],"149":[[1,"652","11","Nuclear Power Plant and Nuclear Medicine Centres Development","Expand peaceful use of nuclear energy through establishment of nuclear power plant (NPP) and nuclear medicine centres (NMC).",""],[1,"653","21","Atomic Energy Development Support","Support the development of Atomic energy.",""]],"150":[[1,"367","16","Cross-Border Electricity Trading Exploration","Exploring electricity-trading options with neighbouring countries (India, Nepal, Bhutan and Myanmar).",""],[1,"385","1","Cross-Border Power Import Expansion","Bangladesh is now importing 500 MW power from India through the 400 KV transmission line & HVDC sub-station.",""],[1,"385","1","Additional Power Import from Palatana","Import of 100 MW power from Palatana, India is under process.",""],[1,"385","1","Expanded Cross-Border Grid Power Import","it would be possible to import additional 500 MW power through Bheramara & Boharampur grid lines from India.",""],[1,"392","3","Power Trade Expansion and Hydropower Import Programme","Building on this experience, the Seventh Plan will further expand trade with India and also explore hydro-power import opportunities with Nepal and Bhutan.",""],[1,"397","3","Energy Trade Contract Negotiation and Monitoring Capacity","Capacities need to be strengthened to negotiate and monitor implementation of energy trade contracts with neighbours.",""],[1,"397","3","Regional Electricity Trade and Cross-Border Power Investment","Regional opportunities should be explored intensely to secure the energy requirement of the economy.",""]],"151":[[1,"491","6","Waste-to-Energy Programme","Waste to energy using CDM or other appropriate programmes.",""],[1,"491","13","Solar Supply Expansion and Biogas and Composting Support Programme","Expanding solar supply and supporting programmes on composting & biogas production from cow dung poultry droppings and organic wastes through piloting and promotional activities.",""]],"152":[[1,"596","1","Literacy and Non-Formal Education Programmes","The Government has been implementing Literacy/NFE programmes in various forms since its Independence in 1971.",""],[1,"596","1","Non-Formal Education Policy Implementation","The government has adopted NFE Policy in 2006 aimed at reducing the number of illiterates, offering need-based continuing education, Pre-voc1 & Pre-voc2 level education, promotion of equivalency between formal and non-formal education, ensuring community ownership and sustainability of NFE programmes.",""],[1,"596","1","Illiteracy Elimination Goal","The goal of the 7th FYP will be to completely eliminate illiteracy as outlined in the NEP.",""],[1,"596","1","Second Chance Schooling Mechanism","In addition, a mechanism supporting 'Second chance' schooling will be considered.",""],[1,"596","10","Community-Based Network of Learning Centres","Establishing a community-based network of learning centres in order to create scope for ICT based continuing and lifelong learning.",""],[1,"596","20","Establishment of Non-Formal Education Board","Establishment of Non-Formal Education Board",""]],"153":[[1,"661","2","Upazila Playground Expansion Programme","Active participation in games, sports and recreational activities will be highly encouraged by developing and extending playgrounds at the upazila level.",""],[1,"661","2","School Sports and Physical Education Strengthening Programme","Efforts will be made to strengthen sports and physical education programme at the school stage, right from the primary level and gradually develop and systematize them up to the College and University levels.",""],[1,"661","2","Football Development Through Tournaments and Academy Management","The game of football will be developed through various tournaments and organized management of the academy in Sylhet.",""],[1,"661","2","Cricket Facilities Upgrading Initiative","The standard of cricket will also be raised through a number of different initiatives, including building and upgrading facilities to meet the international standard.",""],[1,"661","2","Bangladesh Krira Shikkha Protishtan Investment Support","Proper investments in Bangladesh Krira Shikkha Protishtan (BKSP) will ensure talented athletes avail the best training and guidance that will enable them to shine in the regional and international competitions, bringing laurels for the country.",""],[1,"661","5","Talent Identification for Sports Training","Talent identification for expensive training for all kind of sports.",""],[1,"661","7","Upazila-Level Playground Development and Expansion","Development & Extension of Playground at Upazila level.",""],[1,"661","8","Sports Infrastructure Development for Men and Women","To develop of sports infrastructural facilities for men and Women at.",""],[1,"661","9","Indoor Sports Infrastructure Development","To create Sports infrastructure facilities for indoor games.",""],[1,"661","10","Upazila Sports Infrastructure Development for Football and Cricket","To provide Sports infrastructure facilities for Football and Cricket games at Upazila level.",""],[1,"661","11","Development of Regional Sports Institutions","Development of regional sports institutions with proper facilities.",""],[1,"661","12","District Sports Schools under BKSP","Establish Sports Schools under BKSP in all the districts.",""],[1,"661","13","Sports Infrastructure Development in Upazilas and Zilas","Establish sports related infrastructure in all the Upazilas and Zilas.",""],[1,"661","14","Indoor Stadium and Swimming Pool Construction","Establish indoor stadium and swimming pools in Divisional and National level.",""],[1,"661","15","Rural Sports Facilities Development","Develop facilities for Football and Cricket as well as other sports in Rural level.",""]],"154":[[1,"618","7","Mandatory ICT Education at Secondary Level","The Perspective Plan calls for making ICT education mandatory at the secondary level by 2013",""],[1,"618","7","Primary School Computer Lab Establishment","establishment of computer labs at the primary level by 2021also",""],[1,"619","1","ICT Human Resource Development Programme","The human resource development component of ICT consists of four parts: (a) building e-learning infrastructure, i.e., one school, one computer lab, smart class room with e-learning facilities; (b) ICT education; (c) ICT-based education; and, (d) vocational ICT training facilities for the youth.",""],[1,"619","2","E-learning Infrastructure and Multimedia Classroom Expansion","A model is being implemented meeting two interrelated objectives: (a) creation of smart/multimedia classrooms; and, (b) training teachers to create digital contents for their use in classrooms.","Ministry of Education | Ministry of Primary and Mass Education"],[1,"619","2","Multimedia Classroom Establishment Projects","Two separate projects under MoE and MoPME are currently underway aimed at establishing 20,500 and 7,000 MMCs at the secondary and primary level respectively.","Ministry of Education | Ministry of Primary and Mass Education"],[1,"619","4","ICT Courses and E-Learning in Schools","ICT courses for grade VI-XII have been introduced besides e-book conversion of 325 textbooks.",""],[1,"619","4","Electronic Teaching Programme for Students","An electronic teaching Programme for students (e-learning) has been introduced.",""],[1,"619","4","Bangladesh National Library Modernization Project","The Bangladesh National Library Modernization Project is working in the following areas: digital library infrastructure, collect materials for full-text digitization, permanent store, create digital data storage, online data transfer, automatic binding and conservation measures to scientific and research.",""],[1,"619","6","ICT-Based Education Project","Secondary and Higher Secondary ICT based Education project has established 20,000 Multimedia MMCs comprising of 13,700 school, 5,200 madrasas and 1,600 colleges.",""],[1,"619","6","Basic ICT Skills Transfer and School Computer Lab Programme","The Basic ICT Skills Transfer up-to-Upazila-level has set up computer labs at 192 educational institutions.",""],[1,"619","6","Teacher Multimedia Content Development Training","In addition, 12,500 teachers have been trained to create multimedia content.",""],[1,"619","6","Teacher's Portal E-Learning Content Repository","These teachers are creating and sharing multimedia contents through a Teacher's Portal (https://www.teachers.gov.bd/), which is a central repository for e-learning content for teacher training and for all students.",""],[1,"619","6","Teacher Participation Incentive Scheme","Incentives, through public recognition of best contents, are being awarded to encourage teachers' participation.",""],[1,"619","6","Digital Education Events and Conferences","Digital World (international), Digital Innovation Fair (district and sub-district level), Education Leaders' Conference (international), and Teachers' Conference (national) are being organized.",""],[1,"634","2","Interactive Multimedia Classrooms in Schools","Every primary and secondary school will establish a multimedia classroom with a power-saving internet-connected laptop, projector/large-screen-TV and teachers professionally trained to use multimedia content for general subjects.",""],[1,"634","3","Teacher Performance and Innovation Incentive Scheme","Salary increments, bonuses and professional advancement for teachers will be instituted over time based on innovation and educational outcomes.",""],[1,"634","3","Teacher Recognition and Leadership Incentive Measures","Non-fiscal incentives will be designed in terms of recognition and opportunities for leadership in different levels.",""],[1,"634","5","Education TV Channel Development","the almost unused second terrestrial channel of the government may be turned into an education TV channel after the broadcast of parliamentary sessions.",""]],"155":[[1,"600","27","Vocational Courses in Dakhil Stage Madrasas","vocational courses have been introduced in the Dakhil Stage in selected one hundred",""],[1,"601","1","Madrasa Modernization Programme","The Madrasa system will be modernized under the qualitative goal of secondary and higher education.",""],[1,"601","2","Infrastructure Upgrades for Non-Government Madrasas","Construction of furnished academic buildings of non-government Madrasas will be implemented.",""],[1,"601","3","Madrasa Curriculum and Examination Reform","To promote quality education in Madrasas, existing courses and curriculum of Ebtedayee, Dakhil and Alim will be reviewed and revised.",""],[1,"601","4","ICT Integration in Madrasas","there will be wider access of ICT in Madrasas.",""],[1,"601","4","ICT-Based Teaching and Learning in Madrasas","ICT is to be incorporated in the teaching-learning process.",""],[1,"601","4","Madrasa Teacher ICT Capacity Building","Capacity building of Madrasa teachers in using ICT and computer aided learning will take place.",""],[1,"601","4","Multimedia Classroom Upgrading for Government-Approved Madrasas","Government approved Madrasas will be equipped with multi-media classrooms.",""],[1,"601","4","E-Filing Introduction at Bangladesh Madrasa Education Board","Introduction of e-filing at Bangladesh Madrasa Education Board is expected during the plan period.",""]],"156":[[1,"602","1","Private University Regulation and Accreditation Reform","This law replaces the 1992 Act and requires stronger self-regulation, specify the responsibilities of various parties involved in establishing and managing the institutions, and the formation of an accreditation council for academic and instructional standards.","UGC"],[1,"603","5","University Consolidation and Strengthening","Consolidation and strengthening of existing universities",""],[1,"603","11","Virtual Education Introduction","Introduce virtual education",""],[1,"603","13","Strengthening of the University Grants Commission","Further strengthening of University Grants Commission",""],[1,"603","14","Accreditation Council Establishment","Establishment of accreditation council",""],[1,"603","16","University Infrastructure and Scientific Equipment Development","priority will be given to infrastructural development including libraries & laboratories and procurement of scientific equipment.",""],[1,"603","16","Expansion of Science and Technology Universities","More universities, especially belonging to science and technological fields, will be established to meet the demand for higher education.",""],[1,"603","16","Curriculum Modernization for Market Relevance","Curricula will be modified and updated to match market demand.",""],[1,"603","16","University Grants Commission Restructuring","This will include restructuring the UGC to strengthen its capacity as the leader in the policy matters and ensure transparency and accountability in the academic, financial and administrative affairs in the universities as well as in UGC.",""],[1,"603","16","University Oversight and Accountability Strengthening","Financial and administrative accountability will be brought in through efficient supervision of the activities of the universities by the UGC and the relevant Parliamentary Committees.",""],[1,"603","16","University Statute and Rule Review","Relevant statutes/rules of universities will be reviewed to make their operation more transparent and cost effective.",""],[1,"604","1","Completion of Ongoing University Education Development Projects","Ongoing development projects of the university education sub-sector, now under implementation will have to be completed on priority basis",""],[1,"604","2","University Building Repair and Renovation Programme","Repair and renovation works for existing dilapidated university buildings will be undertaken.",""],[1,"604","3","Establishment of New Public Universities","Some new public universities will be established.",""],[1,"604","4","College Quality Improvement and ICT Expansion Programme","The standard and quality of colleges for higher education will be improved by providing necessary library, laboratory & IT facilities and by offering appropriate training and scholarships for the teachers.",""],[1,"604","4","ICT Courses in Post-Graduate Colleges","ICT courses would be introduced in all of the post-graduate colleges of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"604","4","College Strengthening Projects","New projects will be taken up for strengthening these colleges.",""],[1,"604","5","Strengthening of Reputed Degree Colleges","all reputed and established degree colleges offering honours and masters programmes, should be facilitated more in order to maintain the quality of tertiary education.",""],[1,"604","6","Bangladesh Open University Distance Education Expansion","Bangladesh Open University (BOU) will be further developed in order to facilitate distant educational facilities for on the job and distressed people all over the country.",""],[1,"604","7","Foreign Training Programme for University Teachers and Researchers","Programmes for mid-term and short-term training in foreign countries will be taken up for university teachers and researchers.",""],[1,"604","8","Higher Education Quality Enhancement Project","Higher Education Quality Enhancement Project (HEQEP) is now under implementation (2009-2018) with an objective to improve the standard and quality of university education.",""],[1,"604","8","Quality Assurance and Accreditation Projects","further projects will be taken up with regard to quality assurance and accreditation.",""],[1,"604","9","Bangladesh Research Network Expansion","Bangladesh Research Network (Bren) has been established under the HEQEP. This will be further developed during the Seventh Five Year Plan",""],[1,"604","10","University Grants Commission Empowerment and Restructuring","The University Grants Commission will be appropriately empowered in the context of rapidly changing national and global scenario in the higher education sector.",""],[1,"604","12","Scientific Education Promotion and Science Facility Construction","To that end, the Government has already set a goal of creating interest in the young generation in studying science and technology.",""],[1,"605","2","Research Grants and Fellowships","Grants on research assistance and fellowships will be provided.",""],[1,"605","2","Nuclear Power Training and Educational Institute","In the nuclear energy sector, Nuclear Power Training and Educational Institute will be established which will develop qualified and specially trained manpower.",""]],"157":[[1,"608","9","National Technical and Vocational Qualifications Framework Expansion","The NTVQF will expand the number of qualifications available in the country to better reflect the growing and changing occupational and skill profiles in both domestic and international labour markets.",""],[1,"608","9","Integration of Skills Training Across Learning and Work Settings","It will support stronger integration of skills training in community organizations, schools, training institutions and the workplace, by providing a common national benchmark for the naming and achievement of qualifications, up to, but not including, university degrees.",""],[1,"608","9","International Recognition Benchmark for Bangladeshi Workers' Skills","The NTVQF will also provide a new benchmark for the international recognition of the skills and knowledge of Bangladeshi workers, who are recognized as an increasingly important export for this country.",""],[1,"608","11","National Qualifications Quality and Consistency Improvement","improve the quality and consistency of nationally recognized qualifications;",""],[1,"608","12","Standardized Credential Naming for Skills Education and Training","introduce consistent naming of credentials for formal and non-formal skills based education and training;",""],[1,"608","13","Formal Recognition of Workplace Skills","provide formal recognition of workplace skills obtained in both the formal and informal economies;",""],[1,"608","15","Alignment of Formal and Non-Formal Training Programmes with Industry Requirements","improve the alignment of formal and non-formal training programmes with industry requirements;",""],[1,"608","16","Programme and Progression Pathway Expansion","increase options for students by broadening Programme and progression pathways;",""],[1,"609","1","Lifelong Learning Pathways for Workers","support lifelong learning by providing recognized pathways for workers to raise the level of their knowledge and skills throughout their working life, and beyond.",""],[1,"609","2","National Technical and Vocational Qualifications Framework Expansion","The NTVQF will include two pre-vocational levels to introduce additional pathways in general education and to cater for the under privileged and low educated groups in society.",""],[1,"609","2","Statement of Attainment for Partial Completion","Under the NTVQF, training organizations will also be able to issue a Statement of Attainment for specific units of competency when less than the full Programme has been completed.",""],[1,"609","3","Competency-Based Training and Assessment System","The skills development system must be responsive to the present and future industry needs and will move to implement a competency based training and assessment (CBT&A) system to achieve that end.",""],[1,"609","5","Competency-Based Training Progression System","Progression through a competency based training Programme will be determined by whether the student has met the set standards, and not by the time spent in training.",""],[1,"609","7","Competency-Based Training and Assessment Development","An important foundation for the introduction of CBT&A is close dialogue with industry to develop clear descriptions of the skills and knowledge required to perform different tasks in the workplace.",""],[1,"609","8","Industry Engagement and Support for Training Institutions","Under a CBT&A system, industry will be expected to increase its engagement and support of training institutions, so that programmes and graduates are more likely to meet the needs of employers and their staff.",""],[1,"609","8","Instructor and Trainer Capacity-Building Programme","All instructors and trainers will be provided with adequate training so they can develop and implement CBT&A programmes.",""],[1,"609","8","Training Institute Facilities and Equipment Upgrade","Considerable investments will also be made to upgrade the facilities and equipment of select training institutes so they can deliver the new industry endorsed qualifications.",""],[1,"609","8","CBT&A Impact Monitoring Mechanism","The impact of CBT&A will be closely monitored to ensure the opportunities for skills development available to industry and learners are not adversely affected due to additional costs.",""],[1,"609","9","Bangladesh Skills Quality Assurance System","The Bangladesh Skills Quality Assurance System will be introduced to improve the quality of skills development in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"609","11","Development of Nationally Recognized Competency Standards and Qualifications","development of nationally recognized units of competency and qualifications;",""],[1,"610","3","Development and Publication of Quality Procedures and Manuals","the development and publication of quality procedures and manuals and its effective implementation.",""],[1,"610","4","Skills Quality Assurance System","Specific detailed quality standards and criteria will be developed to allow implementation of the new Skills Quality Assurance System.",""],[1,"610","4","Mandatory Registration for Private Training Providers","The new system will also consider a multiple tiered registration process so that mandatory registration for private training providers can be implemented.",""],[1,"610","4","Tiered Registration for Training Provider Recognition","Tiered registration will also allow for the recognition of excellence amongst training providers.",""],[1,"610","5","Skills Training Accreditation and Quality Standards System","all government agencies delivering skills training will become accredited against the new quality standards, so that learners can receive formal recognition of skills learned, through Statements of Attainment and other qualifications from the NTVQF.","Bangladesh Technical Education Board (BTEB) | NSDC (National Skills Development Council)"],[1,"610","5","Fast-Tracked Local Registration for Compliant Training Institutions","Training institutions that provide evidence of meeting these standards will have local registration fast-tracked.",""],[1,"715","5","Marketable Technical and Vocational Education Reform","It is essential to reform the educational curriculum to cater to the needs of the country and the changing global requirements based on labour market analysis and future projections.",""],[1,"715","5","ICT Proficiency Measures in Education","It should also include measures for proficiency in ICT.",""],[1,"715","5","Trade Skills Modernization and Certification System","Modernization of trade skills education; increasing different language proficiency; hands on training; standardization of courses in consistency with international needs; establishing globally acceptable certification system; and improved qualification of teaching staff are the needs of the day.",""]],"158":[[1,"702","3","Early Childhood Development Awareness and Community Childcare Programme","The intervention for early childhood development will include an awareness raising programme for parents to make them aware of early childhood development benefits, promote community- based childcare centres for clusters of families where literate mothers are trained to become caregivers and design facilities for early learners.",""],[1,"702","3","Pre-Primary Education Expansion","Pre-primary education (for children 3-5 years) will be expanded to make formal education more effective.",""],[1,"702","3","Primary Education Access and Quality Improvement Measures","Highest level priority will be given to increase enrolment rate and decrease dropout rate, train primary teachers, increase the attendance rate, increase contact hours, and maintain gender parity in access and achievement.",""],[1,"702","3","Vocational and Technical Education Expansion","Vocational and technical education will be accorded high importance, to create better conditions for future gainful employment.",""],[1,"702","3","Non-Formal Education and Skills Training for Excluded Children","Non-formal education will be provided to diverse types of children deprived of education, like un-enrolled or drop-out children and hard- to-reach children to enhance their employability and productivity through skill training.",""],[1,"702","4","Primary School Sanitation and Safe Drinking Water Provision","Primary schools will be ensured access to sanitation and safe drinking water.",""]],"159":[[1,"588","2","Prioritized Public Investment in Education and Technology","Development plans with education have been prioritized in public sector investments.",""],[1,"589","1","Primary Education Development Programme III","During the period of the 6th FYP, the Ministry of Primary and Mass Education (MoPME) launched the third Primary Education Development Programme (PEDP III).","Ministry of Primary and Mass Education (MoPME)"],[1,"589","3","Third Primary Education Development Programme (PEDP-3)","Third Primary Education Development Programme (PEDP-3) to improve the standard of pre-school and primary level education",""],[1,"589","9","Establishment of Primary Teacher Training Institutes","Establishment of 12 Primary Teacher Training Institutes",""],[1,"589","10","Early Childhood Care and Development Policy Framework","Development of a framework for early childhood care and development policy",""],[1,"589","11","Free Textbook Distribution Programme","Free distribution of textbooks to all primary and secondary students",""],[1,"589","13","Primary Education Development Project 2012","Primary Education Development Project 2012, which provides better infrastructure, including sanitary latrines and safe water",""],[1,"589","14","Expansion of Educational Institutions","Various projects to increase the number of educational institutions - 1500 new primary schools in villages without a school, 306 new model high schools, and 4 new universities",""],[1,"592","5","Primary Education Quality Improvement Measures","Various Quality improvement measures in primary education have been taken.",""],[1,"592","6","Primary Education Development Programme III","The Third Primary Education Development Programme (PEDP III) for the years 2011-16 (extended to June 2017) has been undertaken as a sub-sector wise Programme to improve primary education quality and expand access to primary education.",""],[1,"593","3","Teacher Recruitment under PEDP III","the recruitment of 47000 teachers under PEDP III is continuing",""],[1,"593","4","Organizational Development and Capacity Building Initiative","Target related to organizational development and capacity building, including producing the HRD plan and conducting institutional analyses, will be achieved.",""],[1,"593","6","School-Level Improvement Plan Coverage Expansion","Achieving universal coverage of School-Level Improvement Plans (SLIP) by FY 2015-2016 as on track and additional attention is being given to their scope and quality.",""],[1,"593","7","Decentralization of Planning and Management Functions","The decentralization of planning and management functions is progressing.",""],[1,"593","8","Free Primary School Textbook Provision","Since the academic year 2010, all primary children have received free textbooks.",""],[1,"593","8","Competency-Based Teachers' Guide Development","The Teachers Guide is being developed based on newly revised competency based curriculum.",""],[1,"593","9","Pre-Primary Curriculum and Grade Expansion","pre-primary curriculum has been developed and introduced all GPS.",""],[1,"593","15","Inclusive Education Training Programme","Training on Inclusive Education has been given to all teachers, field level officials and DPEs officers.",""],[1,"593","16","Mother-Tongue Primary Education for Ethnic Communities","In the primary level the ethnic people are given opportunity to study in their mother tongue and ethnic teachers are given priority in areas where ethnic people are residing.",""],[1,"593","16","Introduction of Textbooks in Five Ethnic Languages","Textbooks in five ethnic languages is going to be introduced under PEDP 3 from 2016.",""],[1,"593","17","Education Tools for Children with Mild Disabilities","Education tools are being given by Ministry of Social Welfare for mild disabilities children in the primary education.","Ministry of Social Welfare"],[1,"593","19","PEDP III Communications Strategy and Social Mobilization","PEDP III will develop a communications strategy to improve understanding of the programme at district, upazila, and school, and local community levels.",""],[1,"594","4","Diploma in Education Expansion in Primary Training Institutions","Diploma in Education will be introduced in all Primary Training Institution (PTIs) gradually including improved physical facilities.",""],[1,"594","5","Teacher Job Description Reform","The job description of teachers should be revised with well-defined incentives and career paths.",""],[1,"594","8","Post-PEDP III Planning for Quality Education","Post PEDP III planning is already being undertaken for continued effective and efficient measures to ensure quality education.",""],[1,"594","10","Expansion of Free and Mandatory Primary Education to Eight Years","As per the NEP, proposed changes include a year of pre-primary and the extension of free, mandatory primary school education to a total of eight years by 2018 as per NEP.",""],[1,"594","12","School Teaching and Learning Improvement","Improve the Teaching Learning process in schools",""],[1,"594","13","Teacher Recruitment, Career Path, Training and Remuneration Reform","Teacher recruitment and their career path, training, professional support and remuneration are crucial to the strategies for improving quality in education.",""],[1,"594","13","Learner Assessment Reform","Assessment of learners' achievements will be based on terminal examinations and continuous evaluation by teachers.",""],[1,"594","13","National Learning Assessment Strengthening","National assessment will aim to strengthen cognitive, effective and skills domains rather than memorization.",""],[1,"594","13","Primary Completion Examination Pass Rate Improvement","The pass rate of primary completion exam will be increased.",""],[1,"594","13","Core Curriculum Implementation Across School Types","A core curriculum will be followed in government, nongovernment, private schools and madrasas.",""],[1,"594","15","Mainstreaming Each Child Learn Programme Nationwide","Mainstreaming Each Child Learn Programme all over the country",""],[1,"594","16","In-Service Teacher Training Expansion","Expand in-service training to teachers",""],[1,"594","17","School and Classroom-Based Assessment","Conduct school and classroom based assessment",""],[1,"594","18","Quality Textbook Provision for All Schoolchildren","Provide quality textbooks to all children of all types of schools",""],[1,"594","19","ICT in Schools and Audio-Visual Aids Initiative","Introduce ICT in all schools including audio visual aids",""],[1,"594","20","Academic Curriculum and Pedagogy Quality Improvement Measures","Adopt quality improvement measures in academic curriculum and pedagogy",""],[1,"595","1","One-Year Pre-Primary Education Programme","Preparing children physically and mentally to begin formal education by creating a one-year pre-primary programme for children aged 5+ in all primary schools is envisaged.",""],[1,"595","4","Inclusive Education Support Expansion","Increase support for inclusive education",""],[1,"595","5","School Social Mobilization Initiative","Engage all schools in social mobilization",""],[1,"595","6","Emergency Assistance Provision","Provide assistance in emergency periods",""],[1,"595","7","Primary School Stipend Programme","Provide stipends to 100% of primary school children",""],[1,"595","8","School Health Check-Up and Feeding Programme Expansion","Provide health check-ups for all students and expand school feeding programme",""],[1,"595","9","School and Classroom Construction Programme","Construct more schools and classrooms",""],[1,"595","10","Primary Education Decentralization Reform","Primary education management will be comprehensively decentralized.",""],[1,"595","11","School Funding Increase through SLIP","Increase school funding (SLIP) with the help of local community",""],[1,"595","12","Head Teacher Leadership Training","Provide leadership training to head teachers",""],[1,"595","13","Teacher Recruitment and Vacancy Filling","Fill vacancies as available and recruit more teachers",""],[1,"595","14","Annual Primary School Census","Conduct annual primary school census every year",""],[1,"595","15","National Assessment of G-5 Students","Continue national assessment of G-5 students",""],[1,"595","16","Decentralization of Primary Education Management","Management of primary education will be decentralized to the extent possible with greater involvement of community and parents and greater authority for schools.",""]],"160":[[1,"589","12","Secondary School ICT Labs Programme","Introduction of ICT labs in over three thousand secondary schools",""],[1,"597","2","ICT in Education Master Plan","the Ministry of Education with the assistance of UNESCO has initiated the 'ICT in Education Master Plan' which aims at developing a quality education system based on information technology in connection with attaining the objectives of 'Vision 2021'.","Ministry of Education | UNESCO"],[1,"597","4","Education Institution Infrastructure, ICT and Equipment Support","Infrastructural, ICT and equipment support for education institutions;",""],[1,"597","5","Teacher Financial Support and Training","Financial support and training for teachers;",""],[1,"597","6","Student Financial Support Scheme","Providing financial facilities including stipend, scholarship and other subventions for students.",""],[1,"597","7","Education Management Information System Reform","Reforming Education Management Information System;",""],[1,"597","10","Education Management Modernization","Introducing modern management options for education.",""],[1,"598","3","Teacher, Trainer, and Education Administrator Training Programme","Providing local and foreign training for teachers, trainers and education administrators of government and non- government secondary level institutions",""],[1,"598","4","Teaching and Learning Materials Provision","Providing teaching learning materials",""],[1,"598","6","Education Quality Enhancement Programmes","Undertaking programmes for enhancing the quality of education",""],[1,"598","7","Proxy Means Tested Student Grant Programme","Providing grants to students who are truly deserving in terms of socio-economic status though Proxy Means Testing (a targeting technique)",""],[1,"598","8","Secondary Education Quality Improvement Programme","Initiating programmes for improving the quality of secondary education, increasing the attendance and success rate SSC exam, and raising awareness among guardians and other stakeholders",""],[1,"598","9","Financing the DSHE Monitoring and Evaluation Wing","Financing the Monitoring and Evaluation Wing under the DSHE to strengthen the management, evaluation and assessment of secondary education",""],[1,"598","11","Teacher Training Programme Expansion","Increasing teachers' training programmes through pre-service, in-service and Continuous Professional Development (CPD) training",""],[1,"598","12","Office Equipment and ICT Materials Provision","Providing office equipment and ICT materials",""],[1,"598","13","Government Secondary School Establishment","Establishment of 7 Govt. Secondary- School in Sylhet, Barisal & Khulna Metropolitan City.",""],[1,"598","14","Establishment of Government Secondary Schools in Metropolitan Cities","Establishing 7 Govt. Secondary- Schools in Sylhet, Barisal &Khulna Metropolitan City through:",""],[1,"598","15","Academic and Administrative Building Construction","Building academic cum administrative buildings",""],[1,"598","17","Autistic Academy Establishment in Dhaka Metropolitan City","Establishing an Autistic Academy in Dhaka Metropolitan city with full facilities for the physically and mentally retarded children.",""],[1,"598","20","Female Student Stipend Programme for Degree (Pass) Level","Providing stipends to female students of Degree (Pass) level",""],[1,"598","24","Classroom and Laboratory Construction and Upgrading","Construct/upgrade classrooms and labs to facilitate spacious, healthy environment for the students.",""],[1,"598","25","Inclusive Girls' School Latrine Facilities","Build inclusive and separate latrines for girls in schools with adequate facilities for sanitary napkins and cleansing materials.",""],[1,"599","1","Provision of Teaching and Learning Aids and School Facilities","providing teaching and learning aids, facilities to increase the pupil's interest over education and to modernize the education environment;",""],[1,"599","2","ICT for Education and Student Computer Provision","introducing ICT for education; providing computers to make the students competent with the modern world of ICT and to make them fit for the present day job market;",""],[1,"599","3","Teacher Capacity Building for Quality Teaching","improving capacity for teachers to promote quality teaching;",""],[1,"599","5","Curriculum and Pedagogy Reform","Appropriation of curricula and pedagogy: Appropriation of curricula, pedagogy, texts examination techniques.",""],[1,"599","6","Madrasah Education Modernization and Facility Gap Reduction","Modernize Madrasah Education with changes of the society and reduce the gap of existing facilities for secondary education between General Education and Madrasah Education.",""],[1,"599","8","Student Stipend and Financial Support for Enrolment","Stipend and other financial support will be provided to the poor to encourage enrolment.",""],[1,"599","9","Listening and Speaking Capacity Building","Necessary steps will to be taken to increase listening & speaking capacity building.",""],[1,"599","10","Student Stipend Support and Dropout Prevention","Continuous financial support in terms of stipends will be provided and communications maintained with family to prevent them from sending their children to work.",""],[1,"599","11","Female Student Financial Support and Awareness Campaign","Providing special financial support to the female students and raising awareness in the society about the importance of female education is envisioned.",""],[1,"599","12","Inclusive Education Access for All Children","All children will have access to an appropriate, relevant, affordable and effective education regardless of gender, age, physical or financial ability, ethnicity, autistic & disable, impairment or HIV status.",""],[1,"599","18","Government Secondary School and College Establishment in Dhaka Metropolitan City","Establishment of 11 Secondary Schools & 6 Colleges (Government) in Dhaka Metropolitan City.",""],[1,"599","19","Transformation of Existing Non-Government Schools into Model Schools","Transformation of Existing Non-government Schools into Model schools in selected 310 Upazila Headquarters.",""],[1,"600","3","Development of Government Post Graduate Colleges in District Headquarters","Development of 70 Govt. Post Graduate Colleges In District HQs For Improving of Quality Education.",""],[1,"600","5","Development of Selected Non-Government Colleges with ICT Facilities","Development of Selected Non-Government Colleges Along With ICT Facilities for Improving Quality of Education.",""],[1,"600","6","Establishment of IT Labs in Selected Secondary Level Institutions","Establishment of IT Labs in Selected Secondary Level Institutions in Dhaka",""],[1,"600","10","Foreign Language Training Centres-II","Establishment of Foreign Language Training Centres-II (FLTC-II)",""],[1,"600","23","Establishment of Autistic Academy","Establishment of Autistic Academy",""]],"161":[[1,"672","6","School Meals Programme","the school meals programme",""],[1,"680","4","WASH in Schools Improvement Programme","Special direction is there in the 7th plan for WASH in schools including generation of funds for maintenance of toilets and ensuring the latrines to be kept open during class time, and are of course inclusive with universal accessibility.",""]],"162":[[1,"658","3","Cultural Heritage Preservation and Development Programme","The Ministry of Cultural Affairs, through its different organizations, is focused on enriching the intellectual status of the nation through preservation, research and development of culture, history, heritage, arts and literature.","Ministry of Cultural Affairs"],[1,"658","3","National Cultural Activities Promotion Programme","Under the 7th FYP, various activities will be undertaken that will promote the healthy growth of cultural activities throughout the country.",""],[1,"658","3","Intangible Cultural Heritage Digitization Initiative","To restore and preserve many of the intangible cultural heritages that are on the verge of extinction, digitization efforts will be implemented.",""],[1,"658","3","National Archaeological Survey and Development Programme","The Ministry will also reiterate the importance of archaeological sites by conducting national surveys and programmes for further development.",""],[1,"658","3","Antiquities Act Amendment for Heritage Protection","The Antiquities Act will be amended to strengthen protection of archaeological sites and historical monuments.",""],[1,"659","2","Cultural Preservation and Promotion Programme","Ministry of Cultural Affairs is delivering relentless effort for development, preservation, promotion and extension of the cultural elements of Bangladesh through its different organizations.","Ministry of Cultural Affairs"],[1,"659","2","National Culture Development through Bangladesh Shilpakala Academy","Bangladesh Shilpakala Academy is engaged for preserving, developing, promoting and encouraging national culture through fine arts, drama, music etc.",""],[1,"659","2","Archaeological Site Preservation and Exhibition","Department of Archaeology preserves historical sites and exhibits the antiques.",""],[1,"659","2","National Museum Heritage Preservation Programme","National Museum preserves and exhibits the cultural heritage of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"659","2","Folk Art and Crafts Preservation Programme","Folk Art and Crafts Foundation is working for preservation and development of folk art & crafts.",""],[1,"659","7","National Research on Great Men and Women","Carry out research on the lives and works of great men and women of our nation;",""],[1,"660","3","Research Programmes on Lives and Works of Great People","Research programmes on lives and works of great people will be undertaken and memorial libraries and institutions will be established in respective areas;",""],[1,"660","3","Memorial Libraries and Institutions Establishment","Research programmes on lives and works of great people will be undertaken and memorial libraries and institutions will be established in respective areas;",""],[1,"660","6","National Archaeological Site Survey and Facilities Development","National survey on archaeological sites will be carried out and physical facilities for the department of archaeology will be developed for enhancing archaeological tourism;",""],[1,"660","7","Archaeological Sites, Museums, and Historical Monuments Preservation Programme","Programmes for further development of archaeological sites, museums and ethnological museum will be undertaken and historical monuments will be identified and preserved;",""],[1,"660","11","Cultural Heritage Restoration, Preservation and Digitization Programme","Careful attention needs to be given for their restoration, preservation and digitization.",""],[1,"660","11","Institutional and Human Resource Development for Cultural Heritage Management","Institutional establishment as well as human resources development for such delicate works needs to be made carefully.",""],[1,"660","12","Archaeological Site Exploration, Preservation and Restoration Plan","Proper perspective, short, medium and long-term plan needs to be carried out.",""]],"163":[[1,"56","3","National Cultural Activities Promotion Programme","In 7th FYP period, various activities will be undertaken that will promote the healthy growth of cultural activities throughout the country under the Ministry of Cultural Affairs.","Ministry of Cultural Affairs"],[1,"658","3","National Cultural Activities Promotion Programme","Under the 7th FYP, various activities will be undertaken that will promote the healthy growth of cultural activities throughout the country.",""],[1,"658","3","Ethnic Community Cultural Centres Programme","Within the framework of national unity, steps will be taken to preserve and promote language, arts and culture of ethnic communities through cultural centres in tribal areas.",""],[1,"659","2","Cultural Centres for Small Ethnic Groups","seven cultural centres for small ethnic groups are also playing vital role in order to enhance their cultural activities.",""],[1,"659","14","Small Ethnic Group Language and Cultural Preservation Initiative","Preserve and promote language arts and culture of small ethnic group communities within the framework of national unity;",""],[1,"660","5","Tribal Cultural and Language Centres Expansion Programme","Regional and tribal cultures will be promoted and preserved through various programmes viz. erection of more tribal cultural and language centres within the tribal areas;",""]],"164":[[1,"681","4","National Disaster Risk Reduction Reform Programme","The Ministry of Disaster Management and Relief is mandated to drive national risk reduction reform programmes to address the disaster management issues.","Ministry of Disaster Management and Relief"],[1,"681","4","Hyogo Framework Disaster Risk Reduction Implementation","Efforts are being made to fulfil GoB's promises through the Hyogo Framework of Action towards providing disaster risk reduction services to its citizens.",""],[1,"685","2","National Disaster Risk Reduction Reform Programme","MoDMR has been given the mandate to drive national risk reduction reform programmes.","MoDMR"],[1,"685","4","Disaster Risk Reduction and Emergency Response Management Framework","Formulation, review and execution of legislation, policies, plans, procedures, standing orders and guidelines in relation to overall disaster risk reduction and emergency response management including relief rehabilitation and safety net programmes.",""],[1,"685","5","Relief and Disaster Risk Reduction Programmes, Planning, and Monitoring","Relief and disaster risk reduction programmes, planning, and monitoring.",""],[1,"685","6","Disaster Management and Relief Coordination Mechanism","Coordination of all activities in relation to disaster management and relief incorporating disaster risk reduction and emergency response management.",""],[1,"685","7","Disaster Risk Reduction Mainstreaming","Mainstreaming Disaster Risk Reduction across line ministries and agencies at all levels, local governments, NGO, CBOs, civil society and all other stakeholders.",""],[1,"685","8","Disaster-Related Programmes and Projects Implementation","Implementation of the disaster related programmes/projects undertaken due to adverse impacts of climate change.",""]],"165":[[1,"453","15","Cyclone Shelter and Killa Construction and Rehabilitation","Construction and rehabilitation of Cyclone Shelters and killas (1238 Nos)",""],[1,"454","1","Disaster Risk Reduction Measures","Identification and implementation of preventive, emergency and post-disaster mitigation measures will be made;",""]],"166":[[1,"720","7","Climate Change Adaptation and Community Resilience Investment","Adaptation capacity against climate change impacts will be augmented amongst community including women by investing in DRR and building resilience.",""],[1,"720","7","Community Hazard Orientation Programme","Women equally with men would be oriented in dealing with hazards, including forest",""],[1,"721","1","Climate Change Gender Action Plan Implementation","Resources would be allocated for full implementation of the Climate Change Gender Action Plan of the Government.",""],[1,"721","1","Women’s Participation in Disaster Risk Reduction Committees","Women's capacity to play effective role in DRR related committees should be strengthened.",""],[1,"721","3","Community Radio Early Warning and Livelihood Information Services","Early warning about calamities and information related to services, shelters, livelihood support etc. would be disseminated to women and men through community radio and strengthening community networks.",""]],"167":[[1,"300","10","Tourism Sector Policy and Legislative Framework","The Government has pursued several policies and legislations for the tourism sector including the Bangladesh Tourism Board Act and the Tourism Policy 2010.","Ministry of Civil Aviation and Tourism"],[1,"301","8","Tourism Site Identification and Upgrading Programme","Identifying potential tourist spots scattered over different places of the country and modernizing and expanding existing ones",""],[1,"301","11","Tourism Infrastructure and Management PPP Programme","Creating infrastructure and improving management of the tourism industry through Public Private Partnership (PPP) arrangements",""],[1,"301","12","Tourism Documentary Film Production and Event Publicity","Producing documentary films on Bangladesh Tourism & publicising tourism events",""],[1,"301","13","Procurement of Water Vessels and Tourist Coach for Package Tours","Procurement of Water Vessels and Tourist Coach for Package Tour.",""],[1,"301","14","Tourism Training Courses and Centre Expansion","Maintaining tourism related training courses and establishing 4 more tourist training centres",""],[1,"301","15","Participation in Tourism Fairs and Related Promotional Programmes","Participating in tourism fairs organized home and abroad and arranged related programmes",""],[1,"301","16","National Tourism Master Plan Preparation","Preparation of short Term, Mid-Term and Long-Term Tourism Master Plan for the country for guiding development activities for tourism",""],[1,"301","17","Visit Bangladesh Tourism Promotion Campaign","Visit Bangladesh Campaign. for Development and Promotion of Tourism",""],[1,"304","14","Visa on Arrival Simplification for Tourism","To encourage greater tourism, the visa requirements for visitors will be further simplified through visa on arrival facilities.",""],[1,"304","14","Visitor Safety and Hospitality Measures","Steps will also be taken to ensure the full safety and hospitality of all visitors.",""],[1,"305","4","Tourism Facilities Expansion and Upgrade","to expand and upgrade the tourist industry facilities comprising of visa and currency exchange facilities, hotels, restaurants, tourist resorts and inland transportation.",""],[1,"305","6","Premium Shopping Outlets Development","the Seventh Plan will focus on 5 entry points: (1) establishing 3 premium shopping outlets that meets international standards in the cities of Dhaka, Chittagong and Sylhet",""],[1,"305","6","Eco-Nature Integrated Resort Development","developing an eco-nature integrated resorts near Sundarbans",""],[1,"305","6","Teknaf to Sundarbans Riviera Development","development of a strait Riviera linking Teknaf to Sundarbans",""],[1,"305","6","Archaeological Site Promotion Initiative","promoting the archaeological sites",""],[1,"305","6","Eco-Park Establishment Programme","establishing eco parks in Chittagong and Sylhet",""],[1,"305","6","Professional Tourist Agency and Guide Development","development of professional tourist agencies and guides",""],[1,"305","8","Tourism Workforce Supply and Quality Measures","Ensure an adequate supply of qualified human capital: Introduce measures to address issues pertaining to the supply and quality of workforce in the tourism industry;",""],[1,"306","1","Tourism Environment Improvement Measures","Improve the tourism environment: Improve offerings and accessibility for key tourism enablers (such as taxi services), access to funding, security and regulations as well as improving the service quality of front-line staff;",""],[1,"306","2","Visa Facilitation Services Rollout","Rollout of visa facilitation services: Ensure that tourists from our target markets are not subject to overly strict visa procedures.",""],[1,"306","3","Tourism Public-Private Partnership and Investment Promotion","Successful implementation of the tourism strategy will require a strong public-private partnership.",""]],"168":[[1,"155","1","Technical and Vocational Institute Establishment in Lagging Regions","Lagging regions can be supported with skill development, such as, establishing technical and vocational institutes.",""],[1,"156","11","Technical and Vocational Training Institutions in Lagging Districts","Technical and vocational training institutions would be established in the lagging districts to create opportunities for the people to be semi-skilled and get employment by internal migration to industrial districts of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"610","6","National TVET Gender Equality Strategy","To promote gender equality in TVET, a draft national strategy has been developed.",""],[1,"610","6","Technical Education Enrolment Expansion","Accordingly, the Government plans to increase the enrolment in technical education from the existing 8% to 25% within the next 10 years.",""],[1,"610","6","TVET Female Enrolment Target","A target for 40 percent female enrolment in TVET by 2020 has been set.",""],[1,"610","6","TVET Stipends and Financial Support Scheme","Stipends and other financial support will be provided to the poor, especially female students, to encourage enrolment, retention and completion.",""],[1,"610","6","Additional Women’s Polytechnic Institutes","Three additional women's Polytechnic Institutes will be setup at Barisal, Sylhet and Rangpur divisional headquarters.",""],[1,"610","6","Women’s Technical School and College Expansion","Seven women's technical school and college in seven divisions will be established.",""],[1,"611","4","District Employment and Manpower Offices Establishment","Establishment of 68 (including 4 divisional offices) District Employment and Manpower Offices (DEMO) is on the agenda.",""],[1,"611","4","Overseas Employment Expansion in Lagging Regions","This will help Expand overseas employment opportunities in lagging regions by enhancing logistic support and technical advice.",""],[1,"611","4","Migration and Remittance Cost Reduction Measures","Costs of migration and remittance transfer will be reduced to facilitate the process.",""],[1,"611","5","Catering Institute Market-Oriented Skills Training","A 'Catering Institute' will provide market oriented skill training to address demand for new skills and knowledge.",""],[1,"611","7","Permanent Trainer Training Institute","This will be done through capacity building of trainers by setting up a permanent training institute for trainers.",""],[1,"611","8","Domestic Worker and Female Migrant Worker Training Expansion","Existing training of domestic workers will be extended, and about 50,000 potential female migrant workers will be trained per year.",""],[1,"691","5","National Training Capacity Development","Create a national training capacity to sustain and progressively expand the training efforts.",""],[1,"697","4","Microcredit and Vocational Training Support","the provision of microcredit along with vocational training",""],[1,"702","3","Vocational and Technical Education Expansion","Vocational and technical education will be accorded high importance, to create better conditions for future gainful employment.",""],[1,"703","3","Learning Opportunities for Working Children","Working children such as waste collectors, leather workers, brick breakers, auto- workshop workers and tempo helpers will have access to learning opportunities in formal and non-formal facilities.",""],[1,"704","8","Vocational Skills Training and Support Programme","The Government will provide appropriate training and support to people for development of their vocational skills and knowledge.",""],[1,"706","4","Youth Training and Support Provision","Necessary training and support will be provided to the youth.",""],[1,"706","5","Youth Skills Development and Support for CHT","Appropriate skill development training and support will be provided to the youth of CHT, to provide vocational and social skills and networks.",""],[1,"706","9","Vocational Training for Poor People","Micro-finance activities for poor people and farmers will be expanded (in place of micro-credit) and vocational training provided to the poor.",""],[1,"712","5","Women Skills Training Centres","Training centres have been established to provide women with different income generating skills (e.g. ICT, entrepreneurial, food processing).",""]],"169":[[1,"49","17","Inclusive Urban Planning Based on Sustainable Land Use Planning and Zoning","Inclusive urban planning based on sustainable land use planning and zoning",""],[1,"53","6","Urban Transport Congestion Management","Address the urban transportation challenge of increasing traffic congestion;",""],[1,"54","4","Urban Governance Strengthening and Housing Facilitation Strategy","The nature of urban governance is of crucial importance and should encompass better transparency and accountability of institutions, institutional strengthening and capacity building, decentralization, community participation, more efficient resource mobilization, and involvement of the private sector in the development of the urban sector.",""],[1,"83","16","Inclusive Urban Planning and Sustainable Land Use Zoning","Inclusive urban planning based on sustainable land use planning and zoning",""]],"170":[[1,"44","2","Targeted and Affirmative Education Programmes for Girls","Targeted and affirmative programmes have been designed and implemented for promoting primary and secondary education, in particular for girls who contributed to significant improvement in school retention with the added benefits of reduced under-age marriage, maternal and child mortality and enhanced women empowerment.",""],[1,"50","19","Female Enrollment in Technical and Vocational Education Promotion","Encourage female enrolment in technical and vocational education",""],[1,"51","2","School Multimedia Classroom and ICT Laboratory Expansion","All primary schools to have at least 1 and all secondary schools to have at least 3 multimedia classrooms; 30% of primary schools and 100% of all secondary schools to have an ICT laboratory",""],[1,"56","1","Secondary and Higher Education Expansion","Accordingly, greater emphasis is being placed on secondary and higher education, as well as vocational and technical education, skill development training for employment and life skills training programme.",""],[1,"56","1","Vocational and Technical Education and Skills Training","Accordingly, greater emphasis is being placed on secondary and higher education, as well as vocational and technical education, skill development training for employment and life skills training programme.",""],[1,"56","1","Inclusive Education Support for Disadvantaged Groups","To promote inclusive development, special attention will be given to the disadvantaged groups, women, children and persons with disabilities.",""],[1,"56","1","Education Quality Improvement and School Infrastructure Upgrade","Enhancing the quality of education at all levels, including madrasa, through expanding capacity of the teachers, use of ICT and better infrastructure is also the core of the Plan.",""],[1,"56","3","School Sports and Physical Education Strengthening Programme","Efforts will be made under 7th FYP to strengthen sports and physical education programme at the school stage in all districts.",""],[1,"56","3","Religious Institution-Based Literacy Programme","Religious institution based literacy programmes will be emphasized under Ministry of Religious Affairs.","Ministry of Religious Affairs"],[1,"77","8","Education Stipends for Poor and Vulnerable Children","the equity aspects of education spending can be improved by providing additional resources for stipends for the children of the poor and vulnerable families as proposed under the National Social Security",""],[1,"84","20","Female Enrollment in Technical and Vocational Education","Encourage female enrolment in technical and vocational education",""],[1,"100","6","Continuation of Girls' Education and Female Literacy Efforts","In both these areas Bangladesh has made commendable progress and this effort will continue.",""],[1,"101","1","Technical and Vocational Education and Skills Training Capacity Upgrade","needed to upgrade the capacity to deliver technical and vocational education and skills training.",""],[1,"105","2","Education Access Expansion Programmes","programmes formulated by the Ministry of Education and the Ministry of Primary and Mass Education articulate strategies to make education accessible to all.","Ministry of Education | Ministry of Primary and Mass Education"]],"171":[[1,"569","1","Comprehensive NCD Prevention and Treatment Strategy","Along with proper regulation, the Government will prepare comprehensive strategies for preventing and treating NCDs.",""],[1,"573","3","Coordinated Disease Surveillance System","a single coordinated system will be more effective and yield better results.",""],[1,"575","4","Health Promotion and Disease Prevention Efforts","massive health promotion and prevention efforts for impending non-communicable diseases will be carried out.",""],[1,"575","4","Communicable Disease Control Consolidation","Ongoing efforts to reduce the effects of communicable diseases will be further consolidated.",""],[1,"575","4","Coordinated Health Promotion Campaigns","Health promotion efforts will be further strengthened through better coordinated (among different health and family planning programmes, non-public sectors including private) with the aim of informing people about different aspects of health for changing their attitudes and behaviour resulting improved health outcomes.",""],[1,"575","5","Tobacco Control Law and Policy Enforcement","GoB will ensure effective implementation of tobacco control laws and policies as well as rigorous compliance of Framework Convention on Tobacco Control (FCTC).",""],[1,"575","7","Expanded Medical Waste Management Coverage","Medical waste management will be expanded to cover all medical installation and programmes of public and non-public sectors.",""],[1,"575","7","Health Sector Preparedness for Emerging and Re-emerging Diseases","Appropriate initiatives will be undertaken to manage the emerging and re-emerging health problems together with strengthening emergency preparedness and response capacity by health sector.",""],[1,"577","3","School-Based Health Education","health education will be included in primary schools.",""],[1,"577","3","Mass Media Health Education and Community Awareness Campaign","Steps will be taken to impart health education through mass media and raise awareness at the community level.",""],[1,"577","3","Preventive and Promotional Health Education Services","To tackle this issue, preventive and promotional health education services will be ensured for all.",""],[1,"578","5","Coordinated Health Sector Surveillance System","Develop a well-coordinated surveillance system to guide the Programme initiatives and their effectiveness",""]],"172":[[1,"708","10","Implementation of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities and Their Protection Act","The Rights of the Persons with Disabilities and their Protection Act 2013 will be implemented to ensure international standards on disability rights as set out in the Act.",""],[1,"708","10","Prioritization of Poor and Vulnerable Groups in Implementation","Requirements of the poor and vulnerable, including women and children, will be prioritized in all activities and implemented.",""],[1,"709","1","Child Disability Benefit","The Government will ensure that every child certified as having a severe disability will be provided with a regular transfer, known as the Child Disability Benefit.","Ministry of Social Welfare"],[1,"709","1","Child Disability Identification and Early Screening Mechanism","The Government will develop a mechanism to identify severe disability among children, which will not only include children with physical disability but also other disabilities like autism, cognitive, mental, sensory impairment, etc.",""],[1,"709","2","Reformed Disability Grant Scheme","The current disability grant managed by the Ministry of Social Welfare will be reformed into a scheme that provides a regular transfer to all poor and vulnerable citizens of Bangladesh with a severe disability.","Ministry of Social Welfare"],[1,"709","2","Severe Disability Identification and Appeals Mechanism","The Government will design robust measures for identifying severe disability and will establish an appeals mechanism for those who feel that they have been unfairly excluded.",""],[1,"709","3","Reformed Disability Benefit","The introduction of a reformed Disability Benefit will mark a significant change in the lives of the disabled citizens who are poor.",""],[1,"709","3","Vocational Education and Small Business Support for Disability Benefit Recipients","The Ministry of Social Welfare will complement the Disability Benefit by providing additional support to recipients by ensuring access to vocational education and small business schemes and eliminating discrimination in the labour market.","Ministry of Social Welfare"],[1,"716","6","Disability Survey and Social Protection Measures for Differently Abled Women","the upcoming disability survey would identify extent and types of disability disaggregated by sex.",""]],"173":[[1,"117","1","Sonadia Deep Sea Port Construction","construction of a deep sea port for handling of coal and other imports at Sonadia, Cox's Bazar",""],[1,"155","5","Mongla Port Intensive Utilization Measures","Appropriate measures would be adopted for intensive utilization of Mongla port.",""],[1,"155","5","Export-Oriented Industrial Zone Near Mongla Port","Creating export oriented industrial zone near to Mongla port will be considered along with its international usage opportunities.",""]],"174":[[1,"117","2","Public-Private Partnership Infrastructure Financing Facility","The government has also established the Bangladesh Infrastructure Financing Facility (BIFF) to ensure co- financing of PPP projects.",""],[1,"161","5","Public Investment Financing and Infrastructure Funding Plan","The Seventh Plan will build on the gains made so far with a view to allocating Tk.7.25 trillion in constant FY16 prices, accounting for 22.7% public investment of total investment in the economy.",""],[1,"161","5","Domestic Resource Financing for Public Sector Development Spending","Of the total public sector investment, Tk. 6.38 trillion will be funded by domestic resources (88%).",""],[1,"161","5","Domestic Financing of Annual Development Programme","A major part of the ADP will be financed from domestic sources comprising fiscal savings and borrowing from the domestic banking and nonbank sources.",""],[1,"161","5","Concessional External Financing for Public Development Spending","External financing, primarily in the form of concessional loans from official multilateral and bilateral sources will continue to supplement the public sector development spending.",""],[1,"161","5","Sovereign Bond Financing for Large Infrastructure Projects","Access to international capital market to finance large infrastructure projects by issuing sovereign bonds may also be considered as a source of external financing for domestic public investment.",""],[1,"163","3","Expansion of Government Spending and Public Investment Financing","The Seventh Plan aims to increase the size of the Government spending by about 5 percentage points to 21% of GDP by FY20.",""],[1,"625","3","PPP-Based UISC Service Expansion","New services are always being explored by NILG and a2i under PPP arrangements.",""],[1,"625","3","E-Services and M-Services Expansion","Many e-services and m-services (mobile services) in the areas of agriculture, health and services sector have been introduced by public and private sectors.",""],[1,"632","2","Public-Private Partnership for E-Service Delivery","Promote public-private partnership (PPP): The concept of PPP is new for e-service or m-service delivery in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"632","3","Strengthening the Office of the PPP","The institutional arrangements for PPP will be strengthened with internationally competent professional staff.",""],[1,"632","3","PPP Project Identification and Implementation Collaboration","The line ministries would collaborate with the Office of the PPP to identify, formulate and implement PPP projects in partnership with private sector actors.","line ministries | Office of the PPP"],[1,"632","3","PPP Approval and Implementation Coordination","The Office should coordinate among various government and private agencies for accelerating approval and implementation of PPP projects.","Office"],[1,"632","3","Private Sector Unsolicited Proposal Promotion for E-Services","The Office and line ministries and implementing agencies will encourage private sector to come forward with unsolicited proposals where private sector innovation and dynamism will be leveraged for offering e-services to citizens.","Office | line ministries | implementing agencies"],[1,"632","5","Capacity Building for Project Identification and Approval","The Office can undertake programmes for building capacity of government officials and private sector participants in collaboration with development partners so that project identification and approval process strictly adhere to stipulated time frame.",""],[1,"632","6","PPP International Cooperation and Partner Engagement","The Office needs to work with similar government agencies abroad to share views and exchange experiences to understand best practices and to make the PPP initiatives in Bangladesh vibrant and effective.",""],[1,"632","6","PPP Project Development and Investment Mobilization","The Office should work with the development partners to engage them in PPP projects for participating either in government contribution or investment by the private sector.",""]],"175":[[1,"652","7","International R&D Cooperation and Science Diplomacy Initiative","Allocating resources in establishing and supporting effective R&D cooperation with the global R&D actions supported by EU 8th and 9th Framework Programmes, OECD, ASEAN and similar international science, innovation and technology actions initiating \"science diplomacy\" to ensure partnership for sustainable economic development through knowledge generation and sharing.",""],[1,"652","8","World-Class Research and Development Infrastructure","Establishing more world class infrastructure for R&D; for gaining global recognitions in the leading and emerging areas of science.",""],[1,"652","9","R&D Investment Evaluation and Monitoring Framework","Formulating effective state-of-the-art knowledge based \"means and indicators\" for evaluating, monitoring and ranking Research & Development investments and assessing their impacts on the society and as such improving communication about these evaluation results among the citizens including political leaders, industries and the general tax payers.",""],[1,"653","2","Biotechnology Research and Human Resource Development","Undertake research on biotechnology and develop human resources in the concerned area.",""],[1,"653","3","Chemical Metrology Legal, Institutional, and Technical Capacity Strengthening","Augmenting legal and institutional framework and technical capacity in the Science of Chemical Measurements for ensuring the chemical metrological traceability to enhance the confidence among the national and international stakeholders.",""],[1,"653","4","Bangladesh Environmental Specimen Bank Establishment","Establishing energy efficient green technology based Bangladesh Environmental Specimen Bank.",""],[1,"653","5","Research and Development for Environment-Friendly Sustainable Technology","Research and development for innovation of environment friendly sustainable technology for the economically constrained communities.",""],[1,"653","6","Oceanographic Research Infrastructure Development","Development of infrastructure for conducting research on oceanographic resources.",""],[1,"653","7","Scientific Documentation Centre Data Support","Enable the Scientific Documentation Centre to furnish data for science and technology.",""]],"176":[[1,"146","5","Energy Subsidy Reform and Reallocation of Savings","The energy subsidy can be cut by a half through price increases and better targeting of energy subsidies to the poor.",""],[1,"146","5","Reallocation of Energy Subsidy Savings to Social Services","The saved resources can be diverted to the social service spending in the above- mentioned priority areas.",""],[1,"146","5","Energy Price Adjustment to Reflect Scarcity","price increases to better reflect the scarcity value will help conserve energy.",""],[1,"379","4","Primary Fuel Policy Development","Policy on primary fuel, particularly coal policy is urgently needed.",""],[1,"379","4","Energy Project Implementation Constraint Removal","The other important priority will be to address some of the major institutional constraints that have hampered implementation of energy projects.",""],[1,"379","4","PPP Strategy Reform for Primary Energy Investment","A third priority is the reform the PPP strategy with a view to achieving stronger progress with investments in primary energy during the Seventh Plan.",""],[1,"380","2","National Energy Policy Finalization and Adoption","Most importantly, the Government should urgently finalize and adopt the long-pending National Energy Policy, or alternatively develop an Energy Master Plan.",""],[1,"380","2","Gas Allocation Policy","In this policy, the following items would need to be delineated: i) Gas Allocation Policy, ii) Domestic gas exploration policy, (iii) Domestic coal utilization; iv) Energy import) Demand side management and energy conservation, vi) Improved Cooking Stove (ICS); and vii) Energy subsidy and pricing.",""],[1,"380","2","Domestic Gas Exploration Policy","In this policy, the following items would need to be delineated: i) Gas Allocation Policy, ii) Domestic gas exploration policy, (iii) Domestic coal utilization; iv) Energy import) Demand side management and energy conservation, vi) Improved Cooking Stove (ICS); and vii) Energy subsidy and pricing.",""],[1,"380","2","Domestic Coal Utilization Policy","In this policy, the following items would need to be delineated: i) Gas Allocation Policy, ii) Domestic gas exploration policy, (iii) Domestic coal utilization; iv) Energy import) Demand side management and energy conservation, vi) Improved Cooking Stove (ICS); and vii) Energy subsidy and pricing.",""],[1,"380","2","Energy Import Policy","In this policy, the following items would need to be delineated: i) Gas Allocation Policy, ii) Domestic gas exploration policy, (iii) Domestic coal utilization; iv) Energy import) Demand side management and energy conservation, vi) Improved Cooking Stove (ICS); and vii) Energy subsidy and pricing.",""],[1,"380","2","Energy Subsidy and Pricing Reform","In this policy, the following items would need to be delineated: i) Gas Allocation Policy, ii) Domestic gas exploration policy, (iii) Domestic coal utilization; iv) Energy import) Demand side management and energy conservation, vi) Improved Cooking Stove (ICS); and vii) Energy subsidy and pricing.",""],[1,"380","3","Gas Allocation Policy","it is critical for Bangladesh to establish clear-cut gas allocation policy to best utilize the limited domestic reserve.",""],[1,"380","4","Gas Allocation and Fuel Substitution Policy","policy on how to disseminate gas prepaid meter and LPG should also be defined.",""],[1,"380","5","LPG Promotion in Domestic and CNG Sectors","This figure supports why the Government should implement LPG use particularly in Domestic and CNG sector.",""],[1,"380","6","LPG Price Policy Adjustment","in order to promote the use of LPG, the price policy needs to be adjusted to minimize the difference between LPG and pipelined gas tariffs.",""],[1,"382","5","Energy Subsidy Policy Coordination","Therefore, the Government needs to determine the extent to which Energy Subsidy could be allowed in high priority sectors that also maintains budgetary discipline.",""],[1,"382","5","Energy Pricing Coordination Framework","The subsidy policy will need to be coordinated with pricing of energy products both for fiscal sustainability but also to promote efficient energy use in total as well as by product categories.",""],[1,"383","2","Gas Allocation Policy","Establish Gas Allocation Policy (incl. LPG and Biogas Alternative policy)",""],[1,"383","9","Energy Subsidy Policy Development","Develop Energy Subsidy Policy",""],[1,"383","20","Energy Ministry Technical and Negotiation Capacity Strengthening","improvements are also needed in the technical and negotiation capacity of the Ministry and associated energy agencies","the Ministry and associated energy agencies"],[1,"386","1","Power Sector Reform and Institutional Modernization","Along with greater investment, there has been significant progress with power sector reforms.",""],[1,"388","10","Special Act for Quick Procurement in the Power and Energy Sector","Special Act for Quick Procurement in Power and Energy Sector",""],[1,"394","3","Power System Operation Legal and Regulatory Framework","The detailed legal framework such as rules, regulations or operational manual of the power system operation to realize the aim should be completed quickly and implemented.",""],[1,"395","1","Power Sector Pricing Adjustment and Self-Financing Strategy","So, the pricing strategy for the Seventh Plan should be that along with efficient power generation, pricing will be adjusted to eliminate all operational deficit and generate a surplus such that the sector is able to finance 10-15 percent of its annual investment through own resources.",""],[1,"396","6","Public-Private Partnership Financing for Power Generation","This will be a combination of PPP financing for power generation plus measures to contain energy subsidies.",""],[1,"396","6","Energy Subsidy Reduction and Targeting Reform","This will be a combination of PPP financing for power generation plus measures to contain energy subsidies.",""],[1,"396","6","Electricity Pricing Reform","In power the Government will ensure that the average price of electricity must be at least equal to the average cost of production.",""],[1,"396","7","Power Sector Restructuring and Reform Programme","These include: continue unbundling along the functional line, carry out corporatization of generation and distribution, strengthen generation and distribution companies already in place to improve operating performance and customer satisfaction, implement the power sector restructuring plan; upgrade electricity price gradually to cost level and strengthen BERC to be able to perform its agenda on licensing, energy pricing, quality of utility performance including energy efficiency, and consumer",""]],"177":[[1,"49","15","Peri-Urban Infrastructure and Civic Facilities Investment","Infrastructural investment and civic facilities in peri-urban growth centres especially around Special Economic Zones",""],[1,"54","2","Rural Transformation Support Programme","The rural institutions will be strengthened to support the ongoing rural transformation including support for non-farm job creation, rural mobility, and rural finance along with reducing poverty through undertaking programmes on rural infrastructure, connectivity, water supply and sanitation also with agriculture and employment generation.",""],[1,"55","1","Basic Infrastructure and Essential Services Provision","Provision of adequate and affordable basic infrastructure and services, essential for safeguarding health, safety, welfare and improved living environment of the people, will be an important strategic focus under the 7th Plan.",""],[1,"83","14","Peri-Urban Infrastructure and Civic Facilities Investment","Infrastructural investment and civic facilities in peri-urban growth centres especially around Special Economic Zones",""]],"178":[[1,"234","8","Prison Modernization and Separate Women's Prisons","Under the reformed Prison Code, modernization of prisons and construction of separate prisons for women are undertaken.",""],[1,"234","8","Correctional Education and Skills Training Programme","If the correctional programmes are in place through proper educational campaign and skills trainings to change the attitude of convicts and prisoners under trial, there will be a significant reduction of crime line and they will refrain from stealing, robbery and they would return to normal life and engage themselves in development activities.",""],[1,"234","8","Female Prisoner Rehabilitation and Self-Reliance Activities","Female inmates of these prisons are being engaged in activities to become self-reliant.",""],[1,"234","9","Prison Facilities Improvement","Ensure enhanced facilities for prisoners;",""],[1,"234","10","Prisoner Basic and Professional Training Programme","Impart basic/professional training to prisoners;",""],[1,"234","11","Prison Infrastructure Development","Develop infrastructure of prisons.",""]],"179":[[1,"678","6","Pro-Poor Growth Strategy","For improving poor peoples' access to food, pro-poor growth strategy will have to be pursued.",""],[1,"678","6","Rural Non-Farm Employment Expansion","This calls for increasing employment opportunities, particularly in the rural non-farm sector.",""],[1,"678","6","Food Price Volatility Reduction Measures","Food price volatility will have to be minimized.",""],[1,"679","3","Agro-processing and Small-Scale Rural Enterprise Value Chain Support","In line with the Small and Medium Enterprise (SME) policy, value chain approach will have to be followed by integrating input providers, traders, processors and service producers.",""],[1,"679","4","Support for Income-Generating Activities for Women and Persons with Disabilities","the Government has undertaken numerous development projects such as (i) support to women and the disabled in income generating activities",""],[1,"679","4","Investment in Employment-Enhancing Technology","the Government has undertaken numerous development projects such as (ii) promoting investment in employment enhancing technology",""],[1,"679","4","Incentives for Agro-Based Industry Development","the Government has undertaken numerous development projects such as (iii) providing incentives for development of agro-based industries",""],[1,"679","4","Special Assistance for Rural Industry Expansion","the Government has undertaken numerous development projects such as (iv) special assistance for expansion of rural industries",""],[1,"679","4","Education and Skills Development Programmes","the Government has undertaken numerous development projects such as (v) education and skill development programmes",""],[1,"679","4","Strengthening Implementation and Monitoring of Employment-Generating Activities","Implementation and monitoring of these activities will have to be strengthened to achieve higher income growth from these employment-generating activities",""],[1,"679","4","Expansion of the Employment Generation Programme for the Ultra-Poor","The coverage of the Employment Generation Programme for the Ultra-poor will be enhanced to achieve desired results in this direction",""]],"180":[[1,"716","4","Child Marriage Prevention and Enforcement Measures","The existing age at marriage for girls and boys would be strictly enforced.",""],[1,"716","4","Birth Registration and Child Marriage Act Reform","Compulsory registration after birth of a child will be ensured.",""],[1,"716","4","Civil Society and School Retention Support Against Child Marriage","Civil society movements against child marriage would be strengthened, community orientation improved and support for continuation of education at secondary levels will be ensured to eliminate child marriage.",""]],"181":[[1,"658","3","Bengali Language and Literature Development Programme","Programmes for development of Bengali language and literature and reference books for higher education will be continued with greater emphasis.",""],[1,"659","1","Fine Arts Curriculum Enhancement","To enhance appreciate of fine arts, various subjects will be introduced in primary and secondary level as per education policy.",""],[1,"659","2","Cultural Education and Heritage Support Services","Bangla Academy, Public Library, National Book Centre, National Archives and National Library are responsible for education, research, publishing of books & journals and give support to all categories of readers.",""],[1,"659","4","Bengali Language and Literature Development Initiative","Develop Bengali language and literature and create facilities to develop Bengali as the medium of instruction;",""],[1,"659","5","Quality Book Production and Affordable Publication Support","Help and promote production and publication of quality books and make them available to the masses at reasonable prices;",""],[1,"659","6","National Book Policy Implementation Programmes","Undertake programmes for implementation of the national book policy;",""],[1,"659","9","National-to-Rural Library Network Development","Establish and develop a library network system from the national to the rural level and introduce modern technology to this end;",""],[1,"659","11","Fine and Performing Arts Infrastructure Development","Develop infrastructural facilities for fine and performing arts including drama and theatre and explore private and voluntary involvement in this area;",""],[1,"660","1","Bengali Language, Literature, and Reference Book Development Programme","Programmes for development of Bengali language and literature and reference books for higher education will be continued with greater emphasis;",""],[1,"660","2","Book Development and Reading Habits Programme","Programmes will be undertaken for book development and development of reading habits;",""],[1,"660","4","National to Rural Library Network Development Programme","Programmes will be undertaken to develop library network, infrastructural facilities and services from national to the rural levels in order to meet the education, recreational, cultural and information need of people at all walks of life;",""],[1,"660","10","Fine Arts Introduction in Primary and Secondary Education","Fine arts like music, painting, arts & crafts, recitation, acting; dancing, theatrical performances would be introduced at primary & secondary level as per education policy.",""],[1,"660","12","Arts and Culture Curriculum Support Materials Production","Bangladesh Shilpakala Academy should be equipped to produce a huge numbers of subject oriented texts and teachers for matching with national needs.",""]],"182":[[1,"718","4","Joint Distribution of Khas Land to Spouses","The current practice of distribution of khas land in the name of both spouses would continue.",""],[1,"718","4","Women’s Forestry Co-management Access Expansion","Similarly access to forestry resources through women co- management groups would continue and expand.",""],[1,"718","4","Women’s Inherited Property Rights Promotion and Enforcement","Community orientation on giving women due share of their inherited property is often missing, which would be promoted and enforced.",""],[1,"718","5","Women's Participation in Community Resource Governance","Women's participation in accessing and taking decisions regarding community resources would be ensured by provisions of women's participation under the Social Forestry Rules, Water Management Policy, Forestry Sector Policy, WATSAN Policy and so on.",""],[1,"718","5","Mainstreaming Women's Participation Across Relevant Sectors","Similar practice would be integrated in all relevant sectors.",""],[1,"718","5","Monitoring Women's Participation in Associations and Groups","Women's participation in relevant associations and groups would be ensured and monitored.",""],[1,"719","7","Strengthening Membership in Sectoral Committees and Associations","Memberships in different sectoral committees and associations would be enforced, such as in, water management associations, sanitation committees, water supply committees, which are formed as per the policies/rules for sectoral ministries and agencies.",""]],"183":[[1,"721","4","Positive Portrayal of Women in Media Initiative","Portrayal of women's positive image will be promoted.",""],[1,"721","5","Men's Engagement Programme for Gender Equality","More programmes would include active engagement of men in all spheres to promote women's advancement and curb men's involvement or support of harmful practices.",""],[1,"721","6","Gender Norms Change for Children and Adolescents","Working with children and adolescents to develop norms of more egalitarian relationships:",""],[1,"722","1","Girl-Centred Adolescent Empowerment Programme","Girl-centred programmes equipping adolescent girls with knowledge and skills can build their confidence and contribute to the efforts to end inter-generational poverty, illiteracy, ill health, and gender inequality.",""],[1,"722","3","Joint Gender Equality Advocacy Initiatives","Development and advocacy initiatives on gender equality issues and to form public opinion against harmful practices would be pursued jointly and they should be partners in better delivery of services, especially in rural and remote areas.",""]],"184":[[1,"707","7","Dalit Education Access and Inclusion Measures","The Government will uphold the right to education for children from dalit communities with the expectation to ensure schools becomes non-discriminatory and inclusive spaces for all children.",""],[1,"707","8","Dalit Inclusion and Representation Initiative","Local Government Institutions, i.e. Upazila and Union Parishads, along with NGOs will be involved to locate disadvantaged dalit people and help enable them to participate in development activities.",""],[1,"707","8","Dalit Representation in Political Party Committees","Dalit representation in all committees of political parties at national and local level will be ensured.",""],[1,"707","10","Awareness-Raising Campaign Against Discrimination and Untouchability","Massive awareness raising to stop all kinds of discrimination and untouchability against dalits and excluded communities will be undertaken.",""],[1,"707","11","Special Commission on Dalits","The Government will form a special commission on dalits to evaluate current environment and level of discrimination and provide key recommendations on improving the socio-economic conditions of dalit communities in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"708","1","Capability Enhancement and Confidence Building for Dalit Households","Such affirmative action will be combined with capability enhancement and confidence building, to empower these groups to have a voice and make claims, and an effective grievance mechanism.",""],[1,"708","2","Public Education and Social Accountability for Equity and Inclusion","Massive public education against discrimination and towards equity-inclusion will be promoted, building greater transparency through social audits and public hearings.",""]],"185":[[1,"707","9","Khas Land Allotment for Dalit Settlement","The Ministry of Land will give priority to allotting khas land to people of dalit communities for settlement under the Asrayan type housing project.","Ministry of Land"],[1,"707","9","Land Earmarking for Tea Garden Workers' Housing","For tea garden workers, planters/owners will be encouraged to earmark land within the estates so that they can build their own dwelling.",""],[1,"707","9","Sweeper Colony Construction Programme","Special programmes like construction of sweeper colonies will be implemented.",""],[1,"707","12","Review of Colony Allotment Policy for Marginalized Dalit Groups","The Government will review the allotment policy of colonies under every City Corporation and municipality and ensure that marginalized groups of dalits are allotted harassment free access to electricity, gas and water supply services.",""],[1,"707","13","Preferential Municipal Cleaning Job Access for Dalits","Dalits will be given preferential access to cleaning jobs in municipalities, including lease of public toilets of City Corporations to dalit sweepers.",""],[1,"707","14","Resettlement Support for Evicted Dalit Families","Proper resettlement will be provided for evicted dalit families.",""]],"186":[[1,"7","4","Human Capital Investment in Education and Health","A knowledge based economy will be developed through development of human capital by investing more in education and health sectors.",""],[1,"11","4","Human Capital Investment in Education and Health","A knowledge based economy will be developed through development of human capital by investing more in education and health sectors.",""],[1,"48","4","Increased Funding for Priority Health and Education Programmes","Budgetary allocations to the priority social sector programmes in the health and education sectors will be increased to create better human capital through universal general education, skill development programmes, and greater access to improved public healthcare systems.",""],[1,"49","1","Human Resource Development Investment","Additionally, the public investment programme will emphasize human resource development, enhancing social equity through inclusive growth and ensuring the sustainability of growth through continued macroeconomic stability and protection of the natural environment.",""],[1,"77","7","Reallocation of Budgetary Priorities for Health and Education","a re-examination of budgetary priorities is needed to allocate greater resources for health and education.",""],[1,"78","1","NGO Partnership for Health and Education Service Delivery","Partnership with NGOs could be strengthened to deliver health and education services in the hard-to-reach areas as well as to reach out the socially-excluded groups.",""],[1,"80","5","Equity-Focused Education and Health Spending","the equity aspects of public spending on education and health require considerable effort.",""],[1,"103","3","Human Capital Equality Strategy","An essential precondition for creating such equality of opportunity is to ensure equality in the distribution of human capital.",""],[1,"722","2","Equal Access to Education and Skills for Women","The key areas would be to ensure equal benefit from quality formal education; marketable skills to maximize productivity and potential of women;",""],[1,"722","2","Women's Nutrition and Lifelong Health Care","nutrition and lifelong health care;",""]],"188":[[1,"52","5","Livestock Product Development and Export Promotion","Livestock sub-sector development strategies and policies for 7th FYP includes support for dairy product development, production of better beef breeds and the block Bengal goat for higher meat production, and poultry development for both meat and egg production and finding export markets.",""],[1,"52","5","Fisheries Management and Aquaculture Development","the key elements of the strategy for the Fisheries subsector include improvement and development of open water fisheries management, inland aquaculture through maintaining purity of brood stock of indigenous fish species, shrimp and coastal aquaculture, and that of marine fisheries.",""],[1,"102","8","Expansion of Fishing Areas Using New Technologies and Methods","extending fishing areas using new technologies and methods even beyond EEZ in the international waters,",""],[1,"102","10","Aquaculture and Mariculture Development Initiative","substantially increasing fisheries production and export earnings through improved aquaculture and introduction of mariculture",""]],"189":[[1,"50","13","Multimodal Transport Network Improvement","Improve the multimodal transport network with a significant increase in the share of rail and waterways traffic",""],[1,"52","3","Modern Transport Sector Development","A modern transport sector is also important for the expansion of manufacturing and duly emphasized in the 7th FYP.",""],[1,"53","6","Regional Connectivity and Trans-Asian Highway Support","to promote regional connectivity and support for the Trans-Asian Highway Project;",""],[1,"53","6","River and Rail Transport Expansion","Strengthen the use of river and rail transport to provide a low cost and more environment-friendly alternative to road transport;",""],[1,"84","14","Multimodal Transport Network Improvement","Improve the multimodal transport network with a significant increase in the share of rail and waterways traffic",""],[1,"99","3","Transport Infrastructure Investment and Asset Management","In transport, along with new investments in transport infrastructure based on a careful review of priorities, especially in the neglected area of rail transport, proper management of transport assets and sound urban traffic management will be necessary.",""],[1,"100","2","Transport Infrastructure Cost Recovery Reform","Instituting a proper cost recovery of transport infrastructure will need to be a major element of a sustainable strategy for financing transport infrastructure and proper maintenance.",""]],"190":[[1,"51","12","Governance Reform Strategy for Development Performance","In the 7th Plan, the Government will adopt strategies and policies that are adequately tuned for meeting contemporary challenges with special focus on reforms to improve overall development performance.",""],[1,"78","7","Governance Improvement and Institutional Development Programme","the Sixth Plan adopted a long-term Programme for governance improvement and institutional development.",""],[1,"79","6","Civil Service Merit-Based Promotion and Incentive Reform","Strengthening of civil services with the institution of merit based promotion and improved incentives in terms of remuneration and training facilities",""],[1,"79","10","Anti-Corruption Commission Strengthening","Strengthening the Anti-Corruption Commission in securing better quality investigations and fair resolutions.",""],[1,"80","5","Institutional Strengthening Programme","The Sixth plan's efforts to build important institutions like the local government, the urban institutions, land administration, strengthening of the National Board of Revenue and the Public-Private Partnership require further efforts.",""],[1,"80","5","Judicial and Democratic Institutions Strengthening","The strengthening of the judiciary, the Elections Commission and other democratic institutions are also long-term challenges that will be continued.",""],[1,"80","5","Public Agency Implementation Capacity Building","building implementation capacity in public agencies and ministries requires further efforts.",""]],"191":[[1,"7","3","Policies, Institutions and Programmes for Inclusive Growth and Poverty Reduction","In this regard, the Plan emphasizes on policies, institutions and programmes that will support lowering of income inequality and empowering the citizens.",""],[1,"47","10","Inclusive Growth Strategy","Along with strategies for rapid economic growth of 7% plus, the 7th FYP will ensure that complimentary strategies and policies are in place to make the growth path inclusive, responsive and adaptable to the ongoing transformations, is resilient to climate change and is sustainable over the long term without damaging the natural environment.",""],[1,"47","10","Employment and Labour Force Participation Expansion","It therefore encapsulates a strategy for inclusive growth which empowers people by creating employment opportunities, fostering the scope for greater labour force participation, particularly of women, supporting skill development in response to market demand, enabling access to credit for small and medium enterprises, and improving health and education for people to be more productive.",""],[1,"49","6","Manufacturing Employment Expansion","Creating good jobs for the large pool of under-employed and new labour force entrants by increasing the share of employment in the manufacturing sector from 15 percent to 20 percent",""],[1,"83","5","Manufacturing Employment Expansion Initiative","Creating good jobs for the large pool of under-employed and new labour force entrants by increasing the share of employment in the manufacturing sector from 15 percent to 20 percent",""],[1,"96","5","Manufacturing and Organized Services Growth Shift","The sectoral composition of growth has to change in favour of a much higher share of modern manufacturing and organized services to create a more rapid expansion of good jobs.",""],[1,"96","5","Manufacturing Employment Responsiveness Enhancement","The employment responsiveness of growth in manufacturing needs to increase to absorb more labour.",""],[1,"103","2","Inclusive Growth Strategy","complimentary strategies and policies are in place to make that growth inclusive and sustainable for a long period without damaging the environment.",""],[1,"103","2","Employment and Labour Force Participation Expansion","it therefore encapsulates a strategy for inclusive growth which empowers people by creating employment opportunities, fostering the scope for greater labour force participation, particularly of women, supporting skill development in response to market demand, enabling access to credit for small and medium enterprises, and many other ways for people to be more productive.",""],[1,"103","3","Broad-Based Productive Employment Inclusion","That is why reduction of inequality through broad-based participation in productive employment is one of the pillars on which the growth strategy of the 7th FYP rests.",""],[1,"104","3","Labour Rights Protection and Decent Work Measures","protecting labour rights to organize and strive for decent wages and safe working conditions.",""]],"192":[[1,"57","3","Gender Equality and Women's Empowerment Measures","The objective of 7th FYP regarding gender is to ensure women's advancement as self-reliant human beings and reduce discriminatory barriers by taking both developmental and institutional measures.",""],[1,"57","3","Women's Capability and Access Expansion Strategy","Gender equality and women's empowerment agenda for the 7th FYP is based on pursuing strategies and actions that not only enhance women's capabilities and access to resources and opportunities but also address the barriers in structures and institutions and aim at changing social norms and protecting their rights are critical to integrate within the plan.",""],[1,"57","3","Gender Monitoring and Accountability Mechanism","Establishing monitoring, oversight and accountability mechanisms is equally important.",""],[1,"70","3","Women’s Economic Empowerment and Labour Force Participation Expansion","In the area of economic empowerment progress is ongoing in expanding labour force participation of women.",""],[1,"104","3","Gender Equality in Education and Employment Access","the strengthening of inclusive institutions - pluralistic democracy being one, but many more institutions spread across various sectors such as gender equality in access to education and employment opportunity, social protection schemes for the elderly and disabled, protecting labour rights to organize and strive for decent wages and safe working conditions.",""]],"193":[[1,"57","4","Constitutional Equality and Citizen Empowerment Strategy","The Seventh Plan strategy for inclusion is based on implementation of the Constitution of the People's Republic of Bangladesh, which provides equal rights and opportunities to all citizens irrespective of race, religion, caste, creed or profession.",""],[1,"71","2","Child Focused Budget Pilot","The concept of Child Focused Budget has been introduced and implemented as a pilot in the Ministry of Women and Children Affairs.","Ministry of Women and Children Affairs"],[1,"71","3","Expansion of Basic Social Services for Tribal Population","Efforts are ongoing to expand education, health, social protection and other basic social services to the tribal population.",""],[1,"71","4","Disability Welfare Projects and Services","the Department of Social Services (DSS) has introduced new projects and strengthened existing ones to improve the welfare of PWD.","Department of Social Services (DSS)"],[1,"71","4","Integrated Education Programme for the Visually Impaired","These include the Integrated Education Programme for the Visually Impaired project, the establishment of a hostel for visually impaired children, and the expansion of the PROYASH institute dedicated to the wellbeing of persons and children with special needs.",""],[1,"71","4","One-Stop Service Centers for Persons with Disabilities","various centres were set up to provide one stop services for PWD and mobile physiotherapy with necessary equipment centres have been made available for PWD located in rural areas.",""],[1,"72","2","Strengthen Enforcement of Disability Rights Laws","Additional efforts will be needed on these aspects during the Seventh Plan.",""],[1,"103","3","Equal Opportunity for Disadvantaged Groups","Second, conditions will be created so that people from the currently disadvantaged segments of society are able to seize the opportunities opened up by the growth process-just as much if not more than those coming from the privileged background.",""],[1,"104","3","Inclusive Institutions and Citizens' Empowerment Measures","Accordingly, the 7th FYP endorses the notion of citizens' empowerment as the creation of economic opportunity, the ability to freely choose one's own path in life in accordance with one's distinctive talents and abilities.",""]],"194":[[1,"69","1","Remittance Facilitation through Mobile Banking","To facilitate remittance 27 microfinance institutions have been authorized along with 28 banks through mobile banking.",""],[1,"69","2","Microcredit Expansion and Regulatory Supervision","These programmes have continued to improve access and services during the Sixth Plan.","Bangladesh Bank | Microcredit Regulatory Authority (MRA)"],[1,"69","2","SME Financing Support Policies and Programmes","Policies and programmes for small and medium enterprises (SMEs) were also formulated in 2010 to enhance financing services for SME entrepreneurs.","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"87","2","Extreme Poverty Eradication Strategy","Accordingly, eradication of extreme poverty will be a cardinal principle of the strategies laid out in the 7thFYP document.",""],[1,"103","2","SME Credit Access Support","enabling access to credit for small and medium enterprises",""],[1,"106","1","Structural Transformation for Poverty Reduction","The Seventh Plan will continue this emphasis on structural transformation of the production and employment structures as the fundamental basis for poverty reduction, while complementing this with focused programmes for the poor and extreme poor through facilitating the greater inflow of international remittances, through microcredits, through social security and through better access to health, nutrition, water supply and education services.",""],[1,"110","4","Microcredit Expansion and Strengthening Programme","These programmes will be strengthened and expanded during the Seventh Plan with special focus to less served areas.",""]],"195":[[1,"7","4","ICT Services and Migration for Demographic Dividend","ICT based service sector along with migration will be priority for exploiting the demographic dividend.",""],[1,"11","4","ICT Services and Migration for Demographic Dividend","ICT based service sector along with migration will be priority for exploiting the demographic dividend.",""],[1,"52","2","Service Industry Skills Development","Strengthening the skills base for the service industry;",""],[1,"78","3","Workforce Skills Upgrading and Training Strategy","Greater efforts are needed to learn from the East Asian experiences with training, including stronger partnership with private sector in the design and implementation of training programmes including support for on-the-job training.",""],[1,"78","3","Private Sector Consultation on Training Policy","Consultations with the various chambers of business and commerce on a training strategy and associated policies can be a useful first step.",""],[1,"102","16","Marine Academy Establishment in Khulna","establishment of marine academy in Khulna may be considered.",""],[1,"103","2","Skills Development Aligned with Market Demand","supporting skill development in response to market demand",""]],"196":[[1,"119","5","Industrial Environmental Sustainability Compliance","Both leather and RMG (wet processing washing and dyeing) sectors-considered to be two most important industrial polluters -- would also need to ensure environmental sustainability for their continued growth over the medium and long term.",""],[1,"119","5","Industrial Standards Compliance for Chemical Use and Water Efficiency","These industries must meet global industrial standards in terms of chemical use and discharge and efficient water use for their growth to be sustainable both from Bangladesh and importing countries' perspectives.",""]],"197":[[1,"121","9","Exchange Rate and Monetary Policy for External Sector Stability","Bangladesh Bank in its recent Monetary Policy Statements aimed to use exchange rate and monetary policies for the purpose of preserving external sector stability, maintaining satisfactory building up reserves and avoiding excessive volatility of the exchange rate.","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"121","10","Foreign Exchange Market Dollar Absorption","Bangladesh Bank continued to absorb the excess dollars from the market to maintain exchange rate stability in nominal terms.",""],[1,"122","1","Liquidity Sterilization through Bangladesh Bank Bonds","BB had to mop up the excess liquidity by issuing Bangladesh Bank bonds at appropriate market interest rates.",""],[1,"122","3","Flexible Exchange Rate Management","Certainly, the nominal exchange rate will also be managed flexibly taking into account export competitiveness and Bangladesh's inflation rate differential with its trading partners.",""],[1,"127","8","Positive Real Deposit Interest Rate Policy","banks will continue to offer at least marginally positive real interest rates to the depositors.",""],[1,"127","8","Inflation Reduction Effort","Bangladesh bank will continue its efforts to reduce inflation further to ensure a sustained lowering of the structure of deposit and lending rates.","Bangladesh bank"],[1,"129","8","Prudent Macroeconomic Management and Economic Reform Acceleration","The Government will remain vigilant about the emerging external and domestic risks, and will continue to pursue prudent macroeconomic management and accelerate the pace of economic reforms as envisaged under the Plan.",""],[1,"129","8","Corrective Policy Adjustment Mechanism","The Government is also committed to undertake corrective actions and policy adjustments to mitigate the adverse effect of any unforeseen developments.",""],[1,"178","4","Monetary-Fiscal Coordination for Domestic Borrowing Management","it will require better coordination between monetary and fiscal policy in order to avoid any potential scope for crowding out of private sector credit.",""]],"198":[[1,"127","2","Treasury Bills and Bond Market Development","Development of the treasury bills and bond market will be keys to enhancing the transmission mechanism and effectiveness of monetary policy.",""],[1,"128","3","Financial Inclusion and Market Deepening Measures","The government will strive for expanding access to financial services to the underserved including micro and household enterprises now operating in the informal market and deepen the financial markets with introducing relevant products.",""],[1,"128","3","Core Banking Solution Rollout","Core Banking Solution (CBS) will be introduced in all state owned commercial and specialized banks within 2006.",""],[1,"128","3","Real Time Gross Settlement System Establishment","Real Time Gross Settlement (RTGS) system will established for the banking sector very soon.",""],[1,"128","3","Separate Clearing Corporation for Securities Settlement","The Bangladesh Securities Exchange Commission will establish a separate clearing corporation for the speedy settlement after trade.",""],[1,"128","3","Microfinance Credit Information Bureau Establishment","A separate Credit Information Bureau (CIB) for microfinance will be established.",""],[1,"142","9","Microcredit Expansion and Support Programme","The further expansion of micro-credit will be yet another priority.",""],[1,"156","2","SME Low-Cost Financing Support","Small and medium enterprises would be encouraged with low cost financing facilities.",""],[1,"156","4","Special Priority Agricultural Credit and Subsidy Programme for Lagging Districts","Rural areas of lagging districts would get special priority in agricultural credit disbursement and agricultural subsidy Programme.",""],[1,"156","5","Microfinance Incentives for Poor Districts","Microfinance institutions would be encourage to operate in poverty prone areas by providing special incentives, e.g. providing fund to MFIs at low rate of interest if they disburse this fund in poor districts.",""],[1,"156","6","Microfinance Expansion in Environmentally Vulnerable Areas","Policy measures be taken to attract microfinance in environmentally vulnerable areas such as cyclone prone coastal areas, land locked and other flood prone areas and disaster prone areas.",""],[1,"156","12","Special Financing Scheme for Prospective Migrants from Lagging Districts","Special financing scheme should be directed towards prospective migrants form lagging districts.",""]],"199":[[1,"142","7","Higher GDP Growth Path and Structural Transformation Strategy","emphasis will be placed to break out of the 6 percent growth GDP growth path of the Sixth Plan and move on to the 7 percent plus growth path with a view to achieving the 8 percent growth by the end of the Seventh Plan.",""],[1,"142","7","Higher Income Job Creation in Manufacturing and Formal Services","These will create the basis for higher income job creation in manufacturing and formal services as in the Sixth Plan but with more intensity.",""],[1,"142","8","Worker Service Export Expansion for Remittance Growth","Continued emphasis on worker service exports in order to increase the inflow of remittances with efforts to expand the opportunities to less served areas.",""],[1,"142","10","Rural ICT Expansion for Economic Inclusion","This ICT revolution will be strengthened further during the Seventh Plan with positive benefits for the rural poor.",""],[1,"142","11","Non-Farm Rural Employment Promotion","The combination of continued emphasis on food productivity, agricultural diversification, remittances, microcredits and ICT services will create the basis for growth of non-farm rural jobs in trading,",""],[1,"156","3","Agro-processing and Non-farm Economic Development in Lagging Districts","Special emphasis has to be given to development of agro-processing, non-farm economic activities in the laggard districts.",""],[1,"156","7","Non-Farm Economic Activities Promotion in Lagging Districts","Non-farm economic activities would be promoted in the lagging districts through providing training and financing facilities.",""],[1,"156","7","Government-MFI/NGO Partnership Building for Non-Farm Development","Partnership building between the government and MFIs/NGOs can play an important role in this regard.",""],[1,"213","17","Entrepreneur Training, Workshop, and Mobilization Support","1 per cent of Annual Development Programme (ADP) is invested by the Government together with funding from the DC offices for entrepreneur training, workshop and mobilization.",""]],"200":[[1,"157","2","Development of Stress-Tolerant Agricultural Seeds","To minimize the impact, investment has to be made on the development of new agricultural seeds that would be stress tolerant and be able to grow in such inclement conditions.",""],[1,"157","4","Disaster Victim Shelter Centre Investment","It is necessary to invest and build more centres where the victims can take shelters.",""],[1,"157","5","Agricultural Drought Support for North Western Districts","So these districts should be prioritized to get help in terms of inputs (e.g. irrigation, etc.) for agriculture that would help them to tackle droughts.",""]],"201":[[1,"157","6","Integrated Enclave Area Infrastructure Development","These people need to be mainstreamed with the national wider economy by developing physical infrastructures including educational and health facilities.",""],[1,"157","6","Special Social Protection for Enclave Residents","In the 7th Plan, special social protection programmes would be taken to alleviate sufferings these people and thereby improve their living status.",""],[1,"157","6","Special Welfare Measures for Former Enclave Communities","The relevant implementing ministries/division will take special measures specifically directed for improving the welfare of the people of these erstwhile enclaves during 7th plan period.",""]],"202":[[1,"186","6","Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics Strengthening Initiative","Under the Seventh Plan time interval, the Government will offer greater effort to generate high quality data in a timely fashion by strengthening the capacity and scope of BBS.",""],[1,"187","1","National Strategy for the Development of Statistics Implementation","Hence, under the Seventh Plan time interval, continuous effort will be given to implement policies identified within the NSDS report.",""],[1,"187","1","Expanded Statistical Data Collection for Monitoring and Evaluation","More specifically, greater efforts will be given to strengthen data collection in a few major areas that are particularly important to support an M&E effort: special surveys to supplement HIES at a more frequent interval (ideally on a yearly basis), national accounts and budget data at a district level, data on private investment, data on capital stock, data on selected indicators of governance.",""],[1,"187","2","Small-Scale Interim Survey and Monitoring System","BBS will undertake small scale surveys for enabling regular and frequent monitoring and evaluation exercise.",""],[1,"187","3","Quarterly GDP Data Production by BBS","the GoB will dedicate resources to ensure that BBS produce GDP data on a quarterly basis at both the district and national level.",""],[1,"187","6","Upazila-Level Poverty Data Generation and Poverty Map Updating","Poverty data at the Upazila level will be generated every two years so that authorities can monitor regional disparity on a timely basis and also effectively evaluate how poverty alleviating policies are functioning.",""]],"203":[[1,"160","3","Annual Budget and ADP Synchronization","Annual Budget and ADP ought to be synchronized to use them as tools for achieving the objective of the plan.",""],[1,"202","2","Sectoral Strategy Alignment and Investment Prioritization","the sectoral strategies, policies and programmes must not only be consistent with national targets for growth, employment and poverty reduction but also that sectoral investment requirements add up to the available resources.",""],[1,"202","2","Development of Sectoral Strategies Aligned to the Seventh Plan","developing the proper sectoral strategies that are best aligned to the themes and objectives of the Seventh Plan is of critical importance.",""],[1,"202","3","Public Investment Classification Synchronization","This mismatch between the two approaches for Public Investment Management (PIM) needs to be synchronized for ensuring efficient use of public resources.","Ministry of Finance | Ministry of Planning"],[1,"203","1","Sector Strategy and Plan Preparation","the Government intends to prepare Sector Strategy/Plan for each of these fourteen sectors.",""],[1,"212","1","Sector Strategy Papers Formulation","The Government has decided to formulate 'Sector Strategy Papers (SSP)' for each of the major sector within its scope.",""],[1,"212","3","Planning and Budgeting Linkage Strengthening","Progress has been made in strengthening the link between planning and budgeting through the Sixth Plan as well as through the Annual Development Programmes that are now much better linked to both the Sixth Plan strategies and targets as well as to the MTBF of line Ministries.",""],[1,"212","3","Medium-Term Budget Framework Implementation","The MTBF implementation is well underway and steady progress has been achieved.",""]],"204":[[1,"199","5","Parliamentary Standing Committee Oversight Hearings","Ministry oversight hearings held by the Parliamentary Standing Committees regularly",""],[1,"211","4","Strengthening of the Grievance Redress System","to improve the process further and strengthen the Grievance Redress System (GRS) as an effective instrument, a separate branch has been introduced recently in the Cabinet Division.","Cabinet Division"],[1,"214","3","Parliamentary Transparency and Oversight Strengthening Measures","(a) Increasing the number of hearings open to the public, particularly of important budgetary committees such as the Public Accounts Committee; (b) promoting standards for policy debate, in terms of allowing time and space for parliament (and if possible experts and other stakeholders such as prominent think tanks) to give opinions on policies, with the public generally informed regarding these processes; (c) developing mechanisms to ensure timely responses to recommendations from the Public Accounts Committee, and providing easily accessible and comprehensible data for the public, including a progress report from the PAC; and (d) building on the existing capacity of the Parliamentary Secretariat, and ensure effective implementation of the Parliament Secretariat Act 1994 & Rules.",""]],"205":[[1,"211","5","Public Awareness and Education on Preventive Measures","The Government has taken measures to create public awareness and education in preventive measures, creating the right conditions for the public sector to enhance public service delivery.",""],[1,"211","5","ACC Youth Engagement Committees","ACC is also creating committees to work with young people, but still requires much broader effort.",""]],"206":[[1,"215","2","NGO Service Delivery Partnership","The outreach of NGOs in the delivery of a wide range of services including education, health, training, women's empowerment, micro-credits, climate change and social protection has continued to blossom.",""],[1,"215","2","Partnership with Private Research Institutions","The Government has also established good partnership with a number of private research institutions to strengthen macroeconomic management and policy making.",""]],"207":[[1,"228","11","RTI Data Tracking System Enhancement","Increase its ability to track data at different levels (national, district & upazila) on RTI applications, responses, appeals and decisions.",""],[1,"228","12","Proactive Disclosure Policy Adoption","Enhance proactive disclosure through the adoption of proactive disclosure policies by different ministries, particularly those that enjoy a high level of Government-citizen interface.",""],[1,"229","1","Target-Group Communication Strategy Development","Undertake an audience (e.g., farmers, women, students, and people with disabilities) survey & analysis to identify a target-group specific communication strategy.",""],[1,"229","2","Public Awareness Partnership for RTI Act","Establish partnerships with civil society organizations and media to promote public awareness of RTI Act.",""],[1,"229","4","RTI Strategic Partnership Facilitation","Facilitate RTI strategic partnerships among different stakeholders (e.g., IC, Ministry of Information, different line Ministries, District administration, civil society organizations & private sector entities).","Ministry of Information"],[1,"229","5","Civil Servant Capacity Building Programme","Promote capacity building of civil servants, particularly the Designated Officers, through traditional and on-line means.",""],[1,"229","6","Government Record Management System Reform","Initiate legislative & policy changes in order to establish record management systems among Government agencies in relation to the RTI Act.",""],[1,"230","7","E-Governance Transformation Initiative","Thus, in this section, we summarize the core areas that will receive intervention under the Seventh Plan, which are:",""],[1,"230","8","RTI Portal Update and Mobile Access Expansion","Under the Seventh Plan, the Government will ensure that the RTI-based portals in all 25,000 offices of the Government offices are updated regularly and information is accessible through mobile phones and service access points.",""],[1,"230","8","Whole-of-Government Service Delivery Dashboards","In particular, a whole-of- Government approach will be adopted to set up electronic dashboards with administrative alerts across all ministries, directorates, districts, upazilas and union parishads, in order to monitor the speed and quality of service delivery.",""],[1,"230","8","Citizen Information and Forms Accessibility Strategy","The Govt. will undertake a comprehensive strategy so that maximum amount of information as well as forms, applications, and other documentation are available to citizens.",""],[1,"230","9","Expansion of Service Access Points","Thus, under the Seventh Plan, the Government will increase the number of service access points by",""],[1,"231","1","Expansion of Government E-Services via Mobile Phones","within the duration of the Seventh Plan, it is expected that more than half of the critical Government services will be made available over mobile phones",""],[1,"231","2","Expansion of E-Filing Across Government Offices","under the Seventh Plan, this system will be expanded to all offices of the Government",""],[1,"231","2","Integrated Government Human Resource and Payroll Management System","management systems for human resources, payroll, leave, study tour, and training management will be integrated with e-Filing to broaden and deepen administrative efficiency in Government organizations",""],[1,"231","3","E-Participation and Social Media Engagement Initiative","The Government will use the ever deepening presence of social media to increase G2C and C2G interactions, which will allow the Government to closely connect with the citizens.",""],[1,"231","3","Formalization of the UDC Blog Grievance Platform","lessons from such a virtual platform will be further formalized within the Government structure to mitigate social injustices.",""],[1,"231","4","Judiciary and Public Records Digitization Initiative","The Govt. has already taken an initiative for digitization of Bangladesh Supreme courts.",""],[1,"231","5","Digital Land Management System Expansion","The existing initiative for digital land management system will be replicated all over the country to remove all the constraints/barriers regarding transaction of land for economic development.",""],[1,"231","6","ICT Capacity Building for Public Officials","The Government will continue to expand the existing capacity building measures of officials at all levels.",""],[1,"231","7","Technology Transfer Partnership Building","The Government will build partnership with NGOs, Multinational Companies, and donors so that greater technology transfer is facilitated.",""],[1,"282","11","Automated IP System for Public Service Delivery","Better Public Service Delivery through Automated IP System.",""]],"208":[[1,"231","8","Public Order and Domestic Security Maintenance","The Government will continue its endeavour to maintain public order and ensure the security of assets and lives of the citizens while they will be empowered during the seventh five year plan period.","Ministry of Home Affairs (MoHA)"],[1,"231","8","Domestic and Border Security Operations","Ensuring domestic security, ensuring border security and maintaining the economic & commercial interest, combating narcotics, ensuring security and rehabilitation of prisoners are the major goals of the agencies of MoHA.","Ministry of Home Affairs (MoHA)"],[1,"231","8","Security Support for Economic Activities","The different agencies under the Ministry of Home Affairs will play the major role to ensure the safety and security of the economic activities envisaged in the Plan.","Ministry of Home Affairs"],[1,"231","8","Home Affairs Policy, Programme, and Project Initiatives","Ministry of Home Affairs initiates different policies, programmes and projects","Ministry of Home Affairs"],[1,"232","2","Community Policing and Public Awareness for Counter-Terrorism","Bangladesh Police is holding regular public awareness-building activities in order to curb terrorism and militancy by means of community policing.",""],[1,"232","2","Industrial Police Security and Order Maintenance","The Industrial Police is playing active and fruitful roles in maintaining a stable and industry-friendly atmosphere in the industrial areas.",""],[1,"232","2","River Police Inland Waterway Security Operations","the River Police is working relentlessly while the Special Security and Protection Battalions are ensuring the security of VIPs and important installations.",""],[1,"232","2","Tourist Safety and Security Awareness Programme","the Tourist Police is engaged in maintaining safety and security of tourists and tourist spots through mass awareness programme with a view to making Bangladesh a tourist-friendly country.",""],[1,"232","2","Secure Investment Climate Support by Bangladesh Police","In the 7th plan period Bangladesh Police will play pivotal role for ensuring the secured investment climate by providing quality service to the citizens and the investors.",""],[1,"232","3","Police ICT Connectivity and Data Sharing System","the Government will undertake specific activities on various dimensions, which are: (i) Connectivity: measures will be taken to allow police to exchange and share data both vertically and horizontally in a secured and dependable manner",""],[1,"232","3","Police ICT Literacy and Skills Building Programme","(ii) ICT skill building: IT literacy will be provided to constables and all officers who are ASI or of superior rank",""],[1,"232","3","Automated Complaint Information Management System","(iii) ICT skill building: Information management: A uniform system will be developed where all details of the complaint will be recorded",""],[1,"232","3","Police Crime Data Management and MIS Upgrade","(iv) Crime fighting: The Government will improve management information system (MIS) and crime data management system (CDMS) across all district and divisional headquarters so that police forces can coordinate activities concerning crime prevention and prosecution",""],[1,"232","3","ICT-Enabled Citizen Police Services","(v) Citizens' services: Citizens' access to police services starting with access to police stations to lodge complaints regarding violation of rights will be strengthened using ICT",""],[1,"232","3","Cybercrime Prevention and Prosecution Capacity Programme","(VI) Cybercrime prevention and prosecution: The law enforcing agencies would adopt programmes to enhance their capacity in preventing and prosecuting cybercrimes and protecting citizens from breach of privacy, security and fraudulent activities",""],[1,"233","1","Border Security Infrastructure Expansion","Protection of international boundary between Bangladesh, India and Myanmar through increasing number border out posts (BOP) and construction of border ring road and barbed wire fencing;",""],[1,"233","2","Anti-Smuggling Operation","Carry out anti-smuggling operation;",""],[1,"233","4","Internal Security Support for Regular Agencies","To assist regular agencies to maintain internal security.",""],[1,"233","6","Port, Harbour, and Offshore Installation Safety and Security Measures","To ensure safety and security of the ports, harbours, seafarers including water craft and offshore installations within areas of jurisdiction.",""],[1,"233","11","Rural Police Support for Law and Order","To assist Police in maintaining Law and Order in rural level ensuring the secured rural development.",""],[1,"235","4","National Telecommunication Monitoring Centre","National Tele-communication Monitoring Centre (NTMC) is a newly established Govt. Organization under Ministry of home Affairs.","Ministry of home Affairs"],[1,"235","5","Monitoring Facility for Law Enforcement Agencies","Provide effective and latest monitoring facility to all law enforcing agencies in order to ensure national stability and security:",""],[1,"235","6","NTMC Infrastructure and Security Facilities","Provide necessary infrastructural facilities to accommodate all major components of NTMC like data centre, monitoring station and physical security measures;",""],[1,"235","7","IT Expert Training for Telecommunications Threats","Breeding and grooming necessary IT experts to deal with emerging threats from telecommunication sectors.",""]],"209":[[1,"233","13","Firefighting and Rescue Operations Capacity Enhancement","Fire Service and Civil Defence department will ensure the public safety by firefighting and carrying out rescue operation during any man-made or natural disaster with its trained human resources and modern equipment & communication system.",""],[1,"233","14","Industrial Fire Response Time Improvement","Timely response in any fire call, reaching scene of incident and starting firefighting within 10 minutes of fire break-out in industrial areas, especially garments localized areas to ensure safety of the workers and properties of garments and other industries.",""],[1,"234","1","Modern Training Academy for Fire and Urban Search and Rescue Volunteers","To establish Modern Training Academy for Fire and Urban Search & Rescue Volunteers to reduce the loss of lives and properties.",""]],"210":[[1,"246","5","Long-Term Investment-Friendly Policy for Electrical and Electronics Industry","What is needed is a long term investment friendly policy.",""],[1,"246","5","Central Testing Facility for Electrical Goods","The setting up of a central testing facility for electrical goods to allow standardization of products, along with skill training to workers, research and development, provision of interactive linkages with foreign industrial associations for collaboration and marketing and creation of public awareness in favour of manufacturing SMEs will go a long way in development of this particular industry.",""],[1,"246","5","Worker Skills Training, Research and Development, and SME Awareness Support","The setting up of a central testing facility for electrical goods to allow standardization of products, along with skill training to workers, research and development, provision of interactive linkages with foreign industrial associations for collaboration and marketing and creation of public awareness in favour of manufacturing SMEs will go a long way in development of this particular industry.",""],[1,"246","5","International Industrial Association Linkages for Collaboration and Marketing","The setting up of a central testing facility for electrical goods to allow standardization of products, along with skill training to workers, research and development, provision of interactive linkages with foreign industrial associations for collaboration and marketing and creation of public awareness in favour of manufacturing SMEs will go a long way in development of this particular industry.",""],[1,"248","6","Shipbuilding Industry Development Support","the shipbuilding industry is expected to do the same but in less time (10 years) given that proper facilities and policies for ensuring compliance with international standards in terms of ship quality, worker safety and environmental pollution; attracting FDI; and provision of a strong network of backward linkages industries are provided towards its development.",""],[1,"248","6","Intermediate Financing Support for Shipbuilding","More importantly, the biggest constraint, that of costly intermediate financing needs to be addressed.",""],[1,"258","4","Technical Curriculum Restructuring and Training Institution Upgrading","there is a critical need to restructure curriculum at degree and diploma levels for all technical courses along with the up-gradation of industrial training institutions.",""],[1,"258","4","Demand-Driven Technical Training Centres through PPP and Private Sector Initiatives","The strategy has to be pursued vigorously through PPP and private sector initiatives to operate demand driven technical training centres with public institutions managing quality control and accreditation system with the result that centres of manufacturing technology excellence would be created.",""],[1,"258","4","Industrial Research and Development Investment","Investing in R&D to innovate new technology or processes is also critical.",""],[1,"258","4","Global Technology Acquisition Fund","Government will consider setting up a \"Global Technology Acquisition fund\" to enable Bangladesh industries to acquire very high technology knowledge base.",""],[1,"258","4","Manufacturing Product Design and Supply Chain R&D Development","A paradigm shift in manufacturing sector can be achieved through development of R&D of product design geared to supply chain management and customer relations.",""],[1,"258","4","Export Competitiveness Action Group","Representatives from FBCCI, MCCI, BGMEA, BKMEA, and other stakeholders could form an action group to take this agenda forward.",""],[1,"280","5","Demand-Driven Vocational Training Promotion","steps have been taken in recent years, through business associations, and public-private partnerships to raise awareness on the need for creating demand-driven vocational training",""],[1,"280","5","In-House Training Model Replication in Manufacturing","the RMG sector model of in- house training provides a good approach that could be emulated in other manufacturing sector",""],[1,"281","6","National Certification Marks Scheme for Bangladesh Standards","The institute will oversee the Implementation of Bangladesh Standards through a national certification marks Scheme Promotion of quality control, ensuring compliance of products with the Bangladesh Standards, for local consumption as well as for exports.",""],[1,"281","6","Periodic Review and Updating of Standards","Emphasis will be laid also on periodic review of standards to keep them at par with updated technological developments and establishment of food, cement, bricks and gold testing laboratories, standardization and labelling of energy efficient electrical appliances & equipment of selected 6 BRESL products.",""],[1,"281","6","Development of Policies, Rules, Regulations and Criteria for Standards Implementation","To this end, all policies, rules, regulations and criteria are being developed taking cognizance of relevant internationally available documents.",""],[1,"281","6","Expansion of BSTI Regional Certification Centres","BSTI activities should be spread throughout the country starting with establishment of regional certification centres.",""],[1,"281","6","Strengthening BSTI Technical Capacity","In order to strengthen technical capacity of BSTI, additional trained manpower including appropriate lab facilities will be created during the plan period.",""],[1,"282","2","BITAC Mid-Level Technological Development Initiative","BITAC aims to attain mid-level technological development for Bangladesh.",""],[1,"282","2","BIM Capacity Development and Modern Training Complex","BIM's main focus is making skill development up to international standard through the strengthening and capacity development of BIM by constructing modern training complex with new generation facilities ready for accommodating management development activities.",""],[1,"282","3","Amendment of Bangladesh Steel and Engineering Corporation Laws and Rules","Amendment of laws & rules of Bangladesh Steel & Engineering Corporation is a strategy of BSEC, followed by establishment of agro-machineries factory in 15.42 Acre land acquired and owned by BSEC at Chhoypukuria in Bogra district.",""],[1,"282","7","Laboratory Accreditation to ISO/IEC 17025","Accreditation of qualified testing and calibration laboratories according to ISO/IEC 17025.",""],[1,"282","8","Assessor Pool Training and Supervision","Strengthening Assessor pool through proper training and supervision.",""],[1,"282","10","Accreditation of Certification, Inspection, and Medical Testing Bodies","Accreditation of Certification Bodies and Inspection Bodies and Accreditation of Medical testing laboratories (ISO 15189).",""],[1,"282","17","New Boiler Registration","New Boiler Registration.",""]],"211":[[1,"274","5","TCB Market Intervention and Capacity Expansion","To increase TCB's market intervention and institutional capacity for raising working capital to procure essential commodities with cheaper price, expansion of infrastructure and facilities like Warehouses, Cold Storage and Service Centres etc. to store buffer stocks, are crucial.","Ministry of Commerce"]],"212":[[1,"274","6","Tea Sector Productivity Enhancement and Replanting Programme","BTB has targeted to produce 100.00 million kg by 2025 by enhancing tea productivity up to 1500kg/hectare, new planting, replanting tea and optimal utilization of land.",""]],"213":[[1,"300","15","Security Forces Recruitment and Training Upgrade","Upgrading security forces through new intakes and training.",""]],"214":[[1,"303","3","Time-Bound Zoning Law Compliance Enforcement","This matter needs urgent attention and resolution through a time-bound implementation.",""],[1,"307","4","Education Accreditation Policy","Accreditation policies to ensure minimum quality standards in education.",""],[1,"307","5","Health Practitioner and Private Facility Licensing","Licensing of health practitioners and private hospitals/clinics/labs to ensure health safety and acceptable standards.",""],[1,"307","6","Food Vendor Licensing for Sanitation and Health Safety","Licensing of food vendors in hotels, restaurants and other commercial food vendors to ensure sanitation and health safety standards.",""],[1,"307","12","Commercial Zoning and Parking Regulation Enforcement","Enforcement of proper zoning laws for all commercial enterprises and strict implementation of parking regulations for all vehicles.",""],[1,"307","15","Public Regulatory Compliance and Self-Regulation Enforcement System","The implementation of these regulations will require proper education through mass media as well as cooperation with the private enterprises.",""],[1,"307","15","Online Licensing Administration and Complaint Registry","all licensing requirements will be administered online with established timelines for responses.",""],[1,"307","15","Regulatory Staff Capacity Building and Discipline Enforcement","Staff of public regulatory agencies will be enhanced as necessary and will be given necessary training.",""]],"215":[[1,"306","4","Education and Training Quality Upgrade","The policies and investments to upgrade education and training quality, including the emphasis on expanding tertiary education reviewed in Part 2, Chapter 11 will also benefit the service sector.",""],[1,"306","4","Export-Oriented Services Capability Upgrade Initiatives","there are some additional and more focused initiatives that will be needed to upgrade the capabilities in export -oriented services like aviation, international shipping, tourism and ICT.",""],[1,"306","5","Apprenticeship Programme Strengthening","To facilitate on-the-job training, apprenticeship programme will be strengthened.",""],[1,"306","5","Overseas Apprenticeship Expansion","In this context, apprenticeship at overseas need to be pursued.",""],[1,"306","5","Specialized Non-Traditional Skills Training Centres","Specialized non-traditional skill base training centres (e.g. catering, hospitability) will be established.",""],[1,"306","5","Regulatory Simplification for International Technical Experts","The Government will review regulatory policies to promote these partnership arrangements including further simplifying work permits, visa requirements, security clearances etc. of international technical experts.",""],[1,"306","6","Science and Technology Centres of Excellence Support","The Government will support the growth of centres of excellence in science and technology through grants and PPP initiative.",""],[1,"306","6","Expanded Public R&D Investment","The Government will also expand the spending on R&D for the economy that will support the growth of scientific education and research.",""],[1,"306","6","IT Graduate Expansion Plan","Additionally, a long term plan will be undertaken so that current supply of 5,000 yearly IT graduates can be doubled in next 2-3 years.",""],[1,"306","6","IT Education Expansion in National University Colleges","To facilitate this, colleges under national universities will be required to start IT education.",""],[1,"306","6","Education Loan and Scholarship Support for IT Enrolment","Also, special education loan policy and scholarship programmes will be designed to encourage students for IT education enrolment.",""],[1,"306","6","Industry Participation in Academic Programmes","More industry involvement will be ensured during academic programmes.",""]],"216":[[1,"311","3","Migrant-Sensitive Health Policy Review","Bangladesh would take steps to: (i) review existing policies to promote migrant-sensitive health policies and public health strategies;",""],[1,"311","3","Migrant Health Integration in National Health Information System","consider migrants' health in the national health information system;",""],[1,"311","3","Migrant Health Data Collection and Analysis System","collect, standardize and analyse qualitative and quantitative information in relation to migrants' health for policymaking;",""],[1,"311","3","Migrant Health Knowledge Sharing Platform","gather, document and share information and best practices for meeting migrants' health needs in countries of origin or return, transit and destination;",""],[1,"311","3","Equitable Migrant Health Access and Care","ensure equitable access to health, disease prevention and care for migrants and their families without discrimination;",""],[1,"311","3","Capacity Building for Migrant Health Service Providers","build capacity, guidance and set standards for service providers and professionals promoting cultural and gender sensitivity to deal with migrants' health issues;",""],[1,"311","3","Bilateral and Multilateral Cooperation on Migrant Health","promote bilateral and multilateral cooperation on migrants' health among countries involved in the whole process of migration.",""],[1,"311","4","Migrant Legal and Social Protection Measures","Measures to ensure international and internal migrants' access to legal and social protection; strict contract monitoring; and adequate outreach, follow-up and support (shelter, legal and psychosocial support) need to be put in place.",""],[1,"311","4","Internal Female Migrant Skills and Decent Work Support","The needs of internal female migrants in terms of skills development, access to decent work and justice should also be taken into account in relevant sectoral policies.",""]],"217":[[1,"317","5","Technology and Mechanized Cultivation Expansion","Expand application of technology and mechanized cultivation.",""],[1,"324","3","Agricultural Mechanization Expansion","Rapid expansion of mechanization is needed due to the dearth of animal draft power, dearth of farm labours along with increasing wages, and declining interest of young people in traditional agriculture.",""],[1,"324","4","Solar-Powered Irrigation Research","In BARI, research on the use of solar panel to generate power for irrigation is in progress.",""],[1,"324","4","Agro-Related Metal Industries Development","promotion and development of agro-related metal industries to provide support to agricultural production is a major concern.",""],[1,"324","4","Selective Agricultural Mechanization and Solar Power Use","Selective mechanization based on traditional devices, with strong emphasis on wider use of solar power, conducive to productivity will be adopted.",""],[1,"324","4","Public-Private Agricultural Technology Development Partnership","emphasis will have to be given to the collaborative role of public and private sectors in technology development and its diffusion.",""],[1,"324","4","Private Agricultural Equipment Research and Patent Support","Private sector may also be encouraged to develop research facility for agricultural equipment/tools development and allowed for marketing with patent rights.",""],[1,"331","6","Agricultural Farm Mechanization Promotion","The Government will, of course, have to play its pro-active role in popularizing the use of selected demand-led agricultural tools and machinery, and facilitating use of renewable energy including solar power in agriculture production.",""],[1,"333","12","Agricultural Mechanization Promotion","Promote mechanization of farming operations;",""]],"218":[[1,"346","2","Comprehensive Marine Fisheries Conservation and Management Plan","In order to establish a comprehensive plan for sustainable conservation, management and exploitation of resources from the sovereign marine waters the present status of fisheries resources and its future potential for the national economy needs to be framed out.",""],[1,"350","10","National Marine Fisheries Policy Formulation","Formulation of National Marine Fisheries Policy during the 7th Plan",""],[1,"350","11","Resource Poaching and Illegal Foreign Trawler Control","Restrict and control pouching of resources and illegal entry of foreign trawlers",""],[1,"350","12","Conservation Needs Identification and Monitoring Framework","Identify conservation needs and methods that can be effectively administered and regularly monitored",""],[1,"350","13","Coastal Encroachment and Regulation Enforcement Cooperation","Cooperate with the Coast Guard and Navy on the control of encroachment and breach of regulation, also by local vessels.",""],[1,"350","14","Institutional Capacity Building and MCS Strengthening in the Bay of Bengal","Institutional capacity building of the concerned agencies, strengthening of monitoring, Control and Surveillance System (MCS) in the Bay of Bengal.",""],[1,"350","15","Marine Aquaculture Seed Technology Development","Promote development of technology for production of seed for culturing marine fish, and seaweed.",""],[1,"350","16","Collaborative Distant Water Fishing Initiative","Collaborative effort for distant water fishing (beyond 200 miles of EEZ and Area Beyond National Jurisdiction (ABNJ)) to explore and exploit tuna and large pelagic fishes.",""]],"219":[[1,"346","4","National Shrimp Policy Implementation","The implementation of National Shrimp Policy",""],[1,"349","10","Zoned Coastal Shrimp Farming Development","Government defined shrimp farming zones in the coastal region based on natural advantages of shrimp and prawn farming with restitution of water management infrastructure in each zone to optimize production and environmental sustainability.",""],[1,"350","2","Specific Pathogen Free Shrimp Introduction Facilitation","Introduction of Specific Pathogen Free (SPF) shrimp by private sector, which is duly facilitated by the government.",""],[1,"350","3","Shrimp Parent Stock Conservation and PL Quality Certification","Conservation of shrimp and prawn parent stock and their harvest by stress-free trawling, transportation and rearing in the hatcheries will be facilitated.","DoF"],[1,"350","4","Control of PL Imports and Illegal Border Trading","Import of both golda and bagda PL will be controlled, including illegal border trading.",""],[1,"350","6","Contract Growing Support for Shrimp Farmers","Community organizations of shrimp farmers and other primary stakeholders will be supported with technology, input, financing and market linkage by contract growing system run by the processing plants and monitored by the DOF and partner NGOs.","DOF"],[1,"350","7","Contract Growing and Marketing System for Traceable Supply Chains","Traceability of supply source, with e-Traceability and subsequently screening throughout the supply chain, will be ensured by contract growing and marketing system",""],[1,"350","7","Virus-Free Planting Material and Quality Input Supply Assurance","which will also ensure supply of virus-free PL, good quality and contamination-free feed and other inputs at reasonable price",""]],"220":[[1,"348","6","River Pollution Control","Control of pollution of the rivers in which the main actor will be the Ministry of Environment in collaboration with other concerned agencies.","Ministry of Environment"],[1,"348","7","Environmental Safeguards for Infrastructure Projects in Waterlogged Areas","Prevent further deterioration of water logging, blockade of water-flows and shrinkage of water-bodies by infrastructures like embankment, roads, urban housing projects and industrialization.","Ministry of Fisheries and Livestock"],[1,"348","8","Fish Passage and Canal-River Restoration Programme","projects and programmes will be implemented to construct and maintain fish-passes, fish-friendly regulators, re-excavate canals and rivers restoring and conserving productivity as much as possible.",""],[1,"348","9","Fish and Wetland Sanctuary Establishment and Maintenance","Establish and maintain fish and wetland sanctuaries which will comprise complete ban on fishing in certain eco-sensitive areas like Sundarbans, parts of Kaptai Lake, and several sections of the river Halda, selected beels and haor areas and certain sections of the Bay of Bengal etc.",""],[1,"348","10","Fisheries Conservation Strategy Measures","The conservation strategy will specially include seasonal ban, gear restriction, identifying genuine fishers by providing ID Cards, species restriction, and alike.",""],[1,"348","12","Replacement of Short-Term Khas Jolmohal Leasing System","Present short term leasing system, often benefiting the influential elite and the leaseholder not taking any effort to conserve, will gradually be replaced",""],[1,"349","1","Long-Term Lease Support for Genuine Fishermen","by the long term lease to organizations of genuine fishermen who will be trained in sustainable management and provided other support.",""],[1,"349","2","National Expansion of Seasonal Floodplain Aquaculture","Daudkandi model of seasonal floodplain aquaculture will be further promoted to expand all over the country",""],[1,"349","3","Indigenous Fish Brood Stock and Habitat Conservation","Maintain purity of brood stock of indigenous carp and other indigenous fish species conserving the natural breeding, spawning, nursery and grow-out areas to complete the whole lifecycle and natural reproduction process.",""],[1,"349","8","Integrated Floodplain Aquaculture and Conservation Programme","Aquaculture and conservation will be restructured to reinforce the strengths of each other, sustainable and community based flood plain aquaculture will be combined with maintaining sanctuaries and restocking of indigenous species",""]],"221":[[1,"345","4","Social Safety Net Support for Fisher-Folk","Enhancing Social Safety Net support to fisher-folk will be required.",""],[1,"348","11","Fish Farmer Insurance Scheme","government will look into the possibility of making available insurance schemes for the fish farmers",""],[1,"348","11","Fisherfolk Social Safety Net and Alternative Livelihood Support","government will ... assist the fisher folk accessing Social Safety Nets like VGD and VGF and alternative livelihoods support during the restriction period of fish catching",""]],"222":[[1,"352","2","Forest Department Capacity Strengthening","During the last plan period efforts were made to strengthen capabilities of Forest Department by imparting training to officials and staffs on wildlife conservation, construction of smart green infrastructures in the forests and providing necessary logistics.","Forest Department"],[1,"352","6","Forest Land Record and Demarcation Enforcement","Effective enforcement and prosecution of the Forest Act, 1927, Environment Protection Act, 1995 and Wildlife Protection and Security Act, 2012 can help protect forest resources.",""],[1,"353","2","Forest Department Restructuring and Capacity Strengthening","It needs appropriate institutional framework with adequate trained manpower to face future challenges for sustainable forest management.",""],[1,"353","2","Forest Conservation Capacity Building for Emerging Functions","Moreover, multidimensional activities like wildlife and eco-tourism management, promotion of eco-system services, climate change mitigation and adaptation activities, carbon sequestration and trading etc. are now associated with forest conservation.",""],[1,"355","1","Forest Extension and Nursery Training Centre Strengthening","strengthening of forest extension and nursery training centres.",""],[1,"355","4","Forest Land Survey and Land Record Updating","Emphasis will be given for forest land survey and updating the land record.",""],[1,"355","4","Forest Area Demarcation to Prevent Encroachment","Forest areas will be demarcated to avoid unlawful encroachments.",""]],"223":[[1,"356","2","Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 Preparation","the Planning Commission has undertaken a massive task of preparing Delta Plan, what is titled \"Bangladesh Delta Plan 2100 (BDP 2100)\".",""],[1,"356","2","Delta Commission Establishment","To implement the delta plan Government will establish a 'Delta Commission' which would look after issues concerned like water resource management, land reclamation from the sea and rivers, land protection and agriculture management, and other water related issues.",""],[1,"357","4","Integrated Water Resources Management under the Bangladesh Water Act","The recently enacted Bangladesh Water Act 2013 is designed for integrated development, management, extraction, distribution, usage, protection and conservation of water resources in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"357","4","Water Resources Rules and Regulations Preparation","Water Resources Planning Organization (WARPO) under Ministry of Water Resources, which is working as the Secretariat to the Executive Committee of National Water Resources Council (ECNWRC) is preparing concerned rules and regulation thereof.","Ministry of Water Resources"],[1,"359","7","Spatial Planning for Water Resource Allocation","Spatial planning implications for sources allocation and equitable utilization of resources are another endeavour for water sector development.",""],[1,"361","5","Coastal Zone Special Treatment Policy","The area would be treated as a special zone.",""],[1,"361","9","National Water Management Plan Preparation and Update","Preparing and periodically updating the NWMP for approval of the NWRC;",""],[1,"361","10","National Water Resource Database and Information Management System","Setting up and updating the National Water Resource Database (NWRD) and Information Management System.",""],[1,"361","11","Water Resources Data Archiving Platform Upgrade","WARPO will continue updating and upgrading the collaborative platform for archiving all water resources data and information to be used as reference in any project formulation in the 7th Five Year Plan.",""],[1,"362","2","National Water Resources Plan Updating and Data Archiving","WARPO with the help of all the stakeholders of the water resources sector especially with BWDB, LGED, BHDB, JRC, IWM and CEGIS would update the National Water Resources Management Plan (NWMP).",""],[1,"362","3","Implementation of Water Sector Policy and Regulatory Framework","The National Water Policy adopted by the Government in 1999 would be the guiding document in the water sector activities in 7thFYP period.",""],[1,"362","3","Enforcement of Coastal and Water Governance Instruments","Moreover, the Coastal Zone Policy (2005), Bangladesh Water Act 2013 and Participatory Water Management Regulations (2014) and other relevant document of the government would be taken to put into effect.",""]],"224":[[1,"374","4","Modern Coal Extraction at Barapukuria Mine","Coal production has been increased significantly than previous period through application of modern coal extracting method i.e. Longwall Top Coal Caving (LTCC) method.",""],[1,"374","5","Environmental Mitigation Measures for Coal Mining","The Government is also aware of the environmental consequences of coal mining and is taking steps to address the concerns.",""],[1,"374","6","Feasibility Study for Barapukuria Coal Mine Expansion","feasibility study for extension of existing underground mining operation of Barapukuria Coal Mine towards the southern and the northern side of the basin without interruption of the present production is being undertaken",""],[1,"375","1","Coal Bed Methane Feasibility Study and Drilling Project","A Coal Bed Methane (CBM) feasibility study project has been undertaken to evaluate the methane gas reserve as well as to examine the commercial viability for extraction of CBM from Jamalganj coal field which is about one kilometre deep.",""],[1,"375","2","National Coal Policy Finalization and Adoption","A key step that will be taken in the Seventh Plan is to finalize and adopt the National Coal Policy.",""],[1,"375","3","Deep-Sea Port Expansion and Coal Centre Development","In the near future, however, the Government intends to expand this deep-sea port and develop a coal Centre as \"An Energy Hub\" for the whole country.",""],[1,"381","4","Domestic Coal Utilization Policy","Such utilization would contribute to the higher value-added economic activities, and should be directed by the articulated Domestic Coal Utilization Policy.",""],[1,"381","4","Barapukuria Coal Mine Production Increase Risk Mitigation Measures","At the same time, when Barapukuria Coal Mine realizes production increase, the risk mitigation measures should be taken so that both the production increase and social and environmental concern can be properly addressed.",""],[1,"381","5","Coal Export Feasibility Consideration","This implies that the possibility of coal export shall be considered more proactively.",""],[1,"382","2","Coal Import Port Capacity Planning Study","Based on such studies, a required capacity for coal-import port can be identified.",""],[1,"382","2","Matarbari Coal Centre Design Study","the Government should quickly implement the planned study to design coal Centre with the capacity of 12 million ton in Matarbari area.",""]],"225":[[1,"405","12","Railway System Expansion and Modernization","Expand and improve the railway system to provide safer, better, environment friendly and less expensive and reliable transport system.",""],[1,"408","2","Dhaka Multimodal Integrated Transport System Development","The goal and vision for Dhaka is to take short, medium and long-term measures to develop a multi-modal integrated and safe transportation system for the city.",""],[1,"408","2","Dhaka Traffic Management Improvement Measures","Better traffic management measures and increased public transport including metro-rail are part of that strategy.",""],[1,"408","3","Dhaka Expressway PPP Construction","There is also a PPP contract for building the Dhaka Expressway connecting Uttara and Kamlapur.",""],[1,"408","3","Commuter DEMU Train Service","As part of the multi modal transport system commuter DEMU (Diesel Electric Multiple Unit) train service has been introduced.",""],[1,"408","3","Metro Rail System Development Project","A project to introduce metro rail system has been taken up with support from Government of Japan.",""]],"226":[[1,"406","1","Digitalization of Road Transport Services","Bangladesh Road Transport Corporation (BRTC) and Bangladesh Road Transport Authority (BRTA) have been shifted partially from traditional to digital system.",""],[1,"406","1","Electronic Ticketing and Passenger Service Upgrades","BRTC has introduced e-ticketing, SPASS card and Wi-Fi in buses partially.",""],[1,"406","1","Digital Motor Vehicle Tax and Registration System","BRTA has introduced collection of motor vehicle tax and fee through on-line banking system, retro-reflective vehicle registration number plate, radio-frequency identification (RFID) tag along with 12 RFID reader stations in Dhaka Metropolitan Areas.",""]],"227":[[1,"415","1","Balanced 3R Multimodal Transport Infrastructure Development","The development of a balanced 3R (Rail, River & Road) based multimodal transport infrastructure system.",""],[1,"415","3","Integrated Inland Water and Road Transport System","combining inland water transport with the existing road transport system as well as ensuring a healthy road alignment.",""],[1,"415","6","Integrated Waterfront Land Use and Transport Planning","To promote and revitalize tourism industries, an integrated land use and transport planning for all the potential water front sites viz. Cox's Bazar, Jaflong, Kuakata etc. should be adopted in an urgent basis.",""],[1,"415","8","Controlled Land Use Planning for Road-Adjacent Areas","Controlled land use-planning policy integrating with the drainage infrastructure for the road adjacent areas.",""],[1,"415","12","Strengthening Planning Commission Capacity for Integrated Infrastructure Planning","the Planning Commission could play a vital role by strengthening its sectoral institutional capacity with strong planning wings in key infrastructure Ministries having highly qualified professional planners.","Planning Commission | key infrastructure Ministries"],[1,"415","12","Recasting Budget Approval for Integrated Project Planning","its present major role of approving budgetary allocation of different ministries initiated projects, which are often proposed without proper integration, should be re-casted appropriately.","Planning Commission | different ministries"],[1,"424","2","PPP Unit Establishment in the Ministry of Road Transport and Bridges","For the Ministry of Road Transport and Bridges it is recommended that a separate PPP Unit set up to prepare, evaluate, negotiate and implement PPP projects.","Ministry of Road Transport and Bridges"],[1,"424","3","Turn-key Procurement for Large Foreign-Funded Projects","A particularly pertinent solution will be to arrange for turn-key type procurement for all large foreign-funded projects, either donor funded or arranged through suppliers credit.",""],[1,"424","3","Independent Supervision Technical Assistance for Turnkey Projects","The government can also procure independent supervision technical assistance internationally to serve as government supervision contractors to monitor the implementation of these turnkey projects.",""],[1,"424","4","Infrastructure Operations and Maintenance Spending","The emphasis on operations and maintenance (O&M) spending is essential.",""],[1,"425","1","Comprehensive Roads Network Assessment and Annual O&M Planning","A major priority for the road sector is to do a comprehensive assessment of the entire roads network, both urban and rural and including highways, review the status of each network, estimate the O&M requirements on an annual basis and develop an annual O&M expenditure plan.",""],[1,"426","4","Road User Charges Cost Recovery Policy","The sustainable use of road infrastructure will depend substantially upon the adoption of proper cost recovery policies (road user charges) and should be emphasized for implementation in the Seventh Plan.",""],[1,"426","4","Transit Arrangements Cost Recovery Study Update","The study was done in 2012 and can be updated and adopted for policy making by the Ministry of Road Transport and Bridges.","The Ministry of Road Transport and Bridges"],[1,"426","5","Transport Infrastructure Investment Scale-Up","Increasing the transport investment effort from 1.6 percent of GDP in the base year of the Seventh Plan (FY2015) to 3 percent of GDP on average during the Seventh Plan is a tall order.",""],[1,"426","5","Public-Private Partnership Transport Investment Expansion","The Seventh Plan would aim to increase the amount of PPP transport investment from an average of about 0.2 percent of GDP in FY2015 to at least 1 percent of GDP per year during the Seventh Plan.",""],[1,"426","5","Budget Financing for Transport Investment","The remaining 2 percent of GDP per year of financing will need to come from the budget.",""],[1,"427","1","Urban Transport Institutional Reform","The proper implementation of the proposed transport infrastructure strategy will require significant institutional reforms in the transport sector.","Ministry of Local Government, Rural Development and Cooperatives (MoLGRD&C)"],[1,"427","1","Transport Agency Capacity Enhancement","Additionally, capacity enhancement of Dhaka Transport Coordination Authority (DTCA), Bangladesh Road Transport Authority (BRTA), Traffic Division of Metropolitan Police and related organizations are essential to improve traffic transport management, especially in Dhaka.",""],[1,"428","1","Specialized Public Sector Staffing and Capacity Building","build a quality staff that combines civil servants with special technical skills and strategic professional staff.",""],[1,"428","1","Policy and Strategy Research Funds","Other possibilities include setting up research funds for development of policies and strategies,",""],[1,"428","1","Monitoring and Evaluation System Development","setting up a proper M&E system,",""],[1,"428","1","Transport Planning Centre of Excellence","setting up a Centre of excellence for transport planning, strategy and learning.",""],[1,"431","2","PPP-Based Transport Infrastructure Financing","Since investment needs are large and budget resources alone will not be enough, the Government will put renewed emphasis on PPP based transport infrastructure financing while providing appropriate resources from the budget.",""]],"228":[[1,"417","8","Metropolitan Authority Establishment","there needs to be active consideration for bringing those under a strong unitary metropolitan authority.",""],[1,"418","1","Autonomous Urban Development Authority Establishment","consideration could be given to establishing an autonomous urban development authority (UDA)",""],[1,"418","3","Garment Industry Decentralization Policy","Adopting decentralization policy; it can be started with the gradual shifting of Garment Industries from the core areas.",""]],"229":[[1,"414","17","Jamuna Road-Rail Tunnel Feasibility Study","Feasibility study for construction of a road-rail tunnel underneath the river Jamuna.",""],[1,"416","11","Jamuna River Road-Rail Tunnel Feasibility Study","Furthermore, feasibility study to construct a road-rail tunnel under the river Jamuna would be completed during the 7th plan period.",""],[1,"420","13","Rail Feasibility Survey for Container Terminal Siting","Conducting a survey will assess the feasibility of establishing a container terminal either at Shayestagonj or Srimangal",""]],"230":[[1,"421","7","BIWTA Service Digitization Initiative","digitize all the services provided by BIWTA introducing web based data base application;",""],[1,"421","16","Digitization of Inland Water Transport Services","Digitization of services related to IWT system",""],[1,"421","17","E-Governance Introduction","Introduction of e-governance - Institutional Reform & Restructuring",""],[1,"421","19","Training Institution Establishment","Establishment of Training Institution",""]],"231":[[1,"425","6","River Transport Safety Enforcement and Management Strengthening","Enforcement will be critical and presents a management challenge that needs strong effort in terms of staffing and monitoring capacities.",""],[1,"427","3","River Transport Safety Regulation and Overloading Control","In inland water the main challenge is to strengthen the capacity to monitor the service worthiness of river transport fleet and manage overloading in order to prevent accidents and ensure better service and comfort for passengers.",""]],"232":[[1,"422","3","Chittagong Port Climate Resilience Development","Developing the Chittagong Port as \"Climate resilient\" against sea level rise (SLR) and land subsidence potential.",""],[1,"422","7","Private Sector Port Management and Development PPP Framework","Involving private sector in port management and port development infrastructure on BOO/BOT/PPP model for which a clear, reliable and transparent policy guideline is to be approved by the Government",""],[1,"422","8","Port Institutional Capacity Strengthening","Improving institutional capability in training, planning, safety and environmental management control in the port.",""]],"233":[[1,"423","6","Multi-Mode Surveillance System Supply and Installation","Supply, Installation and Commissioning of a Multi-Mode Surveillance System (Radar, ADS-",""],[1,"423","17","Southern Region New Airport Construction","Construction a new airport at Southern region of the country.",""],[1,"423","17","Southern Disaster Communication Improvement System","Improvement of quick communication system between the reverie and costal belt of southern zone of the country and capital city especially in the time of natural disaster.",""],[1,"423","17","Bangabandhu Sheikh Mujib International Airport Feasibility Study","Detail feasibility study for construction of Bangabandhu Sheikh Mujib International Airport (BSMIA).",""],[1,"423","18","CAAB Headquarters Complex Construction","Construction of CAAB Headquarters Complex",""]],"234":[[1,"430","5","Rural E-commerce and M-commerce Postal Access Service","Ensuring E-commerce and M-commerce services to be reached through post offices in rural localities;",""],[1,"430","6","Post Office E-commerce Centre Transformation","Transforming each post office as e-commerce centre of concerned area;",""],[1,"430","7","Rural International Commercial Services through Post Offices","Making international commercial service available to rural people through post offices;",""],[1,"430","8","Postal Transportation System for Rural Goods Delivery","Establishing a strong postal transportation system for quick handover of goods of rural people to consumers.",""],[1,"430","9","Bangladesh Post Office E-Banking Financial Inclusion","Ensuring financial inclusion through E-banking banking facilities of Bangladesh Post Office;",""],[1,"430","11","Post Office Economic Activity Transformation","Transforming every post office into a centre of economic activities.",""],[1,"430","14","Modern Mail Transport Introduction","Introduction of modern mail transport in every mail line;",""],[1,"430","15","ATM and POS Expansion in Commercial Centres","Establishment of one ATM machine and POS in each of important commercial centres;",""],[1,"430","16","E-commerce and M-commerce Booths and Logistic Mail Management Centres in Post Offices","Establishment of E-commerce & M-commerce booth and logistic mail management centre in every post office;",""],[1,"430","17","Commercial Postal Services Introduction","Introduction of Domestic and International commercial postal services;",""],[1,"430","18","Expansion of Post Office Savings Bank and Postal Life Insurance","Expansion of Post office savings bank and postal life insurance activities;",""],[1,"430","19","Business and Hybrid Mail Services","Introduction of Business mail, Ad mail, logistic mail and Hybrid mail service;",""],[1,"430","20","Rural IT-Based Entrepreneurship Development","Generation of rural IT based entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"430","22","Commercialization of Postal Services","Commercializing postal services;",""],[1,"430","27","Improved Rural Postal Services","Giving importance to rural people in case of proving improved postal services;",""]],"235":[[1,"451","3","Rural Road Safety Engineering Improvement","LGED should focus on road safety engineering during the construction and maintenance of rural roads.",""],[1,"451","3","Local Government Road Safety Awareness and Enforcement","At the same time, the LGIs should take the leading role in awareness building and enforcement.",""],[1,"452","1","Road Quality and Overloading Control Measures","exploring technological options to construct quality roads with available construction materials, introduction of measures to stop overloading,",""],[1,"452","1","Road Construction Quality Assurance Measures","ensuring quality of construction, more involvement of Local Government Institutions (LGI) and ensuring utilization and maintenance of constructed facilities.",""],[1,"452","5","Overloading Control Measures","introduction of measures to stop overloading",""],[1,"452","5","Construction Quality Assurance Measures","ensuring quality of construction",""],[1,"453","6","Road Safety Engineering Improvements at LGED-National Highway Junctions","Improvement of road safety engineering at junctions of LGED roads with National Highways",""]],"236":[[1,"438","4","Tree Plantation and Livelihood Improvement Programme","Side by side successfully implementing tree plantation programme, livelihood improvement projects to contribute towards biodiversity and ecological balance in the environment.","Local Government Engineering Department | Local Government Division | Ministry of Local Government, Rural Development & Cooperatives"],[1,"441","3","Local Planning Linkage with Five-Year Plans and Annual Development Programming","However, local level planning in Bangladesh is underway to link with the Five Year Plans and Annual Development Programing process.",""],[1,"441","3","Bottom-Up Participatory Reform of National Development Planning","A reform in the national development planning process need to shift it towards a bottom-up participatory approach.",""],[1,"442","5","Urban Land Use Planning and Development Control","Ensure land use Planning and Development Control of cities and towns;",""],[1,"442","8","Local Planning Support and Inter-Agency Coordination","To address the issues and to help achieve those targets LGED, DPHE, and WASAs are working.",""],[1,"445","5","Local Plan Alignment and Planning Commission Guidance Framework","The LGIs will not be allowed to spend resources without having their annual and five year plan aligned with the national planning goals and strategies.",""],[1,"445","5","Planning Commission Local Planning Support and Compliance Guidelines","The Planning Commission will be empowered to issue guidelines for local level plan, extend necessary support to prepare the plan and an appropriate order need to be issued to all ministries and departments to comply the Planning Commission Guidelines.","all ministries and departments"],[1,"445","5","Integration of Local and National Development Projects","All national level socio- economic development Projects implemented locally will be integrated with the local plan.",""],[1,"445","6","Local Level Plan Integration Guideline","The Government of Bangladesh has a plan to prepare a guideline to prepare and integrate the Local Level Plans into the National Plan during the seventh plan period to fulfil the constitutional obligation of Bangladesh.",""],[1,"445","7","Technical Assistance for Local Government Five-Year Planning","Current initiatives to provide technical assistance to the local government institutes to prepare five year plan should be further intensified",""],[1,"446","4","Comprehensive Development and Infrastructure Planning Framework","Introduce comprehensive development plan, master plan, Infrastructure investment plan and development control",""],[1,"450","7","Development Planning Supported by Proper Land Use Planning","Therefore, development planning supported by proper land use planning is one of the top priorities of the country.",""],[1,"451","7","Climate-Resilient Rural Infrastructure Mainstreaming","LGED should focus on mainstreaming climate change in all its infrastructure design, implementation and maintenance programme so that changing climate does not jeopardize our continued economic growth.",""],[1,"452","1","Road Master Plan Update","The strategies for the development of the road system include updating of a Road Master Plan,",""],[1,"452","3","Land Use Mapping for Planned Development","Preparation of a Land Use Map to initiate planned development will also be included in the second priority.",""],[1,"452","5","Road Master Plan Update","The strategies for the development of the road system of LGED include updating of a Road Master Plan",""],[1,"452","6","Rural Infrastructure Development Planning and Implementation Based on Feasibility Studies","The rural infrastructure development/improvement will be planned and implemented based on the findings of Effect/Benefit/Impact/feasibility studies carried out in respect of rural infrastructure development projects of LGED.",""],[1,"452","7","Rural Roads Feasibility Study and Economic Rate of Return Methodology","A simpler and quicker way for feasibility study and deriving the ERR will be developed for the rural roads.",""],[1,"452","7","Investment Prioritization and Selectivity Guideline","A guideline for investment prioritization and selectivity will be developed and calculation of economic rate of return will be adopted to guide the major investment decisions.",""]],"237":[[1,"445","2","Expansion of Citizen Committees and Community Participation in Local Government Planning","The Local Government will be charged to expand the role of citizen committees and strengthening participation of citizens from different groups, including women and the poor, ensuring community based participation in prioritizing, implementing and monitoring of development Programme and other functions of the local Government",""],[1,"446","13","Community Action Plan Preparation and Implementation","Preparation and execution of community Action Plan by Community Base Organization (CBO)",""]],"238":[[1,"445","9","Legal and Regulatory Framework Simplification Reform","Review, consolidate and simplify existing laws, regulations, etc. and introduce appropriate regulatory framework to suit the present need.",""]],"239":[[1,"446","16","Small Town Development through Rural Industrialization","Develop small towns based on rural industrialization or create new towns around export-oriented private SMEs.",""],[1,"446","16","New Town Development around Export-Oriented Private SMEs","Develop small towns based on rural industrialization or create new towns around export-oriented private SMEs.",""]],"240":[[1,"447","2","Ektee Bari Ektee Khamar Poverty Reduction Programme","RDCD has been implementing directly an exclusive project Ektee Bari Ektee Khamar (One house one Farm), a poverty reduction programme which is the brain child of Honourable Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina for the last five years.",""],[1,"447","5","Comprehensive Village Development Programme","Comprehensive Village Development Programme (CVDP) is being implemented to promote overall development of all segments of population of a village under a single co-operative organization.",""],[1,"447","6","Rural Development and Poverty Alleviation Programmes","Bangladesh Rural Development Board (BRDB) is engaged in rural development and poverty alleviation programmes; and has so far formed 79,335 cooperatives and 73,762 informal groups helped capital formation of about Tk. 572 crores, provided training to about 50 lacs beneficiaries, provided micro-credit facilities of about Tk. 9,627 crore.","Bangladesh Rural Development Board (BRDB)"],[1,"447","7","Integrated Rural Development Projects","The Rural Development Academy (RDA), Bogra as a specialized rural development institution for training, research and action research has been implementing some projects to integrate water management projects, poverty alleviation through livestock management and bio-gas bottling project and command area development using surface water for rural livelihood improvement.",""],[1,"448","4","Appropriate Technology-Based Rural Production Programme","as part of this vision appropriate technology based production programme in the rural areas will be pursued.",""],[1,"448","4","Rural Poverty Alleviation and Livelihood Support Strategy","The rural development strategy will encompass activities that have poverty alleviation at its core through employment and income generating activities, use of cooperatives, and increasing access to finance for the rural poor, particularly women.",""],[1,"448","5","Rural Appropriate Technology Production Programme","Appropriate technology facilitated production Programme in the rural areas for generating employment and increasing income will have to be pursued.",""],[1,"449","2","Rural Employment Generation and Poverty Reduction Support Programme","Rural employment generation and poverty reduction through setting up organizational institutions at divisional headquarters/larger districts, capital formation, training and post training support.",""],[1,"449","4","Employment Generation for Poverty-Stricken Areas","socio-economic development of the poverty stricken area by generating employment among the people who live in the poverty stricken area.",""],[1,"449","6","Rural Poverty Alleviation and Rural Economy Strengthening","Alleviate rural poverty and strengthening rural economy by increasing agricultural production and through transfer of modern and sustainable relevant technologies to the poor people.",""],[1,"449","7","Micro-Credit and Training Support for Small Farmer Families","Socio-economic development of both men and women of the small farmer families including marginal and landless people in rural areas through providing micro-credit and training for undertaking production, self-employment and income generating activities.",""],[1,"449","8","Rural Economy Promotion and Income Generation Support","Promotion of rural economy by mobilizing rural capital and facilitating income generation activities with guidance, supervision and capital.",""]],"241":[[1,"447","4","Economic Empowerment of the Poorest Project","\"Economic Empowerment of the Poorest in Bangladesh (EEP)\" project aims at livelihood improvement of 10 lac hard core poor people who are unable to meet their daily income needs and suffer from food insecurity particularly in vulnerable environment and remote areas of Bangladesh including flood prone river island (chars) and basins (haors), water-logged areas, cyclone prone coastal regions, river erosion and other areas.",""],[1,"448","1","Making Markets Works for the Jamuna, Padma and Teesta Chars (M4C)","The project \"Making Markets Works for the Jamuna, Padma and Teesta Chars (M4C)\" being implemented from May, 2013 is facilitating better access of char people's agricultural products to markets, improved business services and job opportunities in the selected market systems relevant to the active Char dwellers at 10 northern districts of Bangladesh.",""]],"242":[[1,"448","5","Non-Farm Self-Employment Skills Development Training","Provision of skill development training for generating self-employment in non-farm sector, particularly those for disadvantaged women and other socially backward/ excluded groups, will be an important",""],[1,"449","4","Ethnic Livelihood Improvement through Cooperatives","Livelihood improvement of the ethnic people of plain land through cooperatives by increasing income of ethnic community located in various districts of the country;",""],[1,"449","5","Livelihood Development for Disadvantaged Women","Livelihood development for disadvantaged women reducing vulnerability of women through building awareness, through skill development and employment generation among the disadvantaged women living in south-west area of the country; increasing income of the targeted people; forming capital through savings will pursued.",""]],"243":[[1,"449","12","Cooperative Banking Reform and Legal Amendment","Reforming Bangladesh Cooperative Bank and Central Cooperative Banks; rebuilding central cooperative banks for its optimum use, and making necessary amendment in cooperative act and law.",""],[1,"450","1","Cooperative Union Revitalization and Cooperative Society Monitoring Reform","Revamping and strengthening of Bangladesh Cooperative Union, and development of effective tools for monitoring Credit Cooperative Societies, ensuring effective service to cooperative societies by reducing inactive cooperative societies, promoting cooperative entrepreneurship, establishing a cell to provide necessary advice to the cooperatives.",""],[1,"450","2","Cooperative Training Institutions and BAPARD Modernization","Infrastructure development and modernization of Cooperative Training Institutions and modernization of cooperative offices at field level; and expansion, renovation and modernization of BAPARD.",""]],"244":[[1,"453","12","Growth Centres and Rural Markets Development","Development of Growth Centres and Rural Markets -1200 Nos",""],[1,"453","13","Union Parishad Complex Construction Programme","Construction of all remaining Union Parishad Complexes ( 1900 Nos)",""],[1,"453","14","Upazila Complex Extension Programme","Extension of Upazila Complexes ( 400 Nos)",""],[1,"453","17","Growth Centre-Centric Urban Centre Development","Development of Growth Centre centric Urban centres in selected Upazillas of Bangladesh- 300 Nos",""],[1,"455","12","Increased Budget Allocation for Local Government and Rural Development","The allocation from national budget for LGIs under development and Non-development heads has to be enhanced to strengthen the Local Government and Rural Development.",""]],"245":[[1,"453","22","Transport User Charges and Fees Reform","Improvement in resource mobilization will be made through introduction of user charges and fees by the agencies in all areas of transport and for all use of transport network;",""],[1,"453","23","Private Sector Incentive Package for Transport and Infrastructure","Provision of required incentive packages for the private sector for greater participation will be ensured, not only in transport services, but also for infrastructure building;",""],[1,"454","2","Environmentally Sensitive Transport Network Development","Adequate care will be taken while developing transport network and service so that these do not cause environmental pollution and affect ecological balance;",""],[1,"465","9","Low-Emissions Mass Transport and Environmentally Sustainable Transport Initiative","Promote low emissions mass transport options and establish Environmentally Sustainable Transport (EST) in the country.",""],[1,"478","9","Import Ban on Older Passenger Cars","GoB has banned the import of passenger cars which are more than three years old.",""],[1,"478","9","Tax Remission for Energy-Efficient Imported Cars","The GoB has proposed a significant tax remission for imported cars having upgraded and energy saving technologies.",""],[1,"488","9","Cleaner Fuel and Transport Standards","Introduce cleaner fuel & transport standards to achieve environmental sustainability.",""],[1,"488","10","Public Mass Transit Investment","Facilitate greater investment in public, mass transit options for cities",""]],"246":[[1,"461","4","Climate Change Trust Fund","To implement 44 programmes specified under the six thematic areas of BCCSAP 2009, Climate Change Trust Fund (CCTF) was created in the fiscal year of 2009-10.",""],[1,"461","4","Bangladesh Climate Change Resilience Fund","The Government of Bangladesh (GOB) established the Bangladesh Climate Change Resilience Fund (BCCRF) to support the implementation of the BCCSAP in 2010 with several Development Partners (DPs).","Ministry of Environment and Forests (MoEF)"],[1,"467","12","Climate Change Trust Fund Management","Manage Climate Change Trust Fund addressing the Climate Change impact.",""],[1,"472","6","Bangladesh Climate Change Trust Fund","The government has set up the Bangladesh Climate Change Trust Fund (BCCTF) supported through domestic resources.",""],[1,"472","6","Bangladesh Climate Change Resilience Fund","The government and its bilateral partners have jointly set up the Bangladesh Climate Change Resilience Fund (BCCRF) to support the implementation of BCCSAP.",""],[1,"475","4","Climate Change Adaptation Financing Mobilization","In order to ensure continuous funding, the Government will offer more effort to seek international financial support, in addition to allocating funds towards CCA.",""],[1,"475","4","Green Climate Fund Operationalization","A new financial mechanism in the form of Green Climate Fund (GCF) is about to be made functional.",""],[1,"475","4","National Implementation Entity Accreditation for Climate Funds","The NIE (National Implementation Entity) for both Adaptation Fund and Green Climate Fund (GCF) will be identified, their capacities enhanced significantly so that these are duly accredited with respective funds.",""],[1,"475","4","Development Partner Support for NIE Capacity Building","Support from development partners may be sought to analyse potential NIEs and to enhance their respective capacities including fiduciary capacities and practices.",""],[1,"475","7","National Financing for Climate Change Adaptation and Disaster Risk Reduction","Funding from national budget will be obtained for CCA and DRR, in addition to contributions from development partners.",""]],"247":[[1,"462","10","Tax Incentive Support Scheme","Incentives, in the form of tax-rebate, tax-holiday and subsidies are being considered for implementation.",""],[1,"486","7","Green Labelling Promotion","Promotion of \"Green Labelling\" for environmental friendly products.",""],[1,"488","3","Organic Food Eco-Labelling Option","Eco-labelling of organic foods will be an option.",""],[1,"492","13","Cleaner Production Incentives for WDF Textile Factories","WDF textile factories will be encouraged to adopt low cost cleaner production practices with appropriate monetary policy measures or fiscal incentives.",""],[1,"493","1","Duty Rate Correction and Oversight Committee for Environment Merit Items","Observed anomalies regarding duty rates for environment merit items in the CD/SD rate structures will corrected and thereafter overseen regularly by a committee comprised of representatives from Government; private sector; and civil society organizations.",""]],"248":[[1,"462","18","National Action Plan for Short-Lived Climate Pollutants","A National Action Plan for Short-Lived Climate Pollutants (NAP-SLCP) has been prepared and some of the actions identified are under implementation.",""],[1,"462","18","Low-Sulphur Diesel Introduction Roadmap","A roadmap for introducing low-sulphur diesel has also been developed and some actives are underway.",""],[1,"465","10","Low Sulphur Diesel Roadmap Implementation","Implement of Roadmap to introduce low Sulphur diesel.",""],[1,"465","11","Institutionalization of the National Action Plan on Short-Lived Climate Pollutants","Institutionalize of National Action Plan of Short-Lived Climate Pollutants (SNAP)",""],[1,"466","4","Low-Sulphur Diesel and Vehicle Standards Introduction","Introduce low-sulphur diesel and compatible standards vehicles.",""]],"249":[[1,"463","3","Climate Proofing Guideline Development","Through Climate Change Cell, DoE has already developed DPP based Climate Proofing guideline (final draft) for fisheries and livestock sectors, and developed a comprehensive Training Manual on climate change.","Department of Environment (DoE) | Climate Change Cell"],[1,"463","3","Climate Change Knowledge Network and Database","DoE has also established a Climate Change Knowledge Network (CCKN) including forty Departmental Focal Points (mainly government departments and research institutes) and established a rich web-based Climate Change Database.","Department of Environment (DoE)"],[1,"463","3","Bilateral Offset Credit Mechanism Secretariat","DoE is acting as Secretariat of Bilateral Offset Credit Mechanism (BOCM), a joint initiative of the Government of Bangladesh and Japan to facilitate transfer of world leading low carbon energy efficient technologies, products, services and infrastructure to Bangladesh.","Department of Environment (DoE) | Government of Bangladesh | Japan"],[1,"463","3","Climate Technology Transfer Facilitation through CTCN","DoE is acting as National Designated Entity (NDE) of International Climate Technology Centre and Network (CTCN) in order to facilitate transfer of climate and environment friendly technologies and know how to Bangladesh through CTCN.","Department of Environment (DoE)"],[1,"466","22","Clean Development Mechanism and REDD Mass Initiative","Mass initiative to be taken under Clean Development Mechanism and REDD;",""],[1,"477","2","Climate Change Knowledge Generation","Government will give attention to knowledge generation concerning climate change in the Seventh Plan:",""],[1,"477","7","Low-Carbon Technology Transfer Initiative","the country will seek the transfer of state-of-the-art technologies from developed countries to in order to follow a low-carbon growth path.",""],[1,"479","4","Clean Development Mechanism Projects","Having highlighted mitigation as a priority in the BCCSAP, GoB has initiated the Clean Development Mechanism (CDM) projects.",""],[1,"479","4","Designated National Authority for CDM Support","GoB has established Designated National Authority (DNA) to support CDM-related activities.",""]],"250":[[1,"469","4","Forest Productivity Research and Technological Support","BFRI will emphasize on further research activities to improve the forest productivity through technological backup including non-timber forest products.",""],[1,"469","5","Sundarbans and Coastal Biodiversity Conservation Initiative","Special attention will be given to conserve biodiversity Sundarbans and coastal areas through research and technological innovation.",""],[1,"469","6","Sal and Hill Forest Ecosystem Restoration Research","Research will be conducted on Sal forest and hill forest for eco-system restoration and maximizing carbon sequestration by suitable indigenous species.",""],[1,"469","7","Coastal Afforestation and Enrichment Plantation Research","Research will be conducted on existing coastal afforestation and enrichment plantation to assess the biodiversity change in the context of climate change and salinity intrusion and enhancing livelihood improvement of coastal people.",""],[1,"469","8","Forest Resource Utilization Research","Research will be conducted on better and sustainable utilization of forest resources.",""],[1,"495","4","Baseline Data Development for Environment and Forest Indicators","Utilise BBS to develop baseline data on key environment and forest indicators for future interventions.",""]],"251":[[1,"471","3","Climate Change Adaptation and Mitigation Measures","Climate Change Management under the Seventh Plan will be addressed on two fronts: Adaptation and Mitigation.",""],[1,"472","6","Bangladesh Climate Change Strategy and Action Plan Implementation","the government has adopted a comprehensive Bangladesh climate change strategy and action plan (BCCSAP), focusing on implementing programmes on both adaptation and low carbon development.",""],[1,"472","6","National Adaptation Plan Roadmap","The roadmap for a National Adaptation Plan (NAP) is already developed by MoEF, which will set priorities of projects in the medium and short run.","MoEF"],[1,"473","9","National Adaptation Programme of Action Priority Project","GoB, with the involvement of UNDP, has been implementing the top priority project of NAPA.",""],[1,"476","4","Climate Change Adaptation Facilitation Measures","To ensure a nation resilient to climate change and to facilitate the process of CCA, the following necessary steps will be implemented during the Seventh Plan period:",""],[1,"476","5","BCCSAP Revision","After the expiration of the Action Plan in 2018, BCCSAP should be revised.",""],[1,"476","6","National Action Plan Initiation","NAP will be initiated within the 7th Plan.",""]],"252":[[1,"464","15","Skill-Focused Training for Practical Resilience","Design skill-focused training for resilient agriculture, industry, infrastructure, trade and other fields on principles of practical resilience",""],[1,"464","16","Resilience Research for Education Improvement","Initiate research to understand how resilience principles could be used to improve education at different levels in Bangladesh.",""],[1,"465","14","Public Awareness for Environmental Participation","Create public awareness, in order to participate in environmental activities.",""],[1,"466","23","Education and Research Facilities Expansion","Increase facilities for education, need-oriented co-oriented research and experimental works",""],[1,"468","1","Public Environmental Awareness Campaigns","Expand public awareness efforts",""],[1,"474","8","Climate Change Education Curriculum Revision","Curricula will be revised accordingly to prepare citizens for climate change adaptation in the future by integrating knowledge at all educational levels.",""],[1,"474","8","Civil Servant and Stakeholder Capacity Development Programme","Implement training programmes and capacity development of civil servants and other stakeholders.",""],[1,"474","8","Resilience-Based Technical Skills Development","Steps will be taken to develop resilience-based technical skills through improved technical training and education in multiple dimensions.",""],[1,"475","1","Ground-Level Training and Awareness Programme","This needs to be enhanced by implementing training and awareness programme at the ground level.",""],[1,"475","3","Community Participation and Shared Learning System","The Government will ensure shared learning with all stakeholders.","IMED | MoEF"],[1,"480","5","LCD Training Programmes and Workshops","Government officials and other stakeholders will be trained so that they have a comprehensive knowledge regarding LCD.",""],[1,"489","6","Driver Awareness on Noise Pollution","Raise awareness among drivers on noise pollution",""]],"253":[[1,"464","10","Inclusive Community-Based Adaptation Decision-Making","Ensure effective environmental management activities by allowing inclusive bottom-up participation in adaptation decision making, especially at the community level",""],[1,"464","14","Participatory Community-Based Environmental Resource Management and Protection","Promote participatory, community-based environmental resource management and environmental protection (considering the access for the poor, equity, as well as gender issues) along with community based adaptation.",""],[1,"473","11","Gender Sensitivity Integration in Climate Change Adaptation Projects","GoB has highlighted gender sensitivity as an important issue in climate change adaptation and supported the Ministry of Women and Children Affairs (MoWCA) to take initiative under the BCCTF to integrate gender sensitivity in their respective project designs.","Ministry of Women and Children Affairs (MoWCA)"],[1,"474","1","Participatory Design of CCA-Sensitive Projects","CCA sensitive projects should be designed through a proper participatory process, where the concerns of local people, especially women and the marginalized population, will be duly addressed.",""],[1,"475","5","Gender-Sensitive Project Design Reform","Revise modalities and criteria for ensuring incorporation of gender concerns in project design.",""],[1,"476","2","Local Adaptation Planning and Community-Based Adaptation","An example of such adaptation is the Local Adaptation Plans of Action (LAPA) and the Community Based Adaptation (CBA), which involve the empowerment of vulnerable communities with knowledge and support to become more adaptive.",""],[1,"476","2","Vulnerability Assessment and Multi-Stakeholder Response Planning","A first step is to assess and understand the vulnerability, which could be done through partnerships between local authorities, technical experts and the civil society (local communities, residents).",""],[1,"476","2","Urban Climate Resilience Planning Integration","Urban climate change resilience planning should be linked to urban development processes.",""],[1,"476","2","Social Protection and Local Resilience Measures","This should be accompanied with strong social protection mechanisms, and measures to diversify the local economies and facilitate community level work on improving housing, drainage, and setting up effective early warning, disaster prevention and recovery systems.",""],[1,"476","3","Protection Measures for Displaced People","protection measures for the displaced people need to be framed in keeping with the relevant national and international policies/ initiatives.",""],[1,"476","9","Community-Based Adaptation Integration Mechanism","Efforts must be made to develop mechanisms how institution- led macro- and meso-scale adaptations may integrate CBA, especially making rooms for incorporating local level people-centric participatory CBA planning.",""],[1,"477","1","GAP Dissemination and Implementation","Disseminating and Implementing GAP: The GAP has been developed for MoEF, who will play in initiating and facilitating efforts internally, as well as with strategic partners at the national, regional and international levels.","MoEF"],[1,"477","3","Gender-Sensitive Disaster and Climate Change Studies","Seventh Plan will promote studies looking into violence against women in programmes and policies.",""]],"254":[[1,"485","3","Tannery Relocation to Savar Industrial Estate","The tannery industries operating in Hazaribagh are going to be relocated to the tannery industrial estate at Horindhora of Savar which will dispose the liquid wastes through a common ETP.",""],[1,"485","7","Tannery Relocation and Tannery Estate Development","the Government has decided to relocate existing tanneries from Hazaribagh to Savar, building a Tannery Estate in the process.",""],[1,"486","1","Tannery Relocation Enforcement","The Government intends to shut down tanneries in Hazaribagh if they do not relocate in time.",""],[1,"486","1","Tannery Environmental Clearance Compliance","During the 7th FYP period, the Government will ensure that all tanneries have an environmental clearance certificate for industrial units.",""],[1,"486","1","Tannery Effluent Monitoring and Fining","Tanneries that discharge a comparatively large amount of effluent, or discharge effluent with high concentration of comparatively hazardous will be monitored, and fined if their pollution levels surpass national standards.",""],[1,"486","1","Stronger Penalties for Hazardous Working Conditions","Stronger penalties for hazardous working conditions will be implemented.",""],[1,"490","3","Hazaribagh Tanneries Relocation","a) Relocating Hazaribagh Tanneries (to be completed)",""]],"255":[[1,"463","4","Monthly Public Hearings on Environmental Conservation","To include all level of mass people in environmental conservation activity, DoE arranges Public Hearing in each month.",""],[1,"486","4","Community-Based Pollution Control Enforcement Mechanism","Introduction of Community based pollution control enforcement mechanism to be operated.",""],[1,"495","10","Environmental Monitoring Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening its capacity for and industrial and vehicular enforcement monitoring are necessary.",""]],"256":[[1,"490","5","Common Effluent Treatment Plant Installation in Textile Zones","Installing common effluent treatment plants in around 10 spots in textile zones of the greater Dhaka region.",""],[1,"490","6","Private-Sector Turn-Key Waste Management Facilities","Encouraging turn-key waste management facilities provided by the private sector; determine appropriate sites for common effluent treatment plants for industry clusters.",""],[1,"490","7","Industrial Zero Discharge Policy","Zero Discharge Policy at industrial level will be encouraged.",""],[1,"490","9","Designated Industrial Development Zones with Supporting Infrastructure","Encouraging future industrial development only in designated industrial development zones in Dhaka, Gazipur, and outlying districts, with appropriate waste treatment facilities, sufficient surface water supplies, and adequate infrastructure.",""],[1,"492","8","Textile Sector Water Footprint Mitigation Measures","The Seventh Plan will implement the following specific measures to mitigate the water foot print of the textile sector",""],[1,"492","11","Municipal Water Utility Licensing and Tariff Reform","Municipal water utilities (Dhaka and Chittagong WASA) will review licensing arrangements for large commercial and industrial customers, including scope for redrawing jurisdictional boundaries to include major industrial clusters outside Dhaka city limits; revising volumetric tariffs to reflect environmental externalities; rolling out metering; and developing effective bill collection systems.",""],[1,"492","13","Cluster-Level Stakeholder Consultations for Wet Processing Units","Cluster level stakeholder consultations would be the best way to motivate the wet processing units.",""]],"257":[[1,"492","2","Groundwater Use Regulation and Licensing Reform","Reducing industry dependence on groundwater through strict licensing and fee collection for use of groundwater; banning the drilling of new tube wells by private operators; rationalizing water supply to new development areas and new consumers through a long-term strategy.",""],[1,"492","9","Groundwater Monitoring, Licensing, and Charging Regulation Strengthening","The Ministry of Water Resources will strengthen regulatory provisions for groundwater monitoring, licensing, and charging as part of the rules supporting the Bangladesh Water Act.","Ministry of Water Resources"],[1,"492","10","Differentiated Water Fee and Pricing Rules","differential fees, costs and price structures will be introduced for different locations as well such as for metropolis, urban and semi-urban areas.",""]],"258":[[1,"475","7","Strengthening of National Early Warning Systems","GoB will also strengthen national early warning systems regarding cyclones, storm surge and floods to enable more accurate forecasts.",""],[1,"475","7","Micro-climatic Zone Assessment for Planning","It is necessary to conduct micro-climatic zone specific assessments necessary for more effective planning.",""],[1,"475","7","Institutional Collaboration on Weather Forecasting","Institutional collaboration regarding weather forecasts will be further enhanced.",""],[1,"494","10","National Drought Monitoring System","Establish national drought monitoring system",""]],"259":[[1,"491","12","Integrated Framework for Protection of Common Property Resources","Establishing integrated framework to protect common property resources (ponds, beels etc.) in rural areas and ensuring access of poor community to those resources.",""],[1,"494","12","Payment for Environmental Services Initiative","The notable ones are Payment for Environmental Services (PES).",""],[1,"495","8","CPR Protection and Management Pilot Demonstration","Pilot demonstration on action research for the protection, conservation and expansion of Common Property Resources (CPR) and its management by the vulnerable poor community should be undertaken in Ecologically Critical Area Sites.",""],[1,"495","9","Community Resource Property Restoration and Management","Identify silted up canals and rivers, newly accreted land and bring under CPR for sustainable forest or aquatic resource management by the vulnerable people and establish institutional arrangement.",""]],"260":[[1,"495","7","Cross-Sectoral Coordination for Integrated Green Livelihood Investment","Establish cross-sectoral coordination, collaboration with water, land, fisheries and Planning Ministries to adopt common but differentiated responsibility on policy, planning and budgeting process for investment in integrated programme towards creating green, clean, healthy livelihood opportunities linking to economic transformation.","water | land | fisheries | Planning Ministries"]],"261":[[1,"496","10","BDP 2100 Governance Implementation","Governance issues of BDP 2100 will be implemented.",""],[1,"496","22","Environmental Accountability and Consultation Strengthening","Strengthening the process of accountability for environmental institutions would make them credible.",""],[1,"496","23","Public Consultation Provisions under BECA","Detailed provisions are to be made for holding public consultations in according with the provisions of section 8(2) of the BECA.",""],[1,"497","1","Public Consultations in Environmental Hotspot Areas","Organizing public consultations in different environment hot spot areas",""],[1,"497","2","MoEF/DoE Website Transparency Upgrade","Strengthen the website of MoEF/DoE to conform to the requirement of Right to Information Act (RTI) that requires all government agencies to proactively disclose information.","MoEF/DoE"],[1,"497","3","National Environmental Committee Operational Support","Facilitate effective functioning of National Environmental Committee (NEC).",""],[1,"497","4","Parliamentary Committee Accountability Support","Facilitating effective accountability to Parliamentary Committee on Environment & Forests",""],[1,"497","5","Public Hearings for Inclusive and Transparent Decision-Making","Organize public hearings in different locations around the country to allow a more inclusive and transparent process.",""],[1,"497","6","Environmental Policy and Management Programmes","The following programmes will be implemented to improve environmental policy and aid environmental management.",""],[1,"497","7","Update the Environment Policy","Updating the Environment Policy 1992 taking care of all emerging issues (national, regional & international) with an aim to guide the country's development, economic growth with environmental sustainability involving all relevant stakeholders.",""],[1,"497","8","Action Plan for Policy Implementation","Developing an Action Plan to transform updated policy into actions.",""],[1,"497","9","Update National Environmental Management Action Plan","Updating National Environmental Management Action Plan (NEMAP) through participatory planning process and devising as new Action Plan taking care of all the emerging issues.",""],[1,"497","10","Revised NEMAP Implementation through GoB-NGO Partnership","Implementation of revised NEMAP through GoB/NGO partnership.",""],[1,"499","2","NGO and CBO Environmental Awareness Partnerships","Developing partnerships with NGOs/CBOs to create a wider awareness on environmental issues.",""],[1,"499","3","NGO and CBO Participation in Environmental Committees","Involving NGOs/CBOs in the national environment committee and other national and local committees for the flow of diverse ideas in decision making processes.",""],[1,"499","4","NGO and CBO Participation in Environmental Decision-Making","Involving NGOs/CBOs and facilitate their effective participation in environmental decision making and community mobilization",""]],"262":[[1,"497","11","Environmental Watch Programme Strengthening","a partnership between regulatory institutions and academic institutions could strengthen the environmental watch programme for monitoring the nationwide environment quality.",""],[1,"497","12","Quarterly Environmental Education Newsletter","Publication of a quarterly newsletter with environment education & awareness material.",""],[1,"497","13","Student Civic Engagement and Cleanliness Campaigns","Organizing debates, art competitions, essay writing, cleaning campaign involving students, Scouts and Guides.",""],[1,"497","14","Environmental Awareness Seminars and Symposia","Organizing seminar, symposia on different environmental issues and publish proceeding",""],[1,"497","16","Ambient Environmental Monitoring Network and Environmental Database Strengthening","Strengthening ambient environment monitoring network and establishing a strong environmental data base.",""],[1,"497","17","Environmental Watch Programme with Academic Institutions","Involving academic institutions in the environmental watch programme.",""],[1,"497","18","Environmental Behaviour Change Campaigns","Conduct behaviour change campaigns on key environmental issues",""],[1,"499","5","Hygiene Survey and National Hygiene Promotion Campaign","A hygiene survey will be conducted during the 7th Five Year Plan, and the government will encourage relevant ministries and donor agencies to keep special budgetary provision for dissemination of the survey findings up to district level, as well as designing a nationwide hygiene promotion campaign for awareness building.",""]],"263":[[1,"498","3","Industrial Plant Energy Efficiency Improvement","Achieving energy efficiency by 25% from the current level in the operation of the plant(s).",""],[1,"498","9","Financial Incentives for Waste Treatment Facility Installation","There is a need for financial incentives to promote the procurement & installation of waste treatment facilities.",""],[1,"498","10","Waste Treatment Facility Procurement and Installation Incentives","Provide financial incentives for procurement & installation of waste treatment facilities.",""],[1,"498","11","Tax Rebates for Environmentally Friendly Product Production","Tax rebates for production of environmentally friendly products, including energy efficient appliances, recycled materials, sustainable paper products etc.",""],[1,"498","12","Low-Cost Loan Facility for Environmental Upgrades","Investigate the use of low cost loans for the procurement and installation of environmental upgrades to manufacturing, industry, waste and energy efficiency measures.",""],[1,"507","2","Export Development Fund for Eco-Friendly Textile Technologies","The central bank will develop a new Export Development Fund worth about $500 million to support textile industries in adopting eco-friendly technologies and practices.","the central bank"],[1,"508","2","Tax Incentives for Cleaner and Green Machinery","To encourage firms whose production process heavily impacts the surrounding environment, such as textile industries, to adopt cleaner technology, GoB will consider placing certain tax incentives.",""],[1,"508","4","Green Banking Implementation Measures","GoB will undertake measures so that Bangladesh Bank can implement effectively the newly conceptualized green banking options for some key sectors in the economy.","Bangladesh Bank"]],"264":[[1,"498","14","Women's Environmental Protection and Resource Access Measures","Designing environmental protection and management actions to protect and improve women's access to resources and create scope for their employment and income generation activities.",""],[1,"499","1","Women’s Participation in Implementation and Monitoring","Women participation is to be ensured at the implementation design and monitoring level and through decision making processes.",""]],"265":[[1,"501","4","Forest Land Survey and Land Record Updating","Efforts shall be taken to complete the forest land survey and updating the land record during the plan period.",""],[1,"501","4","Forest Cover Monitoring System","Forest cover shall also be monitored.",""],[1,"501","4","Forest Area Demarcation and Encroachment Prevention","Entire forest area will be demarcated to avoid unlawful encroachments.",""],[1,"502","2","National Biodiversity Strategy and Action Plan Update and Implementation","Initiative will be undertaken to update NBSAP in line with the Aichi Biodiversity Targets and implement the NBSAP as global commitments as a party to the United Nations Convention on Biological Diversity and the Cartagena Protocol on Bio safety to CBD",""],[1,"502","3","Biodiversity Mainstreaming in Plans, Programmes, and Policies","Biodiversity considerations will be integrated into related plans, programmes and policies toward mainstreaming.",""],[1,"502","4","Bangladesh Biological Diversity Act Enactment and Rulemaking","Bangladesh Biological Diversity Act will be enacted as well as necessary rules will be framed.",""],[1,"502","5","Ecosystem and Biodiversity Valuation Integration into National Accounts","Valuation of goods and services provided by ecosystem and biodiversity will be accomplished towards integration of the values into the national accounting system.",""],[1,"502","8","Indigenous and Traditional Knowledge Documentation on Biodiversity","Indigenous and Traditional Knowledge on Biodiversity will be documented.",""],[1,"502","10","Integration of Biodiversity into Climate Planning Instruments","Ensure integration of biodiversity into National Adaptation Plan (NAP) and nationally appropriate mitigation action (NAMA).",""],[1,"502","11","National Biodiversity Benefit-Sharing Policy Framework","National policies will be developed to provide a guiding framework for ensuring equitable sharing of benefits of biodiversity.",""],[1,"502","12","National Research and Development Capacity Building for Genetic Resources Access and Benefit Sharing","National capacities shall be built up to address the research and development issues on identification of products and processes as well as access to genetic resources and sharing of benefits arising out of the use.",""],[1,"502","13","Access and Benefit-Sharing Mechanisms and Nagoya Protocol Ratification","Access and Benefit sharing mechanisms will be established as well as Nagoya Protocol on ABS will be ratified with enactment of Bangladesh Biological Biodiversity Act.",""],[1,"503","2","Herbarium Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening the capacity of the Herbarium shall be undertaken to make it capable of discharging its responsibilities.",""],[1,"503","4","Biodiversity Conservation and Sustainable Use Law","There is a need to enact a law on conservation and sustainable use of biodiversity",""],[1,"503","5","Biodiversity Conservation and Sustainable Use Law","Enactment of a law on conservation and sustainable use of biodiversity",""],[1,"503","7","Fresh Recruitment of Cadres and Other Necessary Staff","Fresh recruitment of cadres officer and other necessary staff",""],[1,"503","8","Conservation Cell and Protected Area Management Cell Establishment","Establishing Conservation Cell & Protected Area Management Cell",""],[1,"503","9","Resource Accounting and Natural Resource Management Capacity Development","Capacity development on resource accounting and natural resource management.",""],[1,"503","10","FD Enforcement and Surveillance Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening enforcement & surveillance capacity of FD.",""],[1,"503","13","Impartial Assessment of Forest Department Programmes","Impartial assessment of all programme of the FD to monitor progress in restoration of forests, protection of biodiversity and impacts on forest dependent communities.",""],[1,"503","14","MoEF/FD Website Strengthening for RTI Compliance","Strengthening website of MoEF/FD to conform to the requirement of Right to Information Act (RTI) that requires all government agencies to proactively disclose information.","MoEF/FD"],[1,"503","15","Parliamentary Committee Accountability Support","Facilitating effective accountability to Parliamentary Committee on Environment & Forests",""],[1,"503","16","Encroachment Identification and Eviction Action Plan","Identification of all areas under encroachments and developing a time bound action plan for eviction.",""]],"266":[[1,"504","5","Toxic Substance Exposure Limit Research","Thus, GoB will promote more work to identify the higher limit of certain toxic substances that humans are able to withstand.",""],[1,"504","6","Landfill Waste Management Research Support","GoB will also facilitate research that looks into effective management of wastes in landfills, which can be used by concerned authorities for policymaking.",""],[1,"504","7","Support for Research on Industrial Pollution Control","This, however, demands more in depth research which the GoB will support under the 7th Five Year Plan.",""],[1,"508","5","Strengthen Environmental Statistics for Green Accounting","To facilitate this process, data for a number of indicators related to environmental performance will be ensured.",""],[1,"508","6","Natural Resource Accounting System","Efforts will be made to generate physical statistics about stocks of natural resources and their changes over time.",""],[1,"508","8","Green GDP Calculation","Using these and other relevant figures, a Green GDP will be calculated.",""],[1,"508","9","Green Growth Research, Analysis, and Innovation Initiative","Green growth is an area that requires extensive research, analysis, and innovation.",""],[1,"508","9","Greening of Existing Activities and Technologies","GoB will explore more opportunities for greening of existing activities and technologies.",""],[1,"509","1","Evaluation Systems Strengthening","evaluation systems will enhance learning, decision making and management, strengthen government accountability, improve public trust and enable stakeholder participation.",""],[1,"509","2","Research Support for Green Initiative Evaluation","As a result, the GoB will support research activities that aim to study the usefulness of such initiatives.",""],[1,"509","3","Renewable Energy Research Support","GoB will support researchers on efficient means to harness the power of wind, biomass and biogas, along with other sources, that will not only be cost-effective and accessible, but will also generate employment and drive growth.",""],[1,"509","4","Green Growth Policy Research Support","Consequently, the GoB will support research activities that helps identify policies and instruments that can facilitate green growth within Bangladesh.",""]],"267":[[1,"505","3","Green Growth Cross-Sector Coordination Strategy","A green growth strategy will cut across many different sectors and institutions.",""],[1,"505","6","Local Government Empowerment for Green Growth Planning","The local levels of the government must be empowered with mandates, manpower, capacity, financial and technical support.",""],[1,"507","4","Green Growth Strategy Vision and Target Framework","To properly initiate an effective green growth strategy, GoB will establish a vision.",""],[1,"507","5","Improved Planning and Coordination Processes","The GoB acknowledges that well- governed institutions can manage long-term planning, implementation, and review, and can align green growth policies with national development.",""],[1,"507","6","Policy Design to Mitigate Market-Driven Externalities","Thus, the authorities will design policies that can mitigate such market driven externalities.",""],[1,"507","6","Analysis and Communication Support for Green Growth Policies","As a result, the GoB will support robust analysis exploring green opportunities and effectively communicating the benefits of such green initiatives is another good practice.",""],[1,"508","3","Access to Climate Change Funds for Green Growth Projects","Access to existing Climate Change Funds, such as BCCTF, will be ensured for projects that advocate sustainability issues.",""],[1,"508","3","Inclusion of Quality Green Growth Projects in Climate Funds","steps will be taken to accommodate quality green growth projects in these funds.",""],[1,"511","31","Sustainable Development Strategy under the Seventh Plan","the Government has used the Seventh Plan to place the building blocks for a strategy to promote economic progress while keeping in sight issues that are important for climate change adaptation and mitigation, harnessing a strong environmental and disaster management capacity and paying attention to green growth dynamics.",""],[1,"512","3","Sustainable Resource Use and Efficiency Measures","sustainable use of resources for production and consumption pattern has been proposed along with measures to ensure further efficiency.",""],[1,"512","3","Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Adaptation Integration","suggestion has been made to integrate DRR and climate change adaptation into the core component of sustainable development, and increase the resilience of communities, and encouraging regional and global cooperation for disaster forecasting and managing post disaster situation.",""],[1,"512","3","Integrated Land, Water, Agriculture, Forest, Urbanization and Energy Planning","a comprehensive perspective linked to use of land, water, agriculture, forest, urbanization and energy has been suggested.",""],[1,"512","3","International Cooperation and Partnership for Sustainable Development","issues of resources sharing, fulfilling of ODA commitment and creating new opportunities for promoting collaboration among government, participation of private sector, civil society and philanthropic entities has been included as targets.",""],[1,"512","4","Climate Change Adaptation and Mitigation Financing Mobilization","The financing strategy involved mobilization of international funding especially for climate change adaptation and mitigation.",""],[1,"512","4","NGO and Development Partner Collaboration for Sustainable Development","The Seventh Plan seeks to build on this progress working closely with NGOs and international development partners to strengthen sustainable development.",""],[1,"512","4","Increased ADP Allocations for Core Sustainable Development Ministries","Accordingly, the Seventh Plan proposes a significant increase in the ADP allocations for the three core ministries dealing with sustainable development programmes (Table 8.4)",""]],"268":[[1,"538","16","Traffic Signal and Solar Panel Installation","Installation of new signal and Solar Panel and Count-down timer",""],[1,"544","5","Rickshaw Puller Rehabilitation and Alternative Mobility Plan","Such measures should be accompanied by rehabilitation plan for rickshaw pullers and provision of alternative modes for the passengers.",""],[1,"544","5","Urban Rickshaw and Van Licensing Reform","Unlicensed rickshaws/vans should not be allowed on roads and licensing procedure should be modernized so that fake licenses cannot be issued.",""],[1,"544","6","Dedicated Bicycle Lane Development","Dedicated bicycle lanes will be established where possible and promoted in city areas.",""],[1,"545","4","Urban Transport Planning for Non-Motorized Mobility","Transportation planning for these urban areas should be directed towards achieving strategy as well as facilitating the operation of the non- motorized transport modes.",""],[1,"545","6","Road and Drainage Maintenance","Maintenance: Proper maintenance of roads and drainage can ensure continuous flow of traffic and lessen traffic congestion;",""],[1,"545","7","Pedestrian Access and Safety Improvement","Pedestrian access and safety: Majority of the trips in urban areas of Bangladesh are made on foot. Pedestrians, therefore, should be treated with utmost importance and their rights should be established by eliminating encroachment of pedestrian facilities by hawkers, building construction activities, garbage disposal bins etc .;",""],[1,"545","8","Traffic Management Capacity Building","Traffic management: Improving management of traffic with clear demarcation of responsibility BRTA, Police and City Corporations/Paurashavas, can reduce the problem of traffic jam significantly.",""],[1,"545","9","Traffic Rules Enforcement and Driver Licensing Improvement","Traffic rules and regulations: By enforcing compliance of traffic rules, driver training, proper licensing, better maintenance and fitness of vehicles etc., pressure on existing infrastructure can be reduced considerably;",""],[1,"545","10","Traffic Demand Management Measures","Demand management: When excessive traffic volume (mainly resulting from use of private vehicles) puts extreme pressure on existing infrastructure, demand management may be required",""],[1,"546","1","Urban Traffic Demand Management Measures","The objective is to reduce traffic volume through such measures as parking prohibitions, fuel pricing, charges for use of specific routes, limiting entry to city centres, encouragement to public transport, creation of pedestrian facilitated pavements in congested areas, etc.",""],[1,"546","2","Coordinated Metropolitan Transport Development Works","Therefore, future development works in transport sector must be implemented with the strong coordination with the agencies involved in this sector.",""],[1,"551","7","Parking Facilities Construction","Construction of parking facilities",""],[1,"551","9","Transport Infrastructure Construction","Construction of flyover/new roads, bridges and culverts etc.",""],[1,"551","11","Road Intersection Improvement","Improvement of existing road intersection",""],[1,"551","15","Multi-storeyed Car Parking Construction","In addition to minimize illegal parking on various roads at Dilkusha, RAJUK plans to build multi-storeyed car parking space.",""],[1,"552","1","Railway Overbridge Provision at Multiple Sites","Provision of Railway over bridge at several sites",""],[1,"552","12","Urban Transport and Road Network Improvement","improving on the traffic and transportation system include development of effective road network, with pedestrian facilities, support introduction of MRTS and better public transport (bus) systems to set up congestion free, safe and sound communication system",""],[1,"553","3","Public Transport and Road Network Improvement","improving the transport system through introduction of public transport (bus) system, and road network and traffic intersection improvement",""]],"269":[[1,"539","4","Action Area Plan Preparation for Immediate Project Implementation","Recently, LGED has started preparing Action Area Plans for Narayanganj and Gazipur City Corporation areas with an intention of immediate project implementation.",""],[1,"539","11","Local Urban Governance Devolution and Capacity Development Programme","Devolving authority at the local urban level and strengthening local governments through transfer of appropriate powers, governance improvement programme, capacity development activities, so that these can improve on resource mobilization, provide better service delivery and regulatory functions, and undertake responsibility for planning and implementing a wide range of , infrastructure provision;",""],[1,"539","12","Community Participation in Decision-Making and Implementation","Involve as much as possible the community, including women and the poor, in participatory decision-making and implementation processes;",""],[1,"539","13","Inclusive Urban Service Delivery Planning and Implementation","Involving public and private agencies with the urban local government institutions and ensure inclusiveness in planning and implementation of service delivery.",""],[1,"539","14","Urban Service Provider Coordination Strengthening","Strengthen coordination among urban service providers.",""],[1,"539","15","Urban Governance Strengthening through Accountability and Inclusiveness","good governance need to be ensured through accountability, responsiveness, equity and inclusiveness in the urban bodies.",""],[1,"540","4","Local Government Capacity and Authority Strengthening","Strengthening of local government capabilities, powers, and responsibilities;",""],[1,"540","5","Urban Local Government Institutional Reform","Reforming the urban local government institutions is a pre-requisite to any meaningful attempt to evolve an efficient urban system.",""],[1,"540","5","Strengthening and Democratization of Urban Local Governments","This would include strengthening and democratization of urban local governments such as paurashavas and city corporations.",""],[1,"540","5","Central Government Financial Support for Poor Urban Regions","Moreover, financial support from central government is especially critical in poor regions where local authorities often fail to generate sufficient revenue at the local level but where provision of infrastructural facilities is very important for economic growth.",""],[1,"540","6","Municipal Capacity Strengthening Programme","Capacity-building efforts at municipal level should focus on augmenting human resources in line with the discharge of responsibilities in major areas of urban planning, community mobilization, and ICT.",""],[1,"540","7","Municipal Revenue Automation and Local Finance Strengthening","The focus of such efforts should be on augmenting municipalities' own resources through automation of property tax and introduction of software-based holding tax assessment, enhancing the effectiveness of intergovernmental transfer of resources to municipalities.",""],[1,"540","7","Improvement of Local Government Expenditure Efficiency","Effectiveness of local government current and capital expenditures should be improved.",""],[1,"540","7","Financing for Sustainable Infrastructure Systems","Adequate financing is necessary for sustainable infrastructure systems.",""],[1,"540","8","Local Government Revenue Strengthening and Tax Administration Modernization","Local government finances, therefore, need to be strengthened and made less dependent on central government grants.",""],[1,"541","1","User Charge Financing and Lifeline Tariff Scheme","User charges are designed to generate revenues to cover operating and finance costs as well as to contribute to investment budgets.",""],[1,"541","4","Municipal Development Fund Transformation into Infrastructure Development Bank","The creation of 'Municipal Development Fund' (MDF) is a right step in this direction. It should be gradually transformed into an Infrastructure Development Bank with activities guided by market forces.",""],[1,"541","5","Transparency and Accountability Enhancement Measures","There are quite a good number of tools which can be used to enhance transparency and accountability as shown below which is proposed to be pursued:",""],[1,"552","12","Property Tax System Revamping","there will be revamping the Property Tax system",""],[1,"552","12","Municipal Financial Management and Capital Budget Planning Strengthening","increasing revenue income, improving municipal financial system and capital budget planning will be a priority for sustainability",""],[1,"553","1","Private Sector Investment Mobilization on BOO/BOT Basis","seek private sector investments on BOO/BOT basis.",""],[1,"553","2","Action Area Plan and Capital Investment Plan Preparation for City Corporations","To ensure the planned development and provide infrastructure facilities, it will require of preparing Action Area Plan or Capital Investment Plan (CIP) for the City Corporations.",""],[1,"553","3","Municipal Financial Management and Revenue Enhancement","increasing revenue income, improving municipal financial system and capital budget planning will be a priority for sustainability",""],[1,"553","4","Urban Local Government Technical Support and Capacity Building","Local Government Engineering Department (LGED) will continue to provide technical support to the urban local government institutions for capacity building and governance improvement.",""],[1,"553","4","Urban Sector Infrastructure Project Design, Implementation and Monitoring Support","It will also contribute to design, implement and monitor of urban sector infrastructure development projects as well as urban sector infrastructure along with support to planning for infrastructure.",""],[1,"553","4","Urban Local Government Officials and Elected Representatives HRD Programme","It also supports to develop skills of ULGI officials and elected representatives through HRD programme.",""],[1,"556","7","Urban Resource Mobilization Measures","Therefore, creative measures will have to be undertaken to mobilize additional resources.",""],[1,"556","7","Holding Tax and User Fee Collection Improvement","While improving collection of holding taxes, other taxes, user fees, levies etc. would be the usual revenue sources, there needs to be capacity building to undertake PPP projects.",""],[1,"556","7","PPP Project Capacity Building","there needs to be capacity building to undertake PPP projects.",""],[1,"556","7","Donor and Concessional Financing Mobilization","There also needs to be efforts to better leverage donor funding, particularly the concessional funds from World Bank, ADB, Government of Japan or any other source, and preparing for long-term debt financing through issuing of bonds.",""]],"270":[[1,"539","8","Public-Private Partnership Economic Development and Employment Interventions","Facilitating economic development, employment generation, reduction of inequality and poverty eradication through appropriate interventions preferably through public-private partnerships;",""],[1,"549","1","Community-Based Infrastructure Project Participation Approach","A community-based approach involving active participation of the members of the community at all stages of planning, designing and implementation of infrastructure projects and in subsequent maintenance should be pursued.",""],[1,"549","6","Supportive Environment for Informal Sector Activities","The urban local government institutions can provide a favourable environment for informal sector activities in a number of ways that may include:",""],[1,"549","7","Access to Credit for Small and Micro-Enterprises","Credit for small scale and micro-enterprises should be established through encouraging and supporting commercial banks to create special purpose facilities for poor groups, such as hawkers and petty traders (market banks); and lending to women and to savings groups (micro- credit).",""],[1,"549","7","Community-Based Credit Union and Bank Facilitation","The urban local government institutions may also encourage the establishment of community-based credit unions or banks and facilitate links among such groups and with the formal banking system.",""],[1,"549","8","Vocational and Practical Skills Training and Capacity-Building Programme","Vocational and other practical training and skills development and capacity building courses and opportunities should be provided.",""],[1,"549","9","Regulatory Support for Home-based Income-Generating Activities","the regulatory framework can be adjusted to permit those activities while maintaining safety and providing infrastructure.",""],[1,"549","10","Infrastructure and Services Support for Home-Based Activities","Provide infrastructure and services which would increase efficiency and productivity of home- based activities;",""],[1,"549","11","Information and Advisory Services for Marketing and Credit Access","Provide information and advisory services for marketing and access to credit facilities;",""],[1,"550","1","Safety Measures Information and Training","Provide information and training on safety measures;",""],[1,"550","2","Practical Vocational Training Courses","Organize practical vocational training courses.",""],[1,"550","4","Khas Land Allocation for Informal Settlers' Businesses","Government may make an arrangement to provide khas land earmarked for business of the informal settlers.",""]],"271":[[1,"545","3","Coordinated Land Use and Transport Planning","Land use planning, therefore, should be directed towards developing transport corridors early so that urban growth takes place along such corridors and not in a haphazard manner.",""],[1,"545","4","Urban Decentralization and Multi-Center Development Planning","Future planning of these urban areas should emphasize decentralization of job centres and activity areas, and development of multiple centres.",""],[1,"546","3","Priority-Based Urban Infrastructure Project Selection","Projects relating to urban development will have to be selected on priorities determined fundamentally through sound comprehensive feasibility studies.",""],[1,"546","4","Project Feasibility Analysis","Feasibility analysis should be done to determine the acceptability of projects to agencies and community groups involved as well as availability of financial, institutional and technical resources;",""],[1,"546","6","Environmental Impact Evaluation of Projects","Projects should be evaluated in terms of their environmental impacts with priority given to those projects having negligible or positive impact on the environment;",""],[1,"546","7","Project Prioritization Based on User Payment Capacity","Projects should be evaluated in terms of user's capacity to pay for proposed services.",""],[1,"550","7","Regional and Local Urban Planning Preparation and Coordination","Urban Development Directorate (UDD) will continue to prepare and coordinate regional plan, master plan and detailed layout and site plan for the existing as well as the new urban centres of the whole country excluding the areas covered by the present town development authorities of Dhaka, Chittagong, Khulna and Rajshahi.",""],[1,"550","7","Paurashava Master Planning with DRR and Climate Change Integration","Hence, UDD will continue to prepare master plan for Paurashava areas along with LGED giving emphasis on Disaster Risk Reduction (DRR) and Climate Change issues.",""],[1,"550","7","Comprehensive National Physical Plan Preparation","A Comprehensive National Physical Plan which was highlighted in 6thFYP can be prepared under the umbrella of the Planning Commission where both UDD and LGED could be the key partner organization for preparation, implementation and monitoring.",""],[1,"550","7","National Comprehensive Development Planning with Interfaced Land Use Plan","Initiative for \"National Comprehensive Development Planning along with Interfaced Land Use Plan for the Whole Country\" may be taken in this regard under the overall guidance of the Planning Commission and in partnership with UDD and LGED.",""],[1,"550","7","Regional, District and Local Comprehensive Development Plans","Regional, District and Local Level Comprehensive Development Plan including physical plans could follow the National Physical Plan.",""],[1,"550","7","Planning Commission Coordination of Urban Plan Preparation","However, a lead role of planning commission is necessary to coordinate the plan preparation by UDD and LGED along with the local government institutions.",""],[1,"551","1","RAJUK Institutional Strengthening","Overcoming the institutional weaknesses will also be a priority for RAJUK during the 7th Five Year Plan.",""],[1,"551","2","Dhaka Metropolitan Regional Development Planning Implementation","To implement Regional Development Planning (Dhaka Structure Plan 2016-2035) for Dhaka Metropolitan Region",""],[1,"551","3","Detailed Area Plan Implementation","To implement Detailed Area Plan (DAP)",""],[1,"551","12","RAJUK Development Control Strengthening","To make RAJUK's development control activities more functional",""],[1,"552","12","Urban Legal and Regulatory Framework Review","there will be review of existing laws, regulations and introduce appropriate framework to cope with present need",""],[1,"552","12","Urban Planning Professional Staffing","Both the city corporation will need to have sufficient number of urban planning professionals for planning, implementation and managing the activities of the corporations",""],[1,"553","3","Urban Planning Legal and Regulatory Review","there will be review existing laws, regulations and introduce appropriate framework to cope with present need",""],[1,"553","3","Urban Planning Section and Professional Staffing","All these city corporations will need urban planning sections with sufficient number of urban planning professionals for planning, implementation and managing the activities of the corporations",""]],"272":[[1,"538","17","Mohila College Building Construction","Construction of Mohila College building",""],[1,"538","20","Cremation Centre Construction","Construction of cremation Centre.",""],[1,"551","10","Recreational and Amusement Centres Facilitation","To facilitate recreational and amusement centres",""],[1,"551","15","Savar Satellite Town Development Project","RAJUK plans to create new township at the proposed a) Savar Satellite Town and b) Keraniganj Model Town projects while ensuring sustainable urban environment through advanced civic amenities.",""],[1,"551","15","Vertical Expansion Housing Development at Three Sites","RAJUK has in plan project that targets to accommodate more people in limited space through vertical expansion at three sites - a) Uttara 3rd phase, b) Jhilmil and c) Purbachal (1st Phase) Project.",""],[1,"551","15","Padma Bridge Traffic Flyover Construction","To provide a new link for traffic from the Padma Multipurpose Bridge and to facilitate north-south traffic movement from Shantinagar to Dhaka-Mawa Road (Jhilmil) a major fly-over is planned for construction by RAJUK.",""],[1,"551","15","Madani Avenue Road Extension","the road connection of current Madani Avenue project will be extended which will create a new link from Balu River (Beraid) to Dhaka-Sylhet highway.",""],[1,"551","15","Purbachal Link Road Khal Development and Protection","the development of100'-0\" Khal along both side of Purbachal link road will be undertaken, to safeguard the lake from illegal encroachment and to maintain the lake natural environment",""],[1,"552","5","Urban Transport and Civic Infrastructure Development","Particularly to minimize the traffic congestion and to improve environment quality the Chittagong Development Authority (CDA) has taken different development activities such as Road Construction, Flyover/Overpass/Elevated Expressway Construction, Land (Plot) Development, Flat Construction, Commercial Building Constructions and Renovation during the 7th Five Year Plan (2016- 2020).",""],[1,"552","5","Attraction of International Hospital and School Chains","Besides to improve civic facilities CDA has plans to facilitate major international hospital and school chains to locate in Chittagong.",""],[1,"552","12","Urban Utility Services Improvement","better provision of utility services like effective solid waste management, sanitation, drainage, for the citizens, optimization of land resources",""],[1,"553","3","Integrated Urban Drainage and Canal Restoration","building of integrated drainage facilities for the entire city, restoring and re-excavating canals",""],[1,"553","3","Solid Waste Management System Development","development of effective solid waste management system",""],[1,"554","11","Safe Water Supply, Sanitation, and Drainage Access Programme","The overall goal will be improving the health and living standard of the people in rural and urban areas by providing access to safe water supply, hygienic sanitation and adequate drainage system.",""],[1,"554","15","Safe Drinking and Domestic Water Supply","Ensure quality water for drinking and domestic purposes.",""]],"273":[[1,"556","8","Serviced Land Development for Urban Housing","the Rajuk develops serviced land to facilitate urban housing","Rajuk"]],"274":[[1,"604","11","Delta Planning Learning Community","A delta planning learning community, therefore, is needed in Bangladesh focused on international oriented knowledge creation, building a knowledge infrastructure and on application of knowledge for policy making and planning purposes.",""],[1,"604","11","National Knowledge Infrastructure for Delta Planning","A knowledge infrastructure should be established as a set of physical, informational, scientific, educational and organizational resources needed to facilitate a delta planning learning community (universities, knowledge institutions and relevant agencies, societal organizations and companies) and action toward a desired collective future.",""]],"275":[[1,"612","2","Skills Development Investment Programme","With donor support, the government has embarked upon an investment programme that will support its reforms in skills development, anchored in the NSDP, 2011.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"612","3","Market Responsive Inclusive Skills Training Programme","Initially, the market responsive inclusive skills training programme will engage public training institutions of three ministries (47,400), 9 industry associations, PKSF (10,000), and Bangladesh Bank Small and Medium Enterprise Department (10,000) to train about 260,000 people in the first phase in six priority sectors, with an average job placement of 70% targeting among others, people from disadvantaged groups (40,000) including people with disabilities and women.",""],[1,"612","3","Ten-Year Inclusive Skills Development Expansion","In three phases the ten year programme will train about 1.5 million people in 15 priority sectors strengthening along the way the training institutions and the quality assurance system.",""],[1,"612","3","Centres of Excellence and Industry Skill Councils Support","To expand the capacity, the programme will support 30 Centres of Excellence and 15 Industry Skill Councils with public-private partnership.",""],[1,"612","3","National Skills Coordination and Human Resources Financing Mechanism","All skill development activities will be coordinated under a National Skill Development Authority (NSDA) with additional and uninterrupted finance to be mobilized and disbursed through a National Human Resources Development Fund (NHRDF).",""],[1,"612","4","Human Capital Strengthening Programmes","Ministry of Primary and Mass Education and Ministry of Education have programmes to strengthen the human capital of Bangladesh.","Ministry of Primary and Mass Education | Ministry of Education"]],"276":[[1,"612","5","Education Sector Human Capital Development Programme","During the Seventh Plan, the Government will involve its resources for improving human capital through development of education sector for higher productive labour force to achieve plan targeted growth.",""],[1,"612","5","Secondary and Tertiary Enrolment Expansion","The Government is focused on raising secondary and tertiary enrolment rates, along with enrolment in vocational and technical education.",""],[1,"612","5","Education Quality and Learning Improvement Initiative","The level of quality and learning will be raised.",""],[1,"612","5","Training and Capacity Enhancement Programmes","To ensure that the labour force are equipped with the right skills, various training programmes and other capacity enhancing activities will",""],[1,"633","17","Curriculum, Pedagogy, and Teacher Capacity Reform","The vision is to establish a system where ultimately every student will be equipped to face the challenges of the globalized 21st century through (a) reforming curriculum, pedagogy and teacher's capacity building to ensure quality education for all;",""],[1,"633","17","Educational Administration Transparency and Efficiency Reform","and, (b) ensuring transparency, efficiency and effectiveness at all levels of educational administration;",""]],"277":[[1,"615","6","Citizen-Centric E-Initiatives and Digital Public Services","Vertical (with government ministries and agencies) and horizontal (i.e., with citizens) policy advocacy and development interventions have resulted in a number of citizen-centric e-initiatives and services such as multimedia classroom and teacher-led education content development in public schools, mobile phone based health service from Upazila Health Complex, agricultural and other livelihood information and services (e-Tathyakosh) online through grassroots outlets.",""],[1,"615","7","Digital Bangladesh Policy and Regulatory Framework","A number of acts, policies and guidelines are in place to guide the nation towards the realization of Digital Bangladesh (see Box 12.1).",""],[1,"615","7","Strategic Priorities for Digital Bangladesh Work Plans","The ICT Policy 2009 and the 'Strategic Priorities for Digital Bangladesh 2011' also contain elaborate work plans.",""],[1,"615","7","Updated ICT Policy 2015","The ICT Policy 2009 has now been updated to ICT Policy 2015.",""],[1,"615","14","Mobile Keypad Standardization Policy","Mobile Keypad Standardization Policy",""],[1,"630","5","Digital Bangladesh Initiative Expansion","The strong progress with the implementation of the Digital Bangladesh Initiative during the Sixth Plan provides a solid foundation on which the Seventh Plan can build forward.",""],[1,"631","1","Equity-Focused ICT Strategy","This equity focus of ICT will be further strengthened during the Seventh Plan.",""],[1,"641","6","National Enterprise Architecture and Interoperability Framework","National enterprise architecture and interoperability framework is being formulated by ICT Division with a view to provide a blue print for automation of government offices and easy and real time information exchange among the government agencies.","ICT Division"],[1,"641","6","Cloud-Based Citizen Services Development","From this Data Centre, a number of cloud based services will be developed and offered to the citizens.",""],[1,"641","6","Big Data and Open Data Analytics Initiative","Hence, initiatives will be undertaken to facilitate big data/ open data analytics for informed and effective decision making and formulation of time- befitting policies and planning.",""]],"278":[[1,"616","1","Mobile Financial Services Guidelines","Guidelines on Mobile Financial Services (MFS) for the Bank",""],[1,"617","1","Online Transaction and Payments Infrastructure","The Bangladesh Bank has already inaugurated the National Payments Switch (NPS) to facilitate interbank electronic transactions that will support online and mobile based financial transactions of customers.","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"618","5","National Payment Switch Expansion","Already many banks have connected with NPS.",""],[1,"627","3","Real Time Gross Settlement Transaction Speed System","To speed up banking transaction, implementation of Real Time Gross Settlement (RTGS) transaction speed system has been undertaken.",""],[1,"632","7","Strengthening Online and Mobile Financial Transactions","As noted earlier, the Bangladesh Bank already has taken a number of steps to facilitate online financial transactions and through the mobile phones. This effort will be further strengthened during the Seventh Plan.","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"632","7","E-Transactions Implementation in the Ministry of Finance","Efforts are also underway to implement e-transactions in the Ministry of Finance.","Ministry of Finance"]],"279":[[1,"623","6","SMS-Based University Admission Registration Service","Since 2009, applications for admission registration at 32 public universities, 400 colleges and all public medical colleges are being done through SMS service.",""],[1,"623","6","Mobile Phone Delivery of Public Examination Results","All public examination results are also being delivered through mobile phone text message service since 2009.",""],[1,"623","6","SMS-Based Paper Re-scrutiny Application Service","Students can also apply for re-scrutiny of their papers through SMS.",""],[1,"634","4","Mandatory ICT Literacy in Tertiary Education","ICT literacy will be mandatorily impart at the tertiary level to prepare students for the job market which increasingly demands ICT skills.",""],[1,"634","4","Internet-Enabled Flexible Learning Expansion","For tertiary education, and partially for secondary education, the internet's capacity for two-way interaction offers the greatest promise for improving access and affordability and for providing flexibility to combine work with further study.",""],[1,"634","4","Specialized ICT Education Promotion","Specialized education in ICTs may be encouraged to feed the burgeoning IT industry.",""],[1,"634","6","ICT Education Loan and Scholarship Scheme","special education loan scheme and scholarship programmes will be introduced for suburban and rural meritorious students who are comparatively less likely to move abroad.",""],[1,"634","6","Long-Term Bank Loan Facility for IT Education","The Government will consider providing long term loan facilities (at least 4 year grace period and maximum 4 per cent interest) via commercial banks to create opportunities for IT education for the poor but meritorious students.",""],[1,"634","7","National Certifying Authority for IT Graduates","A National Certifying Authority would be established immediately for ensuring uniformity in the quality of IT students graduating from different public and private universities.",""],[1,"634","7","MOOCs for Fresh University Graduates","The Authority could begin its work by launching its own massive open online courses (MOOCs) targeting fresh university graduates to groom them into a world class IT manpower.",""],[1,"634","8","Virtual University Establishment Initiative","Initiative will be taken to set up an ICT focused virtual university having campuses throughout the country.",""]],"280":[[1,"619","7","ICT-Related Vocational Training Expansion","in terms of spurring ICT related vocational training, 4 MMCs have been set up in each of the 64 technical teachers training institutes",""],[1,"619","7","Bangladesh Open University E-Learning Programme","Bangladesh Open University (BoU) has undertaken an initiative to launch e-learning/online Programme for its target audiences",""],[1,"619","7","Migrant Worker E-Learning Courses","Bureau of Manpower, Employment and Training (BMET) is also set to launch e-learning courses for migrant workers",""],[1,"627","2","Learning and Earning Training Project","The \"Learning and Earning\" project has been approved to provide training to 55,000 citizens at the district, upazila and union levels.",""],[1,"627","2","Bari Boshe Borolok Outsourcing Training Initiative","The \"Bari Boshe Borolok\" (earn from home) initiative is aimed at providing basic outsourcing training to 12,420 women candidates, of which, 2,240 will be offered advanced training.",""],[1,"627","2","Leveraging ICT for Growth, Employment and Governance Project","Process has been initiated to create 34,000 skilled human resources (30 per cent women) and including 4000 Fast Track Future Leaders in the IT/ITES sector through a project titled \"Leveraging ICT for Growth, Employment and Governance.\"",""],[1,"632","1","ICT Skills Development Programme","Policies will need to focus on expanding ICT infrastructure, improving incentives by lowering taxes on ICT products, greatly expanding the ICT skills base and investing in ICT-related research and development.",""],[1,"635","1","Youth Development Information Network","An organized network to distribute centralized information on various development sectors to local levels that can be spearheaded by youth will be developed to bring about sustained long term development for the youth.",""]],"281":[[1,"622","2","Bangladesh Bank ERP and SAP Automation","Using the enterprise resource planning (ERP) software, financial statements of Bangladesh Bank are being prepared automatically following international systems, applications and products (SAP) standard.",""],[1,"622","3","Integrated Budget and Accounting System (iBAS) Expansion","The latter has been introduced in the Finance Division to bring dynamism in budget formulation and implementation process and to improve the effectiveness of resource mobilization as well as its proper allocation.","Finance Division"],[1,"624","4","Online Investor Registration and Work Permit Service","The Board of Investment (BoI) has allowed online registration and work permit for foreign investors","Board of Investment (BoI)"],[1,"624","4","Online Tax Filing and Payment System","online tax filing has been introduced by the National Board of Revenue (NBR), alongside submission of online income tax returns, VAT and income tax payments","National Board of Revenue (NBR)"],[1,"624","4","National Tax Database Expansion Using National ID Cards","there is still room for making more use of national ID cards in creating a comprehensive tax database including all eligible taxpayers",""],[1,"624","4","SMS-Based Vehicle Registration Confirmation","Vehicle registration confirmation is being sent through SMS",""],[1,"624","4","Customs Automation Reform","Automation of Chittagong and Dhaka Customs has increased transparency and dynamism in the import- export activities",""],[1,"624","4","Deed Registration Digitization Programme","The \"Deed Registration Digitization\" Programme has been undertaken in this regard and work has begun in 3 districts' record rooms - Dhaka, Comilla and Jessore - in addition to 5 sub-registry offices","Ministry of Law, Justice and Parliamentary Affairs | Department of Registration"],[1,"624","6","Integrated Electronic Government Procurement System","The government has introduced online procurement system in phases.",""],[1,"624","6","Online Procurement Management Information System","Additionally, an online procurement management information system (PROMIS) is enabling participants to monitor the administrative public procurement rules compliance with regard to the procurement process.",""],[1,"624","6","Digital Certificate for Electronic Government Procurement","Digital Certificate would be introduced in Electronic government procurement (e-GP) Process.",""],[1,"632","6","Online PPP Proposal and Tracking System","The Office should follow state-of-the-art online process for proposal submission, processing, decision making and implementation progress tracking with individual interface for each ministry and implementing agency.",""],[1,"632","7","Automation of Direct and Indirect Tax Processes","The Ministry of Finance is prioritizing automation of different processes and activities relating to both direct and indirect taxes in order to augment the tax-GDP ratio to an acceptable","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"633","5","e-TIN Unique Identifier System","Use of e-TIN- a Unique Identifier for Income Tax, Customs and VAT to ensure better service delivery and combat tax evasion.",""],[1,"633","6","Online TIN Registration System Linked to National ID Database","Implementation of Online TIN registration system linked with the National Identity Card Database.",""],[1,"633","7","Online VAT Registration and Return Submission System","Online VAT registration and Return Submission to start from January 1, 2015 and June 2015 respectively.",""],[1,"633","8","E-Payment System for Tax and Customs Collection","Introduction of e-payment for Income Tax, Customs Duty and VAT through debit, credit and other prepaid cards.",""],[1,"633","9","Limited-Scale Income Tax E-Filing System","Implementation of e-Filing system for income taxes on a limited scale.",""],[1,"633","10","Electronic Tax Deduction Source Management System","e-TDS (Electronic Tax Deduction Source) management system to be implemented soon.",""],[1,"633","11","Alternative Dispute Resolution for Revenue Litigation Reduction","Use of Alternative Dispute Resolution (ADR) to reduce number of revenue-related litigations.",""],[1,"633","12","Centralized Online VAT and Income Tax Administration System","Introduction of systems for submission, assessment and tax refund of VAT and Income Tax centrally and online.",""],[1,"633","13","ASYCUDA World Customs Automation","Implementation of ASYCUDA World with a view to processing customs data in major customs stations leading to a paperless management system in near future.",""],[1,"633","14","Transfer Pricing Procedures in Customs Law","Inclusion of transfer pricing procedures in Customs law.",""],[1,"633","15","Revenue Officials Higher Training Programme","Provision of higher training to revenue officials at home and abroad to improve their level of efficiency.",""]],"282":[[1,"622","5","Service Innovation Fund","In March 2013, a Service Innovation Fund (SIF) was launched to enable CIOs and Innovation Teams to experiment with new and innovative ideas focused on the TCV (time, cost and number of visits) algorithm.",""],[1,"622","5","Institutionalization of Innovation Awards","Institutionalization of innovation awards, introduced in 2010, will be the key in helping the government officials remain motivated to work honestly and ethically towards the goal of accelerating delivery of public services to its rightful beneficiaries.",""],[1,"622","5","Ethics Committees in Ministries and Divisions","The National Integrity Strategy calls for establishment of an 'Ethics Committee' in each ministry/division for the latter purpose.",""],[1,"623","1","Seed Innovation Fund for Public Service Innovations","In March, 2013, a2i launched the SIF to: (a) provide seed funding to pioneering and creative innovations for more cost-effective provisions for public service to the underserved communities, particularly targeting women; and, (b) enhance capacity of small and medium initiatives working to find creating solutions in technology for development.",""],[1,"623","3","Service Innovation Fund Capacity Building","The SIF functions as an effective capacity building tool for the recently formed Innovation Teams in all Ministries, directorates, divisions, districts and upazilas to learn by experimenting with service delivery innovation prototypes.",""],[1,"623","3","Citizen-Centred Service Delivery Innovation Support","The Fund limits its exposure to innovation that directly improves service delivery to citizens, particularly women, measured around three simple, easy-to-understand, TCV - time, cost and number of visit - parameters to realize the vision of taking \"services to citizens' doorsteps.\"",""],[1,"623","3","Small and Medium Public Service Innovation Support","One of the key specific purposes of SIF includes enhancing capacity of small and medium initiatives creating innovations in public service delivery.",""],[1,"640","5","Civil Service Innovation Incentives","These efforts will continue and will be further strengthened during the Seventh Plan.",""],[1,"641","4","Civil Service Innovation Fund","The fund is in operation for the civil service",""]],"283":[[1,"635","2","ICT Integration for Local Government Service Delivery","the strategy will emphasize the following.",""],[1,"636","3","ICT-Based Local Government Reform","The Seventh Plan will put considerable emphasis on this.",""],[1,"636","4","Seamless Government Connectivity Network","The Ministry of LGRD will create seamless vertical and horizontal as well as reliable and high speed connectivity among the local government and central government institutions and agencies.","Ministry of LGRD"],[1,"636","5","Service Process Simplification and Local Government Digitization","Service process simplification (SPS): The Ministry of LGRD would try to integrate ICTs in local government institutions for back office automation so that front end service delivery is possible through one-stop windows.","Ministry of LGRD"],[1,"636","5","Computerized Local Government Service Management Systems","Application of ICT in office processes such as computerized billing system, inventory management, computerized data entry etc. will help establish more efficient service delivery regime at local levels.",""],[1,"636","8","One-Stop Service Delivery Centers","The Government will create scope for service providers both within the government and private sector to deliver services and disseminate information using multi/alternative channels like Digital",""],[1,"637","1","Digital Centres for Rural and Peri-urban Service Delivery","Digital Centres are envisaged as information dissemination and service delivery outlets for rural and peri-urban citizens.",""],[1,"637","1","Multi-sector Information and Service Delivery System","The information and service delivery system will focus on education (e.g. formal, non-formal and technical/ distance learning), health- care (e.g. healthcare management, telemedicine), agriculture (e.g. pesticide, high-yielding cropping), disaster (e.g. preparedness), self-employment creation, government services, human rights protection and so on.",""],[1,"637","1","Private Sector and NGO Participation in Digital Centre Operations","Such centres are to be run with participation of private sector and non-government organizations for efficient operation and socio-economic viability.",""],[1,"637","2","One-Stop Citizen Service Help Desks","One-stop services/help desk in all unions, upazilas and districts will be created for enhancing citizens' access to services.",""],[1,"637","2","Digital Centre Service Integration","Digital Centres in district, upazila offices, city corporations, municipalities and union parishads present significant opportunities for the government to reduce red tape, streamline work procedures, and co-locate services from multiple agencies into one Centre.",""],[1,"637","2","InfoSarker III Rural Broadband Expansion","To speed up and improve the reliability of the internet connectivity at the Union level, the government has undertaken a new project InfoSarker III to connect at least 1000 unions by optical fibre network within 2 years.",""],[1,"637","3","m-Governance and m-Service Strategy","The Government would design an m-governance or m-service strategy to explicitly set the scope for deploying such tools for improving governance in public service delivery and moving towards a pro-citizen civil service.",""],[1,"637","4","Make the National Portal More Interactive","Nevertheless, the National Portal needs to be made more interactive so that it can add value to the Digital Bangladesh vision.",""]],"284":[[1,"626","6","Online Price Monitoring System","The Ministry of Commerce has implemented an \"online price monitoring system\" which offers daily price updates in its website.","Ministry of Commerce"],[1,"626","6","Mobile Price Information Applications","Therefore, development of mobile apps which could be used by farmers and relevant beneficiaries can increase usage of this information.",""],[1,"627","7","Sugarcane Supply Chain Strengthening Project","To demonstrate such potential, a project has been implemented to strengthen sugarcane supply chain.",""],[1,"628","1","e-Purjee Sugarcane Delivery System","e-Purjee system has been introduced in all state-owned sugar mills.",""],[1,"628","1","Agricultural Supply Chain Capacity Development through Business Portals","This success will lead to wider capacity development to support the agricultural supply chain management system through business portals.",""],[1,"628","1","Agricultural E-commerce Platforms","several e-commerce sites have already come to operation in the country to trade agricultural produce.",""],[1,"637","5","Research and Extension Linkage Development","Research and extension linkages need to be established to reach farmers (crop, fisheries and livestock) and ensure that production is adequate for meeting demand in basic foods from domestic sources.",""],[1,"637","5","Farmer Market Access Improvement","It will be imperative to ensure here that farmers are able to access market for receiving a better price which reflects the market realities.",""],[1,"638","2","Alternative Agricultural Supply Chain Information System","The Ministry of Agriculture would work with the Ministry of Commerce, Ministry of Industry and other relevant ministries, alongside the private sector, for developing alternative supply chain information and promoting fair price for farmers and consumers.","Ministry of Agriculture | Ministry of Commerce | Ministry of Industry"],[1,"638","2","UISCs as Supply Chain Intermediaries","UISCs could be integrated as new intermediaries in the supply chain.",""],[1,"638","2","Farmer E-Commerce Promotion Initiative","e-Commerce for farmers can be promoted for direct trading within country and abroad.",""],[1,"638","2","Projukti haate Joyeeta Rural E-Commerce Initiative","At present, a joint rural e-commerce initiative of Department of Women Affairs of the Ministry of Women and Children Affairs and BRAC called \"Projukti haate Joyeeta\" is being implemented to enable local female artisans to sell their products online for a fairer price.","Department of Women Affairs of the Ministry of Women and Children Affairs"],[1,"638","2","Design Additional Supply Chain Initiatives","Additional initiatives can be designed from good practice international experiences.",""]],"285":[[1,"628","2","GIS-Based Soil Mapping and Digital Mapping System Improvement","To benefit from this opportunity, the Survey Department's project, \"Improvement of Digital Mapping System of Survey of Bangladesh,\" is aimed at creating topographical digital maps: 1: 25,000 scales (over 988 sheets) for the entire country and 1: 5,000 scales (over 263 sheets) for the division-level cities.",""],[1,"637","6","Agricultural Research-to-Use Network","The Ministry of Agriculture and relevant research and extension institutions in association with institutions abroad would take an initiative to create a 'research to use network.'","Ministry of Agriculture"],[1,"637","6","Tailor-Made Agricultural Technology Information Dissemination","Here, researchers and extension workers will supply tailor made technology information to farmers and other players in the agri-value chain in a seamless fashion using different media (CD-DVD, internet, mobile phone, radio and television) for application on the ground.",""],[1,"637","7","ICT-Based Agricultural Surveillance System","An ICT based surveillance system will be developed to assist farmers with timely and accurate detection, diagnosis, prevention, and control of diseases; and, to manage data of input and subsidy distribution.",""],[1,"638","1","ICT-Enabled Agricultural Extension System","The Ministry of Agriculture will equip extension workers with ICTs and/or ICT based extension system so that they can take services to farmers' doorsteps.","Ministry of Agriculture"],[1,"638","1","Mobile Application Development for Livestock and Forestry Extension","Mobile phone based applications would be developed and applied for livestock and forestry.",""],[1,"638","1","Multimedia Content Development for Agricultural Extension","The Ministry of Agriculture and relevant research agencies would work together with private sector to develop effective multimedia content for facilitating agricultural extension workers and tele-centres.","Ministry of Agriculture"]],"286":[[1,"625","3","Rural Life Insurance Service Expansion","the national Life Insurance Corporation has partnered with 2,016 UISCs and it will be introduced to all UISCs in a phased manner.",""],[1,"627","4","Mobile Banking Expansion through Union Information and Service Centers","the government has allowed 5 private commercial banks to provide mobile banking services through 1,700 UISCs across 40 districts",""],[1,"627","4","Postal Mobile Money Order and Cash Card Services","It is estimated that 10 million users have used mobile money order and cash cards through the post offices",""],[1,"627","4","Remittance Disbursement through Mobile Operator Outlets","Bangladesh Bank has also permitted banks to disburse remittance payments through various mobile operators' outlets operating at the grassroots level",""],[1,"633","2","Migration Management System Digitization and Remittance Delivery Support","The Government has undertaken various measures to increase the flow of remittances by digitizing the migration management system and at the same time, easing the process of delivery of inward remittance as a result of mobile banking facilities.",""],[1,"638","3","Rural Financial Access Technology Pilot","Bangladesh Bank in association with commercial banks and financial institutions would explore potential for introduction of automated teller machine (ATM), a point-of-sale (POS) device located at a local retail or postal outlets, to understand whether it can be a sustainable and affordable alternative to connect rural farmers to formal banking system.","Bangladesh Bank"],[1,"638","3","Remote Mobile Loan Payment System","Remote mobile loan payments will also be initiated using SMS and wireless application protocol (WAP) technologies.",""]],"287":[[1,"624","2","Electronic General Diary and FIR Digitization","Introduction of electronic general diary (GD) and first investigation report (FIR) at all police stations by 2021, initially in Dhaka and then in other metropolitan areas by 2015, is mentioned as strategic long-term goals under the Perspective Plan.",""],[1,"624","2","Interactive Police Station Mobile Application","Dhaka Metropolitan Police Service has developed an interactive mobile application.",""],[1,"643","1","Digital Crime Data Management System","digitized crime data management covering information on crime patterns and criminal records also play an important role in serving citizens to make their life safer and more secured.",""],[1,"643","2","Police Secure Connectivity Network Expansion","All district, metropolitan, range and training institutes would be under WAN.",""],[1,"643","3","ICT Literacy Training for Law Enforcement Agencies","All members of law enforcing agencies will be gradually provided basic IT literacy.",""],[1,"643","3","ICT Literacy for Citizen-Facing Law Enforcement Officers","Special emphasis will be given on ICT literacy of officers who have direct interface with citizens for various services such as GD preparation that can be automated through ICTs.",""]],"288":[[1,"626","5","National E-Content Repository Operation","The e-Tathyakosh (www.infokosh.gov.bd), a national e-content repository, is in operation which offers contents prepared by concerned authorities.",""],[1,"627","5","Bangla Digital Language Tools Development Initiative","BCC undertook a few research initiatives on how to expand the use of Bangla through development of (a) Bangla spell checker, (b) \"text to speech, speech to text\" software; and, (c) \"Bangla Word Sorting\" software.",""],[1,"627","5","National E-Content Repository","the e-Tathyakosh, a national e-content repository, is allowing public and non-state actors to publish and share their information in a more targeted manner.",""],[1,"627","6","National Portal Development","the development of National Portal comprising of the 25,000 web sites will also contribute to compile and share indigenous knowledge and innovations.",""]],"289":[[1,"638","4","Sea Fishermen GPS and Radio-Based Safety Initiative","The Ministry of Food and Disaster Management would consider launching an initiative to equip sea fishermen with Global Position System (GPS) to find their way when lost due to protect livelihoods of local small-scale fishermen.","Ministry of Food and Disaster Management"]],"290":[[1,"643","4","Uniform Complaint Information Management System","A uniform system would be developed where all details of the complaint will be recorded.",""],[1,"643","4","Digital Custody Record Use for Court Case Preparation","Custody records for prisoners held in police stations can be used in preparation of cases for court.",""],[1,"643","4","SMS-Based Passport Verification Reporting","Passport verification report can easily be generated using SMS.",""],[1,"643","5","Crime Data Management System Installation","Crime data management system (CDMS) would be installed across all district and divisional headquarters.",""],[1,"643","6","Strengthening Citizens' Access to Police Services","Citizens' access to police services starting with access to police stations to lodge complaints regarding violation of rights will be strengthened keeping in mind the present need.",""],[1,"643","6","ICT-Enabled Emergency Police Communication","ICTs will play a significant role to meet these challenges by making effective use of mobile phones especially in times of emergency.",""]],"291":[[1,"643","7","Cybercrime Prevention and Prosecution Capacity Programme","The law enforcing agencies would adopt programmes to enhance their capacity in preventing and prosecuting cybercrimes and protecting citizens from breach of privacy, security and fraudulent activities.",""],[1,"643","7","Child Online Protection and Cyber Stalking Prevention Programme","The Government will undertake a comprehensive Programme to protect children from child pornography, women from cyber stalking and citizens in general from various financial and privacy related crimes.",""]],"292":[[1,"643","8","Parliamentary Interactive Democracy Capacity Building","It needs to be equipped with the tools of interactive democracy and its stakeholders, both elected representatives and government officials, need to be made comfortable and confident in the use of such methods which could strengthen democratic foundations.",""],[1,"644","2","ICT Support for Legislative Oversight","The oversight functions of the legislative is a key activity which can benefit from the use of ICT.",""],[1,"644","2","Parliamentary Committee Strengthening","Parliamentary committees are a key nexus upon which much of the potential of a parliament can be built.",""],[1,"644","2","Parliamentary Procedural Knowledge Building","Strengthening of members' knowledge of procedural issues can inform more meaningful debate in the House.",""]],"293":[[1,"644","3","E-Dialogue and E-Participation for Democratic Engagement","Using various means of e-Dialogue, e-Participation, e-Deliberation and e- Consultation can strengthen democracy and reinforce trust of the people in democratic processes.",""],[1,"644","3","E-Petitions for Digital Citizen-Government Interaction","For instance, e-Petitions can introduced to allow for digital C2G and G2C interactions.",""]],"294":[[1,"644","8","GIS-Based River Erosion Early Warning and Planning Integration","The immediate priority now is to mainstream the model into development planning so that aversive action can be taken by moving out communities from the probably areas of impact to reduce the probability of loss of life and assets.",""]],"295":[[1,"645","1","Green ICT Education, Training, and Skills Development","The Government will promote green ICT related education, training and skill development to meet demand for environmental skills and expertise at all levels and in all industries.",""],[1,"645","1","Green ICT in Public Administration","Initiatives will be taken to minimize the environmental impact of ICTs in public administration through green ICT approaches, applications and services.",""],[1,"645","1","Teleworking and Videoconferencing for Reduced Travel Externalities","Tele-working and videoconferencing are reducing externalities associated with commuting and travelling.",""],[1,"645","1","ICT Waste Reduction, Reuse, and Recycling Initiative","The government will undertake initiative to minimize ICT- related disposal through reduce, reuse and recycle policies.",""]],"296":[[1,"646","1","Open Data Policy and Platform Development","efforts have been identified to formulate policies and develop platforms to open up data so that other organizations - both government and non-government - can make use of the data to add value to products and services.",""],[1,"646","1","Big Data Initiative","it is opportune to launch big data initiatives which will lead to value added products and services.",""]],"297":[[1,"651","3","Digital Bangladesh Progress Reporting and Data Tracking Mechanism","This initiative will continue with annual updates of the Digital Bangladesh progress.","Ministry of Finance | Information and Communication Technology Division | BCC | Ministry of Information (MoI) | BBS"]],"298":[[1,"649","6","Privacy and Digital Rights Protection Measures","Such steps would include regular review of privacy related laws and guidelines in light of Article 12 of the Universal Declaration of Human Rights and other UN Conventions to preserve privacy in the information society.",""],[1,"664","3","Right to Information Implementation and Capacity-Building Programme","The Information Commission has already taken initiative to impart training and formulated training Manual on RTI implementation mechanism, along with preparation of an electronic data base.",""],[1,"664","3","RTI Public Awareness and Outreach Campaign","The Commission organized awareness campaign in 64 Districts and 19 Upazilas to further strengthen RTI functioning with ability to track data at different level; enhance proactive disclosure, undertake an audience survey and analysis to identify target group strategy and establish partnerships with civil society organizations and media to promote public awareness to fulfill the SDG requirements.",""],[1,"664","3","RTI Strategic Partnership and Legislative Reform Support","The Cabinet Divisions Coordination and Reform Unit will facilitate RTI strategic partnerships, promote capacity Building of officials and initiate legislative and policy changes to Strengthen RTI activities further.","Cabinet Divisions Coordination and Reform Unit"]],"299":[[1,"658","3","Antiquities Act Amendment for Heritage Protection","The Antiquities Act will be amended to strengthen protection of archaeological sites and historical monuments.",""],[1,"659","2","Copyright Protection for Creative Works","The Copyright Office is serving to protect intellectual property rights of creative works from piracy.",""],[1,"660","9","Antiquities Act Amendment for Heritage Protection","Amendment to the Antiquities Act will be undertaken to strengthen protection of archaeological sites and historical monuments;",""]],"300":[[1,"663","1","Buddhist Family Law Formulation","The Ministry also envisions the formulation of Buddhist Family Law in Bangladesh.",""]],"301":[[1,"668","1","Legal and Policy Measures for Women's Empowerment and Social Inclusion","Bangladesh has developed a whole host of laws, regulations and policies to empower the women and to support the socially vulnerable and marginal population with a view to preventing discriminatory practices from hurting these groups and also to provide affirmative actions to enable these groups to participate fully in the development process.",""],[1,"672","1","Expansion of Priority Scheme Coverage","This will be achieved by gradually increasing coverage of priority schemes and ensuring that selection processes priorities the inclusion of poor and vulnerable families.",""],[1,"672","1","Non-Discriminatory NSSS Benefit Access","The NSSS benefits will be non-discriminatory and will be available to all poor and vulnerable people who satisfy the income criteria and other selection criteria relating to life-cycle or disability described below, irrespective of religion, ethnicity, profession and location.",""],[1,"673","14","Proxy Means Test Development for Programme Eligibility","Income eligibility will be determined on the basis of a Proxy Means Test (PMT) that is being developed by the Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics (BBS), Statistics and Informatics Division.","Bangladesh Bureau of Statistics (BBS) | Statistics and Informatics Division"],[1,"674","6","Anti-Discrimination Legislative and Affirmative Action Measures","The Government will also ensure that these groups have similar access as the rest of the population to all Social Security programmes and to all publicly provided basic services in education, health, nutrition, population planning, water supply and sanitation.",""],[1,"674","6","Inclusive Access to Social Security and Basic Services","The Government will also ensure that these groups have similar access as the rest of the population to all Social Security programmes and to all publicly provided basic services in education, health, nutrition, population planning, water supply and sanitation.",""],[1,"674","6","Grievance Redress Mechanism for Excluded Populations","Moreover, an effective grievance redressing mechanism will also be helpful to bring members of these excluded populations into the Social Security network.",""],[1,"676","4","Bangladesh Poverty Database Development","Recently the SID has taken an endeavour to establish a Bangladesh Poverty Database (BPD) using the PMT scorecard approach which will be completed by 2016.",""],[1,"676","4","Community and NGO Vetting for Social Security Targeting","In view of the limitations of the PMT approach, a combination of PMT, support from local government, and support from NGOs will be employed to identify the poor and vulnerable population.",""]],"302":[[1,"671","7","Expansion of Core Social Protection Schemes for the Extreme Poor","Expanding coverage of core schemes for the extreme/hard-core poor, marginalized and most vulnerable people of the society, focusing on mother and child, youth, working age, the elderly and people with disabilities.",""],[1,"671","8","Graduation Programme Scale-Up","consideration will need to be given to progressive but substantive scaling up of the 'graduation' programmes that offer real and direct income earning opportunities and formal and informal work to the poorest, alongside complementary activities that provide poor people with a means to lift themselves out of extreme poverty.",""],[1,"671","9","Income Security and Labour Market Support for Vulnerable Women","Ensuring that the most vulnerable women are provided with income security and greater opportunities to engage in the labour market, in particular as they enter into motherhood.",""],[1,"672","4","Child Grant for Poor and Vulnerable Families","A child grant for children of poor and vulnerable family up to age 4.",""],[1,"673","2","Old Age Allowance for Senior Citizens","The Old Age Allowance for senior citizens who are aged 60 years and above and belong to the poor and vulnerable population.",""],[1,"673","5","Old Age Allowance and Government Service Pension Financing","The Old Age Allowance and the Government Service Pension will be funded by the Budget.",""],[1,"674","2","Open Market Sales Expansion","Open Market Sales (OMS) managed by the Ministry of Food will be expanded as necessary to tackle hunger and food affordability issues as appropriate.","Ministry of Food"],[1,"674","5","Urban Social Security Expansion","steps will be taken to ensure that the priority Social Security schemes for the elderly, children, vulnerable women and people with disabilities are expanded so that urban residents have equal access.",""],[1,"674","5","Expansion of Childcare Proposals and NSIS to Rural Areas","special efforts will be made to expand these benefits to the rural population.",""],[1,"675","7","Social Security Payment Mechanism Strengthening","Strengthening payment mechanisms to minimize leakage and to use the Social Security system to promote financial inclusion, in particular among poor and vulnerable families.",""],[1,"679","2","Targeted Food Distribution Programmes","Targeted distribution of food through Vulnerable Group Feeding (VGF) Programme, distribution of food grain as wages in Food-for-Work (FFW), direct distribution of food to poor households participating in training and development activities (as in the Vulnerable Group Development (VGD), the National Social Security Strategy (NSSS), and expansion and effective implementation of the social safety nets for the ultra-poor and the underprivileged population are some of the strategic means to improve food security of the poor and ultra-poor households.",""],[1,"680","7","Nutrition-Oriented Food-Based Safety Net Channels","Nutrition oriented food-based safety net channels of Public Food Distribution System (PFDS) to be promoted.",""]],"303":[[1,"671","11","Expansion of Urban Social Security Coverage","Expanding coverage of Social Security schemes to include the poor and vulnerable residents of urban areas (Health, Nutrition and Education) and to the socially excluded people.",""],[1,"672","5","School Stipend for Poor and Vulnerable Students","A school stipend for all primary and secondary school going children belonging to the poor and vulnerable households.",""],[1,"672","6","Child Disability Benefit","The children will also have the disability benefit",""],[1,"672","6","Orphans Support Programme","the orphans programme",""],[1,"672","6","Financial Support for Abandoned Children from Responsible Parent","the legal provision to ensure that abandoned children get the financial support from the responsible parent",""],[1,"673","11","Child Disability Benefit","A disability benefit for children suffering from disability.",""],[1,"673","12","Disability Benefit for Working-Age People","A disability benefit for working age population suffering from disability.",""],[1,"676","4","Disability Benefits Access Support","the Government is willing to invest sufficient resources to ensure that the most deserving are able to access the disability benefits.",""]],"304":[[1,"671","12","Social Security Support for Disaster Response System","Ensuring that the Social Security system supports an effective disaster response system.",""],[1,"674","2","Consolidation of Food Transfer Programmes","The transfer of food during and after disaster will continue as a disaster management response under the management of the Ministry of Disaster Management and Relief.","Ministry of Disaster Management and Relief"]],"305":[[1,"672","7","Supply-Side Health, Nutrition, Water and Sanitation Service Strengthening","Supply side interventions relating to immunization, childcare health and nutrition, water supply and sanitation and nutrition outreach will be strengthened.",""],[1,"672","9","Education and Training Programmes for Youth and Workforce Skills","Strengthening education and training programmes to motivate the adolescent and youth to complete education and to enable the working youth and the older workforce to acquire required skills.",""],[1,"673","15","Comprehensive Health Financing Reform Strategy","The Government has already adopted a long-term comprehensive health financing reform strategy, which will be fully implemented.",""],[1,"673","15","Strengthening Health, Nutrition, Water, Sanitation, and Education Services","Additionally, efforts to strengthen the provision of health care, nutrition, water supply and sanitation, and education and training will continue.",""]],"306":[[1,"672","13","Maternal Health Voucher Scheme Expansion","the strategy provides for expansion of the Maternal Health Voucher Scheme (MHVS)","Ministry of Health and Family Welfare"],[1,"672","13","Vulnerable Group Development Training Continuation","continuation of training provided under the ongoing Vulnerable Group Development (VGD) scheme",""],[1,"672","13","Childcare Facilities in Government and Private Offices","provision of childcare facilities in all government offices and in formal private sector",""]],"307":[[1,"673","6","Welfare Programmes for Liberation War Veterans and Descendants","It has been implementing different projects and programmes for the welfare of the freedom fighters and their descendants, wounded veterans and family of the martyrs of Liberation Wars.","Ministry of Liberation War Affairs"],[1,"673","7","Freedom Fighters Benefit Programme","The schemes to support the freedom fighters and their families will continue under the consolidated Freedom Fighters Benefit Programme.",""],[1,"673","8","Digital Certificate Distribution for Freedom Fighters","Prepare and distribute digital certificates among the freedom fighters.",""],[1,"673","9","Self-Employment Training for Insolvent Freedom Fighters and Descendants","Train-up the insolvent freedom fighters and their descendants for self-employment.",""]],"308":[[1,"678","1","Efficient and Sustainable Food Production Measures","Making food production efficient and sustainable: The prime consideration in making food production efficient is to make judicious use of land, water and other critical inputs.",""],[1,"678","1","Rice Production Intensification Through Improved Technologies","Making lesser use of land and greater use of improved technologies will intensify rice production,",""],[1,"678","1","Crop Diversification and High-Value Crop Expansion","inclusion of more high value crops in the cropping pattern, and expanding production in the fishery and livestock sectors will strengthen diversification.",""],[1,"678","2","Agricultural Diversification Research and Extension Strengthening","An integrated approach to diversification calls for strengthening research and extension for non-cereal crops and non-crop agricultural products including fisheries and livestock.",""],[1,"678","2","Integrated Crop-Livestock-Fish Farming System Expansion","Special thrust will have to be given for developing and expanding integrated crop-livestock-fish farming system.",""]],"309":[[1,"678","3","Food Market Connectivity Improvement","improved market connectivity will have to be established at local, regional, national and international level.",""],[1,"678","3","Private Food Storage and Transportation Facilities","Improved private storage and transportation facilities will be important for ensuring spatial and seasonal availability of foods.",""],[1,"678","3","Growth Centre and Rural Market Infrastructure Improvement","Growth centres, hats/ bazars, women market centres, roads, bridges, culverts and railway networks under different agencies will have to continue to be improved under different programmes.",""],[1,"681","1","Private Sector Food Storage Facility Management Initiative","Private sector participation to manage and operate modern food storage facilities to be explored for food stock and management.",""]],"310":[[1,"679","1","Post-Disaster Agricultural Rehabilitation Support","Public and private efforts will need to be strengthened for providing seeds/seedlings and other agricultural inputs following disasters.",""],[1,"679","1","Climate-Resilient Crop Research Programme","Research efforts will be continued to develop weather, submergence and disease tolerant crop varieties.",""],[1,"679","1","Agricultural Early Warning System Development","Effective early warning systems will be developed to provide sufficient lead- time information about occurrence of impending disasters.",""],[1,"679","1","Agricultural Insurance Scheme Introduction","Introduction of agricultural insurance schemes is a special consideration in this regard.",""]],"311":[[1,"679","1","Emergency Food and Relief Stockpiling System","To satisfy the emergency distribution needs, public food grain stock equal to three months of emergency requirement along with relief system to distribute food, clean water, medicine and other essentials are to be maintained.",""]],"312":[[1,"680","9","Annual Monitoring of the National Food Policy Plan of Action and Country Investment Plan","The annual monitoring National Food Policy Plan of Action (NFP-POA) and Country Investment Plan (CIP) to be continued up to preparation & finalization of new National Food and Nutrition Security Policy (NFNSP).",""],[1,"681","3","Public Procurement System Effectiveness Applied Research","The present public procurement system effectiveness through applied research to be explored.",""]],"313":[[1,"681","4","Disaster Resilient Habitats and Community Assets Expansion","substantial improvement is required to increase the number of rural communities with disaster resilient habitats and community assets to 300, with only 2 communities added in 2011.",""],[1,"681","6","Local Government Involvement in Disaster Preparedness and Recovery","Involvement of local government bodies would be an essential part of the strategy.",""],[1,"681","7","Community Disaster Preparedness Training and Public Awareness","Non-structural mitigation measures such as community disaster preparedness training, advocacy, and public awareness must be given a high priority; this would require an integration of structural mitigation with non-structural measures.",""]],"314":[[1,"674","4","Strengthening Climate Change and Disaster Prevention Programmes","The Government's programmes to address climate change and disaster prevention will be further strengthened as a part of its broader development effort.",""],[1,"674","4","Agricultural Research, Embankment, Reforestation, and Disaster Preparedness Programmes","Agricultural research, embankment and reforest programmes, disaster preparedness etc. are already making important inroads in lowering the vulnerability of the population to climate change and natural disasters.",""],[1,"674","4","Delta Region Development Programme","Longer-term programmes such as the planned Delta Region Development can be of further benefit in this regard.",""]],"315":[[1,"686","23","Vulnerability and Risk Database for Impact Anticipation","Utilizing vulnerability and risk databases to anticipate potential impact scenarios",""],[1,"687","6","Climate and Disaster Risk Analysis Requirement for Development Projects","DPP (Development Project Proforma) process has been amended to require climate and disaster risk analysis for new development projects prior to their approval.",""],[1,"688","2","Interactive Voice Response Disaster Information System","In order to promote awareness on disaster-related information, an Interactive Voice Response (IVR) system has been initiated.",""],[1,"688","2","Disaster Management Information Centre","Disaster Management Information Centre (DMIC) has also been established to disseminate disaster related information and early warning in a coordinated way.",""],[1,"688","2","Disaster Alert SMS Dissemination","Initiatives have been taken to send disaster alert through SMS to Union Information Service Centre from DMIC.",""],[1,"691","14","Space-Based Technology Strengthening","Strengthen the use of space based technology",""],[1,"691","15","Capacity Building Strategy Monitoring and Evaluation System","Develop a monitoring and evaluation system to enable the effectiveness of the capacity building strategy to be measured",""],[1,"692","8","Regional Disaster Risk Data Sharing Networks and Agreements","Establish or strengthen regional networks and agreements for real time data sharing on disaster risk.",""],[1,"692","9","Government Risk Assessment and Information Sharing Streamlining","Streamline the risk assessment, analysis and information sharing systems within government.",""],[1,"692","10","National Risk and Vulnerability Monitoring and Reporting","Monitor risk and vulnerability nationwide and widely disseminate regular reports on the changing risk profile.",""],[1,"692","11","Risk Assessment and Climate Change Adaptation Inclusion Guidelines","Develop risk assessment and CCA inclusion guideline and promote DRR and CCA inclusion in district level and below development planning processes.",""],[1,"693","5","Community-Based Early Warning System Using Space Technology and IT","Use of space technology and IT based long lead time EWS at community on flood, flash flood, land slide, cyclone etc.",""],[1,"693","6","National Satellite-Based Disaster Management Monitoring System","Strengthen national space based observation & monitoring disaster management system (satellite)",""],[1,"693","9","National Disaster Information Management Strategy","Develop and implement the National Disaster Information Management Strategy.",""],[1,"693","9","Joint Needs Assessment Protocols and Capacity Building","Approve and implement protocols for the implementation of Joint Needs Assessment and create nationwide capacity to implement it.",""],[1,"693","11","ICT-Based Nationwide Earthquake Seismic Monitoring System","Develop ICT based country wide earthquake seismic monitoring system",""],[1,"693","12","Functionalization of DMIC at DDM and Subnational Levels","Functionalize DMIC at DDM and all district and upazila level",""],[1,"693","17","Multi-Risk Vulnerability Assessment Mapping and Damage and Needs Assessment Cells","Fully operationalize Multi Risk Vulnerability Assessment Mapping (MRVA) cell and Damage and Needs Assessment Cell.",""],[1,"694","4","Vulnerability Index Development for Targeted Resource Allocation","To facilitate the institutional mechanism for monitoring, a vulnerability index will be developed which will help channelize equitable resources to the targeted districts.",""]],"316":[[1,"690","2","Disaster Management Fund Establishment","It is crucial that the Fund be established.",""],[1,"690","2","MoDMR Financial Management Capacity Strengthening","Further strengthening of MoDMR financial management capacity, transparency and accountability is needed.","MoDMR"],[1,"691","7","Disaster Management Fund and National Emergency Operations Centre Establishment","Establishment of DM fund, the National Emergency Operations Centre (NEOC)",""],[1,"691","16","Disaster Risk Reduction Financing Mechanism","Adequate national resources will be identified to finance risk reduction and enable appropriate allocation of resources to disaster resilience through local and national level mechanisms.",""],[1,"693","21","Sustainable Recovery Financing Mechanism","Establish a sustainable financing mechanism to support recovery with Build Bank Better principles",""],[1,"694","5","Financial Management Reform in MoDMR and DDM","A financial management reform in MoDMR and DDM will help improve the implementation capacity to deliver services in a transparent, accountable and cost-effective manner.","MoDMR | DDM"],[1,"694","5","Disaster Risk Reduction Financing Policy","GoB will consider developing a policy on DRR financing, considering different financing models, and allocate sufficient national budget to initiate action whilst welcoming international contributions in support of national efforts, as well as Public- Private Partnerships and the support of civil society and volunteer organisations, to deliver sustainable enhancement of disaster resilience.",""],[1,"707","2","Climate Change Adaptation and Disaster Mitigation Fund","A fund will be provided for adaptation to climate change and disaster mitigation.",""]],"317":[[1,"685","9","Institutional Feeding Programme","Institutional Feeding programme, Rural Infrastructure Maintenance programme, Risk Reduction Programme, Road Maintenance Programme, House Building Grants etc.",""],[1,"685","9","House Building Grants","Institutional Feeding programme, Rural Infrastructure Maintenance programme, Risk Reduction Programme, Road Maintenance Programme, House Building Grants etc.",""],[1,"685","14","Refugee-Related Programmes Implementation","Implementation of the refugee related programmes.",""],[1,"688","3","Strategic Staple Food Storage Expansion","To tackle food insecurity resulting from disasters, the Government keeps a healthy storage of staple which ensures availability during pressing times.",""],[1,"689","1","Social Safety Net Disaster Relief and Recovery Programme","GoB runs Gratuitous Relief, Test Relief, Food for Work, Cash for Works and Employment Generation Programme for the Poorest (EGPP) with SSN allocation.","GoB | MoDMR"],[1,"691","12","Targeted Social Safety Nets for At-Risk Communities","Reduce vulnerability of the at risk communities through effective, targeted social safety nets",""],[1,"693","19","Strategy for Recovery of Vulnerable Groups","Develop and implement a strategy for the recovery of vulnerable groups.",""],[1,"693","22","Safety Net Targeting Mechanism","Establish an effective targeting mechanism for proper utilization of safety nets.",""],[1,"694","1","Disaster and Post-Recovery Support for Vulnerable Groups","Protect & support the most vulnerable groups during disaster & post recovery stage especially women, children & disable groups and older people.",""]],"318":[[1,"696","3","Child Sensitive Social Protection Programme","the \"Child Sensitive Social Protection in Bangladesh\" improves children's access to social protection programmes.",""],[1,"702","2","Expanded Nutrition-Sensitive Social Security Coverage","Nutrition related programme coverage will be expanded, including a nutrition- sensitive approach of the social security system and priority inclusion of poor households with children in social security programmes.",""]],"319":[[1,"696","3","Child Focus Budget Pilot","A Child Focus Budget has been adopted on a pilot basis to monitor the adequacy of budget allocation and actual spending on child related programmes.",""],[1,"701","7","Health Expenditure Efficiency and Governance Reform","The actions will include maximizing the efficiency and cost-effectiveness of health expenditure and improving governance.",""]],"320":[[1,"697","5","Electricity Grid Expansion for Ethnic Communities","extending national power grid and distribution systems for electricity supply to meet these communities' demand for electricity",""],[1,"704","8","Community-Based Technology Adoption Support","The Government will ensure community involvement in the adoption of technologies in line with the traditional food production system.",""],[1,"706","6","Internet Access Expansion and ICT Training for CHT Youth","The Government will provide effective internet facilities throughout the CHT region and will arrange ICT training for the youth of CHT to prepare them for better education and employment.",""],[1,"706","7","Expansion of Rural and Remote Electrification in Hill Districts","The national power grid and distribution system for electricity supply in the different upazilas of the hill districts will be expanded.",""],[1,"706","7","Solar Power Stations for Remote CHT Areas","The Government will expand electrification in rural and remote areas of CHT and will set up solar-based electric power stations in remote and inaccessible areas of the CHT.",""]],"321":[[1,"695","2","Social Exclusion Elimination Agenda","Through the Constitution of the People's Republic of Bangladesh, the Government is committed to eliminating all kind of social exclusion.",""],[1,"697","5","Preferential Social Protection Access for Ethnic Communities","providing ethnic communities with preferential access to social protection programmes",""],[1,"698","5","Disadvantaged People Identification and Participation Support","First the Plan aims to cooperate with local bodies and NGOs to identify the disadvantaged people and enable them to participate in development activities.",""],[1,"698","5","Priority Khas Land Allocation for Disadvantaged Communities","Then priority will be given to the disadvantaged communities in khas land allocation.",""],[1,"698","5","Tea Garden Worker Land Access Initiative","Tea Garden owners will also be encouraged to assign some land within the estate to their extreme poor workers as a mean for them to build their own garden.",""],[1,"698","5","Interagency Coordination for Effective Governance of Disadvantaged Inclusion","Finally, all government functionaries will need to coordinate their activities at all levels to ensure the effective governance of this issue.",""],[1,"698","6","National Social Security Strategy Implementation","The new National Social Security (NSSS) puts considerable emphasis to bring these marginalized groups under the umbrella of social protection.",""],[1,"701","3","Inclusion Strategy Implementation","The Seventh Plan strategy for inclusion is based on implementation of the Constitution of the People's Republic of Bangladesh that provides equal rights and opportunities to all citizens irrespective of race, religion, caste, creed or profession.",""],[1,"708","1","Preferential Social Security Access for Dalit Households","Dalit households will be given preferential access to social security programmes.",""],[1,"708","6","Inclusion of Sexual Minority Groups in Social Protection Mechanisms","Sexual minority groups will be integrated in the national social protection mechanisms including access to social health insurance or other transfers to ensure realization of human rights and fundamental freedom of those socially excluded that are most vulnerable.",""]],"322":[[1,"700","7","Disability Welfare Act Amendment and Coordination Strengthening","Develop the capacity of the ministries and divisions to protect and promote their rights by 1) amending the Bangladesh Disability Welfare Act to clarify definitions of disability and make it consistent with international standards and 2) strengthening the National Coordination Committee for PWD to monitor and coordinate activities of different ministries/divisions.",""],[1,"708","10","Strengthening of the National Coordination Committee for Persons with Disabilities","The National Coordination Committee for Persons with Disabilities will be strengthened to monitor and coordinate activities of different ministries/divisions in implementation of the Act.",""]],"323":[[1,"710","5","Women's Political and Legal Empowerment Initiative","Political and legal empowerment will be ensured by 1) addressing women's advancement and rights issues taking into account the Constitution of the People's Republic of Bangladesh and other commitments to international forums and 2) ensuring participation and representation of women in all national and local political institutions.",""],[1,"710","7","Gender Equality and Women's Social Empowerment Measures","Social empowerment requires 1) eliminating gender health and education disparities, 2) prioritizing women in social programmes, loans and microcredit, 3) eliminating violence against women through adequate reporting of incidents, and medical, legal and psychological treatment, 4) recognizing the multitude of social identities women can have: ethnic, religious, wealth groups, disabilities and taking it into account when formulating policies and programmes to address their needs and 5) promoting women's statuses through media.",""],[1,"712","4","Legal Reforms to Prevent Violence Against Women","the Government is trying hard to change the socio-cultural norms that may hinder women's status and empowerment within the society through adopting laws to ban child marriage, acid throwing, violence against women, eve teasing, dowry etc.",""]],"324":[[1,"710","6","Women's Economic Empowerment Measures","Economic empowerment will be addressed by 1) increasing and improving the opportunities for women's employment; 2) providing an enabling work environment; and 3) strengthening women's economic decision making power by promoting women producers, women trade unions and women entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"712","5","Multipurpose Rehabilitation Centre for Destitute Age-Old People and Socially Disabled Adolescent Girls","Amongst these the \"Multipurpose Rehabilitation Centre for Destitute Age-Old People and Socially Disabled Adolescent Girls\" project, to rehabilitate elderly women and disabled girls through skill training",""],[1,"712","5","Bangladesh Mohila Samity Complex Building for Underprivileged Women","the \"Bangladesh Mohila Samity Complex Building for the Underprivileged Women in the Society\" to create a space for undertaking women development programmes in a safe and proper environment",""],[1,"712","5","Women Employment and Economic Empowerment Initiatives","The Government has carried out various initiatives to help promote women employment and their economic empowerment.",""],[1,"713","8","Women's Human Capabilities Improvement Initiative","Improve women's human capabilities: This deals with women's and girls' access to health care, life expectancy, nutrition, reproductive health, education, information, training, and other services that enables women to achieve better health and educational outcomes.",""]],"325":[[1,"715","1","Mass Media Campaign on Healthy Diet and Physical Activity","Campaign through media on obesity and overweight, and the importance of physical work and healthy food would be undertaken.",""],[1,"715","1","Salt Iodization and School Physical Exercise Measures","Ensuring salt iodization through BSTI and compulsory physical exercise in schools are essential.",""],[1,"715","1","Food Fortification Promotion with Local Producers","Target specific food fortification for micronutrients would be promoted with local producers.",""],[1,"715","1","Maternal Health Vouchers and Nutrition Allowance Support","Food security and safety net programmes including the maternal health vouchers and allowance to cover women's/girls' nutritional deficiencies particularly in the calamity/poverty prone areas would be continued and expanded.",""]],"326":[[1,"715","1","Homestead Gardening and Poultry Expansion","Promotion and expansion of homestead gardening and poultry in the rural and remote areas particularly amongst the poor introducing climate tolerant varieties will be done to ensure protein and vitamin consumption.",""]],"327":[[1,"716","2","Expansion of Safe Water and Sanitation Services","These services, both at home and in public places would be expanded to facilitate women's participation in economic and political activities.",""],[1,"716","2","Arsenic and Salinity Screening and Traditional Water Filtering Dissemination","Arsenic and saline screening would be ensured and traditional filtering methods would be disseminated widely.",""],[1,"716","2","Northern and Coastal Water Conservation Programme","Also water conservation Programme for the Northern region and coastal belt is important to ease water stress and protect from salinity.",""],[1,"716","2","Accessible Drinking Water and Toilet Facilities at Transport Hubs","Arrangement of safe drinking water and accessible toilet facilities would be there for the women and people with disability in rail station, bus stand, and launch terminal.",""],[1,"721","3","Climate-Resilient Water, Flood Refuge, and Sanitation Facilities","Water, flood refuge and sanitation facilities would be expanded with designs that address women's needs including that for child care, delivery and such other, and address women's safety and security concerns.",""]],"328":[[1,"717","4","Public Sector Vacancy Filling and Gender-Inclusive Recruitment Reform","Filling up of the existing vacant positions in the public sector will allow additional employment for a large number of women and men where women with right qualifications may be given preference to increase women's share of employment.",""],[1,"717","4","Improved Working Conditions for Women in Civil Service","Improvements in working conditions are needed to attract more women to the civil service.",""],[1,"717","4","Women’s Recruitment and Promotion Support in Civil Service","Recruitment of women; timely promotions, especially at senior levels; addressing safety and security concerns at field levels; gender sensitivity and elimination of discriminatory attitudes among management will enhance women's participation.",""],[1,"717","4","Transparent Human Resource Management Reform","Institutional weaknesses and constraints should be removed through transparent human resource management functions.",""]],"329":[[1,"718","4","Housing and Land Support for Women Displaced by River Erosion","In case of river erosion or such disaster induced migration, women would be considered as s special group for housing or land support.",""],[1,"721","1","Women’s Livelihood Services for Food Security","Women's livelihood services would continue to ensure food security (e.g. low gestation and less water intensive crops, food storage and preservation technology, and food preservation during calamities) amongst vulnerable groups, including climate induced migrants to urban areas.",""],[1,"721","2","Women's Climate Change Mitigation and Green Livelihoods Initiative","Also women's engagement in climate change mitigation measures would be increased, such as, knowledge of technology with low carbon emission, such as, forest and bio-diversity conservation, water management, access to renewable energy (solar, wind, bio-gas), and scientific waste management, where women also can become entrepreneurs or workers in these areas.",""]],"330":[[1,"720","2","Review and Revision of Discriminatory Laws and Policies","Some laws and policies are yet to incorporate provisions to ensure women's participation and equal rights and these need review and revision.",""],[1,"720","2","Gender Review of Sectoral Policies","It is essential that all sectoral policies are also reviewed from a gender lens in order to make them more conducive to women's participation and empowerment.",""],[1,"720","2","Capacity Strengthening for MOWCA Policy Support","MOWCA's capacity would be improved to provide technical support to line ministries in reviewing such laws.","MOWCA | line ministries"],[1,"720","2","Partnership with Women Groups","Partnership with women groups would be promoted for this.",""],[1,"720","4","Girl Child Rights Mainstreaming in Laws and Policies","Girls as a distinct group would be recognized and their rights and advancement would be upheld in all relevant policies and laws.","Ministry of Women and Children's Affair (MOWCA)"],[1,"722","3","Gender Mainstreaming in Macro-Economic and Sectoral Policies","Mainstreaming of gender would continue and all macro-economic and sectoral policies would integrate gender as a crosscutting theme.",""],[1,"722","3","Gender Equality Action Planning","Action plans should be drawn with a view to reduce inequality and promote an equal relationship between sexes.",""]],"331":[[1,"720","3","Women’s Rights Law Enforcement and Accountability Mechanisms","The enforcement of the legal and policy provisions would be ensured through establishing effective mechanisms and accountability.",""],[1,"720","3","Women’s Legal Aid and Access to Justice Support","Women's access to the legal system would be ensured through expansion of support from Legal Aid Fund, simplification of legal procedures, removal of discriminatory procedures and retention of legal practitioners to support poor women.",""],[1,"720","3","Judicial and Law Enforcement Capacity Strengthening for Gender Cases","Capacity of judiciary and law enforcement agencies to deal with such cases would be strengthened.",""],[1,"720","3","Human Trafficking Tribunal Establishment","A separate tribunal for dealing with human trafficking cases would be formed.",""],[1,"720","5","Transparent Accountability Mechanism for Law Enforcement Agencies","A transparent accountability mechanism for the law enforcing agencies would be in place so that they are accountable to take action fast on offences related to VAW and women's human rights.",""],[1,"720","5","Gender Sensitivity Orientation and Training for Law Enforcement Personnel","Additionally, human resources for the agencies would be provided sufficient orientation and training to make them gender sensitive.",""],[1,"722","2","Gender Equality Law Enforcement and Monitoring","Enforcement of laws and policies and effective monitoring should be ensured for good administration and governance.",""]],"332":[[1,"722","2","Gender Equality Priority Action Framework","Priority areas would be chosen on the basis of contribution towards both economic growth and women's empowerment and actions that can facilitate results in more than one area.",""],[1,"722","2","Geographic Gender Gap Targeting and Resource Allocation","An assessment of geographic areas that lag behind national average as measured by different gender equality indicators would be prioritized for resource allocation and closing the gender gap in the identified areas.",""],[1,"722","2","Gender Equality Resource Mobilization Review","The available resource envelop for 7th FYP would be reviewed, resource requirements to address gender equality objectives and targets should be estimated and additional resources should be sought, as needed.",""],[1,"723","2","Gender Mainstreaming Resource Allocation and Capacity Support","It is therefore important to allocate both financial resources as per targets of each agency and projects and human resources in the institution with capacity development support.",""],[1,"724","2","Gender Equality Accountability Framework","Accountability for the achievement of gender equality targets and results must be ensured.",""]]}});